Object.assign(window.TEM8_DICTIONARY, {"deeply":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/deeply__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deeply__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdiːpli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"very; very much","cn":"很；非常","ex":{"en":"She is deeply religious.","cn":"她非常虔诚。"}},{"en":"used with some verbs to show that something is done in a very complete way","cn":"（与某些动词连用）深刻地，强烈地，深沉地","ex":{"en":"to breathe/inhale deeply (= filling your lungs with air)","cn":"深呼吸；深深地吸气"}},{"en":"to a depth that is quite a long way from the surface of something","cn":"至深处","ex":{"en":"to drill deeply into the wood","cn":"（钻头）往木头深处钻"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"to breathe/sigh/exhale deeply (= using all of the air in your lungs)","cn":"深呼吸；深深地叹息；长长地呼气"},{"en":"Opinion is deeply divided on this issue.","cn":"对这个问题的意见分歧很大。"}]},"death":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/death__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/death__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"deθ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the fact of somebody dying or being killed","cn":"死；死亡","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"the anniversary of his wife’s death","cn":"他妻子的忌日"}},{"en":"the end of life; the state of being dead","cn":"生命的终止；死亡状态","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"Police are trying to establish the cause of death.","cn":"警方在设法确定死因。"}},{"en":"the stopping of biochemical processes of life in a cell or tissue, in a way that cannot be reversed","cn":"（细胞或组织的）死亡","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"This process becomes irreversible and leads to cell death.","cn":"这个过程变得不可逆并导致细胞死亡。"}},{"en":"the permanent end or destruction of something","cn":"永久的灭亡；毁灭；破灭","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"the death of all my plans","cn":"我所有计划的破灭"}},{"en":"the power that destroys life, imagined as human in form","cn":"死神","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"literary","ex":{"en":"Death is often shown in paintings as a human skeleton.","cn":"死神在绘画作品中常以骷髅形式出现。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"死;死亡","en":"Death is the permanent end of the life of a person or animal.","ex":{"en":"1.5 million people are in immediate danger of death from starvation.","cn":"150 万人正面临着被饿死的急迫危险。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(某种）死法，死亡方式","en":"A particular kind of death is a particular way of dying.","ex":{"en":"They made sure that he died a horrible death","cn":"他们让他死得很惨。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"终结;结束;灭亡;破灭","en":"The death of something is the permanent end of it.","ex":{"en":"It meant the death of everything he had ever been or ever hoped to be.","cn":"这意味着他过去的一切存在或曾经希望的存在均已终结。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"病危;行将就木","en":"If you say that someone is at death's door, you mean they are very ill indeed and likely to die.","ex":{"en":"He told his boss a tale about his mother being at death's door","cn":"他向老板谎称自己的母亲病危。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"斗争到底;誓死捍卫","en":"If you say that you will fight to the death for something, you are emphasizing that you will do anything to achieve or protect it, even if you suffer as a consequence.","ex":{"en":"He said they did not want war—but if attacked they would fight to the death","cn":"他说他们不希望有战争——但一旦遭到攻击，定会战斗到底。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"生死决斗;殊死决战","en":"If you refer to a fight or contest as a fight to the death, you are emphasizing that it will not stop until the death or total victory of one of the opponents.","ex":{"en":"...an eleven-hour fight to the death between a baboon and leopard","cn":"一只狒狒和一头美洲豹之间长达 11小时的殊死搏斗"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"生死攸关的;至关重要的","en":"If you say that something is a matter of life and death, you are emphasizing that it is extremely important, often because someone may die or suffer great harm if people do not act immediately.","ex":{"en":"Well, never mind, John, it's not a matter of life and death","cn":"好了，约翰，别太在意了。这又不是什么生死攸关的大事。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"被处死;被处决","en":"If someone is put to death, they are executed.","ex":{"en":"Those put to death by firing squad included three generals.","cn":"行刑队处决的那些人里有 3 名将军。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"(用于动词后）以致死亡","en":"You use to death after a verb to indicate that a particular action or process results in someone's death.","ex":{"en":"He was stabbed to death.","cn":"他被刀刺中身亡。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"(用于形容词或动词后，表示强调)吓得要死/无聊得要命","en":"You use to death after an adjective or a verb to emphasize the action, state, or feeling mentioned. For example, if you are frightened to death or bored to death, you are extremely frightened or bored.","ex":{"en":"He scares teams to death with his pace and power","cn":"他的速度之快、力量之大让其他队胆战不已。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"使…累死累活地工作（或劳动）","en":"If you say that someone works another person to death, you are emphasizing that they make them work very hard indeed, especially in a way that seems cruel or unfair.","ex":{"en":"They worked themselves to death but never lost their humour.","cn":"他们累死累活地干活，但却从没有丢掉幽默感。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"a death camp (= a place where prisoners are killed, usually in a war)","cn":"死亡集中营（常指战争中杀害俘虏的地方）"},{"en":"Death is often shown in paintings as a human skeleton.","cn":"死神在绘画作品中常以骷髅形式出现。"}]},"designer":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈzaɪnə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person whose job is to decide how things such as clothes, furniture, tools, etc. will look or work by making drawings, plans or patterns","cn":"设计者；构思者","ex":{"en":"one of the country's top fashion designers","cn":"国内顶尖时装设计师之一"}},{"en":"made by a famous designer; expensive and having a famous brand name","cn":"由著名设计师设计的；标有设计师姓名的；名牌的","lab":"North American English also","ex":{"en":"designer clothes","cn":"设计师品牌服装"},"pos":"adjective"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"设计师;设计者","en":"A designer is a person whose job is to design things by making drawings of them.","ex":{"en":"Carolyne is a fashion designer.","cn":"卡罗琳是一名时装设计师。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(服装、品牌等)由著名设计师设计的，标有设计师姓名的","en":"Designer clothes or designer labels are expensive, fashionable clothes made by a famous designer, rather than being made in large quantities in a factory.","ex":{"en":"He wears designer clothes and drives an antique car","cn":"他穿着著名设计师设计的服装，开着一部古董车。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"时尚的;时髦的","en":"You can use designer to describe things that are worn or bought because they are fashionable.","ex":{"en":"Tousled hair and designer stubble are chic","cn":"乱蓬蓬的头发和时兴的胡茬都很新潮。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/designer__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/designer__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"He had a trendy haircut, an earring and designer stubble (= a short beard, grown for two or three days and thought to look fashionable).","cn":"他理了个时髦的发型，戴着一只耳环，还留着形似设计师的胡子茬。"},{"en":"a fashion/jewellery, etc. designer","cn":"时装、珠宝等设计师"}]},"descriptive":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈskrɪptɪv","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"saying what somebody/something is like; describing something","cn":"描写的；叙述的；说明的","ex":{"en":"She read out some of the descriptive passages in the novel.","cn":"她把小说中一些描写性段落朗读出来。"}},{"en":"saying how language is actually used, without giving rules for how it should be used","cn":"描写性的（描述语言的实际应用而非使用规则）","lab":"linguistics"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"描述的;描写的;叙述的;说明的","en":"Descriptive language or writing indicates what someone or something is like.","ex":{"en":"...his descriptive way of writing.","cn":"他的描写性写作手法"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/descriptive__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/descriptive__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The term I used was meant to be purely descriptive (= not judging).","cn":"我所用的措辞是纯叙述性的（并非作出判断）。"},{"en":"the descriptive passages in the novel","cn":"小说中的描写性段落"}]},"debate":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/debate__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/debate__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈbeɪt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a formal discussion of an issue at a public meeting or in a parliament. In a debate two or more speakers express opposite views and then there is often a vote on the issue.","cn":"（在公共集会上或议会里就某问题进行的、常以表决结束的）辩论","lab":"especially North American English","ex":{"en":"the first ever televised presidential debate","cn":"有史以来首次电视直播的总统辩论"}},{"en":"an argument or a discussion expressing different opinions","cn":"（各自发表不同意见的）争论，辩论，讨论","ex":{"en":"The issue has sparked debate across the industry.","cn":"这个问题在整个行业引发了争论。"}},{"en":"to discuss something, especially formally, before making a decision or finding a solution","cn":"（尤指正式）讨论，辩论","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","ex":{"en":"Politicians will be debating the bill later this week.","cn":"政界将在本周晚些时候讨论这个议案。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to think carefully about something before making a decision","cn":"仔细考虑；思考；盘算","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","ex":{"en":"She debated with herself for a while, and then picked up the phone.","cn":"她仔细琢磨了一会儿，然后拿起了电话。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"（各自发表不同观点的）辩论，争论，讨论","en":"A debate is a discussion about a subject on which people have different views.","ex":{"en":"An intense debate is going on within the Israeli government","cn":"以色列政府内部正在进行激烈的辩论。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(议会或其他机构就某问题在投票前进行的)辩论","en":"A debate is a formal discussion, for example in a parliament or institution, in which people express different opinions about a particular subject and then vote on it.","ex":{"en":"There are expected to be some heated debates in parliament over the next few days.","cn":"预计接下来的几天里议会将会进行一些激烈的辩论。"}},{"pos":"V-RECIP 相互动词","cn":"（与…）辩论，争论，讨论","en":"If people debate a topic, they discuss it fairly formally, putting forward different views. You can also say that one person debates a topic with another person.","ex":{"en":"The United Nations Security Council will debate the issue today","cn":"联合国安理会今天将就这个问题展开讨论。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"考虑;盘算;权衡","en":"If you debate whether to do something or what to do, you think or talk about possible courses of action before deciding exactly what you are going to do.","ex":{"en":"Taggart debated whether to have yet another double vodka","cn":"塔格特思忖着是否再要一杯双份伏特加。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"存在争论的;有待讨论的;未确定的","en":"If you say that a matter is open to debate, you mean that people have different opinions about it, or it has not yet been firmly decided.","ex":{"en":"Which of them has more musical talent is open to debate.","cn":"他们之中谁更有音乐天赋还未有定论。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The committee will debate whether to lower the age of club membership to 16.","cn":"委员会将讨论是否将参加俱乐部的年龄限制放宽到 16 岁。"},{"en":"The question of the origin of the universe is still hotly debated (= strongly argued about) by scientists.","cn":"关于宇宙起源问题，科学家仍在激烈辩论。"}]},"desire":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/desire__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/desire__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈzaɪə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a strong wish to have or do something","cn":"愿望；欲望；渴望","g":"[countable]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"He now had enough money to satisfy all his desires.","cn":"他现在有足够的钱来满足自己所有的欲望。"}},{"en":"a strong wish to have sex with somebody","cn":"情欲；肉欲；性欲","g":"[uncountable, countable]","ex":{"en":"sexual desire","cn":"性欲"}},{"en":"a person or thing that is wished for","cn":"想望的人；渴望的事物","g":"[countable, usually singular]","ex":{"en":"When she agreed to marry him, he felt he had achieved his heart's desire.","cn":"当她答应嫁给他时，他感到终于得到了自己的心上人。"}},{"en":"to want something; to wish for something","cn":"渴望；期望；想望","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"We all desire health and happiness.","cn":"我们都渴望健康和幸福。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to be sexually attracted to somebody","cn":"对某人有情欲","ex":{"en":"He still desired her.","cn":"他依然渴望拥有她。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"渴望;热望;欲望","en":"A desire is a strong wish to do or have something.","ex":{"en":"I had a strong desire to help and care for people","cn":"我非常渴望能够帮助和照顾他人。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"渴望;想望;想要","en":"If you desire something, you want it.","ex":{"en":"She had remarried and desired a child with her new husband","cn":"她又结婚了，并且渴望和新任丈夫生个小孩。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"情欲;肉欲;性欲","en":"Desire for someone is a strong feeling of wanting to have sex with them.","ex":{"en":"Teenage sex, for instance, may come not out of genuine desire but from a need to get love.","cn":"例如，青少年的性行为可能并不是源于真正的情欲，而是出于一种对爱的需要。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"想与…发生性关系","en":"If you desire someone, you want to have sex with them.","ex":{"en":"It never occurred to him that she might not desire him.","cn":"他从没有想过她可能不想跟他上床。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"（用于说明性的书面语中）如果需要的话,如果愿意的话","en":"If desired is used in instructions in written English to indicate that someone can choose to take the course of action mentioned.","ex":{"en":"Additional courses may be taken if desired","cn":"如有需要可选修额外的课程。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"心里想望之人;心中渴望之物","en":"If you say that someone or something is your heart's desire, you mean that you want that person or thing very much.","ex":{"en":"He was extremely devious in his efforts to achieve his heart's desire.","cn":"他在设法得到自己的中意之物时会不择手段。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"尚有（许多）需要改进之处;有待（大幅）提高","en":"If you say that something leaves a lot to be desired, you mean that it is not as good as it should be.","ex":{"en":"The selection of TV programmes, especially at the weekend, leaves a lot to be desired","cn":"可供选择的电视节目，尤其是在周末的时候，还有大幅提升的空间。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"When she agreed to marry him he felt he had achieved his heart's desire.","cn":"当她答应嫁给他时，他感到终于得到了自己的心上人。"},{"en":"Fewer people desire to live in the north of the country.","cn":"想住在这个国家北方的人减少了。"}]},"delicate":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/delicate__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/delicate__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdelɪkət","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"easily damaged or broken","cn":"易损的；易碎的；脆弱的","ex":{"en":"delicate china teacups","cn":"易碎的瓷茶杯"}},{"en":"not strong and easily becoming ill","cn":"虚弱的；纤弱的","ex":{"en":"a delicate child/constitution","cn":"纤弱的孩子／体质"}},{"en":"small and having a beautiful shape or appearance","cn":"纤细的；微小的；精美的；小巧玲珑的","ex":{"en":"his delicate hands","cn":"他纤细的手"}},{"en":"made or formed in a very careful and detailed way","cn":"精致的；精细的；精密的","ex":{"en":"the delicate mechanisms of a clock","cn":"钟的精密机件"}},{"en":"showing or needing careful or sensitive treatment","cn":"巧妙的；微妙的；需要技巧的；需要小心处理的","ex":{"en":"I admired your delicate handling of the situation.","cn":"我佩服你应付这种局面的娴熟技巧。"}},{"en":"light and pleasant; not strong","cn":"柔和的；清淡可口的；清香的","ex":{"en":"a delicate fragrance/flavour","cn":"清新的芳香；鲜美的味道"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"娇美的;精美的;雅致的;纤细的","en":"Something that is delicate is small and beautifully shaped.","ex":{"en":"He had delicate hands.","cn":"他有一双纤细的手。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(颜色)柔和的;(味道)鲜美的，清淡可口的;（气味）清香的","en":"Something that is delicate has a colour, taste, or smell which is pleasant and not strong or intense.","ex":{"en":"Young haricot beans have a tender texture and a delicate, subtle flavour","cn":"嫩菜豆口感细腻，味道清香、淡雅。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"娇贵的;脆弱的;易碎的","en":"If something is delicate, it is easy to harm, damage, or break, and needs to be handled or treated carefully.","ex":{"en":"Although the coral looks hard, it is very delicate.","cn":"珊瑚虽然看上去坚固，实际上非常易碎。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"娇弱的;柔弱的","en":"Someone who is delicate is not healthy and strong, and becomes ill easily.","ex":{"en":"She was physically delicate and psychologically unstable.","cn":"她身体孱弱，心理上也不够稳定。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"微妙的;棘手的;需要小心处理的","en":"You use delicate to describe a situation, problem, matter, or discussion that needs to be dealt with carefully and sensitively in order to avoid upsetting things or offending people.","ex":{"en":"The European members are afraid of upsetting the delicate balance of political interests","cn":"欧洲成员国害怕会打乱各政治利益集团间的微妙平衡。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"技巧性很强的;注重细节的","en":"A delicate task, movement, action, or product needs or shows great skill and attention to detail.","ex":{"en":"...a long and delicate operation carried out at a hospital in Florence","cn":"在佛罗伦萨一家医院里进行的一场耗时长、难度高的手术"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"I admired your delicate handling of the situation.","cn":"我佩服你应付这种局面的娴熟技巧。"},{"en":"The delicate surgical operation took five hours.","cn":"这精细的外科手术花了五个小时。"}]},"dental":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/dental__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/dental__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdentl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"connected with teeth","cn":"牙齿的；牙科的","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"dental disease/care/treatment/health","cn":"牙齿疾病／护理／治疗／健康"}},{"en":"produced with the tongue against the upper front teeth, for example /θ/ and /ð/ in thin and this","cn":"齿音的","lab":"phonetics"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"牙齿的;牙科的","en":"Dental is used to describe things that relate to teeth or to the care and treatment of teeth.","ex":{"en":"You can get free dental treatment.","cn":"你可以得到免费的牙齿治疗。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"( BrE ) a dental surgery (= where a dentist sees patients)","cn":"牙科诊所"},{"en":"a dental surgery (= where a dentist sees patients)","cn":""}]},"detective":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈtektɪv","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person, especially a police officer, whose job is to investigate crimes and catch criminals","cn":"侦探；警探","ex":{"en":"a police/homicide/undercover detective","cn":"警方／凶杀案／卧底侦探"}},{"en":"a person employed by somebody to find out information about somebody/something","cn":"私人侦探"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（警队或私人）侦探","en":"A detective is someone whose job is to discover what has happened in a crime or other situation and to find the people involved. Some detectives work in the police force and others work privately.","ex":{"en":"Detectives are appealing for witnesses who may have seen anything suspicious","cn":"探员呼吁看到任何可疑情况的人进行举报。"}},{"pos":"N-TITLE; N-VOC 头衔名词；称呼名词","cn":"（用于警察头衔）(英国英语中常用于 constable，sergeant 等词前）侦探，（美国英语中单独使用)警探","en":"In Britain 'detective' is used before words such as 'constable' or 'sergeant', and in the U.S. the word 'detective' is used on its own, to indicate that a police officer is a member of the department concerned with investigating crimes.","ex":{"en":"...Detective Inspector Ian Mosley.","cn":"伊恩·莫斯利探长"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(小说或故事)侦探的，破案的","en":"A detective novel or story is one in which a detective tries to solve a crime."},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"调查;探究","en":"If you do some detective work, you do something to find out more about a subject or situation that puzzles you.","ex":{"en":"Despite careful detective work, many items have never been recovered.","cn":"尽管进行了悉心探查，许多物品还是一直没有找回。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/detective__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/detective__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"detectives from the anti-terrorist squad","cn":"反恐怖主义小组的侦探"},{"en":"Detective Inspector (Roger) Brown （","cn":"罗杰）布朗探长"}]},"department":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/department__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/department__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpɑːtmənt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a section of a large organization such as a government, business, university, etc.","cn":"（政府、企业等的）部门，局，科；（大学的）院，系；（医院的）科","ex":{"en":"the Department of Health","cn":"卫生署"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(政府的)部，司，局，处;(企业的)部门，科;(大学的)系，所;(大型商店的)货品区","en":"A department is one of the sections in an organization such as a government, business, or university. A department is also one of the sections in a large shop.","ex":{"en":"...the U.S. Department of Health, Education and Welfare","cn":"美国卫生、教育和福利部"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"不是…的职责（或知识）范围;并非…的专长","en":"If you say that a task or area of knowledge is not your department, you mean that you are not responsible for it or do not know much about it.","ex":{"en":"'I'm afraid the name means nothing to me,' he said. 'That's not my department.'","cn":"“恐怕这个名字对我来说毫无意义，”他说，“我对此并不熟悉。”"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Don't ask me about it — that's her department.","cn":"这事别问我，那是她的职责范围。"},{"en":"the Department of Trade and Industry","cn":"工业贸易署"}]},"demonstration":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/demonstration__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/demonstration__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdemənˈstreɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a public meeting or a march (= an organized walk by many people) at which people show that they are protesting against or supporting somebody/something","cn":"集会示威；游行示威","g":"[countable]","lab":"informal","ex":{"en":"to take part in/go on a demonstration","cn":"参加／进行示威游行"}},{"en":"an act of showing or explaining how something works or is done","cn":"示范；示范表演；演示","g":"[countable, uncountable]","lab":"informal","ex":{"en":"We were given a brief demonstration of the computer's functions.","cn":"有人给我们简单演示了计算机的功能。"}},{"en":"an act of giving proof or evidence for something","cn":"证明；证实；论证；说明","g":"[countable, uncountable]","ex":{"en":"a demonstration of the connection between the two sets of figures","cn":"论证这两组数字间的联系"}},{"en":"an act of showing a feeling or an opinion","cn":"表达；表露；表现；显露","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"a public demonstration of affection","cn":"公开表露爱慕之情"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"示威;示威游行（或集会）","en":"A demonstration is a march or gathering which people take part in to show their opposition to something or their support for something.","ex":{"en":"Riot police broke up a demonstration by students.","cn":"防暴警察驱散了示威的学生。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"示范;演示","en":"A demonstration of something is a talk by someone who shows you how to do it or how it works.","ex":{"en":"...a cookery demonstration.","cn":"烹饪示范"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"证明;论证;表明;说明","en":"A demonstration of a fact or situation is a clear proof of it.","ex":{"en":"This is a clear demonstration of how technology has changed","cn":"这清楚地表明了技术已有了怎样的进步。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(特质的)显示;(情感的)表露","en":"A demonstration of a quality or feeling is an expression of it.","ex":{"en":"There's been no public demonstration of opposition to the President.","cn":"没有人对总统公开表示反对。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"We were given a brief demonstration of the computer's functions.","cn":"我们看了这种计算机各种功能的简短演示。"},{"en":"a demonstration of how something that seems simple can turn out to be very complicated","cn":"说明看似简单的东西实际上可能非常复杂"}]},"deal":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/deal__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deal__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"diːl","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to give cards to each player in a game of cards","cn":"发牌","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"cards","ex":{"en":"Whose turn is it to deal?","cn":"该谁发牌了？"}},{"en":"to buy and sell illegal drugs","cn":"非法买卖毒品；贩毒","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"drugs","ex":{"en":"You can often see people dealing openly on the streets.","cn":"经常可以看到一些人在大街上公然买卖毒品。"}},{"en":"an agreement, especially in business, on particular conditions for buying or doing something","cn":"协议；（尤指）交易","g":"[countable]","lab":"informal","sc":"business agreement","ex":{"en":"to sign/strike/finalize/close a deal","cn":"签署／达成／敲定／完成一笔交易"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"the way that somebody/something is treated","cn":"待遇","g":"[countable, usually singular]","sc":"treatment","ex":{"en":"If elected, the party has promised a new deal (= better and fairer treatment) for teachers.","cn":"该党承诺如果当选将给教师更好的待遇。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"the action of giving out cards to the players","cn":"发牌","g":"[countable, usually singular]","sc":"in card games","ex":{"en":"It's your deal.","cn":"该你发牌了。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"the soft pale wood of fir or pine trees, especially when it is cut into boards for making things","cn":"冷杉木；松木板","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"especially British English","sc":"wood","ex":{"en":"a deal table","cn":"松木桌子"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"QUANT 数量词","cn":"许多;大量","en":"If you say that you need or have a great deal of or a good deal of a particular thing, you are emphasizing that you need or have a lot of it.","ex":{"en":"...a great deal of money","cn":"大量的钱"}},{"pos":"QUANT 数量词","cn":"许多;很多","en":"A deal of something is a lot of it.","ex":{"en":"He had a deal of work to do.","cn":"他有许多工作要做。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"协议;（尤指）交易，生意","en":"If you make a deal ,do a deal, or cut a deal, you complete an agreement or an arrangement with someone, especially in business.","ex":{"en":"Japan will have to do a deal with America on rice imports","cn":"日本将不得不与美国就大米的进口达成一笔交易。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"经营;买卖","en":"If a person, company, or shop deals in a particular type of goods, their business involves buying or selling those goods.","ex":{"en":"They deal in antiques","cn":"他们做古董买卖。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"贩卖（毒品)","en":"If someone deals illegal drugs, they sell them.","ex":{"en":"I certainly don't deal drugs.","cn":"我当然不贩毒。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"坏运气;不公平的对待","en":"If someone has had a bad deal, they have been unfortunate or have been treated unfairly.","ex":{"en":"The people of Liverpool have had a bad deal for many, many years.","cn":"利物浦人多年来一直没有得到公正的待遇。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(在纸牌游戏中）发(牌)","en":"If you deal playing cards, you give them out to the players in a game of cards.","ex":{"en":"The croupier dealt each player a card, face down","cn":"赌台管理员给每位玩家正面朝下发了一张牌。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"沉重打击;对…造成伤害（或损失）","en":"If an event deals a blow to something or someone, it causes them great difficulties or makes failure more likely.","ex":{"en":"The summer drought has dealt a heavy blow to the government's economic record","cn":"夏季的干旱已经对政府的经济业绩造成了沉重打击。"}},{"pos":"See also:","cn":"","en":"→see: ;"},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：deal out deal with"}]},"examples":[{"en":"She is used to dealing with all kinds of people in her job.","cn":"她已习惯于和工作中遇到的各种各样的人打交道。"},{"en":"You can often see people dealing openly on the streets.","cn":"经常可以看到一些人在大街上公然买卖毒品。"}]},"decade":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/decade__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/decade__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdekeɪd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a period of ten years, especially a continuous period, such as 1910–1919 or 2000–2009","cn":"十年，十年期（尤指一个年代）","ex":{"en":"the early decades of the nineteenth century","cn":"十九世纪的前几十年"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"十年，十年期（尤指一个年代)","en":"A decade is a period of ten years, especially one that begins with a year ending in 0, for example 1980 to 1989.","ex":{"en":"...the last decade of the nineteenth century.","cn":"19 世纪的最后 10 年"}}]}},"deficient":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfɪʃnt","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"not having enough of something, especially something that is essential","cn":"缺乏的；缺少的；不足的","ex":{"en":"a diet that is deficient in vitamin A","cn":"缺乏维生素 A 的饮食"}},{"en":"not good enough","cn":"有缺点的；有缺陷的","ex":{"en":"Deaf people are sometimes treated as being mentally deficient.","cn":"耳聋的人有时被看作智力不健全。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"缺乏的;缺少的;不足的","en":"If someone or something is deficient in a particular thing, they do not have the full amount of it that they need in order to function normally or work properly.","ex":{"en":"...a diet deficient in vitamin B.","cn":"缺乏维生素 B 的饮食"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"有缺点的;有缺陷的;不完善的","en":"Someone or something that is deficient is not good enough for a particular purpose.","ex":{"en":"...deficient landing systems.","cn":"存在缺陷的降落系统"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/deficient__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deficient__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Deaf people are sometimes treated as being mentally deficient.","cn":"耳聋的人有时被看作智力不健全。"},{"en":"a diet that is deficient in vitamin A","cn":"缺乏维生素 A 的饮食"}]},"dent":{"oxford":{"phon":"dent","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to make a hollow place in a hard surface, usually by hitting it","cn":"使凹陷；使产生凹痕","ex":{"en":"The back of the car was badly dented in the collision.","cn":"汽车尾部被撞后严重凹陷。"}},{"en":"to damage somebody’s confidence, reputation, etc.","cn":"损害，伤害，挫伤（信心、名誉等）","ex":{"en":"It seemed that nothing could dent his confidence.","cn":"似乎任何事情都不会使他的信心受挫。"}},{"en":"a hollow place in a hard surface, usually caused by something hitting it","cn":"凹痕；凹坑；凹部","ex":{"en":"a large dent in the car door","cn":"车门上一大块凹陷"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"使凹陷;使产生凹痕","en":"If you dent the surface of something, you make a hollow area in it by hitting or pressing it.","ex":{"en":"A great chunk of loose kerbing smashed into my left-front wheel, bursting the tyre and denting the rim","cn":"我车子的左前轮撞在一大块松动的路缘石上，导致车胎爆裂、轮辋凹陷。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"凹痕;凹坑","en":"A dent is a hollow in the surface of something which has been caused by hitting or pressing it.","ex":{"en":"There was a dent in the car which hadn't been there before.","cn":"车上出现了一处以前没有的凹痕。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"削减;削弱;损害","en":"If something dents your ideas or your pride, it makes you realize that your ideas are wrong, or that you are not as good or successful as you thought.","ex":{"en":"This has not dented the City's enthusiasm for the company.","cn":"这并没有减弱伦敦金融界对这个公司的热情。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"削减;削弱","en":"If one thing makes a dent in another, it reduces it by a large amount.","ex":{"en":"The commission had barely begun to make a dent in the problem","cn":"委员会几乎还没有在这个问题上取得任何进展。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/dent__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/dent__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"It seemed that nothing could dent his confidence.","cn":"似乎任何事情都不会使他的信心受挫。"},{"en":"The lawyer's fees will make a dent in our finances.","cn":"律师费将耗去我们一部分资金。"}]},"delays":{"lemma":"delay"},"dead":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/dead__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/dead__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ded","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"no longer alive","cn":"死的；失去生命的；枯萎的","lab":"informal","sc":"not alive","ex":{"en":"My mother's dead; she died in 2017.","cn":"我母亲不在了，她是 2017 年去世的。"}},{"en":"not working because of a lack of power","cn":"（因为缺电）不运行的，不转动的","sc":"machine","ex":{"en":"a dead battery","cn":"用完的电池"}},{"en":"no longer believed in or aimed for","cn":"不再有人相信（或争取）","g":"[not before noun]","sc":"idea/belief/plan","ex":{"en":"Many believe the peace plan is dead.","cn":"许多人认为和平计划已成泡影。"}},{"en":"belonging to the past; no longer practised or fashionable","cn":"过时的；已废弃的；不流行的","sc":"not used","ex":{"en":"Is the Western a dead art form?","cn":"西部电影这种艺术形式过时了吗？"}},{"en":"finished; not able to be used any more","cn":"用完了的；不能再用的","lab":"informal","sc":"finished","ex":{"en":"dead matches","cn":"划过的火柴"}},{"en":"very quiet, without activity or interest","cn":"死气沉沉的；无活力的；无趣的","lab":"informal, disapproving，，","sc":"place","ex":{"en":"There were no theatres, no cinemas, no coffee bars. It was dead as anything.","cn":"那时没有剧院，没有电影院，也没有咖啡馆，死气沉沉。"}},{"en":"without activity; with nobody buying or selling anything","cn":"停滞的；萧条的","lab":"informal, disapproving，，","sc":"business","ex":{"en":"‘The market is absolutely dead this morning,’ said one foreign exchange trader.","cn":"“今天早上市场萧条极了。”一个外汇交易员说道。"}},{"en":"extremely tired; not well","cn":"筋疲力尽；身体不好","g":"[not usually before noun]","lab":"informal","sc":"tired","ex":{"en":"half dead with cold and hunger","cn":"饥寒交迫，筋疲力尽"}},{"en":"unable to feel because of cold, etc.","cn":"（由于冷等）失去知觉，麻木","g":"[not before noun]","sc":"without feeling","ex":{"en":"My left arm had gone dead.","cn":"我的左胳臂已经麻木了。"}},{"en":"unable to feel or understand emotions","cn":"无动于衷；麻木不仁；无感觉","sc":"without feeling","ex":{"en":"He was dead to all feelings of pity.","cn":"他毫无同情心。"}},{"en":"showing no emotion","cn":"冷冷的","sc":"without feeling","ex":{"en":"She said, ‘I'm sorry, too,’ in a quiet, dead voice.","cn":"她平静而冷漠地说：“我也很抱歉。”"}},{"en":"complete or exact","cn":"完全的；精确的；全然的","g":"[only before noun]","lab":"informal","sc":"complete/exact","ex":{"en":"a dead silence/calm","cn":"死寂；完全静止"}},{"en":"never having been alive","cn":"无生命的；非生物的","sc":"never alive","ex":{"en":"dead matter (= for example rock)","cn":"无生命物质（如岩石）"}},{"en":"outside the playing area","cn":"死球的；出界的","sc":"in sport","ex":{"en":"There was a dead ball with five seconds to go in the game.","cn":"比赛还剩五秒时出现死球。"}},{"en":"people who have died","cn":"死人；死者","g":"[plural]","ex":{"en":"The dead and wounded in that one attack amounted to 6 000.","cn":"仅那一次进攻就死伤达 6 000 人。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"the state of being dead","cn":"死","g":"[singular]","lab":"figurative","ex":{"en":"Christians believe that God raised Jesus from the dead.","cn":"基督徒相信上帝使耶稣复活。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"completely; exactly","cn":"完全地；全然地；确实地","lab":"British English","sc":"completely","ex":{"en":"You're dead right!","cn":"你完全正确！"},"pos":"adverb"},{"en":"very; extremely","cn":"非常；极其","lab":"British English, informal，，","sc":"very","ex":{"en":"The instructions are dead easy to follow.","cn":"这些指令很容易执行。"},"pos":"adverb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"死亡的;去世的","en":"A person, animal, or plant that is dead is no longer living.","ex":{"en":"Her husband's been dead a year now","cn":"她的丈夫已经去世一年了。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(土地或水域)无生命存在的","en":"Land or water that is dead contains no living things.","ex":{"en":"...charred land, mountainsides of dead earth and stumps of trees","cn":"烧焦的土地、无一活物的山坡和残存的树桩"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(地方或时期)无生气的，死气沉沉的","en":"If you describe a place or a period of time as dead, you do not like it because there is very little activity taking place in it.","ex":{"en":"...some dead little town where the liveliest thing is the flies","cn":"某个死气沉沉的小镇，那里最有活力的东西就是苍蝇"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"不再使用的;用尽的","en":"Something that is dead is no longer being used or is finished.","ex":{"en":"The dead cigarette was still between his fingers","cn":"那支已熄灭的香烟仍在他指间。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(想法、计划或话题）不再令人感兴趣的，不值得再考虑的，已停滞的","en":"If you say that an idea, plan, or subject is dead, you mean that people are no longer interested in it or willing to develop it any further.","ex":{"en":"It's a dead issue, Baxter","cn":"这个问题已经没人再谈论了，巴克斯特。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(语言）死的，不再通用的","en":"A dead language is no longer spoken or written as a means of communication, although it may still be studied.","ex":{"en":"We used to grumble that we were wasting time learning a dead language.","cn":"我们过去常常抱怨自己是在浪费时间学一门死语言。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(电话等电气设备）不再运转的，没电的","en":"A telephone or piece of electrical equipment that is dead is no longer functioning, for example because it no longer has any electrical power.","ex":{"en":"On another occasion I answered the phone and the line went dead.","cn":"还有一回，我一接电话，就掉线了。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(体育运动中的球）界外的，死的","en":"In sport, when a ball is dead, it has gone outside the playing area, or a situation has occurred in which the game has to be temporarily stopped, and none of the players can score points or gain an advantage."},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(声音)沉闷的;(颜色)暗淡的，不鲜亮的","en":"A dead sound or colour is dull rather than lively or bright.","ex":{"en":"'That is correct, Meg,' he answered in his cold, dead voice","cn":"“没错，梅格。”他用冰冷、阴沉的声音答道。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"完全的，绝对的（尤用于修饰 centre, silence 和 stop）","en":"Dead is used to mean 'complete' or 'absolute', especially before the words 'centre', 'silence', and 'stop'.","ex":{"en":"He adjusted each chesspiece so that it stood dead centre in its square","cn":"他调整每颗棋子，使它们立于格子的正中央。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"正好;恰好;精确地","en":"Dead means 'precisely' or 'exactly'.","ex":{"en":"Mars was visible, dead in the centre of the telescope","cn":"可以看得见火星，就在望远镜的正中央。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"很;非常","en":"Dead is sometimes used to mean 'very'.","ex":{"en":"Meadowhall is also dead easy for people to get to","cn":"去梅多霍尔购物中心也非常方便。"}},{"pos":"CONVENTION 惯用语","cn":"（表示强烈反对）除非我死了","en":"If you reply 'Over my dead body' when a plan or action has been suggested, you are emphasizing that you dislike it, and will do everything you can to prevent it.","ex":{"en":"'Let's invite her to dinner.' — 'Over my dead body!'","cn":"“我们请她来吃晚饭吧。”——“除非我死了！”"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"完全了结的;彻底过去的","en":"If you say that something such as an idea or situation is dead and buried, you are emphasizing that you think that it is completely finished or past, and cannot happen or exist again in the future.","ex":{"en":"I thought the whole business was dead and buried","cn":"我以为这整件事已经完全了结了。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"突然死亡;猝死","en":"If you say that a person or animal dropped dead or dropped down dead, you mean that they died very suddenly and unexpectedly.","ex":{"en":"He dropped dead on the quayside.","cn":"他猝死在码头区。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"去死吧;见鬼去吧;别再烦人","en":"If you tell someone to drop dead, you are insulting them, rudely disagreeing with them, or refusing to do something, or telling them to stop bothering you.","ex":{"en":"75% of the firms he called were hostile and told him to 'drop dead.'","cn":"在他电话联系的公司里，75% 都怀有敌意，让他“见鬼去吧”。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"不在人世的;去世的","en":"If you say that someone is dead and gone, you are emphasizing that they are dead, and thinking about what happened or will happen after their death.","ex":{"en":"Often a genius is recognized only after he is dead and gone.","cn":"天才往往在离开人世之后才得到认可。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"累得要命;病得半死","en":"If you say that you feel dead or are half dead, you mean that you feel very tired or ill and very weak.","ex":{"en":"You looked half dead after that journey","cn":"经过那趟旅程之后,你看上去真是累坏了。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"在夜晚万籁俱寂之时/在隆冬","en":"If something happens in the dead of night ,at dead of night, or in the dead of winter, it happens in the middle part of the night or the winter, when it is darkest or coldest.","ex":{"en":"I couldn't fly illegally into a country in the dead of night","cn":"我不能在深夜乘飞机非法进入一个国家。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE短语","cn":"(耶稣）复活/使…复活","en":"When Christians say that Jesus Christ rose from the dead or raised someone from the dead, they mean that Jesus came back to life after he had died, or brought a dead person back to life."},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"卷土重来;重新活跃起来（或获得成功）","en":"If you say that someone or something rises or comes back from the dead, you mean that they become active or successful again after being inactive for a while.","ex":{"en":"This was a company that, by all appearances, had risen from the dead","cn":"从一切迹象来看，这是一家已经起死回生的公司。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"死也（不会），绝对（不会）（穿某种衣服、去某个地方或处于某种境地)","en":"If you say that you wouldn't be seen dead or be caught dead in particular clothes, places, or situations, you are expressing strong dislike or disapproval of them.","ex":{"en":"I wouldn't be seen dead in a straw hat.","cn":"我死也不会戴草帽。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"（使）突然停止（发生或移动）","en":"To stop dead means to suddenly stop happening or moving. To stop someone or something dead means to cause them to suddenly stop happening or moving.","ex":{"en":"We all stopped dead and looked at it","cn":"我们一下子全都停了下来看着它。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"败局已定的;不太可能成功的","en":"If you say that someone or something is dead in the water, you are emphasizing that they have failed, and that there is little hope of them being successful in the future.","ex":{"en":"A 'no' vote would have left the treaty dead in the water.","cn":"一张否决票可能就会使这个条约胎死腹中。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"to flog a dead horse→see: ; a dead loss→see: ; a dead ringer→see: ; to stop dead in your tracks→see: ;"}]},"examples":[{"en":"There were no theatres, no cinemas, no coffee bars. It was dead as anything.","cn":"那时既无剧院，又无电影院，也无咖啡馆，简直是死气沉沉。"},{"en":"Though the idea may be dead, it is far from being buried (= people still talk about it, even though there is nothing new to say).","cn":"尽管这种想法可能已无人相信，但还远没被人遗忘。"}]},"decoration":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/decoration__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/decoration__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdekəˈreɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a thing that makes something look more attractive on special occasions","cn":"装饰品","g":"[countable, usually plural]","ex":{"en":"Christmas/festive decorations","cn":"圣诞／节庆装饰品"}},{"en":"a pattern, etc. that is added to something and that stops it from being plain","cn":"装饰图案","g":"[uncountable, countable]","ex":{"en":"the elaborate decoration on the carved wooden door","cn":"木雕门上精美的装饰图案"}},{"en":"the style in which something is decorated","cn":"装饰风格","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"An Oscar was given for the art direction and set decoration.","cn":"有一项奥斯卡奖是为艺术指导和布景而设的。"}},{"en":"the act or process of decorating something such as the inside of a house by painting it, etc.","cn":"（房屋内部等的）装饰，装潢","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"British English"},{"en":"an award or medal that is given to somebody as an honour","cn":"勋章；奖章","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"His jacket was heavy with military decorations.","cn":"他的夹克上饰有厚重的军事勋章。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(室内的)装饰，装潢","en":"The decoration of a room is its furniture, wallpaper, and ornaments.","ex":{"en":"The decoration and furnishings had to be practical enough for a family home","cn":"房子的装潢和家具都必须很实用，适合家居生活。"}},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"装饰（的特定方面）","en":"Decorations are features that are added to something in order to make it look more attractive.","ex":{"en":"The only wall decorations are candles and a single mirror","cn":"墙上唯一的装饰是几支蜡烛和一面镜子。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(彩纸、气球等)装饰品，点缀物","en":"Decorations are brightly coloured objects such as pieces of paper and balloons, which you put up in a room on special occasions to make it look more attractive.","ex":{"en":"Festive paper decorations had been hung from the ceiling.","cn":"喜庆的彩纸已经挂在天花板上。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"勋章;奖章;荣誉称号","en":"A decoration is an official title or honour which is given to someone, usually in the form of a medal, as a reward for military bravery or public service.","ex":{"en":"He was awarded several military decorations.","cn":"他被授予了多枚军功章。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"the elaborate decoration on the carved wooden door","cn":"木雕门上精美的装饰图案"},{"en":"a Chinese theme in the interior decoration","cn":"室内装饰的中国情调"}]},"descent":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/descent__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/descent__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈsent","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an action of coming or going down","cn":"下降；下倾","g":"[countable, usually singular]","lab":"figurative","ex":{"en":"The plane began its descent to Heathrow.","cn":"飞机开始向希思罗机场降落。"}},{"en":"a slope going downwards","cn":"斜坡；坡道","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"There is a gradual descent to the sea.","cn":"有一片斜坡缓缓伸延到海边。"}},{"en":"a person’s family origins","cn":"血统；祖籍；祖先；出身","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"to be of Scottish descent","cn":"祖籍是苏格兰"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"下降;降落","en":"A descent is a movement from a higher to a lower level or position.","ex":{"en":"Sixteen of the youngsters set off for help, but during the descent three collapsed in the cold and rain.","cn":"16 名年轻人出发去寻求帮助，但在下山过程中有 3 人因寒冷和大雨晕倒了。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"斜坡;斜面","en":"A descent is a surface that slopes downwards, for example the side of a steep hill.","ex":{"en":"On the descents, cyclists spin past cars, freewheeling downhill at tremendous speed.","cn":"在坡道上，自行车手飞驰着超越了一辆辆汽车，靠着惯性一路疾冲下山。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"(形势的)恶化;(人的)堕落，沦落","en":"When you want to emphasize that a situation becomes very bad, you can talk about someone's or something's descent into that situation.","ex":{"en":"The only lasting solution lies in a political settlement. Without it, their descent into chaos will be guaranteed.","cn":"唯一的长久之计是通过政治手段解决。否则，他们势必会陷入一片混乱。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"血统;家世;出身","en":"You use descent to talk about a person's family background, for example their nationality or social status.","ex":{"en":"All the contributors were of African descent.","cn":"所有的撰稿人都是非裔人士。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He traces his line of descent from the Stuart kings.","cn":"他的家族可追溯到斯图亚特王朝。"},{"en":"The plane began its descent to Heathrow.","cn":"飞机开始向希思罗机场降落。"}]},"defends":{"lemma":"defend"},"demonstrate":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/demonstrate__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/demonstrate__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdemənstreɪt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to show something clearly by giving proof or evidence","cn":"证明；证实；论证；说明","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"New research convincingly demonstrates that age-related memory loss is not inevitable.","cn":"新的研究证据确凿地表明，与年龄相关的记忆丧失并非不可避免。"}},{"en":"to show by your actions that you have a particular quality, feeling or opinion","cn":"表达；表露；表现；显露","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"The team demonstrated breathtaking skills.","cn":"这个团队展示了惊人的技能。"}},{"en":"to show and explain how something works or how to do something","cn":"示范；演示","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"Her job involves demonstrating new educational software.","cn":"她的工作包括演示新的教学软件。"}},{"en":"to take part in a public meeting or march (= an organized walk by many people), usually as a protest or to show support for something","cn":"游行示威","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"Hundreds of protesters demonstrated outside the court.","cn":"数百名抗议者在法庭外示威。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"证明;论证;表明;说明","en":"To demonstrate a fact means to make it clear to people.","ex":{"en":"The study also demonstrated a direct link between obesity and mortality","cn":"该研究还表明了肥胖症和死亡率之间存在直接的联系。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"显示;表露","en":"If you demonstrate a particular skill, quality, or feeling, you show by your actions that you have it.","ex":{"en":"Have they, for example, demonstrated a commitment to democracy?","cn":"例如，他们是否已表现出会致力于民主？"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"示威;进行示威游行（或集会）","en":"When people demonstrate, they march or gather somewhere to show their opposition to something or their support for something.","ex":{"en":"30,000 angry farmers demonstrated against possible cuts in subsidies","cn":"3万名愤怒的农场主示威抗议可能对农产品补贴进行的削减。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"示范;演示","en":"If you demonstrate something, you show people how it works or how to do it.","ex":{"en":"The BBC has just successfully demonstrated a new digital radio transmission system","cn":"英国广播公司刚刚成功地演示了一套新的数字无线电传输系统。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"These results demonstrate convincingly that our campaign is working.","cn":"这些结果有力地证明，我们的运动正在发挥作用。"},{"en":"They are demonstrating in favour of free higher education.","cn":"他们参加示威游行，要求实行免费高等教育。"}]},"deferentially":{"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"polite behaviour that shows that you respect someone and are therefore willing to accept their opinions or judgment","cn":""}]},"examples":[{"en":"Lewis was annoyed that Adam did not show enough respect and deference to him.","cn":"","src":"ld"},{"en":"They were married in church out of deference to their parents’ wishes.","cn":"","src":"ld"}],"media":{"uk":"media/uk/deferentially__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deferentially__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdefəˈrenʃəli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"in a way that shows that you respect somebody/something, especially somebody older or more senior than you","cn":"尊敬地：以某种方式表明您尊重某人/某物，特别是比您年长或更高的人"}]}},"defend":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfend","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to protect somebody/something from attack","cn":"防御；保护；保卫","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","sc":"protect against attack/loss","ex":{"en":"The role of the military is to defend the country.","cn":"军队的职能是保卫国家。"}},{"en":"to protect something that you value and prevent it from being taken away","cn":"保卫；保护；看守","g":"[transitive]","sc":"protect against attack/loss","ex":{"en":"The organization works to defend human rights wherever they are threatened.","cn":"该组织致力在任何人权受到威胁的地方捍卫人权。"}},{"en":"to say or write something in support of somebody/something that has been criticized","cn":"辩解；辩白","g":"[transitive]","sc":"support","ex":{"en":"They defended their decision to pull out of the event.","cn":"他们为退出这项活动的决定进行了辩解。"}},{"en":"to protect your own goal to stop your opponents from scoring","cn":"防守","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"in sport","ex":{"en":"They were forced to defend for long periods.","cn":"他们被迫长期防守。"}},{"en":"to take part in a competition that you won the last time and try to win it again","cn":"参加比赛（或选举）保住（头衔、席位等）","g":"[transitive]","lab":"politics","sc":"in competitions","ex":{"en":"He is defending champion.","cn":"他在参加卫冕赛。"}},{"en":"to act as a lawyer for somebody who has been charged with a crime","cn":"（为…）辩护；当辩护律师","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","sc":"law","ex":{"en":"He has employed one of the UK's top lawyers to defend him.","cn":"他请了英国一位顶尖律师为他辩护。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"防御;保卫;保护","en":"If you defend someone or something, you take action in order to protect them.","ex":{"en":"Every man who could fight was now committed to defend the ridge","cn":"每个能够参加战斗的男子现在都决心要保卫这条山脊。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"替…辩护;为…辩解;维护","en":"If you defend someone or something when they have been criticized, you argue in support of them.","ex":{"en":"Matt defended all of Clarence's decisions, right or wrong","cn":"克拉伦斯的决定，不管对错，马特都予以维护。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(律师)为(被告)辩护","en":"When a lawyer defends a person who has been accused of something, the lawyer argues on their behalf in a court of law that the charges are not true.","ex":{"en":"...a lawyer who defended political prisoners during the military regime","cn":"在军人政权时期为政治犯辩护的律师"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"卫(冕)","en":"When a sports player plays in the tournament which they won the previous time it was held, you can say that they are defending their title.","ex":{"en":"Torrence expects to defend her title successfully in the next Olympics","cn":"托伦斯希望在下届奥运会上能够卫冕成功。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/defend__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/defend__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"All our officers are trained to defend themselves against knife attacks.","cn":"我们所有的警察都接受过自卫训练，能够对付持刀袭击。"},{"en":"Politicians are skilled at defending themselves against their critics.","cn":"从政者都善于为自己辩解，反驳别人的批评。"}]},"destructive":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/destructive__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/destructive__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈstrʌktɪv","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"causing destruction or damage","cn":"引起破坏（或毁灭）的；破坏（或毁灭）性的","ex":{"en":"The war demonstrated the destructive power of modern weapons.","cn":"这次战争显示了现代武器的毁灭性力量。"}},{"en":"negative or not helpful","cn":"负面的；破坏性的","ex":{"en":"destructive behaviour/impulses/tendencies","cn":"破坏性行为／冲动／倾向"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"破坏(性)的;毁灭(性)的","en":"Something that is destructive causes or is capable of causing great damage, harm, or injury.","ex":{"en":"...the awesome destructive power of nuclear weapons","cn":"核武器可怕的毁灭性力量"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"the destructive power of modern weapons","cn":"现代武器的毁灭性力量"},{"en":"the destructive effects of anxiety","cn":"焦虑的破坏性影响"}]},"destiny":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/destiny__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/destiny__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdestəni","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"what happens to somebody or what will happen to them in the future, especially things that they cannot change or avoid","cn":"命运；天命；天数","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"The destinies of five nations were decided at the peace conference.","cn":"五个国家的命运在和平会议上决定了。"}},{"en":"the power believed to control events","cn":"主宰事物的力量；命运之神","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"I believe there's some force guiding us—call it God, destiny or fate.","cn":"我总认为有某种力量在指引着我们，称之为上帝也罢，天意也罢，还是命运也罢。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"命运","en":"A person's destiny is everything that happens to them during their life, including what will happen in the future, especially when it is considered to be controlled by someone or something else.","ex":{"en":"We are masters of our own destiny","cn":"我们是自己命运的主宰者。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"天命;神意;命运之神","en":"Destiny is the force which some people believe controls the things that happen to you in your life.","ex":{"en":"Is it destiny that brings people together, or is it accident?","cn":"人们的相遇是天意还是偶然？"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"I believe there's some force guiding us — call it God, destiny or fate.","cn":"我总认为有某种力量在指引着我们，称之为上帝也罢，天意也罢，还是命运也罢。"},{"en":"He wants to be in control of his own destiny.","cn":"他想要掌握自己的命运。"}]},"detract":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈtrækt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"( not used in the progressive tenses","cn":"不用于进行时 ) to make sth seem less good or enjoyable 减损；毁损；贬低"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"减损;诋毁;贬低","en":"If one thing detracts from another, it makes it seem less good or impressive.","ex":{"en":"The publicity could detract from our election campaign.","cn":"这些宣传报道可能会有损我们的竞选活动。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/detract__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/detract__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"He was determined not to let anything detract from his enjoyment of the trip.","cn":"他下决心这次旅行不让任何事情影响他的兴致。"},{"en":"One mistake is not going to detract from your achievement.","cn":"一个失误无损于你的成就。"}]},"decorated":{"lemma":"decorate"},"decision":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/decision__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/decision__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈsɪʒn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a choice or judgement that you make after thinking and talking about what is the best thing to do","cn":"（作出的）决定，抉择","g":"[countable]","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"I think I've made the right decision.","cn":"我想我作出了正确的决定。"}},{"en":"the process of deciding something","cn":"作决定；决策","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"The moment of decision had arrived.","cn":"决策的时刻已经到了。"}},{"en":"the ability to decide something clearly and quickly","cn":"决断（力）；果断","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"This is not a job for someone who lacks decision.","cn":"不果断的人不适宜做这工作。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"决定;抉择","en":"When you make a decision, you choose what should be done or which is the best of various possible actions.","ex":{"en":"A decision was taken to discipline Marshall","cn":"已作出对马歇尔进行处罚的决定。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"作决定;作抉择","en":"Decision is the act of deciding something or the need to decide something.","ex":{"en":"The moment of decision cannot be delayed","cn":"作出决定的时刻由不得耽搁。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"果断;决断（力）","en":"Decision is the ability to decide quickly and definitely what to do.","ex":{"en":"He is very much a man of decision and action.","cn":"他是一个遇事非常果断、行动极为迅速的人。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"We must come to a decision about what to do next by tomorrow.","cn":"我们必须最晚明天就下一步做什么作出决定。"},{"en":"It's a difficult decision for any doctor.","cn":"这对任何医生来说都是一个困难的决定。"}]},"deaf":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/deaf__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deaf__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"def","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"unable to hear anything or unable to hear very well","cn":"聋的","ex":{"en":"to become/go deaf","cn":"变聋"}},{"en":"people who cannot hear","cn":"耳聋的人；聋子","g":"[plural]","lab":"old-fashioned","ex":{"en":"television subtitles for the deaf","cn":"聋人电视字幕"}},{"en":"not willing to listen or pay attention to something","cn":"不愿听；不去注意","g":"[not before noun]","ex":{"en":"He was deaf to my requests for help.","cn":"他对我的求助充耳不闻。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"聋的;失聪的","en":"Someone who is deaf is unable to hear anything or is unable to hear very well.","ex":{"en":"She is now profoundly deaf.","cn":"她现在已经严重失聪了。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"对…充耳不闻的;不愿听…的","en":"If you say that someone is deaf to people's requests, arguments, or criticisms, you are criticizing them because they refuse to pay attention to them.","ex":{"en":"The provincial assembly were deaf to all pleas for financial help.","cn":"省议会对所有的经济救助请求都充耳不闻。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"to fall on deaf ears→see: ; to turn a deaf ear→see: ;"}]},"examples":[{"en":"television subtitles for the deaf and hard of hearing","cn":"为耳聋和耳背者做的电视字幕"},{"en":"He was deaf to my requests for help.","cn":"他对我的求助充耳不闻。"}]},"demographics":{"lemma":"demographic","media":{"uk":"media/uk/demographics__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/demographics__us_1.mp3"}},"depiction":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/depiction__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/depiction__us_1.mp3"},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"描绘;描画;描写;描述;刻画","en":"A depiction of something is a picture or a written description of it.","ex":{"en":"The lecture will trace the depiction of horses from earliest times to the present day.","cn":"这个讲座将探究从古至今的画马艺术。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"They object to the movie's depiction of gay people.","cn":"他们反对这部影片对同性恋者的刻画。"},{"en":"a book depicting life in pre-revolutionary Russia","cn":""}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpɪkʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the act of showing somebody/something in a particular way in words or pictures, especially in a work of art","cn":"描绘，描述，描写","ex":{"en":"They object to the movie's depiction of gay people.","cn":"他们反对这部影片对同性恋者的刻画。"}}]}},"deliver":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈlɪvə(r)","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to take goods, letters, etc. to the person or people they have been sent to","cn":"传送；交付；运送；投递","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","sc":"take goods/letters","ex":{"en":"I get my food delivered from the supermarket to save time.","cn":"为了节省时间，我让超市把食品送过来。"}},{"en":"to give or send information or ideas to somebody","cn":"传送；传递","g":"[transitive]","sc":"give/send information","ex":{"en":"Let me deliver the good news first.","cn":"让我先传达一个好消息。"}},{"en":"to give a speech, talk, performance, etc. or to make an official statement","cn":"发表；表演；宣布","g":"[transitive]","sc":"give speech","ex":{"en":"She will deliver a major speech on foreign policy tomorrow.","cn":"她明天将发表一次关于外交政策的重要演讲。"}},{"en":"to do what you promised to do or what you are expected to do; to produce or provide what people expect you to","cn":"履行诺言；不负所望；兑现","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"keep promise","ex":{"en":"He has promised to finish the job by June and I am sure he will deliver.","cn":"他答应在六月底完成这项工作，我相信他会履行诺言。"}},{"en":"to take somebody somewhere; to give somebody into somebody else's care or control","cn":"送某人去某地；移交；托付","g":"[transitive]","sc":"give to somebody’s care or control","ex":{"en":"She delivered the kids on time at their father's house.","cn":"她准时把孩子们送到他们的父亲家。"}},{"en":"to help a woman to give birth to a baby","cn":"助产；接生","g":"[transitive]","sc":"baby","ex":{"en":"The baby was delivered by Caesarean section.","cn":"这个婴儿是剖腹产下的。"}},{"en":"to give birth to a baby","cn":"分娩；生孩子","g":"[transitive]","lab":"formal","sc":"baby","ex":{"en":"The number of women delivering their babies in hospital increased.","cn":"在医院分娩的妇女增多了。"}},{"en":"to throw or aim something","cn":"投掷；把…瞄准；用…对准","g":"[transitive]","sc":"throw","ex":{"en":"He delivered the blow (= hit somebody hard) with all his force.","cn":"他打这一下使出了全身的力气。"}},{"en":"to rescue somebody from something bad","cn":"解救；拯救；使摆脱","g":"[transitive]","lab":"old use","sc":"rescue","ex":{"en":"Deliver us from evil.","cn":"‘圣经’救我们脱离邪恶"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"递送;投递;运送","en":"If you deliver something somewhere, you take it there.","ex":{"en":"The Canadians plan to deliver more food to southern Somalia","cn":"加拿大计划向索马里南部地区运送更多的食品。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"履行;兑现;实现","en":"If you deliver something that you have promised to do, make, or produce, you do, make, or produce it.","ex":{"en":"They have yet to show that they can really deliver working technologies","cn":"他们尚未证明自己真的能够开发出实用技术。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"托付;交托","en":"If you deliver a person or thing into someone's care, you give them responsibility for that person or thing.","ex":{"en":"Mrs Montgomery was delivered into Mr Hinchcliffe's care","cn":"蒙哥马利夫人托给了欣奇利夫先生照顾。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"作(讲座);发表(讲话)","en":"If you deliver a lecture or speech, you give it in public.","ex":{"en":"The president will deliver a speech about schools","cn":"总统将就学校问题发表讲话。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"接生(婴儿)","en":"When someone delivers a baby, they help the woman who is giving birth to the baby.","ex":{"en":"Her husband had to deliver the baby himself.","cn":"她丈夫不得不自己接生孩子。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"给予(打击)","en":"If someone delivers a blow to someone else, they hit them.","ex":{"en":"Those blows to the head could have been delivered by a woman.","cn":"头部所受的那些重击有可能出自一个女人之手。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"解救;拯救;使解脱","en":"If someone delivers you from something, they rescue or save you from it.","ex":{"en":"I have given thanks to God for delivering me from that pain.","cn":"我感谢上帝把我从那种痛苦中拯救出来。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"to deliver the goods→see: ;"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/deliver__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deliver__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"He has promised to finish the job by June and I am sure he will deliver.","cn":"他答应在六月底完成这项工作，我相信他会履行诺言。"},{"en":"If you can't deliver improved sales figures, you're fired.","cn":"如果你不能按照要求提高销售额，就会被解雇。"}]},"decorating":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdekəreɪtɪŋ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the activity of putting paint, wallpaper, etc. on the walls and ceilings of a room or house","cn":"粉刷；油漆；糊墙纸","ex":{"en":"We are planning to do some decorating before we move in.","cn":"我们计划在搬进去之前做一些装饰。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/1/decorate0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/2/decorate.mp3","img":["media/ldoce/img/decorate1.jpg"]},"examples":[{"en":"The bathroom is decorated in green and yellow.","cn":""},{"en":"We plan to spend the weekend decorating.","cn":""}],"base":"decorate"},"depressed":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈprest","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"very sad and without hope","cn":"抑郁的；沮丧的；意志消沉的","ex":{"en":"You mustn't let yourself get depressed.","cn":"你绝对不能让自己沮丧。"}},{"en":"affected by the medical condition of depression","cn":"患抑郁症的","ex":{"en":"She became severely depressed.","cn":"她患上了严重的抑郁症。"}},{"en":"without enough economic activity or jobs for people","cn":"不景气的；萧条的；经济困难的","ex":{"en":"They have made little attempt to bring jobs to economically depressed areas.","cn":"在为经济萧条地区创造就业机会方面他们几乎没有作过什么努力。"}},{"en":"having a lower amount or level than usual","cn":"低于一般水准的；降低了的；削弱了的","ex":{"en":"depressed prices","cn":"降低了的价格"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"抑郁的;沮丧的;消沉的","en":"If you are depressed, you are sad and feel that you cannot enjoy anything, because your situation is so difficult and unpleasant.","ex":{"en":"He seemed somewhat depressed","cn":"他似乎有些抑郁。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"萧条的;不景气的","en":"A depressed place or industry does not have enough business or employment to be successful.","ex":{"en":"...legislation to encourage investment in depressed areas","cn":"鼓励向经济困难地区投资的法律法规"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"凹陷的;低陷的","en":"A depressed point on a surface is lower than the parts around it.","ex":{"en":"Acupressure is manual pressure applied to a specific slightly depressed point on the body.","cn":"指压按摩是用手按压人体某个轻微凹陷的穴位。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/depressed__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/depressed__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"an attempt to bring jobs to depressed areas","cn":"给经济萧条地区创造就业机会的努力"},{"en":"She felt very depressed about the future.","cn":"她感到前途无望。"}]},"dense":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/dense__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/dense__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dens","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"containing a lot of people, things, plants, etc. with little space between them","cn":"密集的；稠密的","ex":{"en":"a dense crowd/forest","cn":"密集的人群；密林"}},{"en":"difficult to see through","cn":"浓密的；浓重的","ex":{"en":"dense fog/smoke/fumes","cn":"浓雾；浓烟；浓烈的气体"}},{"en":"stupid","cn":"愚笨的；迟钝的；笨拙的","lab":"informal","ex":{"en":"How can you be so dense?","cn":"你怎么会这么笨？"}},{"en":"difficult to understand because it contains a lot of information","cn":"（信息量大得）难理解的，难懂的","ex":{"en":"a dense piece of writing","cn":"难懂的文章"}},{"en":"heavy in relation to its size","cn":"密度大的；密实的","lab":"specialist","ex":{"en":"Less dense substances move upwards to form a crust.","cn":"密度小的物质向上浮动并形成一个硬层。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"稠密的;密集的","en":"Something that is dense contains a lot of things or people in a small area.","ex":{"en":"Where Bucharest now stands, there once was a large, dense forest","cn":"布加勒斯特的所在地过去曾是一大片茂密的森林。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(雾、烟等)浓的，浓重的","en":"Dense fog or smoke is difficult to see through because it is very heavy and dark.","ex":{"en":"A dense column of smoke rose several miles into the air.","cn":"一股浓烟升到了几英里的高空。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(物质)密度大的","en":"In science, a dense substance is very heavy in relation to its volume.","ex":{"en":"...a small dense star.","cn":"密度很大的小恒星"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(文章、电影等因信息量大而)难懂的，费解的","en":"If you describe writing or a film as dense, you mean that it is difficult to understand because it contains a lot of information and ideas.","ex":{"en":"His prose is vigorous and dense, occasionally to the point of obscurity.","cn":"他的散文文笔有力、内容庞杂，有时几近晦涩。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"愚蠢的;愚钝的;鲁钝的","en":"If you say that someone is dense, you mean that you think they are stupid and that they take a long time to understand simple things.","ex":{"en":"He's not a bad man, just a bit dense.","cn":"他人不坏，就是有点儿愚钝。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Less dense substances move upwards to form a crust.","cn":"密度小的物质向上浮动并形成一硬层。"},{"en":"How can you be so dense?","cn":"你怎么会这么笨？"}]},"decorative":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdekərətɪv","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"decorated in a way that makes it attractive; intended to look attractive or pretty","cn":"装饰性的；作装饰用的","ex":{"en":"The mirror is functional yet decorative.","cn":"这镜子能照人，但也有装饰作用。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"装饰性的;用作装饰的","en":"Something that is decorative is intended to look pretty or attractive.","ex":{"en":"The curtains are for purely decorative purposes and do not open or close.","cn":"那些窗帘纯粹是作装饰用的，不能拉开或合上。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/decorative__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/decorative__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The mirror is functional yet decorative.","cn":"这镜子能照人，但也有装饰作用。"},{"en":"purely decorative arches","cn":"纯属装饰性的拱门"}]},"delay":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈleɪ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a period of time when somebody/something has to wait because of a problem that makes something slow or late","cn":"延迟（或耽搁、拖延）的时间","g":"[countable, uncountable]","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"Commuters will face long delays on the roads today.","cn":"路远乘车上下班的人今天要在路上耽误很多时间了。"}},{"en":"failure to do something quickly or at the right time; the act of delaying","cn":"拖延；耽搁；延误","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"There's no time for delay.","cn":"没有时间了，不能拖延了。"}},{"en":"to make somebody/something late or force them to do something more slowly","cn":"使迟到；使耽搁；使拖延","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"My flight was delayed.","cn":"我的航班延误了。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to not do something until a later time or to make something happen at a later time","cn":"延迟；延期；推迟","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","ex":{"en":"Don't delay—call us today!","cn":"别拖延，今天就给我们打电话！"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"使延期;使延迟;推迟","en":"If you delay doing something, you do not do it immediately or at the planned or expected time, but you leave it until later. →see usage note at:","ex":{"en":"For sentimental reasons I wanted to delay my departure until June","cn":"因为感情方面的原因，我想把离开的日期延迟至6月。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"使延误;使耽搁","en":"To delay someone or something means to make them late or to slow them down.","ex":{"en":"Can you delay him in some way?","cn":"你能想办法拖住他一会儿吗？"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（故意）拖延，磨蹭","en":"If you delay, you deliberately take longer than necessary to do something.","ex":{"en":"If he delayed any longer, the sun would be up.","cn":"如果他再拖延，太阳就要出来了。"}},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"延期;延迟;推迟","en":"If there is a delay, something does not happen until later than planned or expected.","ex":{"en":"They claimed that such a delay wouldn't hurt anyone","cn":"他们声称这样的延期对谁都不会造成损害。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"延误;耽搁","en":"Delay is a failure to do something immediately or in the required or usual time.","ex":{"en":"There is no time left for delay","cn":"已经没有时间再耽误了。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/delay__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/delay__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Commuters will face long delays on the roads today.","cn":"路远乘车上下班的人今天要在路上耽误很多时间了。"},{"en":"The judge will delay his verdict until he receives medical reports on the offender.","cn":"法官将推迟判决，直到收到有关违法者的医疗报告。"}]},"devoted":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/devoted__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/devoted__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈvəʊtɪd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"having great love for somebody/something and supporting them in everything","cn":"挚爱的；忠诚的；全心全意的","ex":{"en":"a devoted son/friend/fan","cn":"孝子；忠诚的朋友；狂热的崇拜者"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"深爱的;挚爱的;忠诚的","en":"Someone who is devoted to a person loves that person very much.","ex":{"en":"...a loving and devoted husband","cn":"深情且忠诚的丈夫"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"爱好的;热衷的;致力（于…）的","en":"If you are devoted to something, you care about it a lot and are very enthusiastic about it.","ex":{"en":"I have personally been devoted to this cause for many years","cn":"多年来我个人一直一心扑在这项事业上。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"专用于…的","en":"Something that is devoted to a particular thing deals only with that thing or contains only that thing.","ex":{"en":"...a major touring exhibition devoted to the work of disabled artists.","cn":"专门展出残疾人艺术家作品的一个重要巡回展"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"They are devoted to their children.","cn":"他们深爱着自己的孩子。"},{"en":"a devoted son/friend/fan","cn":"孝子；忠诚的朋友；狂热的崇拜者"}]},"deserving":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/deserving__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deserving__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈzɜːvɪŋ","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"that deserves help, praise, a reward, etc.","cn":"值得的；应得的","ex":{"en":"to give money to a deserving cause","cn":"把钱捐给值得赞助的事业"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"值得帮助的;应受支持的","en":"If you describe a person, organization, or cause as deserving, you mean that you think they should be helped.","ex":{"en":"The money saved could be used for more deserving causes.","cn":"省下来的钱可以用于更有意义的事业。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"应得…的;应受…的;值得…的","en":"If someone is deserving of something, they have qualities or achievements which make it right that they should receive it.","ex":{"en":"...artists deserving of public subsidy.","cn":"应该得到政府津贴的艺术家"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"This family is one of the most deserving cases.","cn":"这是最应当得到帮助的一户人家。"},{"en":"to give money to a deserving cause","cn":"把钱捐给值得赞助的事业"}],"base":"deserve"},"democratic":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/democratic__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/democratic__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdeməˈkrætɪk","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"controlled by representatives who are elected by the people of a country; connected with this system","cn":"民主的；民主政体的；民主制度的","ex":{"en":"a democratic country","cn":"民主国家"}},{"en":"based on the principle that all members have an equal right to be involved in running an organization, etc.","cn":"民主权利的","ex":{"en":"democratic participation","cn":"民主参与"}},{"en":"based on the principle that all members of society are equal rather than divided by money or social class","cn":"有民主精神的；平等的","ex":{"en":"a democratic society","cn":"民主社会"}},{"en":"connected with the Democratic Party in the US","cn":"（美国）民主党的","ex":{"en":"the Democratic senator from Oregon","cn":"（美国）俄勒冈州的民主党参议员"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"民主的;民主制度的;民主政体的","en":"A democratic country, government, or political system is governed by representatives who are elected by the people.","ex":{"en":"Bolivia returned to democratic rule in 1982, after a series of military governments.","cn":"在经历了数届军人政府后，玻利维亚于 1982 年恢复了民主政权。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"民主精神的;民主作风的","en":"Something that is democratic is based on the idea that everyone should have equal rights and should be involved in making important decisions.","ex":{"en":"Education is the basis of a democratic society","cn":"教育是民主社会的基础。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(用于政党名称中)民主的","en":"Democratic is used in the titles of some political parties.","ex":{"en":"...the Social Democratic Party.","cn":"社会民主党"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"the Democratic senator from Oregon （","cn":"美国）俄勒冈州的民主党参议员"},{"en":"The decision was taken democratically.","cn":"这是通过民主讨论作出的决策。"}]},"delivers":{"lemma":"deliver"},"dens":{"lemma":"den"},"delayed":{"lemma":"delay","media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/1/delay_v0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/b/delay1.mp3"}},"decadence":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/decadence__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/decadence__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdekədəns","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"behaviour, attitudes, etc. that show a fall in standards, especially moral ones, and an interest in pleasure and fun rather than more serious things","cn":"堕落；颓废；贪图享乐","ex":{"en":"the decadence of modern Western society","cn":"现代西方社会的颓废现象"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"the decadence of modern Western society","cn":"现代西方社会的颓废现象"}]},"desperation":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/desperation__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/desperation__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdespəˈreɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the state of being desperate","cn":"绝望；拼命；铤而走险","ex":{"en":"In desperation, she called Louise and asked for her help.","cn":"在走投无路的情况下，她给路易丝打了个电话请她帮忙。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"绝望;孤注一掷;铤而走险;拼命","en":"Desperation is the feeling that you have when you are in such a bad situation that you will try anything to change it.","ex":{"en":"This feeling of desperation and helplessness was common to most of the refugees","cn":"大多数难民都有这种绝望和无助的感觉。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"In desperation, she called Louise and asked for her help.","cn":"在走投无路的情况下，她给路易丝打了个电话请她帮忙。"},{"en":"There was a note of desperation in his voice.","cn":"听他的语气他急得要命。"}]},"despised":{"lemma":"despise"},"deliberately":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/deliberately__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deliberately__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈlɪbərətli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"done in a way that was planned, not by chance","cn":"故意；蓄意；存心","ex":{"en":"She's been deliberately ignoring him all day.","cn":"她故意整天都不理他。"}},{"en":"slowly and carefully","cn":"不慌不忙地；小心翼翼地；从容不迫地","ex":{"en":"He packed up his possessions slowly and deliberately.","cn":"他慢慢地、小心翼翼地收拾好自己的物品。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He packed up his possessions slowly and deliberately.","cn":"他慢慢地、小心翼翼地收拾好自己的物品。"},{"en":"She's been deliberately ignoring him all day.","cn":"她故意整天都不理他。"}]},"depressing":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/depressing__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/depressing__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpresɪŋ","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"making you feel very sad and without enthusiasm","cn":"令人抑郁的；令人沮丧的；令人消沉的","ex":{"en":"a depressing sight/thought/experience","cn":"令人沮丧的景象／想法／经历"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"令人抑郁的;使人沮丧的;让人消沉的","en":"Something that is depressing makes you feel sad and disappointed.","ex":{"en":"Yesterday's unemployment figures were depressing","cn":"昨天的失业数字令人沮丧。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Looking for a job these days can be very depressing.","cn":"如今求职有时会令人非常沮丧。"},{"en":"a depressing sight/thought/experience","cn":"令人沮丧的景象/想法/经历"}]},"delivering":{"lemma":"deliver"},"deserted":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/deserted__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deserted__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈzɜːtɪd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"with no people in it","cn":"无人居住的；空寂无人的","ex":{"en":"deserted streets","cn":"空无一人的街道"}},{"en":"left by a person or people who do not intend to return","cn":"被抛弃的；被遗弃的；被舍弃的","ex":{"en":"a deserted village","cn":"被舍弃的村庄"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"deserted streets","cn":"空无一人的街道"},{"en":"a deserted village","cn":"被舍弃的村庄"}],"base":"desert"},"delivery":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/delivery__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/delivery__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈlɪvəri","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the act of taking goods, letters, etc. to the people they have been sent to","cn":"传送；递送；交付","g":"[uncountable, countable]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"Allow 28 days for delivery.","cn":"请留出 28 天送货时间。"}},{"en":"the act of making a service or information available to people","cn":"信息提供；服务提供","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"the delivery of public services","cn":"提供公共服务"}},{"en":"the process of giving birth to a baby","cn":"分娩","g":"[countable, uncountable]","ex":{"en":"an easy/a difficult delivery","cn":"顺产；难产"}},{"en":"the way in which somebody speaks, sings a song, etc. in public","cn":"演讲方式；表演风格","g":"[singular]","ex":{"en":"The beautiful poetry was ruined by her poor delivery.","cn":"这优美的诗被她拙劣的朗诵给糟蹋了。"}},{"en":"a ball that is thrown, especially in cricket or baseball","cn":"投球（尤指板球或棒球）","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"a fast delivery","cn":"一个快投球"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"(信件、包裹等的)递送，投递，运送","en":"Delivery or a delivery is the bringing of letters, parcels, or other goods to someone's house or to another place where they want them.","ex":{"en":"Please allow 28 days for delivery","cn":"递送将需要 28 天的时间。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"递送之物;投递之物;运送之物","en":"A delivery of something is the goods that are delivered.","ex":{"en":"I got a delivery of fresh eggs this morning.","cn":"我今天早上收到了送来的新鲜鸡蛋。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"递送的;投递的;运送的","en":"A delivery person or service delivers things to a place.","ex":{"en":"...a pizza delivery man.","cn":"比萨饼递送员"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"发言(或演说)的方式","en":"You talk about someone's delivery when you are referring to the way in which they give a speech or lecture.","ex":{"en":"His speeches were magnificently written but his delivery was hopeless.","cn":"他的发言稿写得非常精彩，但他的演讲风格真是无可救药。"}},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"分娩;生产","en":"Delivery is the process of giving birth to a baby.","ex":{"en":"In the end, it was an easy delivery: a fine baby boy","cn":"分娩过程最终非常顺利，生了个健康的男婴。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The beautiful poetry was ruined by her poor delivery.","cn":"这优美的诗被她拙劣的朗诵给糟蹋了。"},{"en":"Allow 28 days for delivery.","cn":"请留出 28 天送货时间。"}]},"departure":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/departure__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/departure__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpɑːtʃə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an act of leaving a place","cn":"离开；启程；出发","g":"[countable, uncountable]","ex":{"en":"His sudden departure threw the office into chaos.","cn":"他的突然离去使整个办公室陷入一片混乱。"}},{"en":"a plane, train, etc. leaving a place at a particular time","cn":"（在特定时间）离开的飞机（或火车等）","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"arrivals and departures","cn":"到站和离站班次"}},{"en":"the part of an airport where you go before catching a plane","cn":"（机场的）出发大厅","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"There were long delays and queues in departures.","cn":"出现了长时间的延误，出发大厅里排起了长队。"}},{"en":"an action that is different from what is usual or expected","cn":"背离；违反；逾越","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"Their latest single represents a new departure for the band.","cn":"他们最新推出的单曲唱片体现了这支乐队的新尝试。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"离开;启程;动身;出发","en":"Departure or a departure is the act of going away from somewhere.","ex":{"en":"...the President's departure for Helsinki","cn":"总统动身前往赫尔辛基"}},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"辞职;离职;（从某组织的）脱离","en":"The departure of a person from a job, or a member from an organization, is their act of leaving it or being forced to leave it.","ex":{"en":"This would inevitably involve his departure from the post of Prime Minister","cn":"这将不可避免地导致他辞去首相一职。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"违背;背离","en":"If someone does something different or unusual, you can refer to their action as a departure .","ex":{"en":"Taylor announced another departure from practice in that England will train at Wembley","cn":"泰勒再次一改常规地宣布英格兰队将在温布利球场进行训练。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Their latest single represents a new departure for the band.","cn":"他们最新推出的单曲唱片体现了这支乐队的新尝试。"},{"en":"They had received no news of him since his departure from the island.","cn":"自从他离开这座岛后，他们再没听过他的消息。"}]},"declaration":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/declaration__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/declaration__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdekləˈreɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an official or formal statement, especially about the plans of a government or an organization; the act of making such a statement","cn":"公告；宣告；宣言","g":"[countable, uncountable]","ex":{"en":"to issue/sign a declaration","cn":"发布／签署公告"}},{"en":"a written or spoken statement, especially about what people feel or believe","cn":"声明（书）；宣布；表白；宣称","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"a declaration of love/faith/guilt","cn":"表白爱情；表达信念；宣判有罪"}},{"en":"an official written statement giving information","cn":"申报（单）","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"a declaration of income","cn":"收益申报表"}},{"en":"an official announcement of the number of votes each candidate has received in an election","cn":"申报（单）","g":"[countable]","lab":"British English, politics，，","ex":{"en":"The declaration of the poll will take place tomorrow morning.","cn":"投票结果将于明天上午公布。"}},{"en":"the act of ending an innings before all your players have batted","cn":"对一赛局结束的宣布","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"After England's declaration at 379 for 6, they overwhelmed their hapless opponents.","cn":"英格兰队以 379 胜 6 负的成绩击败了倒霉的对手。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"宣布;宣言;公告","en":"A declaration is an official announcement or statement.","ex":{"en":"They will sign the declaration tomorrow","cn":"他们明天将签署这份公告。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"宣称;声明;表白","en":"A declaration is a firm, emphatic statement which shows that you have no doubts about what you are saying.","ex":{"en":"She needed time to adjust to Clive's declaration.","cn":"她需要时间来适应克莱夫的表白。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(可用作法庭证据的）书面声明;报单","en":"A declaration is a written statement about something which you have signed and which can be used as evidence in a court of law.","ex":{"en":"On the customs declaration, the sender labeled the freight as agricultural machinery","cn":"在报关单上，寄货人将货物列为农用机械。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"customs declarations (= giving details of goods that have been brought into a country)","cn":"报关单（带入境内物品的详细清单）"},{"en":"the Declaration of Independence (= of the United States) （","cn":"美国）独立宣言"}]},"decline":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/decline__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/decline__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈklaɪn","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to become smaller, fewer, weaker, etc.","cn":"减少；下降；衰弱；衰退","g":"[intransitive]","lab":"rather formal","ex":{"en":"Support for the party continues to decline.","cn":"对该党的支持继续下降。"}},{"en":"to refuse politely to accept or to do something","cn":"谢绝；婉言拒绝","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"I offered to give them a lift but they declined.","cn":"我主动提议开车送他们，但他们婉言谢绝了。"}},{"en":"if a noun, an adjective or a pronoun declines, it has different forms according to whether it is the subject or the object of a verb, whether it is in the singular or plural, etc. When you decline a noun, etc., you list these forms.","cn":"（名词、形容词或代词）变格，有词形变化；列出词形变化","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","lab":"grammar"},{"en":"a continuous decrease in the number, value, quality, etc. of something","cn":"（数量、价值、质量等的）减少，下降，衰落，衰退","ex":{"en":"There has been a 5 per cent decline in student numbers.","cn":"学生人数下降了 5%。"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"下降;减少;衰退;衰落","en":"If something declines, it becomes less in quantity, importance, or strength.","ex":{"en":"The number of staff has declined from 217,000 to 114,000","cn":"员工人数从 21.7万减少到了11.4万。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"婉拒;谢绝","en":"If you decline something or decline to do something, you politely refuse to accept it or do it.","ex":{"en":"He declined their invitation","cn":"他谢绝了他们的邀请。"}},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"下降;减少;衰退;衰落","en":"If there is a decline in something, it becomes less in quantity, importance, or quality.","ex":{"en":"There wasn't such a big decline in enrollments after all","cn":"注册人数终究还是没有出现如此大幅度的下降。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"逐渐势微;正在衰退","en":"If something is in decline or on the decline, it is gradually decreasing in importance, quality, or power.","ex":{"en":"Thankfully the smoking of cigarettes is on the decline","cn":"令人欣慰的是，吸烟量在逐渐下降。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"走下坡路;开始衰退","en":"If something goes or falls into decline, it begins to gradually decrease in importance, quality, or power.","ex":{"en":"Libraries are an investment for the future and they should not be allowed to fall into decline.","cn":"图书馆是对未来的一项投资，不应任其日趋萎缩。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Industry in Britain has been in decline since the 1970s.","cn":"英国工业自 20 世纪 70 年代以来一直在走下坡路。"},{"en":"The number of tourists to the resort declined by 10% last year.","cn":"去年到这个胜地旅游的人数减少了 10%。"}]},"deliberate":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/deliberate__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deliberate__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈlɪbərət","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"done on purpose rather than by accident","cn":"故意的；蓄意的；存心的","ex":{"en":"a deliberate act of vandalism","cn":"故意毁坏公物的行为"}},{"en":"done slowly and carefully","cn":"不慌不忙的；小心翼翼的；从容不迫的","ex":{"en":"She spoke in a slow and deliberate way.","cn":"她说话慢条斯理不慌不忙。"}},{"en":"to consider something very carefully, usually before making a decision","cn":"仔细考虑；深思熟虑；反复思考","ex":{"en":"The jury deliberated for five days before finding him guilty.","cn":"陪审团认真讨论了五天才裁定他有罪。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"故意的;蓄意的;早有计划的","en":"If you do something that is deliberate, you planned or decided to do it beforehand, and so it happens on purpose rather than by chance.","ex":{"en":"It has a deliberate policy to introduce world art to Britain","cn":"它在政策上有意识地将世界艺术介绍给英国。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"从容的;不慌不忙的;审慎的;小心翼翼的","en":"If a movement or action is deliberate, it is done slowly and carefully.","ex":{"en":"His movements were gentle and deliberate.","cn":"他举止文雅而从容。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（尤指作出重大决定前）慎重考虑，仔细思考","en":"If you deliberate, you think about something carefully, especially before making a very important decision.","ex":{"en":"She deliberated over the decision for a long time before she made up her mind","cn":"她慎重考虑了好久才下定决心作出这一决定。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The jury deliberated for five days before finding him guilty.","cn":"陪审团认真讨论了五天才认定他有罪。"},{"en":"They deliberated (on) whether to continue with the talks.","cn":"他们仔细考虑了是否继续谈判的问题。"}]},"depth":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/depth__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/depth__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"depθ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the distance from the top or surface to the bottom of something; a particular distance down from the surface of something","cn":"向下的距离；深（度）；纵深","g":"[countable, uncountable]","sc":"measurement","ex":{"en":"What's the depth of the water here?","cn":"这儿的水有多深？"}},{"en":"the distance from the front to the back of something","cn":"向里的距离；深（度）","g":"[countable, uncountable]","sc":"measurement","ex":{"en":"The depth of the shelves is 30 centimetres.","cn":"书架的深度为 30 厘米。"}},{"en":"the strength and power of feelings","cn":"深厚；诚挚；强烈","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"of feelings","ex":{"en":"the depth of her love","cn":"她那爱情之深"}},{"en":"qualities that give somebody/something extra character and make them/it interesting","cn":"深度","g":"[uncountable, countable]","lab":"approving","sc":"of character/qualities","ex":{"en":"The separate storylines really add depth and personality to the characters.","cn":"独立的故事情节确实增加了人物的深度和个性。"}},{"en":"the quality of knowing or understanding a lot of details about something; the ability to provide and explain these details","cn":"渊博；深刻；洞察力","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"approving","sc":"of knowledge","ex":{"en":"a writer of great wisdom and depth","cn":"有卓越智慧和洞察力的作家"}},{"en":"the deepest, most extreme or serious part of something","cn":"最深处；深渊；极限","g":"[countable, usually plural]","sc":"deepest part","ex":{"en":"the depths of the ocean","cn":"海洋深处"}},{"en":"the strength of a colour","cn":"浓度；强度","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"of colour","ex":{"en":"Strong light will affect the depth of colour of your carpets and curtains.","cn":"强烈的阳光会使你的地毯和窗帘褪色。"}},{"en":"the quality in a work of art or a photograph that makes it appear not to be flat","cn":"立体感","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"specialist","sc":"picture/photograph"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"（从上到下的）深（度）","en":"The depth of something such as a river or hole is the distance downwards from its top surface, or between its upper and lower surfaces.","ex":{"en":"The smaller lake ranges from five to fourteen feet in depth","cn":"小一些的湖深度从 5 英尺到 14 英尺不等。"}},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"（从前到后的）深（度）；纵深","en":"The depth of something such as a cupboard or drawer is the distance between its front surface and its back."},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"(感情的)深厚，深切","en":"If an emotion is very strongly or intensely felt, you can talk about its depth .","ex":{"en":"I am well aware of the depth of feeling that exists in Londonderry","cn":"我很清楚存在于伦敦德里市的那种强烈情绪。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"严重性;严峻性","en":"The depth of a situation is its extent and seriousness.","ex":{"en":"The country's leadership had underestimated the depth of the crisis.","cn":"该国领导人低估了这场危机的严重性。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(知识等的)渊博","en":"The depth of someone's knowledge is the great amount that they know.","ex":{"en":"We felt at home with her and were impressed with the depth of her knowledge","cn":"我们与她在一起很自在，而她渊博的知识令我们叹服。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(颜色的)浓度","en":"The depth of a colour is its intensity and strength.","ex":{"en":"White wines tend to gain depth of colour with age","cn":"白葡萄酒年头愈久，颜色愈深。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(照片、画作等的)景深","en":"In photography and art, you say that a picture has depth or depth of field when you mean that it appears three-dimensional rather than flat.","ex":{"en":"All the paintings are startlingly dramatic as a result of their depth of field and colour.","cn":"景深和色彩的运用令所有的画作都展现出令人惊叹的戏剧性效果。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"深刻;深奥","en":"If you say that someone or something has depth, you mean that they have serious and interesting qualities which are not immediately obvious and which you have to think about carefully before you can fully understand them.","ex":{"en":"His music lacks depth","cn":"他的音乐缺乏深度。"}},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"(海洋或陆地的)深处,深渊","en":"The depths are places that are a long way below the surface of the sea or earth.","ex":{"en":"The ship vanished into the depths.","cn":"船消失在了大海深处。"}},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"（某一区域的）深处，腹地","en":"If you talk about the depths of an area, you mean the parts of it which are very far from the edge.","ex":{"en":"...the depths of the countryside","cn":"乡村腹地"}},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"(某一不快感情的)极限","en":"If you are in the depths of an unpleasant emotion, you feel that emotion very strongly.","ex":{"en":"I was in the depths of despair when the baby was sick.","cn":"孩子生病时我陷入了绝望的深渊之中。"}},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"…的中间部分;…最严重的时候;…最强烈的时候","en":"If something happens in the depths of a difficult or unpleasant period of time, it happens in the middle and most severe or intense part of it.","ex":{"en":"The country is in the depths of a recession.","cn":"该国正遭遇最严重的经济衰退。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"深入地;彻底地;全面地","en":"If you deal with a subject in depth, you deal with it very thoroughly and consider all the aspects of it.","ex":{"en":"We will discuss these three areas in depth","cn":"我们将深入探讨这3个领域。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"应付不了;力所不及","en":"If you say that someone is out of their depth, you mean that they are in a situation that is much too difficult for them to be able to cope with it.","ex":{"en":"Mr Gibson is clearly intellectually out of his depth","cn":"吉布森先生显然才智不逮。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"在水深没顶的地方","en":"If you are out of your depth, you are in water that is deeper than you are tall, with the result that you cannot stand up with your head above water."},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"to plumb new depths→see: ; to plumb the depths→see: ;"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Strong light will affect the depth of colour of your carpets and curtains.","cn":"强烈的阳光会使你的地毯和窗帘褪色。"},{"en":"He felt totally out of his depth in his new job.","cn":"他感到自己根本不能胜任这新工作。"}]},"determination":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/determination__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/determination__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˌtɜːmɪˈneɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the quality that makes you continue trying to do something even when this is difficult","cn":"决心；坚毅；坚定","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"fierce/grim/dogged determination","cn":"坚强的／不屈不挠的／顽强的决心"}},{"en":"the process of deciding something officially","cn":"（正式）决定，确定，规定","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"factors influencing the determination of future policy","cn":"影响未来决策的各种因素"}},{"en":"the act of finding out or calculating something","cn":"查明；测定；计算","g":"[uncountable, countable]","lab":"specialist","ex":{"en":"Both methods rely on the accurate determination of the pressure of the gas.","cn":"两种方法都依赖于对气体压力的准确测定。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"决心;坚决;坚定;果断","en":"Determination is the quality that you show when you have decided to do something and you will not let anything stop you.","ex":{"en":"Everyone concerned acted with great courage and determination","cn":"所有相关人员都表现出了极大的勇气和决心。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Both methods rely on the accurate determination of the pressure of the gas.","cn":"两种方法都依赖于对气体压力的准确测定。"},{"en":"I admire her determination to get it right.","cn":"我赞赏她非把事情弄清楚的决心。"}]},"desirable":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈzaɪərəbl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"that you would like to have or do; worth having or doing","cn":"想望的；可取的；值得拥有的；值得做的","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"She chatted for a few minutes about the qualities she considered desirable in a secretary.","cn":"她用了几分钟谈了谈她认为一个秘书应有的品质。"}},{"en":"causing other people to feel sexual desire","cn":"引起性欲的；性感的","ex":{"en":"She suddenly saw herself as a desirable young woman.","cn":"她突然发现自己是一个令人向往的年轻女子。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"值得想望（或拥有）的;合意的;可取的;受欢迎的","en":"Something that is desirable is worth having or doing because it is useful, necessary, or popular.","ex":{"en":"Prolonged negotiation was not desirable","cn":"拖长了的谈判并不是大家所想要的。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"性感的;可人的","en":"Someone who is desirable is considered to be sexually attractive.","ex":{"en":"...the young women whom his classmates thought most desirable.","cn":"他的同班同学认为最性感的年轻女子"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/desirable__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/desirable__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"She chatted for a few minutes about the qualities she considered desirable in a secretary.","cn":"她用了几分钟谈了谈她认为一个秘书应有的品质。"},{"en":"It is no longer desirable for adult children to live with their parents.","cn":"孩子长大成人后便不再想与父母住在一起了。"}]},"dedicate":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdedɪkeɪt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to give a lot of your time and effort to a particular activity or purpose because you think it is important","cn":"献身；把（时间、努力等）奉献给","ex":{"en":"She dedicates herself to her work.","cn":"她献身于自己的工作。"}},{"en":"to say at the beginning of a book, a piece of music or a performance, or when receiving an award, that you are doing it for somebody, as a way of thanking them or showing respect","cn":"把（书、音乐作品、演出、所获奖项等）献给","ex":{"en":"This book is dedicated to my parents.","cn":"谨以此书献给我的父母。"}},{"en":"to hold an official ceremony to say that a building or an object has a special purpose or is special to the memory of a particular person","cn":"为…举行奉献典礼；为（建筑物等）举行落成典礼","ex":{"en":"The chapel was dedicated in 1880.","cn":"这座小教堂于 1880 年举行献堂典礼。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"献(身);投(身);致力","en":"If you say that someone has dedicated themselves to something, you approve of the fact that they have decided to give a lot of time and effort to it because they think that it is important.","ex":{"en":"Back on the island, he dedicated himself to politics","cn":"回到岛上后，他便投身于政治。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"把(书、戏剧、音乐作品等)献（给）","en":"If someone dedicates something such as a book, play, or piece of music to you, they mention your name, for example in the front of a book or when a piece of music is performed, as a way of showing affection or respect for you.","ex":{"en":"She dedicated her first album to Woody Allen","cn":"她把自己的第一张专辑献给了伍迪·艾伦。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"为(建筑物或教堂)举行奉献（或落成）典礼","en":"If a building or church is dedicated to someone, a formal ceremony is held to show that the building will always be associated with them.","ex":{"en":"The other day, in a little church near Brighton, a window was dedicated to the memory of the Revd. Michael Scott","cn":"几天前，在布赖顿附近的一个小教堂，人们以一扇窗户来纪念迈克尔·斯科特牧师。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/dedicate__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/dedicate__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The chapel was dedicated in 1880.","cn":"这座小教堂于 1880 年举行献堂典礼。"},{"en":"A memorial stone was dedicated to those who were killed in the war.","cn":"为阵亡将士纪念碑举行了落成典礼。"}]},"decadent":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/decadent__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/decadent__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdekədənt","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"having or showing low standards, especially moral ones, and an interest only in pleasure and fun rather than serious things","cn":"堕落的；颓废的；贪图享乐的","ex":{"en":"the decadent rich","cn":"贪图享乐的富豪"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"堕落的;颓废的","en":"If you say that a person or society is decadent, you think that they have low moral standards and are interested mainly in pleasure.","ex":{"en":"...restrictions on the number of decadent western films that were allowed to be shown.","cn":"对颓靡的西方电影在上映数量上的限制"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"a decadent lifestyle/society","cn":"堕落的生活方式；腐朽的社会"},{"en":"the decadent rich","cn":"贪图享乐的富豪"}]},"dependent":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/dependent__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/dependent__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpendənt","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"needing somebody/something in order to survive or be successful","cn":"依靠的；依赖的","ex":{"en":"a woman with several dependent children","cn":"一个女人带着几个未自立的孩子"}},{"en":"addicted to something (= unable to stop taking or using it)","cn":"有瘾的","ex":{"en":"to be dependent on drugs","cn":"有毒瘾"}},{"en":"affected or decided by something","cn":"受…的影响；取决于","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"A child's development is dependent on many factors.","cn":"孩子的成长受多种因素影响。"}},{"en":"secondary to another clause, phrase or word","cn":"从属的","lab":"grammar","ex":{"en":"The word ‘because’ forces the clause to be dependent on some other main clause.","cn":"“because”这个词使得从句依赖于其他主要从句。"}},{"en":"a person, especially a child, who depends on another person for a home, food, money, etc.","cn":"受扶养者（尤指孩子）；靠他人生活者","lab":"British English also","pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"依靠的;依赖的","en":"To be dependent on something or someone means to need them in order to succeed or be able to survive.","ex":{"en":"The local economy is overwhelmingly dependent on oil and gas extraction","cn":"当地经济过于依赖石油和天然气的开采。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"取决（于…）的;有赖（于…）的","en":"If one thing is dependent on another, the first thing will be affected or determined by the second.","ex":{"en":"The results you get from weight training are largely dependent upon how you use those weights and what type of exercise programme you follow.","cn":"举重训练的效果在很大程度上取决于如何使用那些举重器械以及遵照何种锻炼方案。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The festival is heavily dependent on sponsorship for its success.","cn":"这次节日庆祝活动成功与否，在很大程度上就看赞助了。"},{"en":"The price is dependent on how many extras you choose.","cn":"价格取决于你挑选额外收费项目的多少。"}]},"despicable":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/despicable__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/despicable__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈspɪkəbl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"very unpleasant or evil","cn":"令人厌恶的；可鄙的；卑鄙的","ex":{"en":"a despicable act/crime","cn":"卑鄙的行为／罪行"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"可鄙的;卑鄙的","en":"If you say that a person or action is despicable, you are emphasizing that they are extremely nasty, cruel, or evil.","ex":{"en":"The Minister said the bombing was a despicable crime.","cn":"部长说这次爆炸是一起卑劣的罪行。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"I hate you! You're despicable.","cn":"我恨你！你真卑鄙。"},{"en":"a despicable act/crime","cn":"卑鄙的行为/罪行"}]},"decay":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/decay__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/decay__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈkeɪ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the process or result of being destroyed by natural causes or by not being cared for (= of decaying)","cn":"腐烂；腐朽","ex":{"en":"tooth decay","cn":"蛀牙"}},{"en":"the process of a society, an institution, a system, etc. being gradually destroyed","cn":"（社会、机构、制度等的）衰落，衰退，衰败","ex":{"en":"economic/moral/urban decay","cn":"经济衰退；道德败坏；城市衰落"}},{"en":"the process by which a radioactive substance changes to a different form by sending out radiation","cn":"（放射性物质的）衰变","lab":"physics","ex":{"en":"Radioactive decay happens at a constant rate regardless of exposure to air.","cn":"无论是否暴露在空气中，放射性衰变都会以恒定的速率发生。"}},{"en":"to be destroyed gradually by natural processes; to destroy something in this way","cn":"（使）腐烂，腐朽","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","ex":{"en":"decaying leaves/teeth/food","cn":"烂叶；蛀齿；腐烂食物"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"if a building or an area decays, its condition slowly becomes worse","cn":"（建筑、地方等）破败，衰落，衰败","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"decaying inner city areas","cn":"日益衰败的内城区"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to become less powerful and lose influence over people, society, etc.","cn":"（力量、影响等）衰弱，衰退，衰减","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"decaying standards of morality","cn":"日趋低下的道德标准"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(尸体或死去的植物）腐烂，腐朽，腐败;(牙齿）遭蛀蚀","en":"When something such as a dead body, a dead plant, or a tooth decays, it is gradually destroyed by a natural process.","ex":{"en":"The bodies buried in the fine ash slowly decayed","cn":"埋在灰烬里的尸体慢慢地腐烂了。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(社会、制度、机构等）衰败，衰退，衰落","en":"If something such as a society, system, or institution decays, it gradually becomes weaker or its condition gets worse.","ex":{"en":"Popular cinema seems to have decayed","cn":"大众电影似乎已经衰落了。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The smell of death and decay hung over the town.","cn":"城镇上空弥漫着死人和腐烂的气味。"},{"en":"The landlord had let the building fall into decay.","cn":"房东任由房子变得破烂不堪。"}]},"deep":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/deep__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deep__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"diːp","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"having a large distance from the top or surface to the bottom","cn":"深的；厚的","lab":"figurative","sc":"top to bottom","ex":{"en":"a deep hole/well/river","cn":"很深的洞／井／河"}},{"en":"having a large distance from the front edge to the furthest point inside","cn":"纵深的；宽的","sc":"front to back","ex":{"en":"a deep cut/wound","cn":"很深的划口／伤口"}},{"en":"used to describe or ask about the depth of something","cn":"有…深的","sc":"measurement","ex":{"en":"The water is only a few centimetres deep.","cn":"这水只有几厘米深。"}},{"en":"as far up or down as the point mentioned","cn":"远至…的；有…深的","sc":"-deep","ex":{"en":"The water was only waist-deep so I walked ashore.","cn":"水只有齐腰深，所以我涉水上了岸。"}},{"en":"in the number of rows mentioned, one behind the other","cn":"成…排的；有…层的","sc":"-deep","ex":{"en":"They were standing three-deep at the bar.","cn":"他们在吧台前站成三排。"}},{"en":"taking in or giving out a lot of air","cn":"深（呼吸）的","g":"[usually before noun]","sc":"breath/sigh","ex":{"en":"She took a deep breath.","cn":"她深深地吸了一口气。"}},{"en":"a person in a deep sleep is difficult to wake","cn":"酣睡的；沉睡的","sc":"sleep","ex":{"en":"She fell into a deep sleep.","cn":"她进入酣睡中。"}},{"en":"strong and dark","cn":"深的","sc":"colours","ex":{"en":"a rich deep red","cn":"浓重的深红色"}},{"en":"low","cn":"深沉的；低沉的","sc":"sounds","ex":{"en":"I heard his deep warm voice filling the room.","cn":"我听到他低沉暖人的话语在整个房间里回荡。"}},{"en":"strongly felt","cn":"剧烈的；强烈的","sc":"emotions","ex":{"en":"a very deep feeling of love","cn":"非常深厚的爱恋"}},{"en":"extreme or serious","cn":"极度的；严重的","sc":"serious","ex":{"en":"He's in deep trouble.","cn":"他陷入极度困境之中。"}},{"en":"showing great knowledge or understanding","cn":"渊博的；深刻的","sc":"knowledge","ex":{"en":"She had reached a deep understanding of the local culture.","cn":"她对本土文化有深入的了解。"}},{"en":"difficult to understand","cn":"难解","sc":"difficult to understand","ex":{"en":"This discussion's getting too deep for me.","cn":"这讨论越来越深奥，使我难以理解。"}},{"en":"fully involved in an activity or a state","cn":"专心；全神贯注；深陷","sc":"involved","ex":{"en":"to be deep in thought/conversation","cn":"陷入深思；专心谈话"}},{"en":"if a person is deep, they hide their real feelings and opinions","cn":"深沉的；摸不透的；城府深的","sc":"person","ex":{"en":"She's always been a deep one, trusting no one.","cn":"她这个人一直城府很深，对谁也不相信。"}},{"en":"to or from a position far down or across the field","cn":"远端的","sc":"in sport","ex":{"en":"a deep ball from Brown","cn":"布朗踢到球场远端的一脚球"}},{"en":"a long way below the surface of something or a long way inside or into something","cn":"深深地；在深处；至深处","lab":"figurative","ex":{"en":"Dig deeper!","cn":"再挖深点！"},"pos":"adverb"},{"en":"the sea","cn":"深海；海洋","g":"[singular]","lab":"literary","ex":{"en":"His body was committed to the deep (= he was buried at sea).","cn":"他的尸体被投入深海（=他被埋在海里）。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a deep part of something; the deepest part of something","cn":"深处；最深处","g":"[singular]","lab":"figurative","ex":{"en":"in the deep of night/winter (= in the middle of the night/of winter)","cn":"在深夜／隆冬"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(从上到下)深的，厚的","en":"If something is deep, it extends a long way down from the ground or from the top surface of something.","ex":{"en":"The water is very deep and mysterious-looking","cn":"水看上去幽深叵测。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(从前到后)深的，宽的","en":"A deep container, such as a cupboard, extends or measures a long distance from front to back.","ex":{"en":"The wardrobe was very deep.","cn":"这个衣柜很深。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"有…深的","en":"You use deep to talk or ask about how much something measures from the surface to the bottom, or from front to back.","ex":{"en":"I found myself in water only three feet deep","cn":"我发现脚下的水只有 3 英尺深。"}},{"pos":"ADV-GRADED 副词","cn":"深入地;在（或至）深处","en":"Deep in an area means a long way inside it","ex":{"en":"They were now deep inside rebel territory.","cn":"他们现在已深入叛军占领区。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(足球、网球等运动中球)纵深的，靠近对方端线的","en":"In sports such as football and tennis, a deep shot or pass is one that sends the ball a long way towards the end of the pitch or court.","ex":{"en":"...Steve Staunton's deep cross.","cn":"史蒂夫·斯汤顿的纵深横传"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"成…排地;有…层地","en":"If you say that things or people are two ,three, or four deep, you mean that there are two, three, or four rows or layers of them there.","ex":{"en":"A crowd three deep seemed paralysed by the images on these monitors","cn":"里里外外三层的人群看到显示屏上的画面似乎全都惊呆了。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"严重的;深切的;深厚的;深深的","en":"You use deep to emphasize the seriousness, strength, importance, or degree of something.","ex":{"en":"I had a deep admiration for Sartre","cn":"我对萨特怀有深深的敬意。"}},{"pos":"ADV-GRADED 副词","cn":"在内心深处;在心底","en":"If you experience or feel something deep inside you or deep down, you feel it very strongly even though you do not necessarily show it.","ex":{"en":"I kept reassuring them but deep in my heart I knew we had no hope","cn":"我一再安慰他们，但在内心深处我知道我们没有任何希望。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(睡眠)沉的，酣的","en":"If you are in a deep sleep, you are sleeping peacefully and it is difficult to wake you.","ex":{"en":"Una soon fell into a deep sleep.","cn":"尤娜很快便沉沉睡去。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"沉浸在…中的;专注于…的;埋头于…的","en":"If you are deep in thought or deep in conversation, you are concentrating very hard on what you are thinking or saying and are not aware of the things that are happening around you.","ex":{"en":"Abby had been so deep in thought that she had walked past her aunt's car without even seeing it","cn":"阿比沉浸在自己的思绪中，以至于从她姨妈的车边经过时都没有注意到。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(目光)锐利的，深邃的","en":"A deep look seems to see right into your mind.","ex":{"en":"Peter gave him a long deep look.","cn":"彼得深邃的目光长久地注视着他。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(呼吸或叹息)深重的，深长的","en":"A deep breath or sigh uses or fills the whole of your lungs.","ex":{"en":"Cal took a long, deep breath, struggling to control his own emotions","cn":"卡尔深长地吸了一口气，努力控制自己的情绪。"}},{"pos":"COMB in COLOUR 与颜色词构成的词","cn":"(颜色)深的，浓的","en":"You use deep to describe colours that are strong and fairly dark.","ex":{"en":"The sky was deep blue and starry","cn":"天空一片深蓝色，其间星光闪烁。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(声音)深沉的，低沉的","en":"A deep sound is low in pitch.","ex":{"en":"His voice was deep and mellow","cn":"他的声音深沉而柔和。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"（人）深沉的，内敛的","en":"If you describe someone as deep, you mean that they are quiet and reserved in a way that makes you think that they have good qualities such as intelligence or determination.","ex":{"en":"James is a very deep individual","cn":"詹姆斯是一个非常内敛的人。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(问题、文章等)重要的，严肃的，深刻的","en":"If you describe something such as a problem or a piece of writing as deep, you mean that it is important, serious, or complicated.","ex":{"en":"This is a very deep question","cn":"这是一个非常严肃的问题。"}},{"pos":"ADV-GRADED 副词","cn":"深陷(债务等中)","en":"If you are deep in debt, you have a lot of debts.","ex":{"en":"He is so deep in debt and desperate for money that he's apparently willing to say anything","cn":"他负债累累，急需要钱，很显然什么话都说得出来。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"海洋;大海","en":"The deep means the sea.","ex":{"en":"...a vast unfrequented pool, traversed by whales and creatures of the deep.","cn":"一个面积巨大、人迹罕至的水池，鲸和其他海洋动物穿游其间"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"在内心深处，在心底（知道）","en":"If you know something deep down or deep down inside, you know that it is true, but you are not always conscious of it or willing to admit it to yourself.","ex":{"en":"We knew deep down that we could do it","cn":"在内心深处，我们知道自己能够做到。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"深吸一口气(以使自己坚强自信)","en":"If you say that you took a deep breath before doing something dangerous or frightening, you mean that you tried to make yourself feel strong and confident.","ex":{"en":"I took a deep breath and went in.","cn":"我深吸一口气，然后走了进去。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"非常严重;极为强烈;根深蒂固","en":"If you say that something goes deep or runs deep, you mean that it is very serious or strong and is hard to change.","ex":{"en":"His anger and anguish clearly went deep","cn":"他的愤怒和痛苦显然是深切而强烈的。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"in at the deep end→see: ; in deep water→see: ;"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Junior hospital doctors are thrown in at the deep end in their first jobs.","cn":"医院的初级医生开始工作时会遇上未曾料到的困难。"},{"en":"I heard his deep warm voice filling the room.","cn":"我听到他低沉暖人的话语在整个房间里回荡。"}]},"demesne":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/demesne__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/demesne__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈmeɪn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"(in the past) land attached to a manor (= large house) that was kept by the owners for their own use","cn":"（旧时）领主自留地产"},{"en":"a region or large area of land","cn":"地区；地域","lab":"old use"}]}},"density":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/density__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/density__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdensəti","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the quality of being dense; the degree to which something is dense","cn":"密集；稠密；密度；浓度","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"The population density in this city is very high.","cn":"这座城市的人口密度很高。"}},{"en":"how thick a solid, liquid or gas is, measured by its mass per unit of volume","cn":"密度（固体、液体或气体单位体积的质量）","g":"[countable, uncountable]","lab":"physics","ex":{"en":"the density of a gas","cn":"一种气体的密度"}},{"en":"the amount of space available on a disk for recording data","cn":"密度（磁盘存储数据的可用空间）","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"computing"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"密度;稠密;密集","en":"Density is the extent to which something is filled or covered with people or things.","ex":{"en":"...a law which restricts the density of housing","cn":"限制房屋密集程度的法规"}},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"（物质或物体的）密度","en":"In science, the density of a substance or object is the relation of its mass or weight to its volume.","ex":{"en":"Jupiter's moon Io, whose density is 3.5 grams per cubic centimetre, is all rock.","cn":"密度为每立方厘米 3.5 克的木星卫星木卫一上遍布岩石。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"a high/double density floppy","cn":"高密度/双密度软盘"},{"en":"the density of a gas","cn":"一种气体的密度"}]},"determine":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/determine__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/determine__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈtɜːmɪn","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to discover the facts about something; to calculate something exactly","cn":"查明；测定；准确算出","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"An inquiry was set up to determine the cause of the accident.","cn":"已展开调查以确定事故原因。"}},{"en":"to make something happen in a particular way or be of a particular type","cn":"决定；形成；支配；影响","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"Rural voters in key states will determine the outcome of the election.","cn":"关键州的农村选民将决定选举结果。"}},{"en":"to officially decide and/or arrange something","cn":"确定；裁决；安排","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"A date for the meeting has yet to be determined.","cn":"会议日期尚待确定。"}},{"en":"to decide definitely to do something","cn":"决定，决心（做某事）","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","ex":{"en":"They determined to start early.","cn":"他们决定早点儿出发。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"是…的决定因素","en":"If a particular factor determines the nature of a thing or event, it causes it to be of a particular kind.","ex":{"en":"The size of the chicken pieces will determine the cooking time","cn":"鸡块的大小将决定烹饪时间的长短。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"确定;查明","en":"To determine a fact means to discover it as a result of investigation.","ex":{"en":"The investigation will determine what really happened","cn":"调查会查明到底发生了什么事情。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"决定;敲定","en":"If you determine something, you decide it or settle it.","ex":{"en":"The Baltic people have a right to determine their own future","cn":"波罗的海各国人民有权决定自己的未来。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"下决心;决意;决定","en":"If you determine to do something, you make a firm decision to do it.","ex":{"en":"He determined to rescue his two countrymen","cn":"他决意营救自己的两名同胞。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Upbringing plays an important part in determining a person's character.","cn":"后天培养对于一个人性格的形成起着重要作用。"},{"en":"Age and experience will be determining factors in our choice of candidate.","cn":"年龄和经验是我们选择候选人的决定因素。"}]},"demerit":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/demerit__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/demerit__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"diːˈmerɪt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a fault in something or a disadvantage of something","cn":"过失；缺点；短处","g":"[usually plural]","ex":{"en":"the merits and demerits of the scheme","cn":"这个方案的优缺点"}},{"en":"a mark on somebody’s school record showing that they have done something wrong","cn":"（学校给学生记的）过失分","lab":"North American English","ex":{"en":"You'll get three demerits if you're caught smoking on school grounds.","cn":"在校内抽烟一经发现将被记过失分三分。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"过失;缺点","en":"The demerits of something or someone are their faults or disadvantages.","ex":{"en":"...articles debating the merits and demerits of the three candidates.","cn":"就 3 位候选人的优缺点进行辩论的文章"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"You'll get three demerits if you're caught smoking on school grounds.","cn":"在校内抽烟一经发现将被记过失分三分。"},{"en":"the merits and demerits of the scheme","cn":"这个方案的优缺点"}]},"demanding":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/demanding__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/demanding__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈmɑːndɪŋ","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"needing a lot of skill, effort, etc.","cn":"需要高技能的；要求高的；费力的","ex":{"en":"The work is physically demanding.","cn":"这工作需要有很好的体力。"}},{"en":"expecting a lot of work or attention from others; not easily satisfied","cn":"要求极严的；苛求的；难满足的","ex":{"en":"a demanding boss/child","cn":"苛刻的老板；难满足的孩子"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"费时的;费力的;劳神的;要求很高的","en":"A demanding job or task requires a lot of your time, energy, or attention.","ex":{"en":"He found he could no longer cope with his demanding job","cn":"他发现自己已无力应对那份劳神费力的工作了。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"难伺候的;难取悦的;挑剔的;苛刻的","en":"People who are demanding are not easily satisfied or pleased.","ex":{"en":"Ricky was a very demanding child","cn":"里基是个非常难伺候的孩子。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The work is physically demanding.","cn":"这工作需要有很好的体力。"},{"en":"a demanding boss/child","cn":"苛刻的老板；难满足的孩子"}],"base":"demand"},"derisive":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/derisive__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/derisive__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈraɪsɪv","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"unkind and showing that you think somebody/something is silly","cn":"嘲笑的；嘲弄的；取笑的","ex":{"en":"She gave a short, derisive laugh.","cn":"她讥讽地笑了笑。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"嘲弄的;嘲笑的;侮蔑的","en":"A derisive noise, expression, or remark expresses contempt.","ex":{"en":"There was a short, derisive laugh.","cn":"有人短促、嘲弄地笑了一声。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"She gave a short, derisive laugh.","cn":"她讥讽地笑了笑。"},{"en":"derisive laughter","cn":"嘲讽的笑"}]},"dealt":{"lemma":"deal","media":{"uk":"media/uk/dealt__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/dealt__us_1.mp3"}},"define":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/define__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/define__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfaɪn","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to say or explain what the meaning of a word or phrase is","cn":"解释（词语的含义）；给…下定义","ex":{"en":"The term ‘normal’ is difficult to define.","cn":"“正常”这个词很难定义。"}},{"en":"to describe or show the nature or range of somebody/something","cn":"阐述；明确；界定","ex":{"en":"The goals of the project are clearly defined.","cn":"项目的目标定得很清晰。"}},{"en":"to make or establish the essential character or somebody/something","cn":"解释（词语的含义）；给…下定义","ex":{"en":"For some, the football club defines their identity.","cn":"对有些人来说，足球俱乐部定义了他们的身份。"}},{"en":"to show clearly a line, shape or edge","cn":"画出…的线条；描出…的外形；确定…的界线；界定","ex":{"en":"The mountain was sharply defined against the sky.","cn":"那座山在天空的衬托下显得轮廓分明。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"阐明;规定;限定;使明确","en":"If you define something, you show, describe, or state clearly what it is and what its limits are, or what it is like.","ex":{"en":"We were unable to define what exactly was wrong with him","cn":"我们说不清楚他到底哪里不对劲。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"给…下定义;解释","en":"If you define a word or expression, you explain its meaning, for example in a dictionary.","ex":{"en":"When people are asked 'What is intelligence?' they tend to reply: 'I don't know how to define it, but I can certainly recognize it when I see it.'","cn":"当被问及“智力是什么”的时候，人们往往会回答说：“我不知道该如何定义它，但我见到了肯定就能认得出。”"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The difficulty of a problem was defined in terms of how long it took to complete.","cn":"问题的难易度是以解决这个问题所花时间的长短而定的。"},{"en":"Life imprisonment is defined as 60 years under state law.","cn":"按照州法律终身监禁定义为 60 年。"}]},"destination":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/destination__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/destination__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdestɪˈneɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a place to which somebody/something is going or being sent","cn":"目的地；终点","ex":{"en":"popular tourist/holiday destinations like the Bahamas","cn":"像巴哈马那样深受大众喜爱的旅游／度假胜地"}},{"en":"a hotel, store, etc. that people will make a special trip to visit","cn":"作为目的地的（旅馆、商店、饭店等）","ex":{"en":"Sun Valley Lodge was the first destination ski resort in the US.","cn":"太阳谷酒店是美国第一个目的地滑雪度假区。"},"pos":"adjective"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"目的地;终点","en":"The destination of someone or something is the place to which they are going or being sent.","ex":{"en":"Spain is still our most popular holiday destination","cn":"西班牙仍是我们最喜爱的度假去处。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"popular holiday destinations like the Bahamas","cn":"像巴哈马那样深受大众喜爱的度假胜地"},{"en":"Our luggage was checked all the way through to our final destination.","cn":"我们的行李一直被托运到最终目的地。"}]},"desert":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/desert__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/desert__us_1.mp3","img":["media/ldoce/img/ldoce_066.png"]},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdezət","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a large area of land that has very little water and very few plants growing on it. Many deserts are covered by sand.","cn":"沙漠；荒漠；荒原","lab":"figurative","ex":{"en":"the Sahara Desert","cn":"撒哈拉大沙漠"}},{"en":"to leave somebody without help or support","cn":"抛弃，离弃，遗弃（某人）","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"She was deserted by her husband.","cn":"她被丈夫遗弃了。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to go away from a place and leave it empty","cn":"舍弃，离弃（某地方）","g":"[transitive, often passive]","ex":{"en":"The villages had been deserted.","cn":"这些村庄已经荒无人烟了。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to leave the armed forces without permission","cn":"擅离（部队）；逃走；开小差","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","ex":{"en":"Large numbers of soldiers deserted as defeat became inevitable.","cn":"战败已成定局，许多士兵开小差跑了。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to leave an organization or stop doing an activity, especially in a way that is considered bad and disloyal","cn":"背弃；脱离","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"Millions of voters are deserting the party.","cn":"数以百万计的选民正在抛弃该党。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"if a particular quality deserts you, it is not there when you need it","cn":"背离；使失望","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"Her courage seemed to desert her for a moment.","cn":"她一时间似乎失去了勇气。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"沙漠;荒漠","en":"A desert is a large area of land, usually in a hot region, where there is almost no water, rain, trees, or plants.","ex":{"en":"...the Sahara Desert.","cn":"撒哈拉大沙漠"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"枯燥乏味的地方（或境况）","en":"If you refer to a place or situation as a desert, you think it is bad for people because it is not interesting, exciting, or useful in any way.","ex":{"en":"They live in 12 high-rise apartment buildings that sit in a desert of concrete","cn":"他们居住的地方是坐落于一片钢筋水泥丛林中的12栋高层公寓楼。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"离弃，舍弃(某地)","en":"If people or animals desert a place, they leave it and it becomes empty.","ex":{"en":"Farmers are deserting their fields and coming here looking for jobs","cn":"小农场主正舍弃他们的土地，到这里来寻找工作。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"抛弃，遗弃(某人)","en":"If someone deserts you, they go away and leave you, and no longer help or support you.","ex":{"en":"Mrs Roding's husband deserted her years ago","cn":"罗丁太太的丈夫数年前抛弃了她。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"背弃;放弃;脱离","en":"If you desert something that you support, use, or are involved with, you stop supporting it, using it, or being involved with it.","ex":{"en":"The paper's price rise will encourage readers to desert in even greater numbers","cn":"报纸价格的上涨将导致更多的读者不再订阅。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"突然丧失(特质、技巧等)","en":"If a quality or skill that you normally have deserts you, you suddenly find that you do not have it when you need it or want it.","ex":{"en":"Even when he appeared to be depressed, a dry sense of humour never deserted him","cn":"即使在他看上去很沮丧的时候，他也从没有丧失过自己的冷面幽默。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"擅离(职守);（尤指从军队)开小差","en":"If someone deserts, or deserts a job, especially a job in the armed forces, they leave that job without permission.","ex":{"en":"He was a second-lieutenant in the army until he deserted","cn":"他在擅离部队之前是一名陆军少尉。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"应得的惩罚;报应","en":"If you say that someone has got their just deserts, you mean that they deserved the unpleasant things that have happened to them, because they did something bad.","ex":{"en":"At the end of the book the child's true identity is discovered, and the bad guys get their just deserts.","cn":"在书的结尾，那个孩子的真实身份大白于世，坏人则得到了应有的惩罚。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Large numbers of soldiers deserted as defeat became inevitable.","cn":"战败已成定局，许多士兵开小差跑了。"},{"en":"She felt betrayed by her husband's desertion.","cn":"她感到丈夫遗弃她辜负了她的心。"}]},"det":{"oxford":{"phon":"","pos":"abbreviation","senses":[{"en":"(in writing) detective","cn":"（书写形式）侦探","ex":{"en":"Det Insp (= Inspector) Cox","cn":"考克斯探长"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Det Insp (= Inspector) Cox","cn":"考克斯探长"}]},"delicacy":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/delicacy__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/delicacy__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdelɪkəsi","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the fact of being, or appearing to be, easy to damage or break","cn":"脆弱；娇嫩","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"the delicacy of the fabric","cn":"织物的精细脆弱"}},{"en":"the quality of being done carefully and gently","cn":"仔细；温柔","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"the delicacy of his touch","cn":"他那温柔的抚摸"}},{"en":"very careful behaviour in a difficult situation so that nobody is offended","cn":"周到；体贴","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"She handled the situation with great sensitivity and delicacy.","cn":"她慎重而周到地处理了这个情况。"}},{"en":"the fact that a situation is difficult and somebody may be easily offended","cn":"棘手；微妙","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"I need to talk to you about a matter of some delicacy.","cn":"我需要与你谈个有点棘手的问题。"}},{"en":"a type of food considered to be very special in a particular place","cn":"精美的食物；佳肴","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"local delicacies","cn":"当地的美味佳肴"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"娇美;精美;雅致;纤细","en":"Delicacy is the quality of being easy to break or harm, and refers especially to people or things that are attractive or graceful.","ex":{"en":"...the delicacy of a rose.","cn":"玫瑰的娇丽"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"微妙;棘手;难处理","en":"If you say that a situation or problem is of some delicacy, you mean that it is difficult to handle and needs careful and sensitive treatment.","ex":{"en":"There is a matter of some delicacy which I would like to discuss","cn":"有件有点儿棘手的事我想要商量一下。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"审慎;体贴;周到","en":"If someone handles a difficult situation with delicacy, they handle it very carefully, making sure that nobody is offended.","ex":{"en":"Both countries are behaving with rare delicacy","cn":"两个国家都表现出少有的谨慎。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"珍馐;佳肴","en":"A delicacy is a rare or expensive food that is considered especially nice to eat.","ex":{"en":"Smoked salmon was considered an expensive delicacy","cn":"熏鲑鱼被认为是一道昂贵的珍馐。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"She handled the situation with great sensitivity and delicacy.","cn":"她慎重而周到地处理了这个情况。"},{"en":"I need to talk to you about a matter of some delicacy.","cn":"我需要与你谈个有点棘手的问题。"}]},"depot":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/depot__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/depot__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdepəʊ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a place where large amounts of food, goods or equipment are stored","cn":"（大量物品的）贮藏处，仓库","ex":{"en":"an explosion at an arms depot","cn":"发生在军火库的爆炸"}},{"en":"a place where buses or other vehicles are kept and repaired","cn":"车库；修车厂","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"on its way back to the bus depot","cn":"回公共汽车站的途中"}},{"en":"a small station where trains or buses stop","cn":"火车小站；公共汽车小站","lab":"North American English","ex":{"en":"The bus depot is on Lincoln Avenue.","cn":"公共汽车站在林肯大街上。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"仓库;库房","en":"A depot is a place where large amounts of raw materials, equipment, arms, or other supplies are kept until they are needed.","ex":{"en":"...food depots.","cn":"食品仓库"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(停放公共汽车或火车头的)车库，停车场","en":"A depot is a large building or open area where buses or railway engines are kept when they are not being used."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"公共汽车站;火车站","en":"A depot is a bus station or railway station.","ex":{"en":"...a bus depot in Ozark, Alabama.","cn":"亚拉巴马州欧扎克市的一个公共汽车站"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"an arms depot","cn":"军械库"},{"en":"the company’s distribution depot","cn":"公司的发货仓库"}]},"detachment":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/detachment__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/detachment__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈtætʃmənt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the state of not being involved in something in an emotional or personal way","cn":"超然；超脱；冷漠","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"He answered with an air of detachment.","cn":"他回答时带着冷漠的神态。"}},{"en":"the state of not being influenced by other people or by your own feelings","cn":"公正；客观；独立","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"approving","ex":{"en":"In judging these issues a degree of critical detachment is required.","cn":"在裁决这些争议时须要有一定程度的公正判断力。"}},{"en":"a group of soldiers, ships, etc. sent away from a larger group, especially to do special duties","cn":"分遣队；支队；特遣小分队","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"a detachment of artillery","cn":"炮兵支队"}},{"en":"the act of detaching something; the process of being detached from something","cn":"拆卸；分离；分遣","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"to suffer detachment of the retina","cn":"出现视网膜脱落"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"超然;冷漠;冷静;客观","en":"Detachment is the feeling that you have of not being personally involved in something or of having no emotional interest in it.","ex":{"en":"...a doctor's professional detachment","cn":"医生职业性的冷静"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"分遣队;独立小分队","en":"A detachment is a group of soldiers who are sent away from the main group to do a special job.","ex":{"en":"...a detachment of marines.","cn":"海军陆战队独立小分队"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"In judging these issues a degree of critical detachment is required.","cn":"在裁决这些争议时须要有一定程度的公正判断力。"},{"en":"She felt a sense of detachment from what was going on.","cn":"她对眼前发生的事感到很超然。"}]},"descend":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/descend__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/descend__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈsend","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to come or go down from a higher to a lower level","cn":"下来；下去；下降","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"The plane began to descend.","cn":"飞机开始降落。"}},{"en":"to slope downwards","cn":"下斜；下倾","g":"[intransitive]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"At this point the path descends steeply.","cn":"小路从这里陡然而下。"}},{"en":"to arrive and begin to affect somebody/something","cn":"降临；来临","g":"[intransitive]","lab":"literary","ex":{"en":"Night descends quickly in the tropics.","cn":"热带地区天黑得快。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"下来;下降;走下","en":"If you descend or if you descend a staircase, you move downwards from a higher to a lower level.","ex":{"en":"Things are cooler and more damp as we descend to the cellar","cn":"当我们往下走去地窖时，四周愈见阴冷潮湿。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(情绪、气氛等)降临，笼罩","en":"When a mood or atmosphere descends on a place or on the people there, it affects them by spreading among them.","ex":{"en":"An uneasy calm descended on the area","cn":"一种令人不安的平静笼罩了该地区。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（大批人）突然到来，突然造访","en":"If a large group of people arrive to see you, especially if their visit is unexpected or causes you a lot of work, you can say that they have descended on you.","ex":{"en":"3,000 city officials descended on Capitol Hill to lobby for more money","cn":"3,000名市政官员齐聚国会山，为筹集更多的款项进行游说。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(夜幕、黄昏、黑暗等)降临","en":"When night, dusk, or darkness descends, it starts to get dark.","ex":{"en":"Darkness has now descended and the moon and stars shine hazily in the clear sky.","cn":"夜幕现在已经降临，晴朗的天空里月影婆娑，星光朦胧。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"降低身份;堕落;沦落","en":"If you say that someone descends to behaviour which you consider unacceptable, you are expressing your disapproval of the fact that they do it.","ex":{"en":"We're not going to descend to such methods","cn":"我们不会沦落到使用这种手段。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"陷入(糟糕境地)","en":"When you want to emphasize that the situation that someone is entering is very bad, you can say that they are descending into that situation.","ex":{"en":"He was ultimately overthrown and the country descended into chaos.","cn":"他最终被推翻，整个国家则陷入了混乱。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"They descended to the level of personal insults.","cn":"他们竟卑鄙到进行人身侮辱的地步。"},{"en":"He claims to be descended from a Spanish prince.","cn":"他声称是一位西班牙王子的后裔。"}]},"devastating":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdevəsteɪtɪŋ","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"causing a lot of damage and destroying things","cn":"破坏性极大的；毁灭性的","ex":{"en":"a devastating explosion/fire/cyclone","cn":"毁灭性的爆炸／火灾／旋风"}},{"en":"that shocks or upsets you very much","cn":"令人震惊的；骇人的；令人悲痛的","ex":{"en":"It was then that she heard the devastating news that her father was dead.","cn":"就在那时，她惊悉父亲去世的噩耗。"}},{"en":"impressive and powerful","cn":"给人印象深刻的；令人钦佩的；强有力的","ex":{"en":"his devastating performance in the 100 metres","cn":"他在 100 米赛跑中的惊人表现"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"毁灭性的;极具破坏力的","en":"If you describe something as devastating, you are emphasizing that it is very harmful or damaging.","ex":{"en":"The city of Ormac took the full force of the winds and devastating floods","cn":"奥马克城受到了狂风和灾难性洪水的猛烈袭击。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"令人极为震惊的;使人极度不安的;可怕的","en":"You can use devastating to emphasize that something is very shocking, upsetting, or terrible.","ex":{"en":"The diagnosis was devastating. She had cancer.","cn":"诊断结果令人震惊：她得了癌症。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"极其引人注目的;令人印象深刻的","en":"You can use devastating to emphasize that something or someone is very impressive.","ex":{"en":"...a devastating display of galloping and jumping","cn":"令人难忘的骑马飞奔和跳跃表演"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/devastating__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/devastating__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"It will be a devastating blow to the local community if the factory closes.","cn":"如果这家工厂倒闭，将给当地居民以毁灭性的打击。"},{"en":"Oil spills are having a devastating effect on coral reefs in the ocean.","cn":"石油泄漏对海洋里的珊瑚礁有着毁灭性影响。"}]},"demeaning":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/demeaning__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/demeaning__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈmiːnɪŋ","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"putting somebody in a position that does not give them the respect that they should have","cn":"降低身份的；失去尊严的","ex":{"en":"He found it demeaning to work for his former employee.","cn":"他觉得为自己以前的雇员工作有失体面。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"降低身份的;贬低的;贬损的","en":"Something that is demeaning makes people have less respect for the person who is treated in that way, or who does that thing.","ex":{"en":"...demeaning sexist comments","cn":"侮辱性的性别歧视言论"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He found it demeaning to work for his former employee.","cn":"他觉得为自己以前的雇员工作有失体面。"},{"en":"I refuse to do demeaning work.","cn":"我拒绝做有失身份的工作。"}]},"demolition":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"(建筑物的)摧毁，拆毁，拆除","en":"The demolition of a building is the act of deliberately destroying it, often in order to build something else in its place.","ex":{"en":"The project required the total demolition of the old bridge","cn":"该项目要求将老桥完全拆毁。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(体育运动等中的)大败，击溃","en":"The demolition of a team or opponent is their defeat by a great amount.","ex":{"en":"...Lazio's impressive 3-1 demolition of Inter Milan.","cn":"拉齐奥队以 3 比 1 大比分击败国际米兰队"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/demolition__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/demolition__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"His speech did a very effective demolition job on the government's proposals.","cn":"他的发言非常成功地驳倒了政府的提案。"},{"en":"The whole row of houses is scheduled for demolition.","cn":"整排房子均预定拆除。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdeməˈlɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the act of pulling or knocking down a building","cn":"拆毁，拆除（建筑物）","g":"[uncountable, countable]","ex":{"en":"The whole row of houses is scheduled for demolition.","cn":"整排房子均列入拆除计划。"}},{"en":"the act of showing that an idea or theory is completely wrong","cn":"推翻，驳倒（观点或理论）","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"His speech did a very effective demolition job on the government's proposals.","cn":"他的发言非常有力地驳倒了政府的提案。"}},{"en":"the act of defeating somebody easily and completely","cn":"轻易而彻底地打败","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"Ferguson completed the demolition with a fifth goal 13 minutes from time.","cn":"距离比赛结束还有 13 分钟时，弗格森攻入第五个进球，完成了比赛。"}}]}},"debit":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/debit__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/debit__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdebɪt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a written note in a bank account or other financial record of a sum of money owed or spent","cn":"借记；借方；收方","lab":"figurative","ex":{"en":"on the debit side of an account","cn":"账户的借方"}},{"en":"a sum of money taken from a bank account","cn":"借项","ex":{"en":"The total debits on the account were £2 000 last month.","cn":"上月账户中的借方总额为 2 000 英镑。"}},{"en":"when a bank debits an account or debits money from an account, it takes money from the account","cn":"（从银行账户）扣除；记入（账户）的借方；借记","lab":"informal","ex":{"en":"The money will be debited from your account each month.","cn":"这笔钱将逐月从你的账户中扣除。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"记入（账户）的借方","en":"When your bank debits your account, money is taken from it and paid to someone else.","ex":{"en":"We will always confirm the revised amount to you in writing before debiting your account.","cn":"在记入您账户的借方之前，我们总是会就发生变动的数额书面通知您。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(银行账户的)借记，借入","en":"A debit is a record of the money taken from your bank account, for example when you write a cheque.","ex":{"en":"The total of debits must balance the total of credits.","cn":"借记总额必须与贷记总额相平衡。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"( figurative ) On the debit side (= a negative result will be that) the new shopping centre will increase traffic problems.","cn":"负面影响是新购物中心会使交通问题加剧。"},{"en":"The money will be debited from your account each month.","cn":"这笔钱将逐月记入你账户的借方。"}]},"despite":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/despite__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/despite__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈspaɪt","pos":"preposition","senses":[{"en":"used to show that something happened or is true although something else might have happened to prevent it","cn":"即使；尽管","ex":{"en":"Her voice was shaking despite all her efforts to control it.","cn":"尽管她竭尽全力控制自己，声音仍然在颤抖。"}},{"en":"used to show that somebody did not intend to do the thing mentioned","cn":"尽管（自己）不愿意","ex":{"en":"He had to laugh despite himself.","cn":"他不想笑，但没法不笑。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"尽管;虽然","en":"You use despite to introduce a fact which makes the other part of the sentence surprising.","ex":{"en":"Despite a thorough investigation, no trace of Dr Southwell has been found","cn":"尽管进行了彻底的调查，还是没有发现索思韦尔博士的任何踪迹。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"不由自主;情不自禁","en":"If you do something despite yourself you do it although you did not really intend or expect to.","ex":{"en":"Despite myself, Harry's remarks had caused me to stop and reflect.","cn":"哈里的话让我不由自主地停下来细想。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Her voice was shaking despite all her efforts to control it.","cn":"尽管她竭尽全力控制自己，声音仍然在颤抖。"},{"en":"Despite applying for hundreds of jobs, he is still out of work.","cn":"尽管他申请了数百个工作，但仍然在失业中。"}]},"depended":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpend","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"according to","cn":"视乎；决定于"},{"en":"used to say that you are not certain about sth because other things have to be considered","cn":"那得看情况"}]}},"development":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/development__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/development__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈveləpmənt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the steady growth of something so that it becomes more advanced, stronger, etc.","cn":"发展；发育；成长；壮大","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"growth","ex":{"en":"a baby’s development in the womb","cn":"胎儿在子宫内的发育"}},{"en":"the growth of the economy of a country or region through increased business activity","cn":"（经济的）发展","lab":"economics","sc":"growth","ex":{"en":"Increased tourism will promote job creation and economic development.","cn":"旅游业的增长将促进创造就业机会和经济发展。"}},{"en":"the process of producing or creating something new or more advanced; a new or advanced product or idea","cn":"开发；研制；研制成果；开发创意","g":"[uncountable, countable]","sc":"new product or idea","ex":{"en":"the development of new technology","cn":"新技术的开发"}},{"en":"a new event or stage that is likely to affect what happens in a continuing situation","cn":"（新的）发展势态，进展情况，发展阶段","g":"[countable, usually plural]","sc":"new event","ex":{"en":"Have there been any further developments?","cn":"有新的进展吗？"}},{"en":"a piece of land with new buildings on it","cn":"新建住宅区；新开发区","g":"[countable]","sc":"new buildings","ex":{"en":"I live in a brand-new housing development.","cn":"我住在一个全新的住宅开发区。"}},{"en":"the process of using an area of land, especially to make a profit by building on it, etc.","cn":"（尤指房地产的）开发","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"new buildings","ex":{"en":"He bought the land for development.","cn":"他买了这块地准备开发。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"发展;成长;发育;生长;形成","en":"Development is the gradual growth or formation of something.","ex":{"en":"...an ideal system for studying the development of the embryo","cn":"研究胎儿发育过程的理想方法"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(企业、行业等的)发展，扩展，壮大","en":"Development is the growth of something such as a business or an industry.","ex":{"en":"Education is central to a country's economic development","cn":"教育对一个国家的经济发展至关重要。"}},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"研制;开发","en":"Development is the process or result of making a basic design gradually better and more advanced.","ex":{"en":"We are spending $850m on research and development.","cn":"我们在研发上的投入是 8.5 亿美元。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(地区的)发展;(土地、水域的)开发","en":"Development is the process of making an area of land or water more useful or profitable.","ex":{"en":"The talks will focus on economic development of the region.","cn":"会谈将着重讨论该地区的经济发展。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（事态的）发展，进展，新情况","en":"A development is an event or incident which has recently happened and is likely to have an effect on the present situation.","ex":{"en":"Police said there had been a significant development in the case.","cn":"警方说此案已经有了重大进展。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"新建住宅区;新开发的楼盘","en":"A development is an area of houses or buildings which have been built by property developers."}]},"examples":[{"en":"This piece of equipment is an exciting new development.","cn":"这台设备是一项振奋人心的最新研究成果。"},{"en":"the development of basic skills such as literacy and numeracy","cn":"诸如识字与识数等基本技能的发展"}]},"developing":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/developing__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/developing__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈveləpɪŋ","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"poor, and trying to make its industry and economic system more advanced","cn":"发展中的","ex":{"en":"developing countries/nations/economies","cn":"发展中国家／经济体"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(国家或地区)发展中的","en":"If you talk about developing countries or the developing world, you mean the countries or the parts of the world that are poor and have few industries.","ex":{"en":"In the developing world cigarette consumption is increasing.","cn":"在发展中国家，香烟的消费量正在上升。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"developing countries/nations/economies","cn":"发展中国家/经济体"},{"en":"poverty and hunger in the developing world","cn":"发展中国家存在的贫困和饥饿"}],"base":"develop"},"depend":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpend","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"according to","cn":"视乎；决定于"},{"en":"used to say that you are not certain about sth because other things have to be considered","cn":"那得看情况"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"取决(于);有赖(于)","en":"If you say that one thing depends on another, you mean that the first thing will be affected or determined by the second.","ex":{"en":"The cooking time needed depends on the size of the potato","cn":"所需的烹饪时间取决于土豆的大小。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"依靠;依赖","en":"If you depend on someone or something, you need them in order to be able to survive physically, financially, or emotionally.","ex":{"en":"They may hate what he does but their survival depends on him","cn":"他们或许讨厌他的营生，但他们要想活下来必须依靠他。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"指望;信赖","en":"If you can depend on a person, organization, or law, you know that they will support you or help you when you need them.","ex":{"en":"'You can depend on me,' Cross assured him.","cn":"“你可以信赖我，”克罗斯向他保证。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"视情形而定;看情况","en":"You use depend in expressions such as it depends to indicate that you cannot give a clear answer to a question because the answer will be affected or determined by other factors.","ex":{"en":"'But how long can you stay in the house?' – 'I don't know. It depends.'","cn":"“但你能在这所房子里呆多久呢？”——“我不知道，这要看情况。”"}},{"pos":"PREP-PHRASE 短语介词","cn":"取决于;根据;由…决定","en":"You use depending on when you are saying that something varies according to the circumstances mentioned.","ex":{"en":"I tend to have a different answer, depending on the family","cn":"根据家庭的不同，我往往会给出不同的答案。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/depend__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/depend__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"‘Your job sounds fun.’ ‘It depends what you mean by ‘fun’.’ “","cn":"你的工作听起来很有乐趣。” “这就要看你说的‘乐趣’是什么意思了。”"},{"en":"Starting salary varies from £26 000 to £30 500, depending on experience.","cn":"起薪为 26 000 至 30 500 英镑不等，依个人经验而定。"}]},"den":{"oxford":{"phon":"den","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the hidden home of some types of wild animal","cn":"兽穴；兽窝","ex":{"en":"a bear’s/lion’s den","cn":"熊的／狮子的洞穴"}},{"en":"a place where people meet in secret, especially for some illegal activity","cn":"窝点（尤指非法活动秘密聚会处）","lab":"disapproving","ex":{"en":"a den of thieves","cn":"贼窝"}},{"en":"a room in a house where people go to relax, watch television, etc.","cn":"休息室","lab":"North American English"},{"en":"a room in a house where a person can work or study without being interrupted","cn":"书斋；书房","lab":"British English, old-fashioned, informal，，，，","ex":{"en":"He would often retire to his den.","cn":"他往往躲在自己的书房里。"}},{"en":"a secret place, often made roughly with walls and a roof, where children play","cn":"（儿童的）隐蔽玩耍处","ex":{"en":"They made themselves a den in the woods.","cn":"他们在树林里为自己搭了个窝，在里面玩。"}},{"en":"a group of Cub Scouts","cn":"（幼年童子军）小组，小队","lab":"North American English"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(狮子、狐狸等野生动物的)兽穴，兽窝","en":"A den is the home of certain types of wild animals such as lions or foxes."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(家里用来学习、工作或从事业余爱好的)书房，私室","en":"Your den is a quiet room in your house where you can go to study, work, or carry on a hobby without being disturbed."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(通常指为了从事非法活动的)秘密聚集处，窝点，巢穴","en":"A den is a secret place where people meet, usually for a dishonest purpose.","ex":{"en":"I could provide you with the addresses of at least three illegal drinking dens.","cn":"我可以为你提供至少 3 处非法饮酒窝点的地址。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(某一不良行为或非法活动的猖獗)场所，渊薮","en":"If you describe a place as a den of a particular type of bad or illegal behaviour, you mean that a lot of that type of behaviour goes on there.","ex":{"en":"...the one-bedroomed flat that was to become his den of savage debauchery.","cn":"即将成为他野蛮放荡之所的一居室公寓"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/den__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/den__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"They made themselves a den in the woods.","cn":"他们在树林里为自己搭了个窝，在里面玩。"},{"en":"He thought of New York as a den of iniquity.","cn":"他把纽约视为罪恶的渊薮。"}]},"demurely":{"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"quiet, serious, and well-behaved – used especially about women in the past","cn":""},{"en":"demure clothes do not show much of a woman’s body","cn":""}]},"examples":[{"en":"Old photos of Maggie show her young and demure.","cn":"","src":"ld"},{"en":"a demure white dress","cn":"","src":"ld"}],"media":{"uk":"media/uk/demurely__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/demurely__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈmjʊəli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"in a quiet and serious way that does not attract attention","cn":"（尤指女性表现）端庄地，文静地，安静地","ex":{"en":"‘I’ll think about it,’ she said demurely.","cn":"“我会考虑一下。”她严肃地说。"}}]}},"defeat":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/defeat__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/defeat__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfiːt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to win against somebody in a war, competition, sports game, etc.","cn":"击败；战胜","ex":{"en":"He defeated the champion in three sets.","cn":"他三盘击败了冠军。"}},{"en":"to stop something from being successful","cn":"使失败；阻挠；挫败","ex":{"en":"They are united in their determination to defeat global terrorism.","cn":"他们团结一致，决心战胜全球恐怖主义。"}},{"en":"if something defeats you, you cannot understand it","cn":"使困惑；难住","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"The instruction manual completely defeated me.","cn":"这操作指南把我完全弄糊涂了。"}},{"en":"failure to win or to be successful","cn":"失败；战败；挫败","g":"[uncountable, countable]","ex":{"en":"The party faces defeat in the election.","cn":"这个党面临选举失败。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"the act of winning a victory over somebody/something","cn":"击败；战胜","g":"[countable, usually singular]","ex":{"en":"The army inflicted a heavy defeat on rebel forces.","cn":"军队重挫叛军。"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"击败;战胜","en":"If you defeat someone, you win a victory over them in a battle, game, or contest.","ex":{"en":"His guerrillas defeated the colonial army in 1954","cn":"1954 年他领导的游击队打败了殖民军队。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"否决(提案或动议)","en":"If a proposal or motion in a debate is defeated, more people vote against it than for it.","ex":{"en":"The proposal was defeated by just one vote.","cn":"该提案仅以一票之差被否决。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(任务或问题)难住，难倒","en":"If a task or a problem defeats you, it is so difficult that you cannot do it or solve it.","ex":{"en":"There were times when the challenges of writing such a huge novel almost defeated her.","cn":"有些时候，创作如此宏大的一部小说所面临的挑战几乎把她给难倒了。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"挫败(行动或计划);使落空","en":"To defeat an action or plan means to cause it to fail.","ex":{"en":"The navy played a limited but significant role in defeating the rebellion","cn":"海军在平息这场叛乱的过程中起到了有限但却十分重要的作用。"}},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"战败;失利;失败","en":"Defeat is the experience of being beaten in a battle, game, or contest, or of failing to achieve what you wanted to.","ex":{"en":"The most important thing is not to admit defeat until you really have to","cn":"最重要的是不到万不得已绝不要认输。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Staying late at the office to discuss shorter working hours rather defeats the object of the exercise!","cn":"迟迟待在办公室讨论缩短工作时间恰恰是在阻挠这一目标的实现！"},{"en":"The world champion has only had two defeats in 20 fights.","cn":"这个世界冠军在 20 场赛事中只败过两场。"}]},"defending":{"lemma":"defend"},"desk":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/desk__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/desk__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"desk","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a piece of furniture like a table, often with drawers (= parts like boxes in it with handles on the front for pulling them open), that you sit at to read, write, work, etc.","cn":"书桌；写字台；办公桌","ex":{"en":"I spend all day sitting at a desk.","cn":"我一整天都坐在桌旁。"}},{"en":"a place where you can get information or be served at an airport, a hotel, etc.","cn":"（机场、旅馆等的）问讯处，服务台","ex":{"en":"There was a long queue at the check-in desk.","cn":"登记处排起了长队。"}},{"en":"an office at a newspaper, television company, etc. that deals with a particular subject","cn":"（报社、电视台等的）办公处，部，室，组","ex":{"en":"the sports desk","cn":"体育部"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"书桌;写字台;办公桌","en":"A desk is a table, often with drawers, which you sit at to write or work."},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"(宾馆、医院、机场等的)服务台，问询台","en":"The place in a hotel, hospital, airport, or other building where you check in or obtain information is referred to as a particular desk .","ex":{"en":"I spoke to the girl on the reception desk","cn":"我跟服务台的女孩说了一下。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"(广播公司、报社、杂志社等的)部，室，组","en":"A particular department of a broadcasting company, or of a newspaper or magazine company, can be referred to as a particular desk .","ex":{"en":"Let our news desk know as quickly as possible on 414 3926","cn":"请尽快拨打电话 4143926 通知我们的新闻部。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He used to be a pilot but now he has a desk job.","cn":"他曾是飞行员，但现在做办公室工作。"},{"en":"the check-in desk （","cn":"机场）验票领取登机卡处"}]},"devil":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/devil__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/devil__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdevl","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the most powerful evil being","cn":"魔王；撒旦","ex":{"en":"belief in the Devil","cn":"对魔鬼的信仰"}},{"en":"an evil spirit","cn":"魔鬼；恶魔","ex":{"en":"They believed she was possessed by devils.","cn":"他们认为她是魔鬼附身。"}},{"en":"a person who behaves badly, especially a child","cn":"淘气鬼；冒失鬼；调皮鬼","lab":"informal","ex":{"en":"a naughty little devil","cn":"小淘气鬼"}},{"en":"used to talk about somebody and to emphasize an opinion that you have of them","cn":"（强调对某人的看法）人，家伙","lab":"old-fashioned, informal，，","ex":{"en":"I miss the old devil, now that he's gone.","cn":"老家伙这一走，我还真想他。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-PROPER 专有名词","cn":"(犹太教、基督教和伊斯兰教中的)魔王，撒旦","en":"In Judaism, Christianity, and Islam, the Devil is the most powerful evil spirit."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"魔鬼;恶魔","en":"A devil is an evil spirit.","ex":{"en":"...the idea of angels with wings and devils with horns and hoofs.","cn":"天使长着翅膀、魔鬼长着角和蹄这样的观念"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(用于强调)家伙，人","en":"You can use devil to emphasize the way you feel about someone. For example, if you call someone a poor devil, you are saying that you feel sorry for them. You can call someone you are fond of but who sometimes annoys or irritates you an old devil or a little devil .","ex":{"en":"I felt sorry for Blake, poor devil","cn":"我替布莱克感到难过，这个可怜的家伙。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"淘气鬼;冒失鬼","en":"If you refer to someone as a devil, you mean that they do not behave very well but you like them and are not angry with them.","ex":{"en":"'I think he was a bit of a devil,' Constance said.","cn":"“我想他有点儿淘气，”康斯坦丝说道。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"(用于强调)极其讨厌（或糟糕、麻烦）的","en":"Devil can be used to emphasize what you think about someone or something. For example, if you say that someone is a devil of a nuisance, you mean that they are very annoying. If you say that something is a devil of a problem, you mean that it is a very difficult problem.","ex":{"en":"He was always a devil of a nuisance","cn":"他总是极讨人厌。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"宁可跟熟识的魔鬼打交道(也比跟未知的魔鬼打交道好)","en":"If you say better the devil you know or better the devil you know than the devil you don't know, you mean that you would prefer to have contact with or do business with a person you already know, even though you don't like them, than with a person you don't know."},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"(用于强调)需煞费苦心（做），要大费周折（做）","en":"If you say that you had the devil's own job to do something or that you had a devil of a job doing something, you are emphasizing that it was difficult to do it.","ex":{"en":"We had the devil's own job to persuade him to take part.","cn":"我们说服他参加可费了一番周折。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"拼命地;竭力地;（开车）飞快地","en":"If you say that someone does something like the devil, you are emphasizing that they put a lot of effort into it. If you say that someone drives like the devil, you are emphasizing that they drive very fast.","ex":{"en":"He drives himself on, working like the devil from seven in the morning until midnight","cn":"他不断敦促自己，从早上 7 点一直拼命工作到午夜。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"落后者遭殃(形容或评论人人都只考虑自己而不顾别人)","en":"You can say the devil take the hindmost to describe or comment on a situation you disapprove of because people do only what is best for themselves without thinking about other people.","ex":{"en":"Every one for himself and the devil take the hindmost.","cn":"人人都只考虑自己，谁落后谁倒霉。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"进退维谷;左右为难","en":"If you say that you are between the devil and the deep blue sea, you mean that you are in a difficult situation where you have to choose between two equally unpleasant courses of action."},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"出卖灵魂;违背良心","en":"If you say that someone has sold their soul to the devil, you mean that you disapprove of them because they have done something that you think is not right in order to get what they want."},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"说曹操，曹操到","en":"People say speak of the devil, or in British English talk of the devil, if someone they have just been talking about appears unexpectedly.","ex":{"en":"Well, talk of the devil!","cn":"呵，说曹操，曹操就到！"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"(用于强调)究竟,到底","en":"When you want to emphasize how annoyed or surprised you are, you can use an expression such as what the devil ,how the devil, or why the devil .","ex":{"en":"'What the devil's the matter?'","cn":"“究竟出了什么事？”"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"She blamed the crimes on the local jobless teenagers. ‘The devil makes work for idle hands,’ she would say.","cn":"她认为那些违法活动是当地的无业青少年所为，总是说：“人一闲，惹麻烦”。"},{"en":"Well, speak of the devil — here's Alice now!","cn":"嗬，说曹操，曹操就到 — 瞧，艾丽斯这就来啦！"}]},"definition":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/definition__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/definition__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdefɪˈnɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an explanation of the meaning of a word or phrase, especially in a dictionary","cn":"（尤指词典里的词或短语的）定义；释义","g":"[countable, uncountable]","ex":{"en":"The dictionary provides clear, simple definitions.","cn":"该词典的释义简单明了。"}},{"en":"what an idea means","cn":"定义；含义","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"What's your definition of happiness?","cn":"你对幸福的定义是什么？"}},{"en":"the act of saying what a word or an idea means","cn":"定义；释义；解释","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"The term ‘partner’ requires careful definition.","cn":"“伴侣”一词需要仔细定义。"}},{"en":"the quality of being clear and easy to see; the ability of a device to give clear images","cn":"清晰度","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"The clarity and definition of the images are excellent.","cn":"图像的清晰度极佳。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(尤指词典中给出的)定义，释义","en":"A definition is a statement giving the meaning of a word or expression, especially in a dictionary.","ex":{"en":"There is no general agreement on a standard definition of intelligence","cn":"“智力”一词目前还没有一个普遍认可的标准释义。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"清晰;分明;明确","en":"Definition is the quality of being clear and distinct.","ex":{"en":"Give your brows extra definition with Outdoor Girl's Eyebrow Pencil in Brown","cn":"用“户外女孩”品牌的棕色眉笔更加清晰地勾勒出眉形。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Neighbours by definition live close by (= this is what being a neighbour means).","cn":"按照释义，“邻居”就是住在邻近地方的人。"},{"en":"The definition of the digital TV pictures is excellent.","cn":"数字电视图像的清晰度很高。"}]},"decimal":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdesɪml","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"based on or counted in tens or tenths","cn":"十进位的；小数的","ex":{"en":"the decimal system","cn":"十进制"}},{"en":"a fraction (= a number less than one) that is shown as a point followed by the number of tenths, hundredths, etc.","cn":"小数","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"The decimal 0.61 stands for 61 hundredths.","cn":"小数 0.61 代表 61%。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"the system of numbers that counts in tens or tenths","cn":"十进制","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"The computer converts the data from decimal to binary.","cn":"计算机把数据从十进制转换成二进制。"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"十进位的","en":"A decimal system involves counting in units of ten.","ex":{"en":"...the decimal system of metric weights and measures","cn":"公制度量衡的十进制"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"小数","en":"A decimal is a fraction that is written in the form of a dot followed by one or more numbers which represent tenths, hundredths, and so on: for example .5, .51, .517.","ex":{"en":"...simple math concepts, such as decimals and fractions.","cn":"简单的数学概念，如小数和分数"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/decimal__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/decimal__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The decimal 0.61 stands for 61 hundredths.","cn":"小数 0.61 代表 61%。"},{"en":"the decimal system","cn":"十进制"}]},"desires":{"lemma":"desire","media":{"uk":"media/uk/desire__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/desire__us_1.mp3"}},"defect":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdiːfekt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a fault in something or in the way it has been made that means that it is not perfect","cn":"缺点；缺陷；毛病","ex":{"en":"a defect in the glass","cn":"玻璃杯的缺陷"}},{"en":"a physical problem with part of somebody’s body or the way that it works","cn":"生理缺陷;生理障碍","lab":"sometimes offensive","ex":{"en":"a speech defect","cn":"言语缺陷"}},{"en":"to leave a political party, country, etc. to join another that is considered to be an enemy","cn":"背叛；叛变；投敌","ex":{"en":"A number of writers and musicians defected from the Soviet Union to the West in the 1960s.","cn":"20 世纪 60 年代，许多作家和音乐家从苏联叛逃到西方。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"缺点;缺陷;毛病;瑕疵","en":"A defect is a fault or imperfection in a person or thing.","ex":{"en":"He was born with a hearing defect.","cn":"他患有先天性听力缺损。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"叛逃;背叛;变节;倒戈","en":"If you defect, you leave your country, political party, or other group, and join an opposing country, party, or group.","ex":{"en":"He tried to defect to the West last year","cn":"去年他试图叛逃到西方。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/defect__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/defect__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"There have been several defections from the ruling party.","cn":"执政党已有好几位党员倒戈。"},{"en":"a defect in the glass","cn":"玻璃杯的缺陷"}]},"despise":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈspaɪz","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to dislike and have no respect for somebody/something","cn":"鄙视；蔑视；看不起","ex":{"en":"She despised gossip in any form.","cn":"她对任何形式的流言蜚语都嗤之以鼻。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"鄙视;藐视;看不起","en":"If you despise something or someone, you dislike them and have a very low opinion of them.","ex":{"en":"I can never, ever forgive him. I despise him","cn":"我永远不会原谅他。我鄙视他。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/despise__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/despise__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"She despised gossip in any form.","cn":"她对任何形式的流言蜚语都嗤之以鼻。"},{"en":"He despised himself for being so cowardly.","cn":"他为自己如此怯懦而自惭形秽。"}]},"device":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/device__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/device__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈvaɪs","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an object or a piece of equipment that has been designed to do a particular job","cn":"装置；仪器；器具；设备","ex":{"en":"a tracking/recording/listening device","cn":"跟踪／录音／监听设备"}},{"en":"a piece of computer equipment, especially a small one such as a smartphone","cn":"（智能手机等）电子设备；（小型）智能设备","ex":{"en":"You can store thousands of photos on your device.","cn":"你可以在设备上存储数千张照片。"}},{"en":"a bomb or weapon that will explode","cn":"炸弹；爆炸性武器；爆炸装置","ex":{"en":"A powerful device exploded outside the station.","cn":"一枚威力巨大的炸弹在车站外爆炸了。"}},{"en":"a method of doing something that produces a particular result or effect","cn":"手段；策略；方法；技巧","ex":{"en":"Targeted advertising on social media is very successful as a marketing device.","cn":"作为一种营销手段，社交媒体上的定向广告非常成功。"}},{"en":"a plan or trick that is used to get something that somebody wants","cn":"花招；计谋；诡计","ex":{"en":"The report was a device used to hide rather than reveal problems.","cn":"这份报告不是揭露问题而是耍花招掩盖问题。"}},{"en":"a form of words that is intended to produce a particular effect in speech or writing","cn":"手段；策略；方法；技巧","ex":{"en":"a rhetorical device","cn":"修辞手法"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"装置;设备;器具;仪器","en":"A device is an object that has been invented for a particular purpose, for example for recording or measuring something.","ex":{"en":"...an electronic device that protects your vehicle 24 hours a day.","cn":"24小时保护车辆的电子装置"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"手段;策略;方法;技巧","en":"A device is a method of achieving something.","ex":{"en":"They claim that military spending is used as a device for managing the economy.","cn":"他们声称军费开支是用来作为调控经济的手段的。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"听任…自便;让…自行发展;不去管","en":"If you leave someone to their own devices, you leave them alone to do as they wish.","ex":{"en":"Left to his own devices, Osborn is a fluent — and often original — guitarist.","cn":"任其自由发挥时，奥斯本是一个弹奏流畅、常常富有创意的吉他手。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Sending advertising by email is very successful as a marketing device.","cn":"作为一种营销手段，用电子邮件发送广告是非常成功的。"},{"en":"The report was a device used to hide rather than reveal problems.","cn":"这份报告不是揭露问题而是为掩盖问题而耍的花招。"}]},"desolation":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/desolation__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/desolation__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdesəˈleɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the feeling of being very lonely and unhappy","cn":"孤寂；悲哀；忧伤","ex":{"en":"Her death left him with a terrible sense of desolation.","cn":"她的去世使他甚感孤寂。"}},{"en":"the state of a place that is badly damaged or destroyed and offers no joy or hope to people","cn":"废墟；荒芜；荒凉","ex":{"en":"a scene of utter desolation","cn":"满目疮痍的景象"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"凄凉;孤寂;悲怆;绝望","en":"Desolation is a feeling of great unhappiness and hopelessness.","ex":{"en":"Kozelek expresses his sense of desolation absolutely without self-pity.","cn":"科泽莱克不带一丝顾影自怜地表达了自己的凄凉悲怆之感。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"荒凉;荒芜;荒废;满目疮痍","en":"If you refer to desolation in a place, you mean that it is empty and frightening, for example because it has been destroyed by a violent force or army.","ex":{"en":"We looked out upon a scene of desolation and ruin","cn":"我们放眼望去，眼前是一片荒凉的废墟。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"a scene of utter desolation","cn":"满目疮痍的景象"}]},"dedication":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdedɪˈkeɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the hard work and effort that somebody puts into an activity or a purpose because they think it is important","cn":"献身；奉献","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"approving","ex":{"en":"hard work and dedication","cn":"勤奋和奉献"}},{"en":"a ceremony that is held to show that a building or an object has a special purpose or is special to the memory of a particular person","cn":"（建筑物等的）落成典礼","g":"[countable, uncountable]","ex":{"en":"the dedication of a new city church","cn":"新城市教堂的落成典礼"}},{"en":"the words that are used at the beginning of a book, piece of music, a performance, etc., or when receiving an award, to offer it to somebody as a sign of thanks or respect","cn":"献词（表示把书、音乐作品、演出、所获奖项等献给某人的一段话）","g":"[countable]"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(书等的）题献;（戏剧、音乐作品等表演之前的)献词","en":"A dedication is a message which is written at the beginning of a book, or a short announcement which is sometimes made before a play or piece of music is performed, as a sign of affection or respect for someone."}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/dedication__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/dedication__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"hard work and dedication","cn":"勤奋和奉献"},{"en":"To reach a high level of skill requires talent, dedication, and a lot of hard work.","cn":"要达到高级技术水平需要天分﹐还需要全身心的投入和很多的努力。"}]},"democracy":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈmɒkrəsi","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a system of government in which the people of a country can vote to elect their representatives","cn":"民主；民主政体；民主制度","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"parliamentary democracy","cn":"议会民主"}},{"en":"a country that has this system of government","cn":"民主国家","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"Western democracies","cn":"西方民主国家"}},{"en":"fair and equal treatment of everyone in an organization, etc., and their right to take part in making decisions","cn":"民主精神；民主权利；民主","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"the fight for justice and democracy","cn":"为正义和民主的斗争"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"民主;民主制度;民主政体","en":"Democracy is a system of government in which people choose their rulers by voting for them in elections.","ex":{"en":"...the spread of democracy in Eastern Europe.","cn":"民主制度在东欧的传播"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"民主国家","en":"A democracy is a country in which the people choose their government by voting for it.","ex":{"en":"The new democracies face tough challenges.","cn":"这些新兴的民主国家面临着严峻挑战。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"民主管理制度;民主作风","en":"Democracy is a system of running organizations, businesses, and groups in which each member is entitled to vote and take part in decisions.","ex":{"en":"...the union's emphasis on industrial democracy.","cn":"该工会对工业民主的强调"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/democracy__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/democracy__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"I thought we were supposed to be living in a democracy.","cn":"我还以为我们应该是生活在一个民主国家里。"},{"en":"the fight for justice and democracy","cn":"为正义和民主的斗争"}]},"decrease":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/decrease__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/decrease__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈkriːs","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to become smaller in size, number, etc.; to make something smaller in size, number, etc.","cn":"（使大小、数量等）减少，减小，降低","ex":{"en":"Donations have decreased significantly over the past few years.","cn":"在过去的几年里，捐赠已大大减少。"}},{"en":"the process of reducing something; the amount that something is reduced by","cn":"减少；降低；减少量","ex":{"en":"Sales for May show a decrease compared with the same month last year.","cn":"5月份的销售额与去年同月相比有所下降。"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"(使)减少;(使)减小;(使)降低","en":"When something decreases or when you decrease it, it becomes less in quantity, size, or intensity.","ex":{"en":"Population growth is decreasing by 1.4% each year","cn":"人口增长率正在以每年 1.4% 的速度下降。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"减少;减小;降低","en":"A decrease in the quantity, size, or intensity of something is a reduction in it.","ex":{"en":"...a decrease in the number of young people out of work","cn":"失业青年人数的减少"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The number of new students decreased from 210 to 160 this year.","cn":"今年新生人数从 210 减少到 160。"},{"en":"a decrease of nearly 6% in the number of visitors to the museum","cn":"参观博物馆人数下降将近 6%"}]},"deserve":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/deserve__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deserve__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈzɜːv","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to do something or show qualities that mean a particular reaction, reward or punishment is appropriate","cn":"应该得到；值得","ex":{"en":"You deserve a rest after all that hard work.","cn":"辛苦劳累那么久，你该休息一下了。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"应得;应受;值得","en":"If you say that a person or thing deserves something, you mean that they should have it or receive it because of their actions or qualities.","ex":{"en":"Government officials clearly deserve some of the blame as well","cn":"政府官员显然也应当承担部分责任。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"罪有应得;活该","en":"If you say that someone got what they deserved, you mean that they deserved the bad thing that happened to them, and you have no sympathy for them.","ex":{"en":"One of them said the two dead joy riders got what they deserved.","cn":"他们中的一个人说这两名开偷来的车去兜风的人死得活该。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"You deserve a rest after all that hard work.","cn":"辛苦劳累那么久，你该休息一下了。"},{"en":"What have I done to deserve this?","cn":"我做了什么事而要得到这种待遇呢？"}]},"densely":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdensli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"in a way that contains a lot of people, things, plants, etc. with little space between them","cn":"密集的；稠密的","ex":{"en":"a densely populated area","cn":"人口密集地区"}},{"en":"in a way that is difficult to understand because it contains a lot of information","cn":"（信息量大得）难理解的，难懂的","ex":{"en":"a densely written volume","cn":"写得密密麻麻的一卷"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/densely__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/densely__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"densely covered/packed","cn":"盖得/包得严实的"},{"en":"a densely populated area","cn":"人口密集地区"}]},"defence":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/defence__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/defence__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfens","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the act of protecting somebody/something from attack, criticism, etc.","cn":"防御；保护；保卫","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"protection against attack","ex":{"en":"soldiers who died in defence of their country","cn":"为保卫祖国而献身的战士"}},{"en":"something that provides protection against attack from enemies, the weather, illness, etc.","cn":"防御物；防务；防御能力","g":"[countable, uncountable]","sc":"protection against attack","ex":{"en":"They are responsible for maintaining coastal flood defences.","cn":"他们负责维护海岸防洪。"}},{"en":"the organization of the people and systems that are used by a government to protect a country from attack","cn":"国防机构；国防体系","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"British English","sc":"protection against attack","ex":{"en":"the Ministry of Defence","cn":"国防部"}},{"en":"something that is said or written in order to support something","cn":"辩解；辩白","g":"[countable]","sc":"support","ex":{"en":"a defence of Marxism","cn":"为马克思主义辩解"}},{"en":"what is said in court to prove that a person did not commit a crime; the act of presenting this argument in court","cn":"辩护；辩词；答辩","g":"[countable, usually singular]","sc":"law","ex":{"en":"Her defence was that she was somewhere completely different at the time of the crime.","cn":"她的辩词是案发时她根本就不在现场。"}},{"en":"the lawyer or lawyers whose job is to prove in court that a person did not commit a crime","cn":"辩护律师","g":"[singular + singular or plural verb]","lab":"US English also","sc":"law","ex":{"en":"The defence requested more time to prepare their case.","cn":"辩护律师要求有更多的时间为案件做准备。"}},{"en":"the players who must prevent the other team from scoring; the position of these players on the sports field","cn":"防守队员；防守；后卫","g":"[singular, uncountable]","lab":"British English","sc":"in sport","ex":{"en":"Welford cut through the defence to score the winning goal.","cn":"韦尔福特突破防守射进了制胜的一球。"}},{"en":"a contest, game, etc. in which the previous winner or winners compete in order to try to win again","cn":"卫冕赛","g":"[countable]","sc":"in sport","ex":{"en":"Barcelona’s defence of the Champions League title","cn":"巴塞罗那队的欧洲冠军联赛卫冕赛"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"防御;保卫;保护","en":"Defence is action that is taken to protect someone or something against attack.","ex":{"en":"The land was flat, giving no scope for defence","cn":"这一地区非常平坦，根本没法进行防御。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"国防;军事防御","en":"Defence is the organization of a country's armies and weapons, and their use to protect the country or its interests.","ex":{"en":"Twenty eight percent of the federal budget is spent on defense.","cn":"28%的联邦预算用于国防。"}},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"(国家或地区的)防御力量","en":"The defences of a country or region are all its armed forces and weapons.","ex":{"en":"...the need to maintain Britain's defences at a sufficiently high level.","cn":"维持英国的防御力量在足够高水平之上的需要"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"防御物;防卫手段","en":"A defence is something that people or animals can use or do to protect themselves.","ex":{"en":"The immune system is our main defence against disease","cn":"人体的免疫系统是抵御疾病的主要屏障。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"辩护;辩解","en":"A defence is something that you say or write which supports ideas or actions that have been criticized or questioned.","ex":{"en":"Chomsky'sdefence of his approach goes further","cn":"乔姆斯基对自己方法的辩护不止于此。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(法庭上被告的)辩护，答辩","en":"In a court of law, an accused person's defence is the process of presenting evidence in their favour.","ex":{"en":"He has insisted on conducting his own defence.","cn":"他坚持自己进行辩护。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"(被告律师的)辩护方法（或理由）;辩护律师","en":"The defence is the case that is presented by a lawyer in a trial for the person who has been accused of a crime. You can also refer to this person's lawyers as the defence .","ex":{"en":"The defence was that the records of the interviews were fabricated by the police","cn":"辩护论点为问讯记录是警方捏造的。"}},{"pos":"N-SING-COLL 单数集合名词","cn":"(足球、曲棍球等运动中的)防守（队员）","en":"In games such as football or hockey, the defence is the group of players in a team who try to stop the opposing players scoring a goal or a point.","ex":{"en":"Their defence, so strong last season, has now conceded 12 goals in six games","cn":"他们的防守上个赛季牢不可破，但在本赛季的 6 场比赛里已经丢了 12 个球。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"替…辩护;为…辩解","en":"If you come to someone's defence, you help them by doing or saying something to protect them.","ex":{"en":"He realized none of his schoolmates would come to his defense","cn":"他意识到没有一个同学会挺身为他辩护。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"When her brother was criticized she leapt to his defence.","cn":"她的哥哥受到批评时，她马上跳出来卫护。"},{"en":"What points can be raised in defence of this argument?","cn":"有什么论点能提出来为这个说法辩护呢？"}]},"dementia":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/dementia__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/dementia__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈmenʃə","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a brain condition, mostly affecting older people, in which a person has difficulties with memory, thinking, control of the body, etc. that are severe enough to affect daily life","cn":"（尤指老年性）痴呆","ex":{"en":"patients with dementia","cn":"痴呆症患者"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"痴呆","en":"Dementia is a serious illness of the mind."}]}},"desktop":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/desktop__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/desktop__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdesktɒp","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a screen on a computer that shows the icons of programs and files that can be used","cn":"（计算机）桌面","ex":{"en":"desktop icons","cn":"桌面图标"}},{"en":"the top of a desk","cn":"桌面"},{"en":"a computer with a keyboard, screen and main processing unit that fits on a desk","cn":"台式计算机；台式电脑"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(计算机)台式的","en":"Desktop computers are a convenient size for using on a desk or table, but are not designed to be portable.","ex":{"en":"When launched, the Macintosh was the smallest desktop computer ever produced.","cn":"当初上市的时候，麦金塔电脑是所有台式电脑里最小的。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"台式计算机","en":"A desktop is a desktop computer."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(计算机的)桌面","en":"The desktop of a computer is the display of icons that you see on the screen when the computer is ready to use."}]}},"devoid":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈvɔɪd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"completely without something","cn":"缺乏；完全没有","ex":{"en":"The letter was devoid of warmth and feeling.","cn":"这封信既无热情又无感情。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"毫无…的;没有…的","en":"If you say that someone or something is devoid of a quality or thing, you are emphasizing that they have none of it.","ex":{"en":"I have never looked on a face that was so devoid of feeling","cn":"我从来没有见过一张如此面无表情的脸。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/devoid__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/devoid__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The letter was devoid of warmth and feeling.","cn":"这封信既无热情又无感情。"},{"en":"His face was devoid of any warmth or humour.","cn":"他的脸冷若冰霜﹐没有一丝幽默的表情。"}]},"decisively":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈsaɪsɪvli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"in a way that is very important for the final result of a particular situation","cn":"以对特定情况的最终结果非常重要的方式","ex":{"en":"At Waterloo Napoleon was decisively defeated.","cn":"在滑铁卢，拿破仑被彻底击败。"}},{"en":"in a way that shows the ability to decide quickly and with confidence","cn":"坚决的；果断的；决断的","ex":{"en":"Congress must act decisively against this threat.","cn":"国会必须果断采取行动应对这一威胁。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/decisively__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/decisively__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Women can play a decisive role in the debate over cloning.","cn":""},{"en":"We will take decisive steps towards political union with Europe.","cn":""}]},"describe":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/describe__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/describe__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈskraɪb","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to say what somebody/something is like","cn":"描述；形容；把…称为","ex":{"en":"The next section describes our findings in detail.","cn":"下一节详细介绍我们的发现。"}},{"en":"to make a movement that has a particular shape; to form a particular shape","cn":"沿…形状移动；画出…图形；形成…形状","lab":"formal or specialist","ex":{"en":"The shark described a circle around the shoal of fish.","cn":"这条鲨鱼围绕着鱼群游动。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"描述;描写;形容;叙述","en":"If you describe a person, object, event, or situation, you say what they are like or what happened.","ex":{"en":"We asked her to describe what kind of things she did in her spare time","cn":"我们请她描述一下她业余时间都在做什么。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"把…说成;把…称为;认为","en":"If a person describes someone or something as a particular thing, he or she believes that they are that thing and says so.","ex":{"en":"He described it as an extraordinarily tangled and complicated tale","cn":"他说那是一个非常曲折复杂的故事。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"描画，画出(图形);形成…的形状","en":"If something describes a particular shape, it forms that shape or makes a movement that follows the line of that shape.","ex":{"en":"His pass described a perfect arc through the leaden sky.","cn":"他的传球在阴沉的天空中划出了一道完美的弧线。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The man was described as tall and dark, and aged about 20.","cn":"据描述这男人高个子，深色皮肤，年龄在 20 岁左右。"},{"en":"Several people described seeing strange lights in the sky.","cn":"好几个人都说看到天上出现了奇异光芒。"}]},"depending":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpend","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"according to","cn":"视乎；决定于"},{"en":"used to say that you are not certain about sth because other things have to be considered","cn":"那得看情况"}]}},"decide":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/decide__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/decide__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈsaɪd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to think carefully about the different possibilities that are available and choose one of them","cn":"对…作出抉择；决定；选定","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","ex":{"en":"It's up to you to decide.","cn":"这事由你来决定吧。"}},{"en":"to make an official or legal judgement","cn":"裁决；判决","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","lab":"law","ex":{"en":"The case will be decided by a jury.","cn":"这案件将由陪审团裁决。"}},{"en":"to affect the result of something","cn":"影响（或决定）…的结果","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"A mixture of skill and good luck decided the outcome of the game.","cn":"技术和运气结合在一起决定了比赛的结果。"}},{"en":"to be the reason why somebody does something","cn":"成为（某人）做某事的原因","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"For most customers, price is the deciding factor.","cn":"对大多数顾客来说，价格是决定性因素。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"决定，拿定主意（做）","en":"If you decide to do something, you choose to do it, usually after you have thought carefully about the other possibilities.","ex":{"en":"She decided to do a secretarial course","cn":"她决定修一门文秘课程。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"解决;判决;裁决","en":"If a person or group of people decides something, they choose what something should be like or how a particular problem should be solved.","ex":{"en":"She was still young, he said, and that would be taken into account when deciding her sentence","cn":"他说，她还年轻，而这一点在对她量刑时将会予以考虑。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（事件或事实）决定，确定（某一选择或结果)","en":"If an event or fact decides something, it makes it certain that a particular choice will be made or that there will be a particular result.","ex":{"en":"The goal that decided the match came just before the interval","cn":"决定本场比赛结果的进球是在中场休息前一刻打入的。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"断定;判定","en":"If you decide that something is true, you form that opinion about it after considering the facts.","ex":{"en":"He decided Franklin must be suffering from a bad cold","cn":"他断定富兰克林一定是得了重感冒。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"使决定，使拿定主意（做）","en":"If something decides you to do something, it is the reason that causes you to choose to do it.","ex":{"en":"The banning of his play decided him to write about censorship","cn":"他的戏剧被禁演，这促使他下定决心就审查制度的问题下笔。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：decide on"}]},"examples":[{"en":"They offered me free accommodation for a year, and that decided me.","cn":"他们愿意免费为我提供一年的住宿，这就使我下定了决心。"},{"en":"We might be hiring more people but nothing has been decided yet.","cn":"我们或许会再多雇些人，不过现在什么都还没定下来。"}]},"decided":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/decided__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/decided__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈsaɪdɪd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"obvious and definite","cn":"明显的；明白无误的；确实无疑的","g":"[only before noun]","ex":{"en":"His height was a decided advantage in the job.","cn":"干这项工作，他的身高是明显优势。"}},{"en":"having very strong opinions","cn":"坚定的；坚决的","lab":"especially British English","ex":{"en":"She was a very decided young woman, eager to do some good in the world.","cn":"她是一个非常坚定的年轻女子，渴望在世上做点有益的事。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"确实无疑的;明白无误的;明显的","en":"Decided means clear and definite.","ex":{"en":"Her ignorance of the area put her at a decided disadvantage","cn":"她对该地区一无所知，这显然对她不利。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"She was a very decided young woman, eager to do some good in the world.","cn":"她是一个非常坚定的年轻女子，渴望在世上做点有益的事。"},{"en":"The child is very decided about what she wants and doesn't want.","cn":"这孩子对她想要和不想要的东西非常有主见。"}],"base":"decide"},"deserts":{"lemma":"desert","media":{"uk":"media/uk/deserts__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deserts__us_1.mp3"}},"destroy":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈstrɔɪ","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to damage something so badly that it no longer exists, works, etc.","cn":"摧毁；毁灭；破坏","ex":{"en":"The building was completely destroyed by fire.","cn":"这栋建筑物被大火彻底焚毁了。"}},{"en":"to take all the value and pleasure from somebody's life; to ruin (= completely damage) somebody's life or reputation","cn":"毁坏（某人生活或名誉）","ex":{"en":"Failure was slowly destroying him.","cn":"失败渐渐地把他毁了。"}},{"en":"to kill an animal deliberately, usually because it is sick or not wanted","cn":"（因动物有病或不再需要而）杀死，消灭，人道毁灭","ex":{"en":"The injured horse had to be destroyed.","cn":"这匹马受了伤，只好把它杀了。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"毁坏;破坏;毁灭;摧毁","en":"To destroy something means to cause so much damage to it that it is completely ruined or does not exist any more.","ex":{"en":"That's a sure recipe for destroying the economy and creating chaos","cn":"那样做肯定会破坏经济、制造混乱。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"毁掉…的生活;使垮掉","en":"To destroy someone means to ruin their life or to make their situation impossible to bear.","ex":{"en":"If I was younger or more naive, the criticism would have destroyed me.","cn":"如果我再年轻一些，或是再单纯一些，那些批评可能就会把我给毁了。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"杀死，消灭（生病或具危险性的动物）","en":"If an animal is destroyed, it is killed, either because it is ill or because it is dangerous.","ex":{"en":"Lindsay was unhurt but the horse had to be destroyed.","cn":"林赛没有受伤，但那匹马却不得不被人道毁灭。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/destroy__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/destroy__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The injured horse had to be destroyed.","cn":"这匹马受了伤，只好送它回老家了。"},{"en":"The building was completely destroyed by fire.","cn":"这栋建筑物被大火彻底焚毁了。"}]},"democrat":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/democrat__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/democrat__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdeməkræt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person who believes in or supports democracy","cn":"民主主义者"},{"en":"a member or supporter of the Democratic Party of the US","cn":"（美国）民主党党员，民主党人，民主党支持者"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"民主党党员;民主党支持者","en":"A Democrat is a member or supporter of a particular political party which has the word 'democrat' or 'democratic' in its title, for example the Democratic Party in the United States.","ex":{"en":"...a senior Christian Democrat","cn":"资深的基督教民主党党员"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"民主主义者;民主人士","en":"A democrat is a person who believes in the ideals of democracy, personal freedom, and equality.","ex":{"en":"This is the time for democrats and not dictators.","cn":"现在需要的是民主主义者，而不是独裁者。"}}]}},"decent":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/decent__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/decent__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdiːsnt","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"of a good enough standard or quality","cn":"像样的；相当不错的；尚好的","lab":"informal","ex":{"en":"a decent meal/place to live","cn":"相当不错的饭菜／住所"}},{"en":"honest and fair; treating people with respect","cn":"正派的；公平的；合乎礼节的","ex":{"en":"ordinary, decent, hard-working people","cn":"勤劳正派的普通人"}},{"en":"acceptable to people in a particular situation","cn":"得体的；合宜的；适当的","ex":{"en":"a decent burial","cn":"体面的葬礼"}},{"en":"wearing enough clothes to allow somebody to see you","cn":"穿好衣服的；适宜于见人的","lab":"informal","ex":{"en":"I can't go to the door—I'm not decent.","cn":"我不能去开门，我还没穿好衣服。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"像样的;尚好的;过得去的","en":"Decent is used to describe something which is considered to be of an acceptable standard or quality.","ex":{"en":"Nearby is a village with a decent pub","cn":"附近的村子里有一家还不错的酒馆。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"合宜的;得体的;适当的;正当的","en":"Decent is used to describe something which is morally correct or acceptable.","ex":{"en":"But, after a decent interval, trade relations began to return to normal","cn":"但是适当地间断一段时间后，贸易关系开始恢复正常。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"（人）正派的，正直的，规矩的","en":"Decent people are honest and behave in a way that most people approve of.","ex":{"en":"The majority of people around here are decent people","cn":"这里的大多数人都很正派。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"做（不想做但）应该做的事","en":"If you say that someone should do the decent thing, you mean that they should do something which they do not really want to do, but which you think they ought to do.","ex":{"en":"He should do the decent thing and resign.","cn":"他应该识时务地辞职。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"She ought to have waited for a decent interval before getting married again.","cn":"她再次嫁人也应该适当等上一段时间。"},{"en":"Everyone said he was a decent sort of guy.","cn":"人人都说他是个品行端正的小伙子。"}]},"def":{"oxford":{"phon":"def","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"definition","cn":"清晰度","ex":{"en":"You can now view the trailer in high def online.","cn":"您现在可以在线观看高清预告片。"}},{"en":"excellent","cn":"极好的；很棒的","ex":{"en":"a def band","cn":"出色的乐队"},"pos":"adjective"},{"en":"definitely","cn":"一定地；肯定","ex":{"en":"This will def be a good movie.","cn":"这部电影肯定会好看。"},"pos":"adverb"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/def__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/def__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"a def band","cn":"出色的乐队"}]},"dept":{"oxford":{"phon":"","pos":"abbreviation","senses":[{"en":"(in writing) department","cn":"（书写形式）部，部门，系"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"","cn":"(通常用于名称中)","en":"Dept is used as a written abbreviation for (书面缩略=) department, usually in the name of a particular department.","ex":{"en":"...the Internal Affairs Dept.","cn":"内政部"}}]}},"dealing":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/dealing__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/dealing__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdiːlɪŋ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"business activities; the relations that you have with somebody in business","cn":"（商业）活动，往来","g":"[plural]","ex":{"en":"I knew nothing of his business dealings.","cn":"我对他生意上的事一概不知道。"}},{"en":"a way of doing business with somebody","cn":"经营作风；经营方式","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"a reputation for fair/honest dealing","cn":"公平交易／诚信经营的美名"}},{"en":"buying and selling","cn":"买卖；交易","g":"[uncountable, countable]","ex":{"en":"drug dealing","cn":"毒品交易"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"She has always been very polite in her dealings with me.","cn":"她在与我交往的过程中总是彬彬有礼。"},{"en":"Have you had any previous dealings with this company?","cn":"你曾与这家公司有过业务往来吗？"}],"base":"deal"},"delaying":{"lemma":"delay"},"depends":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpend","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"according to","cn":"视乎；决定于"},{"en":"used to say that you are not certain about sth because other things have to be considered","cn":"那得看情况"}]}},"deposition":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/deposition__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deposition__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdepəˈzɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the natural process of leaving a layer of a substance on rocks or soil; a substance left in this way","cn":"沉积（物）；沉淀（物）；淤积（物）","g":"[uncountable, countable]","lab":"specialist","ex":{"en":"marine/river deposition","cn":"海洋／河流沉积物"}},{"en":"the act of removing somebody, especially a leader, from power","cn":"罢免；废黜","g":"[uncountable, countable]","ex":{"en":"the deposition of the King","cn":"废黜国王"}},{"en":"a formal statement, taken from somebody and used in court","cn":"书面证词","g":"[countable]","lab":"law"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(未到庭证人提供的)作证书，书面证词","en":"A deposition is a formal written statement, made for example by a witness to a crime, which can be used in a court of law if the witness cannot be present.","ex":{"en":"The jury heard 200 pages of depositions.","cn":"陪审团听取了长达 200 页的书面证词。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"沉淀;沉积","en":"Deposition is a process in which layers of a substance are formed inside something or on its surface over a period of time.","ex":{"en":"Continued deposition of silt along the coast is crucial in counteracting the rise in sea level","cn":"海岸边泥沙的不断沉积对于抑制海平面的上升起着至关重要的作用。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"罢免;废黜","en":"The deposition of a political leader is the removal of him or her from office.","ex":{"en":"It was this issue which led to the deposition of the king.","cn":"正是这件事导致了国王被废黜。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"marine/river deposition","cn":"海洋/河流沉积物"},{"en":"the deposition of the King","cn":"废黜国王"}]},"deep-seated":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"根深蒂固的;难以改变的","en":"A deep-seated problem, feeling, or belief is difficult to change because its causes have been there for a long time.","ex":{"en":"The country is still suffering from deep-seated economic problems.","cn":"该国仍然受到根深蒂固的经济问题的困扰。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/1/deep_seated0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/6/deep-seated.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"a deep-seated fear of failure","cn":"对失败难以消除的恐惧感"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdiːp ˈsiːtɪd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"very fixed and strong; difficult to change or to destroy","cn":"根深蒂固的；强烈的；坚定的","ex":{"en":"The country's political divisions are deep-seated.","cn":"这个国家的政治分歧根深蒂固。"}}]}},"denim":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdenɪm","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a type of strong cotton cloth that is usually blue and is used for making clothes, especially jeans","cn":"蓝粗棉布；劳动布；牛仔布","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"a denim jacket","cn":"牛仔布夹克衫"}},{"en":"trousers or other clothes made of denim","cn":"牛仔裤；牛仔服","g":"[plural]"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(通常为蓝色、用来做牛仔裤等的)粗斜纹棉布，劳动布，牛仔布","en":"Denim is a thick cotton cloth, usually blue, which is used to make clothes. Jeans are made from denim.","ex":{"en":"...a light blue denim jacket","cn":"浅蓝色的牛仔布夹克Dennis was dressed in denim jeans. 丹尼斯穿了一条劳动布牛仔裤。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/denim__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/denim__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"a denim jacket","cn":"牛仔布夹克衫"}]},"developed":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/developed__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/developed__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈveləpt","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"having many industries and a complex economic system","cn":"发达的；高度发展的","ex":{"en":"financial aid to less developed countries","cn":"对欠发达国家的经济援助"}},{"en":"in an advanced state","cn":"先进的；成熟的","ex":{"en":"children with highly developed problem-solving skills","cn":"具有非常熟练解决问题能力的孩子"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(国家、地区等)发达的","en":"If you talk about developed countries or the developed world, you mean the countries or the parts of the world that are wealthy and have many industries.","ex":{"en":"The developed nations have to recognize the growing gap between rich and poor around the world","cn":"发达国家必须认识到世界范围内的贫富差距正在不断扩大。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The average citizen in the developed world uses over 155kg of paper per year.","cn":"发达国家中普通公民每年的用纸量超过 155 公斤。"},{"en":"children with highly developed problem-solving skills","cn":"具有非常熟练解决问题能力的孩子"}],"base":"develop"},"delight":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/delight__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/delight__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈlaɪt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a feeling of great pleasure","cn":"高兴；愉快；快乐","g":"[uncountable, singular]","ex":{"en":"a feeling of sheer/pure delight","cn":"十分高兴的心情"}},{"en":"something that gives you great pleasure","cn":"令人高兴的事；乐事；乐趣","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"This guitar is a delight to play.","cn":"这吉他弹起来很惬意。"}},{"en":"to give somebody a lot of pleasure and joy","cn":"使高兴；使愉快；使快乐","ex":{"en":"This news will delight his fans all over the world.","cn":"这消息将使全世界崇拜他的人都感到高兴。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"高兴;愉快;快乐","en":"Delight is a feeling of very great pleasure.","ex":{"en":"Throughout the house, the views are a constant source of surprise and delight","cn":"从房子各处看到的景色不断给人以惊奇和欣喜。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"（以…）为乐;喜欢;爱好","en":"If someone takes delight or takes a delight in something, they get a lot of pleasure from it.","ex":{"en":"Haig took obvious delight in proving his critics wrong","cn":"黑格显然以证明他的批评者是错误的为乐。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"令人高兴的人(或物);乐事;乐趣","en":"You can refer to someone or something that gives you great pleasure or enjoyment as a delight .","ex":{"en":"Isn't she a delight?","cn":"她真讨人喜欢，不是吗？"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"使高兴;使愉快;使快乐","en":"If something delights you, it gives you a lot of pleasure.","ex":{"en":"She has created a style of music that has delighted audiences all over the world","cn":"她创造出了一种能令全世界的听众都感到快乐的音乐风格。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（以…）为乐;喜欢;爱好","en":"If you delight in something, you get a lot of pleasure from it.","ex":{"en":"Generations of adults and children have delighted in the story","cn":"一代又一代的成年人和儿童都很喜欢这个故事。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"She won the game easily, to the delight of all her fans.","cn":"这场比赛她赢得很轻松，令所有的崇拜者大为高兴。"},{"en":"This news will delight his fans all over the world.","cn":"这消息将使全世界崇拜他的人都感到高兴。"}]},"dependency":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/dependency__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/dependency__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpendənsi","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the state of relying on somebody/something for something, especially in a way you do not consider right or necessary","cn":"（尤指不正常或不必要的）依靠，依赖","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"financial dependency","cn":"财政上的依赖"}},{"en":"a country, an area, etc. that is controlled by another country","cn":"附属国；附属地","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"The Orkney Islands were formerly dependencies of Norway and Denmark.","cn":"奥克尼群岛以前是挪威和丹麦的属地。"}},{"en":"the state of being addicted to something (= unable to stop taking or using it)","cn":"瘾","ex":{"en":"alcohol dependency","cn":"酒精依赖"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"附属国;附属地;托管地","en":"A dependency is a country which is controlled by another country.","ex":{"en":"...the tiny British dependency of Montserrat in the eastern Caribbean.","cn":"位于加勒比海东部巴掌大的英国附属领地蒙特塞拉特"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"（尤指过分或不利的）依靠，依赖","en":"You talk about someone's dependency when they have a deep emotional, physical, or financial need for a particular person or thing, especially one that you consider excessive or undesirable.","ex":{"en":"We worried about his dependency on his mother","cn":"我们担心他可能对母亲太过依赖。"}},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"(对酒精、毒品等的)依赖，瘾，癖","en":"If you talk about alcohol dependency or chemical dependency, you are referring to a situation where someone is an alcoholic or is addicted to drugs.","ex":{"en":"In 1985, he began to show signs of alcohol and drug dependency","cn":"在1985年，他开始表现出酗酒嗜毒的迹象。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Their aim is to reduce people's dependency on the welfare state.","cn":"他们旨在减少人们对福利制度的依赖。"},{"en":"the dependency culture (= a way of life in which people depend too much on money from the government)","cn":"依赖文化（过分依赖政府资助）"}]},"detailed":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/detailed__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/detailed__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdiːteɪld","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"giving many details and a lot of information; paying great attention to details","cn":"详细的；细致的；精细的","ex":{"en":"a detailed description of the events","cn":"对事件的详细描述"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"详细的;详尽的;细致的","en":"A detailed report or plan contains a lot of details.","ex":{"en":"Yesterday's letter contains a detailed account of the decisions","cn":"昨天的那封信里有对这些决议的详细说明。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He gave me detailed instructions on how to get there.","cn":"他详细地告诉我如何到达那里。"},{"en":"a detailed description/analysis/study","cn":"详细的描述/分析/研究"}],"base":"detail"},"delighted":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/delighted__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/delighted__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈlaɪtɪd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"very pleased","cn":"高兴的；愉快的；快乐的","ex":{"en":"a delighted smile","cn":"愉快的微笑"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"高兴的;愉快的;快乐的","en":"If you are delighted, you are extremely pleased and excited about something.","ex":{"en":"I know Frank will be delighted to see you","cn":"我知道弗兰克见到你会很高兴的。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"乐意的;荣幸的","en":"If someone invites or asks you to do something, you can say that you would be delighted to do it, as a way of showing that you are very willing to do it.","ex":{"en":"'You must come to Tinsley's graduation party.' — 'I'd be delighted.'","cn":"“你一定要来参加廷斯利的毕业聚会。”——“我很乐意。”"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"She was delighted by/at the news of the wedding.","cn":"听到婚礼的消息她很高兴。"},{"en":"I was delighted with my presents.","cn":"我对我收到的礼物很满意。"}],"base":"delight"},"dependence":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpendəns","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the state of needing the help and support of somebody/something in order to survive or be successful","cn":"（生存或成功必需的）依靠，依赖，依存","ex":{"en":"Our relationship was based on mutual dependence.","cn":"我们的关系建立在相互依存的基础上。"}},{"en":"the state of being addicted to something (= unable to stop taking or using it)","cn":"瘾","ex":{"en":"drug/alcohol dependence","cn":"毒瘾；酒瘾"}},{"en":"the fact of one thing being affected by another","cn":"相关（性）；相依（性）","lab":"specialist","ex":{"en":"the close dependence of soil and landforms","cn":"土壤和地貌的密切相关"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"（为了成功或存活的）依靠，依赖","en":"Your dependence on something or someone is your need for them in order to succeed or be able to survive.","ex":{"en":"...the city's traditional dependence on tourism","cn":"该市传统上对旅游业的依赖"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(对毒品或酒精的)依赖，瘾，癖","en":"If you talk about drug dependence or alcohol dependence, you are referring to a situation where someone is addicted to drugs or is an alcoholic.","ex":{"en":"French doctors tend to regard drug dependence as a form of deep-rooted psychological disorder.","cn":"法国医生倾向于把毒瘾看作是一种根深蒂固的心理障碍。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"（受其影响或决定的）依赖（关系）","en":"You talk about the dependence of one thing on another when the first thing will be affected or determined by the second.","ex":{"en":"...the dependence of circulation on production.","cn":"流通对生产的依赖"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/dependence__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/dependence__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Our relationship was based on mutual dependence.","cn":"我们的关系建立在相互依存的基础上。"},{"en":"the dependence of Europe on imported foods","cn":"欧洲对进口食物的依赖"}]},"dear":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/dear__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/dear__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪə(r)","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"used at the beginning of a letter before the name or title of the person that you are writing to","cn":"（用于信函抬头的名字或头衔前）亲爱的","lab":"old-fashioned","ex":{"en":"Dear Sir or Madam","cn":"亲爱的先生或女士"}},{"en":"loved by or important to somebody","cn":"亲爱的；宝贵的；珍视的","ex":{"en":"He's one of my dearest friends.","cn":"他是我最亲密的朋友之一。"}},{"en":"used in speech or writing to address somebody in a polite or friendly way","cn":"（用于称呼他人，表示礼貌或友善）亲爱的","g":"[only before noun]","lab":"old-fashioned","ex":{"en":"Martin, my dear fellow…","cn":"马丁，我亲爱的朋友…"}},{"en":"expensive; costing a lot of money","cn":"昂贵；价格高","g":"[not usually before noun]","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"Everything's so dear now, isn't it?","cn":"现在什么东西都那么贵，是不是？"}},{"en":"used in expressions that show that you are surprised, upset, annoyed or worried","cn":"（惊奇、不安、烦恼、担忧等时说）啊，哎呀，糟糕，天哪","ex":{"en":"Oh dear! I think I've lost my purse!","cn":"糟糕，我可能把钱包给丢了！"},"pos":"exclamation"},{"en":"a kind person","cn":"仁慈的人；可爱的人","lab":"informal","ex":{"en":"Isn't he a dear?","cn":"他不是很可爱吗？"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"used when speaking to somebody you love","cn":"（称呼所爱的人）亲爱的","ex":{"en":"Would you like a drink, dear?","cn":"喝点什么吗，亲爱的？"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"used when speaking to somebody in a friendly way, for example by an older person to a young person or a child","cn":"（对较年轻的人或孩子说话时用）亲爱的，乖乖","ex":{"en":"What's your name, dear?","cn":"你叫什么名字，亲爱的？"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"at a high price","cn":"高价地；昂贵地","ex":{"en":"to buy cheap and sell dear","cn":"贱买贵卖"},"pos":"adverb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"亲爱的;可爱的","en":"You use dear to describe someone or something that you feel affection for.","ex":{"en":"Mrs Cavendish is a dear friend of mine","cn":"卡文迪什夫人是我的一位亲密朋友。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"对…来说心爱的;在…（心中）宝贵的","en":"If something is dear to you or dear to your heart, you care deeply about it.","ex":{"en":"His family life was very dear to him","cn":"他很珍视自己的家庭生活。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(用于表示喜爱或带有屈尊俯就意味的称呼中）亲爱的;小…","en":"You use dear in expressions such as 'my dear fellow', 'dear girl', or 'my dear Richard' when you are addressing someone whom you know and are fond of. You can also use expressions like this in a rude way to indicate that you think you are superior to the person you are addressing.","ex":{"en":"Of course, Toby, my dear fellow, of course","cn":"当然，托比，我亲爱的朋友，当然。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(用于信函抬头的名字或头衔前）亲爱的，尊敬的","en":"Dear is written at the beginning of a letter, followed by the name or title of the person you are writing to.","ex":{"en":"Dear Peter, I have been thinking about you so much during the past few days","cn":"亲爱的彼得，过去的这几天里我一直都在想你。"}},{"pos":"CONVENTION 惯用语","cn":"尊敬的先生/尊敬的女士(英国英语中用于正式信函的开头，美国英语中则用 Sir 或 Madam)","en":"In British English, you begin formal letters with 'Dear Sir' or 'Dear Madam'. In American English, you begin them with 'Sir' or 'Madam'.","ex":{"en":"'Dear sir,' she began.","cn":"“尊敬的先生，”她开头写道。"}},{"pos":"N-VOC 称呼名词","cn":"(用于称呼喜爱的人）亲爱的","en":"You can call someone dear as a sign of affection.","ex":{"en":"You're a lot like me, dear","cn":"亲爱的，你很多地方都很像我。"}},{"pos":"EXCLAM 感叹语","cn":"(表示伤心、失望或吃惊）啊呀，哎哟，天哪","en":"You can use dear in expressions such as 'oh dear', 'dear me', and 'dear, dear' when you are sad, disappointed, or surprised about something.","ex":{"en":"'Oh dear, oh dear.' McKinnon sighed. 'You, too.'","cn":"“哎呀，哎呀！”麦金农叹息道，“你也一样。”"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"可爱的人;好人","en":"You can call someone a dear when you are fond of them and think that they are nice.","ex":{"en":"He's such a dear.","cn":"他人真好。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"昂贵的;价高的","en":"If you say that something is dear, you mean that it costs a lot of money, usually more than you can afford or more than you think it should cost.","ex":{"en":"CDs here are much dearer than in the States","cn":"这儿的 CD 价格比美国那边贵多了。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"使…付出巨大代价;使…饱尝苦头","en":"If something that someone does costs them dear, they suffer a lot as a result of it.","ex":{"en":"Such complacency is costing the company dear.","cn":"这种自满情绪正使公司付出沉重代价。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Everything's so dear now, isn't it?","cn":"现在什么东西都那么贵，是不是？"},{"en":"Dear old Sue! I knew she'd help.","cn":"亲爱的苏啊！我知道她会帮忙的。"}]},"deep-rooted":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"同 deep-seated","en":"Deep-rooted means the same as deep-seated .","ex":{"en":"...long-term solutions to a deep-rooted problem.","cn":"针对一个根深蒂固的问题的长期解决方案"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/1/ld41deep-rooted.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/f/deep-rooted.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"a deep-rooted suspicion of lawyers","cn":"对律师根深蒂固的不信任"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdiːp ˈruːtɪd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"very fixed and strong; difficult to change or to destroy","cn":"根深蒂固的；强烈的；坚定的","ex":{"en":"a deep-rooted desire","cn":"强烈的愿望"}}]}},"delivered":{"lemma":"deliver"},"defects":{"lemma":"defect"},"determiner":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈtɜːmɪnə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a word such as the, some, my, etc. that comes before a noun to show how the noun is being used","cn":"限定词（置于名词前起限定作用，如 the、some、my 等）"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(语法中的)限定词","en":"In grammar, a determiner is a word which is used at the beginning of a noun group to indicate, for example, which thing you are referring to or whether you are referring to one thing or several. Common English determiners are 'a', 'the', 'some', 'this', and 'each'."}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/determiner__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/determiner__us_1.mp3"}},"desperate":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/desperate__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/desperate__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdespərət","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"feeling or showing that you have little hope and are ready to do anything without worrying about danger to yourself or others","cn":"（因绝望而）不惜冒险的，不顾一切的，拼命的","ex":{"en":"The prisoners grew increasingly desperate.","cn":"犯人因绝望而越来越胆大妄为。"}},{"en":"giving little hope of success; tried when everything else has failed","cn":"绝望的；孤注一掷的；铤而走险的","g":"[usually before noun]","ex":{"en":"He made a desperate bid for freedom.","cn":"他为获自由孤注一掷。"}},{"en":"needing or wanting something very much","cn":"非常需要；极想；渴望","g":"[not usually before noun]","lab":"informal","ex":{"en":"He was so desperate for a job he would have done anything.","cn":"他当时太想找份工作了，什么事都愿意干。"}},{"en":"extremely serious or dangerous","cn":"极严重的；极危险的；很危急的","ex":{"en":"The children are in desperate need of love and attention.","cn":"这些孩子非常需要爱心和关注。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"（因绝望而）孤注一掷的，铤而走险的，拼命的","en":"If you are desperate, you are in such a bad situation that you are willing to try anything to change it.","ex":{"en":"Troops are needed to help get food into Kosovo where people are in desperate need","cn":"需要军队帮助将科索沃人民亟需的食品送抵那里。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"极需要的;渴望的","en":"If you are desperate for something or desperate to do something, you want or need it very much indeed.","ex":{"en":"They'd been married nearly four years and June was desperate to start a family","cn":"他们结婚已快4年了，琼非常渴望要个孩子。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"极困难的;极严重的;极危险的","en":"A desperate situation is very difficult, serious, or dangerous.","ex":{"en":"India's United Nations ambassador said the situation is desperate","cn":"印度驻联合国大使说形势非常危急。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Somewhere out there was a desperate man, cold, hungry, hunted.","cn":"那外面有个男人又冷又饿，还有人抓他，走投无路了。"},{"en":"His increasing financial difficulties forced him to take desperate measures.","cn":"不断增加的经济困难迫使他采取了铤而走险的办法。"}]},"design":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/design__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/design__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈzaɪn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the general arrangement of the different parts of something that is made, such as a building, book, machine, etc.","cn":"设计；布局；安排","g":"[uncountable, countable]","sc":"arrangement","ex":{"en":"The basic design of the car is very similar to that of earlier models.","cn":"这种汽车的基本设计与早期的型号非常相似。"}},{"en":"the art or process of deciding how something will look, work, etc. by drawing plans, making computer models, etc.","cn":"设计艺术；构思","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"drawing/plan/model","ex":{"en":"the design and development of new products","cn":"新产品的设计和开发"}},{"en":"a drawing or plan from which something may be made","cn":"设计图样；设计方案","g":"[countable]","sc":"drawing/plan/model","ex":{"en":"He has created some new and original designs.","cn":"他创造了一些新颖的原创设计。"}},{"en":"an arrangement of lines and shapes as a decoration","cn":"装饰图案；花纹","g":"[countable]","sc":"pattern","ex":{"en":"floral/abstract/geometric designs","cn":"花卉／抽象／几何图案"}},{"en":"a plan or an intention","cn":"打算；意图；目的","g":"[uncountable, countable]","sc":"intention","ex":{"en":"It happened—whether by accident or design—that the two of them were left alone after all the others had gone.","cn":"不知道是偶然还是有意安排，其他人走后，竟然只剩下他们两个人。"}},{"en":"to decide how something will look, work, etc., by drawing plans, making computer models, etc.","cn":"设计；制图；构思","sc":"draw plans","ex":{"en":"He designed and built his own house.","cn":"他设计并建造了自己的房子。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to think of and plan a system, a way of doing something, etc., usually for a particular purpose or use","cn":"计划；筹划；制订","g":"[often passive]","sc":"plan something for special purpose","ex":{"en":"We need to design a comprehensive professional development programme.","cn":"我们需要制订一个全面职业发展计划。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"设计(服装、建筑、机械等)","en":"When someone designs a garment, building, machine, or other object, they plan it and make a detailed drawing of it from which it can be built or made.","ex":{"en":"They wanted to design a machine that was both attractive and practical.","cn":"他们想设计一种既美观又实用的机械。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"设计(调查问卷);规划;制订","en":"When someone designs a survey, policy, or system, they plan and prepare it, and decide on all the details of it.","ex":{"en":"We may be able to design a course to suit your particular needs","cn":"我们或许可以专门设计一门课程以满足你的特殊需求。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"设计过程;设计艺术","en":"Design is the process and art of planning and making detailed drawings of something.","ex":{"en":"He was a born mechanic with a flair for design","cn":"他生来就是个有设计天赋的机械师。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"设计（样式）","en":"The design of something is the way in which it has been planned and made.","ex":{"en":"These machines are constantly updated by improving the design of the computers.","cn":"通过改善计算机的设计，这些机器不断得到更新。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"设计图;图样;图纸","en":"A design is a drawing which someone produces to show how they would like something to be built or made.","ex":{"en":"They drew up the design for the house in a week.","cn":"他们在一周内就画出了房子的图样。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"图案;花纹","en":"A design is a pattern of lines, flowers, or shapes which is used to decorate something.","ex":{"en":"Their range of tableware is decorated with a blackberry design","cn":"他们的整套餐具上都饰有黑莓图案。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"计划;打算;意图;企图","en":"A design is a general plan or intention that someone has in their mind when they are doing something.","ex":{"en":"Is there some design in having him in the middle?","cn":"让他呆在中间是不是有什么目的？"}},{"pos":"V-PASSIVE 被动动词","cn":"预定;指定","en":"If something is designed for a particular purpose, it is intended for that purpose.","ex":{"en":"This project is designed to help landless people","cn":"这一项目旨在帮助那些没有土地的人。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"有意地;故意地;蓄意地","en":"If something happens or is done by design, someone does it deliberately, rather than by accident.","ex":{"en":"The pair met often — at first by chance but later by design.","cn":"这两个人经常见面——开始是偶然的，后来就是有意的了。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"图谋得到;打…的主意","en":"If someone has designs on something, they want it and are planning to get it, often in a dishonest way.","ex":{"en":"His colonel had designs on his wife","cn":"他的上校在打他妻子的主意。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"It happened — whether by accident or design — that the two of them were left alone after all the others had gone.","cn":"不知道是偶然还是有意安排，其他人走后，竟然只剩下他们两个人。"},{"en":"This course is primarily designed as an introduction to the subject.","cn":"这门课程开设的主要目的是教授这门学科的概论。"}]},"debut":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/debut__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/debut__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdeɪbjuː","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the first public appearance of a performer or sports player","cn":"（演员、运动员的）首次亮相；初次登台（或上场）","ex":{"en":"He will make his debut for the first team this week.","cn":"本周他将在第一支出场的队伍中首次亮相。"}},{"en":"(of a performer or show) to make a first public appearance","cn":"（演员）首次亮相，初次登台；（表演）首次上演","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"The ballet will debut next month in New York.","cn":"这出芭蕾舞剧将于下月在纽约首演。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to be presented to the market for the first time; to present a new product or advertising campaign to the market","cn":"推出；首发","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","lab":"especially North American English, business，，","ex":{"en":"The model is expected to debut at $19 000.","cn":"预计这款产品的首发价为 1.9 万美元。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(表演者或运动员的）首次登台，初次露面；（歌手的）首次录音","en":"The debut of a performer or sports player is their first public performance, appearance, or recording.","ex":{"en":"Dundee United's Dave Bowman makes his international debut.","cn":"邓迪联队的戴夫·鲍曼首次亮相国际比赛。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He will make his debut for the first team this week.","cn":"本周他将在第一支出场的队伍中首次亮相。"},{"en":"The ballet will debut next month in New York.","cn":"这出芭蕾舞剧将于下月在纽约首演。"}]},"debt":{"oxford":{"phon":"det","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a sum of money that somebody owes","cn":"借款；欠款；债务","g":"[countable]","lab":"informal","ex":{"en":"to pay/repay a debt","cn":"偿还债务"}},{"en":"the situation of owing money, especially when you cannot pay","cn":"负债情况","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"He died heavily in debt.","cn":"他死时负债累累。"}},{"en":"the fact that you should feel grateful to somebody because they have helped you or been kind to you","cn":"人情债；情义；恩情","g":"[countable, usually singular]","ex":{"en":"I owe them a debt of gratitude that I can never repay.","cn":"我欠他们一份永远无法偿还的恩情。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"债务;欠款","en":"A debt is a sum of money that you owe someone.","ex":{"en":"Three years later, he is still paying off his debts","cn":"都3年了，他仍在偿还债务。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"负债（状态）","en":"Debt is the state of owing money.","ex":{"en":"Stress is a main reason for debt.","cn":"重压是负债的一个主要原因。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(表示感激）我欠你个人情/我受你的恩惠","en":"You use debt in expressions such as I owe you a debt or I am in your debt when you are expressing gratitude for something that someone has done for you.","ex":{"en":"He was so good to me that I can never repay the debt I owe him","cn":"他对我太好了，我永远也还不清这份人情。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/debt__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/debt__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The club is £4 million in debt.","cn":"这家俱乐部负债 400 万英镑。"},{"en":"I would like to acknowledge my debt to my teachers.","cn":"我想向我的老师表达我的感激之情。"}]},"dedicated":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/dedicated__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/dedicated__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdedɪkeɪtɪd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"working hard at something because it is very important to you","cn":"献身的；专心致志的；一心一意的","ex":{"en":"a dedicated teacher","cn":"富有献身精神的教师"}},{"en":"designed to do only one particular type of work; used for one particular purpose only","cn":"专用的；专门用途的","g":"[only before noun]","ex":{"en":"Software is exported through a dedicated satellite link.","cn":"软件通过专用卫星链路出口。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"献身的;一心一意的;热忱的","en":"You use dedicated to describe someone who enjoys a particular activity very much and spends a lot of time doing it.","ex":{"en":"Her great-grandfather had clearly been a dedicated and stoical traveller.","cn":"她的曾祖父显然是一位非常投入而且坚忍不拔的旅行爱好者。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"专用（于…）的;专门（为…而）设计制造的","en":"You use dedicated to describe something that is made, built, or designed for one particular purpose or thing.","ex":{"en":"Such areas should also be served by dedicated cycle routes.","cn":"这些区域也应该设专门的自行车道。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Software is exported through a dedicated satellite link.","cn":"软件通过专用卫星线路出口。"},{"en":"She is dedicated to her job.","cn":"她对工作专心致志。"}],"base":"dedicate"},"develops":{"lemma":"develop","media":{"uk":"media/uk/develop__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/develop__us_1.mp3"}},"devote":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/devote__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/devote__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈvəʊt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to give most of your time, energy, attention, etc. to sb/sth","cn":"献身；致力；专心"},{"en":"to give an amount of time, attention, etc. to sth","cn":"把 … 用于"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"献（身）；奉献，投入(时间、精力等)","en":"If you devote yourself, your time, or your energy to something, you spend all or most of your time or energy on it.","ex":{"en":"He decided to devote the rest of his life to scientific investigation","cn":"他决定将自己的余生献给科学研究事业。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"将(文章或讲话的某一部分)专用（于）","en":"If you devote a particular proportion of a piece of writing or a speech to a particular subject, you deal with the subject in that amount of space or time.","ex":{"en":"He devoted a major section of his massive report to an analysis of US aircraft design","cn":"在他的长篇报告中，他用了很大的篇幅来分析美国飞机的设计。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"I could only devote two hours a day to the work.","cn":"我一天只能在这个工作上花两个小时。"},{"en":"She devoted herself to her career.","cn":"她全力倾注于自己的事业。"}]},"decisive":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/decisive__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/decisive__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈsaɪsɪv","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"very important for the final result of a particular situation","cn":"决定性的；关键的","ex":{"en":"a decisive factor/victory/battle","cn":"决定性的因素／胜利／战役"}},{"en":"able to decide something quickly and with confidence","cn":"坚决的；果断的；决断的","ex":{"en":"decisive management","cn":"果断的管理层"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"决定性的;关键的;明确的","en":"If a fact, action, or event is decisive, it makes it certain that there will be a particular result.","ex":{"en":"...his decisive victory in the presidential elections","cn":"他在总统大选中取得的压倒性胜利"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"果断的;决断的","en":"If someone is decisive, they have or show an ability to make quick decisions in a difficult or complicated situation.","ex":{"en":"He should give way to a younger, more decisive leader.","cn":"他应该让位于更年轻、更有决断力的领导者。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The government must take decisive action on gun control.","cn":"政府必须在枪支管制方面采取果断措施。"},{"en":"a decisive step (= an important action that will change a situation) towards a cleaner environment","cn":"朝着更清洁的环境迈出的关键一步"}]},"devotion":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/devotion__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/devotion__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈvəʊʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"great love, care and support for somebody/something","cn":"挚爱；关爱；关照","g":"[uncountable, singular]","ex":{"en":"His devotion to his wife and family is touching.","cn":"他对妻子和家人的关爱感人至深。"}},{"en":"the action of spending a lot of time or energy on something","cn":"奉献；忠诚；专心；热心","g":"[uncountable, singular]","ex":{"en":"her devotion to duty","cn":"她对职责的忠诚"}},{"en":"religious worship","cn":"（宗教的）虔诚，崇拜","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"The statue of the emperor became an object of devotion.","cn":"皇帝的雕像成了人们敬拜的对象。"}},{"en":"prayers and other religious practices","cn":"宗教敬拜","g":"[plural]","ex":{"en":"She went to her devotions.","cn":"她去参加灵修活动。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"深爱;挚爱;仰慕","en":"Devotion is great love, affection, or admiration for someone.","ex":{"en":"At first she was flattered by his devotion.","cn":"刚开始他的爱慕让她感到荣幸。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"献身;奉献","en":"Devotion is commitment to a particular activity.","ex":{"en":"...devotion to the cause of the people and to socialism","cn":"献身于人民的事业，献身于社会主义"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"（对宗教的）虔诚","en":"Devotion is religious worship or strong religious feeling.","ex":{"en":"He was kneeling by his bed in an attitude of devotion.","cn":"他虔诚地跪在床边。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Her devotion to the job left her with very little free time.","cn":"她全身心投入工作，几乎没有闲暇。"},{"en":"His devotion to his wife and family is touching.","cn":"他对妻子和家人的关爱感人至深。"}]},"destroying":{"lemma":"destroy"},"degree":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/degree__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/degree__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈɡriː","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a unit for measuring temperature","cn":"度，度数（温度单位）","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"Water freezes at 32 degrees Fahrenheit (32°F) or zero/nought degrees Celsius (0°C).","cn":"水在 32 华氏度或零摄氏度结冰。"}},{"en":"a unit for measuring angles","cn":"度，度数（角的量度单位）","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"an angle of ninety degrees (90°)","cn":"90 度角"}},{"en":"the amount or level of something","cn":"程度","g":"[countable, uncountable]","ex":{"en":"Her job demands a high degree of skill.","cn":"她的工作要求有高超的技能。"}},{"en":"the qualification obtained by students who successfully complete a university or college course","cn":"（大学）学位","g":"[countable]","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"My brother has a master's degree from Harvard.","cn":"我哥哥有哈佛大学的硕士学位。"}},{"en":"a university or college course, normally lasting three years or more","cn":"（大学通常三年或以上的）学位课程","g":"[countable]","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"I'm hoping to do a chemistry degree.","cn":"我希望攻读化学学位课程。"}},{"en":"a level in a scale of how serious something is","cn":"严重程度（或级别）","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"murder in the first degree (= of the most serious kind)","cn":"一级谋杀（最严重）"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"程度;级别","en":"You use degree to indicate the extent to which something happens or is the case, or the amount which something is felt.","ex":{"en":"These man-made barriers will ensure a very high degree of protection","cn":"这些人造屏障将会确保提供高度的保护。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"（表示相对的数量、规模或范围）程度问题/ 程度上不同","en":"You use degree in expressions such as a matter of degree and different in degree to indicate that you are talking about the comparative quantity, scale, or extent of something, rather than other factors.","ex":{"en":"The first change is a matter of degree, the second is a fundamental shift","cn":"第一个改变只是程度上的变化，而第二个则是根本性的转变。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(温度的)度，度数","en":"A degree is a unit of measurement that is used to measure temperatures. It is often written as ˚, for example 23˚.","ex":{"en":"It's over 80 degrees outside","cn":"外面的温度超过了 80 度。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"度，度数(可以表示角度、经度、纬度等)","en":"A degree is a unit of measurement that is used to measure angles, and also longitude and latitude. It is often written as as '˚', for example 23˚.","ex":{"en":"It was pointing outward at an angle of 45 degrees.","cn":"它向外指向 45 度角的方向。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"学位课程;学位;学衔","en":"A degree at a university or college is a course of study that you take there, or the qualification that you get when you have passed the course.","ex":{"en":"He took a master's degree in economics at Yale.","cn":"他选择了攻读耶鲁大学的经济学硕士学位。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"逐渐地;慢慢地","en":"If something happens by degrees, it happens slowly and gradually.","ex":{"en":"The crowd in Robinson's Coffee-House was thinning, but only by degrees.","cn":"鲁宾逊咖啡屋里的人正在变少，但也只是渐少而已。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"在一定/很大/ 某种程度上","en":"You use expressions such as to some degree ,to a large degree, or to a certain degree in order to indicate that something is partly true, but not entirely true.","ex":{"en":"These statements are, to some degree, all correct.","cn":"这些声明从某种程度上来说全都属实。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"到…的程度;在…程度上","en":"You use expressions such as to what degree and to the degree that when you are discussing how true a statement is, or in what ways it is true.","ex":{"en":"To what degree would you say you had control over things that went on?","cn":"你认为发生的事情在多大程度上是在你的掌控之下？"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"to the nth degree→see: ;"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Most pop music is influenced, to a greater or lesser degree, by the blues.","cn":"多数流行音乐都不同程度地受到布鲁斯音乐的影响。"},{"en":"To what degree can parents be held responsible for a child's behaviour?","cn":"父母应在多大程度上对孩子的行为负责呢？"}]},"deals":{"lemma":"deal","media":{"uk":"media/uk/deal__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deal__us_1.mp3"}},"detail":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/detail__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/detail__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdiːteɪl","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a small individual fact or item; a less important fact or item","cn":"细微之处；枝节；琐事","g":"[countable]","sc":"facts/information","ex":{"en":"an expedition planned down to the last detail","cn":"计划详尽的探险"}},{"en":"the small facts or features of something, when you consider them all together","cn":"详情；细节","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"facts/information","ex":{"en":"The report was criticized for its lack of detail.","cn":"这份报告因缺少细节而受到批评。"}},{"en":"information about something","cn":"具体情况；（关于某事物的）资料，消息","g":"[plural]","sc":"facts/information","ex":{"en":"Please provide the following details: name, age and sex.","cn":"请提供以下详情：姓名、年龄和性别。"}},{"en":"a small part of a picture or painting; the smaller or less important parts of a picture, pattern, etc. when you consider them all together","cn":"（照片、绘画等的）细部，局部，次要部分","g":"[countable, uncountable]","sc":"small parts","ex":{"en":"This is a detail from the 1844 Turner painting.","cn":"这是透纳 1844 年画作的局部。"}},{"en":"a group of soldiers given special duties","cn":"特遣队；小分队；支队","g":"[countable]","sc":"soldiers"},{"en":"to give a list of facts or all the available information about something","cn":"详细列举；详细说明；详述","sc":"give facts/information","ex":{"en":"The brochure details all the hotels in the area and their facilities.","cn":"这本小册子详细介绍了当地所有旅馆及其设施。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to give an official order to somebody, especially a soldier, to do a particular task","cn":"派遣；选派；分遣","g":"[often passive]","sc":"order soldier","ex":{"en":"Several of the men were detailed to form a search party.","cn":"几个人被派组成一个搜索队。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to clean a car carefully and completely","cn":"彻底清洗（汽车）","lab":"North American English","sc":"clean car","ex":{"en":"He got work for a while detailing cars.","cn":"他干了一段时间的清洗汽车的工作。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"细节","en":"The details of something are its individual features or elements.","ex":{"en":"The details of the plan are still being worked out","cn":"计划的细节仍在制订中。"}},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"详情;信息;资料","en":"Details about someone or something are facts or pieces of information about them.","ex":{"en":"See the bottom of this page for details of how to apply for this exciting offer","cn":"有关如何申请这一令人兴奋的工作的详情请参见本页底部。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"枝节;末节;琐事","en":"A detail is a minor point or aspect of something, as opposed to the central ones.","ex":{"en":"Only minor details now remain to be settled.","cn":"现在仅剩一些细枝末节的问题需要解决。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(难以觉察的)细微之处","en":"You can refer to the small features of something which are often not noticed as detail .","ex":{"en":"We like his attention to detail and his enthusiasm.","cn":"我们喜欢他的细心和热情。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(画等的)细部","en":"A detail of a picture is a part of it that is printed separately and perhaps made bigger, so that smaller features can be clearly seen."},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"详述;详细列举（或说明）","en":"If you detail things, you list them or give information about them.","ex":{"en":"The report detailed the human rights abuses committed during the war.","cn":"这份报告详述了战争期间所发生的践踏人权的情况。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"派遣;指示","en":"If someone is detailed to do a task or job, they are officially ordered to do it.","ex":{"en":"He detailed a constable to take it to the Incident Room.","cn":"他派了一名警察把它送到重案调查室。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"详细叙述;逐一说明","en":"If someone does not go into details about a subject, or does not go into the detail, they mention it without explaining it fully or properly.","ex":{"en":"He said he had been in various parts of Britain but did not go into details","cn":"他说曾去过英国的许多地方，但没有细讲。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"详细地;全面地;仔细地","en":"If you examine or discuss something in detail, you do it thoroughly and carefully.","ex":{"en":"We examine the wording in detail before deciding on the final text.","cn":"我们彻底仔细地检查了措词后才最终定稿。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"‘We had a terrible time — ’ ‘Oh, spare me the details (= don't tell me any more). ’ “","cn":"我们倒霉透了 — ” “唉呀，别给我细说了。”"},{"en":"He stood still, absorbing every detail of the street.","cn":"他一动不动地站着，不放过街上的每一细微之处。"}]},"despair":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈspeə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the feeling of having lost all hope","cn":"绝望","ex":{"en":"She uttered a cry of despair.","cn":"她发出了绝望的叫声。"}},{"en":"to stop having any hope that a situation will change or improve","cn":"绝望；失去希望；丧失信心","ex":{"en":"Don't despair! We'll think of a way out of this.","cn":"别灰心！我们会找到出路的。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"绝望","en":"Despair is the feeling that everything is wrong and that nothing will improve.","ex":{"en":"I looked at my wife in despair","cn":"我绝望地看着妻子。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"感到绝望;失去希望","en":"If you despair, you feel that everything is wrong and that nothing will improve.","ex":{"en":"'Oh, I despair sometimes,' he says in mock sorrow","cn":"“啊，我有时会感到绝望，”他假装悲伤地说。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"对…感到绝望;对…不抱希望","en":"If you despair of something, you feel that there is no hope that it will happen or improve. If you despair of someone, you feel that there is no hope that they will improve.","ex":{"en":"He wished to earn a living through writing but despaired of doing so.","cn":"他想通过写作来谋生，不过他对此不抱希望。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/despair__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/despair__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"I despair of him; he can't keep a job for more than six months.","cn":"我对他都绝望了，他做任何工作都不超过半年。"},{"en":"One harsh word would send her into the depths of despair.","cn":"一句严厉的话就会使她陷入极度的绝望之中。"}]},"description":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/description__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/description__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈskrɪpʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a piece of writing or speech that says what somebody/something is like; the act of writing or saying in words what somebody/something is like","cn":"描写（文字）；形容；说明","ex":{"en":"Follow the link below for a more detailed description.","cn":"请点击下面的链接，获取更详细的说明。"}},{"en":"of some, etc. type","cn":"类型","ex":{"en":"In the bay were boats of every description.","cn":"海湾里停满了各种各样的船只。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"描述;形容;叙述;说明","en":"A description of someone or something is an account which explains what they are or what they look like.","ex":{"en":"Police have issued a description of the man who was aged between fifty and sixty","cn":"警方已经发布了那名年龄在 50 到 60 岁之间的男子的相貌特征通告。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"种类;类型;性质","en":"If something is of a particular description, it belongs to the general class of items that are mentioned.","ex":{"en":"...the oldest Catholic church of any description in England","cn":"英国所有天主教堂中最古老的一座"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"无法描述；难以形容","en":"You can say that something is beyond description, or that it defies description, to emphasize that it is very unusual, impressive, terrible, or extreme.","ex":{"en":"His face is weary beyond description","cn":"他一脸难以形容的疲惫。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"A child answering the description of the missing boy was found safe and well in London yesterday.","cn":"昨天在伦敦发现了一个与失踪男孩情况相符的孩子，安然无恙。"},{"en":"‘Scared stiff’ is an apt description of how I felt at that moment. “","cn":"吓得呆若木鸡”是我当时感受的贴切描述。"}]},"deference":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/deference__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deference__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdefərəns","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"behaviour that shows that you respect somebody/something","cn":"尊重；遵从；听从","ex":{"en":"The women wore veils in deference to the customs of the country.","cn":"这些妇女戴着面纱是遵从这个国家的习俗。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"（尤指对位重者的）敬重，尊敬，遵从","en":"Deference is a polite and respectful attitude towards someone, especially because they have an important position.","ex":{"en":"The old sense of deference and restraint in royal reporting has vanished","cn":"在对皇室进行的新闻报道中，那种由来已久的尊重和收敛意识已经消失了。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The women wore veils in deference to the customs of the country.","cn":"这些妇女戴着面纱是遵从这个国家的习俗。"},{"en":"The flags were lowered out of deference to the bereaved family.","cn":"降旗是出于对死者家属的尊重。"}]},"december":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/december__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/december__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈsembə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the 12th and last month of the year","cn":"十二月","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"She was born in December.","cn":"她是在12月出生的。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"十二月","en":"December is the twelfth and last month of the year in the Western calendar.","ex":{"en":"...a bright morning in mid-December","cn":"12 月中旬的一个明媚的早晨"}}]}},"delete":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈliːt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to remove something that has been written or printed, or that has been stored on a computer","cn":"删去；删除","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"Your name has been deleted from the list.","cn":"你的名字已从名单上删掉。"}},{"en":"a key or command on a computer, phone, etc. that removes text, records or images","cn":"（计算机、手机等的）删除（键），删除命令","ex":{"en":"Just use delete to remove a specific record from the database.","cn":"只需使用删除即可从数据库中删除特定记录。"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"删除;画掉","en":"If you delete something that has been written down or stored in a computer, you cross it out or remove it.","ex":{"en":"He also deleted files from the computer system","cn":"他还从计算机系统里删除了文件。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/delete__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/delete__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"This command deletes files from the directory.","cn":"这一指令把文档从目录中删除。"},{"en":"( BrE ) Mr/Mrs/Ms ( delete as appropriate )","cn":"先生/太太/女士（酌情删除）"}]},"definite":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/definite__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/definite__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdefɪnət","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"sure or certain; unlikely to change","cn":"肯定的；确定的；不会改变的","ex":{"en":"Can you give me a definite answer by tomorrow?","cn":"你最晚明天能给我一个确定的答复吗？"}},{"en":"easily or clearly seen or understood; obvious","cn":"清楚的；明显的","ex":{"en":"The look on her face was a definite sign that something was wrong.","cn":"一看她的神色就知道出事了。"}},{"en":"sure that something is true or that something is going to happen and stating it to other people","cn":"肯定；有把握","g":"[not before noun]","ex":{"en":"I'm definite about this.","cn":"我对这事毫无疑问。"}},{"en":"something that you are certain about or that you know will happen; somebody who is sure to do something","cn":"肯定的事（或人）","ex":{"en":"‘We're moving our office to Glasgow.’ ‘That's a definite, is it?’","cn":"“我们的办事处要搬到格拉斯哥去。”“这事儿定了，是吗？”"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"明确的;确定的","en":"If something such as a decision or an arrangement is definite, it is firm and clear, and unlikely to be changed.","ex":{"en":"It's too soon to give a definite answer","cn":"要给出一个明确的答复，现在还为时过早。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(证据或信息)确凿的，确切的","en":"Definite evidence or information is true, rather than being someone's opinion or guess.","ex":{"en":"We didn't have any definite proof","cn":"我们没有任何确实的证据。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"清楚的;明显的;无疑的","en":"You use definite to emphasize the strength of your opinion or belief.","ex":{"en":"There has already been a definite improvement","cn":"已经有了显著的改进。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"肯定的;有把握的","en":"Someone who is definite behaves or talks in a firm, confident way.","ex":{"en":"Mary is very definite about this.","cn":"玛丽对此非常肯定。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"清晰的;分明的","en":"A definite shape or colour is clear and noticeable.","ex":{"en":"Studying his face in the bathroom mirror he wished he had more definite features.","cn":"看着浴室镜子中的脸，他真希望自己的五官能够更分明一些。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"‘We're moving our office to Glasgow.’ ‘That's a definite, is it?’ “","cn":"我们的办事处要搬到格拉斯哥去。” “这事儿定了，是吗？”"},{"en":"‘Is Sarah coming to the party?’ ‘Yes, she's a definite.’ “","cn":"萨拉要来参加聚会吗？” “是的，她肯定来。”"}]},"deadline":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdedlaɪn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a point in time by which something must be done","cn":"最后期限；截止日期","ex":{"en":"I prefer to work to a deadline.","cn":"我喜欢按规定的期限完成工作。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"最后期限;截止时间","en":"A deadline is a time or date before which a particular task must be finished or a particular thing must be done.","ex":{"en":"We were not able to meet the deadline because of manufacturing delays","cn":"因为制造方面的延误，我们没能赶上最后期限。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/deadline__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deadline__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The deadline for applications is 30 April.","cn":"交申请书的截止日期是 4 月 30 日。"},{"en":"the January 15 deadline set by the United Nations","cn":"联合国规定的 1 月 15 日最后期限"}]},"defense":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"→see: ;"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/defense__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/defense__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfens","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the act of protecting somebody/something from attack, criticism, etc.","cn":"防御；保护；保卫","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"protection against attack","ex":{"en":"soldiers who died in defense of their country","cn":"为保卫国家而牺牲的士兵"}},{"en":"something that provides protection against attack from enemies, the weather, illness, etc.","cn":"防御物；防务；防御能力","g":"[countable, uncountable]","sc":"protection against attack","ex":{"en":"They are responsible for maintaining coastal flood defenses.","cn":"他们负责维护沿海防洪。"}},{"en":"the organization of the people and systems that are used by a government to protect a country from attack","cn":"国防机构；国防体系","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"US English","sc":"protection against attack","ex":{"en":"the Department of Defense","cn":"国防部"}},{"en":"something that is said or written in order to support something","cn":"辩解；辩白","g":"[countable]","sc":"support","ex":{"en":"a defense of Marxism","cn":"对马克思主义的捍卫"}},{"en":"what is said in court to prove that a person did not commit a crime; the act of presenting this argument in court","cn":"辩护；辩词；答辩","g":"[countable, usually singular]","sc":"law","ex":{"en":"Her defense was that she was somewhere completely different at the time of the crime.","cn":"她的辩护是，案发时她身处完全不同的地方。"}},{"en":"the lawyer or lawyers whose job is to prove in court that a person did not commit a crime","cn":"辩护律师","g":"[singular + singular or plural verb]","sc":"law","ex":{"en":"The defense requested more time to prepare their case.","cn":"辩方要求更多时间准备案情。"}},{"en":"the players who must prevent the other team from scoring; the position of these players on the sports field","cn":"防守队员；防守；后卫","g":"[singular, uncountable]","lab":"North American English","sc":"in sport","ex":{"en":"Lattimore cut through the defense for a 52-yard touchdown.","cn":"拉铁摩尔突破防守，完成 52 码达阵。"}},{"en":"a contest, game, etc. in which the previous winner or winners compete in order to try to win again","cn":"卫冕赛","g":"[countable]","sc":"in sport","ex":{"en":"Osaka begins her defense of the US Open title.","cn":"大阪开始卫冕美国公开赛冠军。"}}]}},"depression":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/depression__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/depression__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpreʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a medical condition in which a person feels very sad, anxious and without hope and often has physical symptoms such as being unable to sleep, etc.","cn":"抑郁症","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"She was diagnosed as having clinical depression.","cn":"她被诊断患有临床抑郁症。"}},{"en":"the state of feeling very sad and without hope","cn":"抑郁；沮丧；消沉","g":"[uncountable, countable]","ex":{"en":"There was a feeling of gloom and depression in the office when the news of the job cuts was announced.","cn":"裁员消息宣布时办公室里一片忧郁和沮丧的气氛。"}},{"en":"a period when there is little economic activity and many people are poor or without jobs","cn":"萧条期；（经济）衰退；不景气","g":"[countable, uncountable]","ex":{"en":"The country was in the grip of (an) economic depression.","cn":"当时国家处于经济萧条期。"}},{"en":"a part of a surface that is lower than the parts around it","cn":"洼地；凹地；坑","g":"[countable]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"Rainwater collects in shallow depressions on the ground.","cn":"雨水积在地上的浅坑里。"}},{"en":"a weather condition in which the pressure of the air becomes lower, often causing rain","cn":"低气压；气压降低","g":"[countable]","lab":"specialist","ex":{"en":"an atmospheric depression moving east from the Atlantic","cn":"从大西洋向东移动的低气压"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"抑郁;沮丧;消沉","en":"Depression is a mental state in which you are sad and feel that you cannot enjoy anything, because your situation is so difficult and unpleasant.","ex":{"en":"Mr Thomas was suffering from depression","cn":"托马斯先生患有抑郁症。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"萧条（期）；不景气","en":"A depression is a time when there is very little economic activity, which causes a lot of unemployment and poverty.","ex":{"en":"He never forgot the hardships he witnessed during the Great Depression of the 1930s.","cn":"他永远不会忘记 20 世纪 30 年代经济大萧条时期他所亲眼目睹的困苦情形。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"凹陷;凹坑;洼地","en":"A depression in a surface is an area which is lower than the parts surrounding it.","ex":{"en":"...an area pockmarked by rain-filled depressions.","cn":"密布着雨水洼的地区"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"低气压","en":"A depression is a mass of air that has a low pressure and that often causes rain."}]},"examples":[{"en":"There was a feeling of gloom and depression in the office when the news of the job cuts was announced.","cn":"裁员消息宣布时办公室里一片忧郁和沮丧的气氛。"},{"en":"the great Depression of the 1930s * 20","cn":"世纪 30 年代的经济大萧条"}]},"deserves":{"lemma":"deserve","media":{"uk":"media/uk/deserve__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deserve__us_1.mp3"}},"dean":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/dean__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/dean__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"diːn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a priest of high rank who is in charge of the other priests in a cathedral","cn":"座堂主任牧师"},{"en":"a priest who is in charge of the priests of several churches in an area","cn":"（乡间主管若干教堂牧师的）主任牧师","lab":"British English"},{"en":"a person in a university who is in charge of a department of studies","cn":"（大学的）学院院长，系主任","ex":{"en":"the dean of the Faculty of Medicine","cn":"医学院院长"}},{"en":"(in a college or university, especially at Oxford or Cambridge) a person who is responsible for the discipline of students","cn":"（大学，尤指牛津、剑桥大学的）学监"},{"en":"the most respected or most experienced member of a group or profession","cn":"（某团体或职业中的）老前辈，资格最老者，元老","lab":"North American English"},{"en":"a first name for boys","cn":"迪安（男子名）","pos":""}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(大学或学院的）院长，教务长","en":"A dean is an important official at a university or college.","ex":{"en":"She was Dean of the Science faculty at Sophia University.","cn":"她是上智大学科学院的院长。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"教长;座堂主任牧师","en":"A dean is a priest who is the main administrator of a large church.","ex":{"en":"...Alan Webster, former Dean of St Paul's.","cn":"艾伦·韦伯斯特，圣保罗大教堂前教长"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"泰斗;首席;资历最深者","en":"The dean of a group is the most important member of that group.","ex":{"en":"...Aaron Copland, who was known as the dean of American composers.","cn":"阿隆·科普兰，美国最资深的作曲家"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Neier is the dean of American human rights activism.","cn":""}]},"develop":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/develop__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/develop__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈveləp","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to gradually grow or become bigger, more advanced, stronger, etc.; to make something do this","cn":"（使）成长，发展，壮大","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"grow/improve","ex":{"en":"From birth to age 5, a child's brain develops rapidly.","cn":"从出生到5岁，孩子的大脑发育迅速。"}},{"en":"to start to have a skill, ability, quality, etc. that becomes better and stronger; to become better and stronger","cn":"加强；增强；发挥","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","sc":"grow/improve","ex":{"en":"He's developed a real flair for management.","cn":"他在管理方面已经变得很有一套。"}},{"en":"to think of or produce a new idea, product, etc. and make it successful","cn":"开发；研制","g":"[transitive]","sc":"new idea/product","ex":{"en":"The company develops and markets new software.","cn":"这家公司开发并销售新软件。"}},{"en":"to begin to have something such as a disease or a problem; to start to affect somebody/something","cn":"患（病）；出现（问题）；（疾病）开始侵袭；（问题）开始影响","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","sc":"disease/problem","ex":{"en":"She developed lung cancer at the age of sixty.","cn":"她六十岁时患上肺癌。"}},{"en":"to start to happen or change, especially in a bad way","cn":"（尤指开始向坏的方面）发展，变化","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"happen/change","ex":{"en":"A crisis was rapidly developing in the Gulf.","cn":"海湾危机迅速加剧。"}},{"en":"to build new houses, factories, etc. on an area of land, especially land that was not being used effectively before","cn":"修建；开发","g":"[transitive]","sc":"build houses","ex":{"en":"The site is being developed by a French company.","cn":"这块地正由一家法国公司开发利用。"}},{"en":"to build or improve a building or other facilities","cn":"创建；改进","g":"[transitive]","sc":"create/improve facilities","ex":{"en":"The company is developing a chain of hotels.","cn":"公司正在创建连锁酒店。"}},{"en":"to become economically and socially more advanced","cn":"发展","g":"[intransitive]","lab":"economics","sc":"become economically advanced","ex":{"en":"For a country to develop, a good road network is essential.","cn":"一个国家要发展，良好的道路网络必不可少。"}},{"en":"to add further explanation or details to an idea, story or musical theme","cn":"阐明（思想）；展开（故事或音乐主题）","g":"[transitive]","sc":"idea/story/musical theme","ex":{"en":"She develops the theme more fully in her later books.","cn":"她在后来写的书中更详尽地阐明了这个主题。"}},{"en":"to treat film that has been used to take photographs with chemicals so that the pictures can be seen","cn":"使（胶卷）显影；显像；冲洗（胶片）","g":"[transitive]","sc":"photographs","ex":{"en":"When Lewis developed the film, he was astonished by what he saw.","cn":"当刘易斯冲洗胶片时，他对所看到的感到惊讶。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"发展;成长;发育;生长","en":"When something develops, it grows or changes over a period of time and usually becomes more advanced, complete, or severe.","ex":{"en":"As children develop, some of the most important things they learn have to do with their sense of self","cn":"在成长过程中，孩子学到的一些最重要的东西与他们的自我意识有关。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(问题或困难)出现，产生","en":"If a problem or difficulty develops, it begins to occur.","ex":{"en":"A huge row has developed about the pollution emanating from a chemical plant.","cn":"一家化工厂造成的污染已经引发了激烈争论。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(国家从贫穷的农业国向富有的工业国)发展","en":"If you say that a country develops, you mean that it changes from being a poor agricultural country to being a rich industrial country.","ex":{"en":"All countries, it was predicted, would develop and develop fast.","cn":"据预测，所有国家都会实现发展而且发展速度会很快。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"（使）（企业或行业）发展；（使）扩展；（使）壮大","en":"If you develop a business or industry, or if it develops, it becomes bigger and more successful.","ex":{"en":"She won a grant to develop her own business","cn":"她赢得了一笔拨款，用以扩展自己的企业。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"开发(土地或地产)","en":"To develop land or property means to make it more profitable, by building houses or factories or by improving the existing buildings.","ex":{"en":"Entrepreneurs developed fashionable restaurants and bars in the area.","cn":"实业家在这一地区建起了许多时尚的餐馆和酒吧。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"养成(习惯);获得(名声);形成(信仰)","en":"If you develop a habit, reputation, or belief, you start to have it and it then becomes stronger or more noticeable.","ex":{"en":"She later developed a taste for expensive nightclubs","cn":"她后来逐渐变得喜欢去消费高昂的夜总会。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"（使）提高;（使）加强","en":"If you develop a skill, quality, or relationship, or if it develops, it becomes better or stronger.","ex":{"en":"Now you have an opportunity to develop a greater understanding of each other","cn":"现在你们有一个好机会，可以大大增进对彼此的了解。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"患(病);得(病)","en":"If you develop an illness, or if it develops, you become affected by it.","ex":{"en":"The test should identify which smokers are most prone to develop lung cancer","cn":"这项检查应该可以确认哪些吸烟者更容易得肺癌。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"发生(故障等)","en":"If a piece of equipment develops a fault, it starts to have the fault.","ex":{"en":"The aircraft made an unscheduled landing after developing an electrical fault.","cn":"飞机由于发生电力故障而作了临时降落。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"研制(新产品)","en":"If someone develops a new product, they design it and produce it.","ex":{"en":"He claims that several countries have developed nuclear weapons secretly.","cn":"他声称有几个国家已经秘密研制出了核武器。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"阐释(想法、理论、故事或主题)；（使）展开；（使）完善","en":"If you develop an idea, theory, story, or theme, or if it develops, it gradually becomes more detailed, advanced, or complex.","ex":{"en":"I would like to thank them for allowing me to develop their original idea","cn":"我想感谢他们允许我深入完善他们最初的想法。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"冲洗(胶片);使显影","en":"To develop photographs means to make negatives or prints from a photographic film.","ex":{"en":"...after developing one roll of film.","cn":"冲洗了一卷胶卷后"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The place has rapidly developed from a small fishing community into a thriving tourist resort.","cn":"这地方由原来的小渔村迅速发展成一个繁荣的旅游胜地。"},{"en":"We need more time to see how things develop before we take action.","cn":"我们采取行动之前需要有更多时间观察情况的发展。"}]},"desks":{"lemma":"desk","media":{"uk":"media/uk/desk__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/desk__us_1.mp3"}},"demise":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/demise__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/demise__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈmaɪz","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the end or failure of an institution, an idea, a company, etc.","cn":"终止；失败；倒闭","ex":{"en":"He praised the union's aims but predicted its early demise.","cn":"他对联盟的目标表示赞赏，但预言联盟很快会失败。"}},{"en":"death","cn":"死亡；逝世；一命呜呼","lab":"formal or humorous","ex":{"en":"his imminent/sudden/sad demise","cn":"他死到临头；他的猝死；他悲惨的死亡"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"终止;消亡;死亡","en":"The demise of something or someone is their end or death.","ex":{"en":"...the demise of the reform movement","cn":"改革运动的消亡"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"his imminent/sudden/sad demise","cn":"他死到临头；他的猝死；他悲惨的死亡"},{"en":"the imminent demise (= happening soon ) of the local newspaper","cn":"地方报纸的即将停刊"}]},"decayed":{"lemma":"decay","media":{"uk":"media/uk/decay__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/decay__us_1.mp3"}},"derail":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/derail__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/derail__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"diːˈreɪl","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to leave the track; to make a train do this","cn":"（使）脱轨，出轨","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","ex":{"en":"The train derailed and plunged into the river.","cn":"火车脱轨栽进了河里。"}},{"en":"to stop a process from continuing in the way it was intended to","cn":"扰乱…的进程；阻断","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"This latest incident could derail the peace process.","cn":"最近这个事件可能会扰乱和平进程。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"阻挠;使离开正常进程","en":"To derail something such as a plan or a series of negotiations means to prevent it from continuing as planned.","ex":{"en":"The present wave of political killings is the work of people trying to derail peace talks.","cn":"当前的这一系列政治谋杀乃是那些想阻挠和平谈判的人所为。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"(使)(火车)出轨;（使）脱轨","en":"If a train is derailed or if it derails, it comes off the track on which it is running.","ex":{"en":"Several people were injured today when a train was derailed","cn":"今天有数人在一列火车出轨时受了伤。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"( figurative ) This latest incident could derail the peace process.","cn":"最近这个事件可能会扰乱和平进程。"},{"en":"The train derailed and plunged into the river.","cn":"火车脱轨栽进了河里。"}]},"deb":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"同 debutante","en":"A deb is the same as a debutante ."}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/deb__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deb__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"deb","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a debutante (= a young, rich or upper-class woman who is going to fashionable social events for the first time)","cn":"初次登台的人"},{"en":"a first name for girls, short for Deborah","cn":"德布（女子名，Deborahl 缩写）","pos":""}]}},"deer":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an animal with long legs that eats grass, leaves, etc. and can run fast. Most male deer have antlers (= parts on their heads that are like branches in shape). There are many types of deer.","cn":"鹿","ex":{"en":"a herd of deer","cn":"一群鹿"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"鹿","en":"A deer is a large wild animal that eats grass and leaves. A male deer usually has large, branching horns."}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/deer__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deer__us_1.mp3","img":["media/ldoce/img/deer.jpg"]},"examples":[{"en":"a herd of deer","cn":"一群鹿"},{"en":"a deer park","cn":"鹿苑"}]},"delusion":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/delusion__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/delusion__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈluːʒn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a false belief or opinion about yourself or your situation","cn":"错觉；谬见；妄想","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"Don't go getting delusions of grandeur (= a belief that you are more important than you actually are).","cn":"不要变得妄自尊大。"}},{"en":"the act of believing or making yourself believe something that is not true","cn":"自欺","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"He seems to have retreated into a world of fear and delusion.","cn":"他似乎退回到了一个充满恐惧和幻想的世界。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"错觉;谬见;误会","en":"A delusion is a false idea.","ex":{"en":"I was under the delusion that he intended to marry me.","cn":"我误认为他要娶我。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"妄想;幻想","en":"Delusion is the state of believing things that are not true.","ex":{"en":"This was not optimism, it was delusion.","cn":"这不是乐观，这是妄想。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"妄自尊大;自以为是","en":"If someone has delusions of grandeur, they think and behave as if they are much more important or powerful than they really are.","ex":{"en":"He suggested that we suffer delusions of grandeur as a football nation.","cn":"他暗示我们妄自尊大地以为自己是个足球民族。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Don't go getting delusions of grandeur (= a belief that you are more important than you actually are).","cn":"不要变得妄自尊大。"},{"en":"the delusions of the mentally ill","cn":"精神病患者的妄想"}]},"deck":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/deck__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/deck__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dek","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the top outside floor of a ship or boat","cn":"甲板；舱面","ex":{"en":"I was the only person on deck at that time of night.","cn":"夜里当时只有我一个人在甲板上。"}},{"en":"one of the floors of a ship or a bus","cn":"（船或公共汽车的）一层，层面","ex":{"en":"the upper/lower/main deck of a ship","cn":"船的上层／下层／主甲板"}},{"en":"a floor or platform similar to the deck of a ship","cn":"平台；地面","ex":{"en":"There is an open-air observation deck on the building's top floor.","cn":"大楼顶层有一个露天观景台。"}},{"en":"a complete set of 52 playing cards","cn":"一副（为 52 张）","lab":"both especially North American English"},{"en":"a wooden floor that is built outside the back of a house where you can sit and relax","cn":"（屋后供憩息的）木制平台","lab":"especially North American English","ex":{"en":"After dinner we sat out on the deck.","cn":"晚饭后我们坐在屋外的木头平台上。"}},{"en":"a part of a sound system that records and/or plays sounds on a disc or tape","cn":"（唱机的）转盘装置；（音响系统的）走带机构，录音座","ex":{"en":"a cassette/tape deck","cn":"磁带转动机械装置"}},{"en":"a set of slides (= pages created on a computer that contain text and images) that are used to accompany a person’s presentation","cn":"（计算机上的）一个演示文稿，一套幻灯片","ex":{"en":"Three slides into my 35-slide deck, they asked me to turn off the projector.","cn":"将三张幻灯片放入我的 35 张幻灯片中，他们要求我关闭投影仪。"}},{"en":"to decorate somebody/something with something","cn":"装饰；布置；打扮","g":"[often passive]","ex":{"en":"The room was decked out in flowers and balloons.","cn":"房间里装点着鲜花和气球。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to hit somebody very hard so that they fall to the ground","cn":"用力击倒；打倒在地；揍趴下","lab":"informal","pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(公共汽车、船等的）层面，（一）层","en":"A deck on a vehicle such as a bus or ship is a lower or upper area of it.","ex":{"en":"...sitting on the top deck of the number 13 bus.","cn":"坐在 13 路公共汽车的顶层"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（最上层露天的）甲板，舱面","en":"The deck of a ship is the top part of it that forms a floor in the open air which you can walk on.","ex":{"en":"She stood on the deck and waved.","cn":"她站在甲板上挥手告别。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(录音机的)走带装置，匣仓;(唱机的)转盘支托面","en":"A tape deck or record deck is a piece of equipment on which you play tapes or records.","ex":{"en":"...the tape deck in my car","cn":"我车里的磁带仓"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(纸牌的)一副","en":"A deck of cards is a complete set of playing cards.","ex":{"en":"Matt picked up the cards and shuffled the deck.","cn":"马特把牌拢起来洗牌。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(房屋旁的)木制平台","en":"A deck is a flat wooden area next to a house, where people can sit and relax or eat.","ex":{"en":"A natural timber deck leads into the main room of the home.","cn":"有一个天然的木制平台通到房子的客厅。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"装饰;装点","en":"If something is decked with pretty things, it is decorated with them.","ex":{"en":"Villagers decked the streets with bunting","cn":"村民用彩旗装饰街道。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"击倒;打翻","en":"If someone decks you, they hit you so that you fall over.","ex":{"en":"I hear you decked him and scared the hell out of his buddies.","cn":"我听说你一拳把他打倒在地，吓得他那些狐朋狗友屁滚尿流。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"在甲板下","en":"If someone or something is below decks, they are inside a ship in the part of it that is underneath the deck.","ex":{"en":"The crew of the trawler were gathered below decks.","cn":"托网渔船上的船员被聚集到甲板下。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"清除障碍以准备开始新的工作（或行动）","en":"If you clear the decks, you get ready to start something new by finishing any work that has to be done or getting rid of any problems that are in the way.","ex":{"en":"The hostage release could clear the decks for war.","cn":"人质的获释可能会为发动战争扫清障碍。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"倒在地上","en":"If someone or something hits the deck, they fall to the ground.","ex":{"en":"Andover's body hit the deck.","cn":"安多弗摔倒在地。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：deck out"}]},"examples":[{"en":"As the storm began, everyone disappeared below deck(s).","cn":"暴风雨来临时，所有的人都躲到甲板下面去了。"},{"en":"I was the only person on deck at that time of night.","cn":"夜里当时只有我一个人在甲板上。"}]},"destruction":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/destruction__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/destruction__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈstrʌkʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the act of destroying something; the process of being destroyed","cn":"摧毁；毁灭；破坏","ex":{"en":"the destruction of the rainforests","cn":"对热带雨林的破坏"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"破坏;毁灭;消灭","en":"Destruction is the act of destroying something, or the state of being destroyed.","ex":{"en":"...an international agreement aimed at halting the destruction of the ozone layer.","cn":"一项旨在阻止臭氧层破坏的国际协议"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The central argument is that capitalism sows the seeds of its own destruction (= creates the forces that destroy it).","cn":"主要论点是资本主义播下了自我毁灭的种子。"},{"en":"a tidal wave bringing death and destruction in its wake","cn":"海啸以及随之而来的死亡与破坏"}]},"determines":{"lemma":"determine","media":{"uk":"media/uk/determine__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/determine__us_1.mp3"}},"dentist":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdentɪst","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person whose job is to take care of people’s teeth","cn":"牙科医生","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"to see/visit/consult your dentist","cn":"看牙医；咨询牙医"}},{"en":"a place where a dentist sees patients","cn":"牙科诊所","ex":{"en":"I hate going to the dentist.","cn":"我讨厌去看牙医。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"牙科医生;牙医","en":"A dentist is a person who is qualified to examine and treat people's teeth.","ex":{"en":"Visit your dentist twice a year for a check-up.","cn":"每年去牙医处做两次牙齿检查。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/dentist__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/dentist__us_1.mp3","img":["media/ldoce/img/dentist.jpg"]},"examples":[{"en":"an appointment at the dentist's","cn":"牙科诊所的门诊预约"},{"en":"I’m going to the dentist this afternoon.","cn":"今天下午我要去看牙医。"}]},"definitely":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdefɪnətli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"a way of emphasizing that something is true and that there is no doubt about it","cn":"肯定；没问题；当然；确实","ex":{"en":"I definitely remember sending the letter.","cn":"我记得这封信肯定发出去了。"}},{"en":"in a way that is certain or that shows that you are certain","cn":"确切地；明确地；清楚地","ex":{"en":"The date of the move has not been definitely decided yet (= it may change).","cn":"搬迁日期还未完全确定下来。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADV-GRADED 副词","cn":"清楚地;明显地;肯定地;当然","en":"You use definitely to emphasize that something is the case, or to emphasize the strength of your intention or opinion.","ex":{"en":"I'm definitely going to get in touch with these people","cn":"我肯定会跟这些人取得联系。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"明确地;确定地","en":"If something has been definitely decided, the decision will not be changed.","ex":{"en":"He told them that no venue had yet been definitely decided.","cn":"他告诉他们还没有确定下场地。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/definitely__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/definitely__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"‘Do you plan to have children?’ ‘Definitely not!’ “","cn":"你们打算要孩子吗？” “绝对没这个打算！”"},{"en":"Some old people want help; others most definitely do not.","cn":"有些老人想要得到帮助，有些却根本不需要。"}]},"decorate":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdekəreɪt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to make something look more attractive by putting things on it","cn":"装饰；装潢","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"They decorated the room with flowers and balloons.","cn":"他们用花和气球装饰了房间。"}},{"en":"to put paint, wallpaper, etc. on the walls and ceilings of a room or house","cn":"粉刷；油漆；糊墙纸","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","lab":"especially British English","ex":{"en":"I hate decorating.","cn":"我讨厌粉刷墙壁。"}},{"en":"to be placed on something in order to make it look more attractive","cn":"点缀；装点","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"Photographs of actors decorated the walls of the restaurant.","cn":"演员的照片装点着餐馆的墙壁。"}},{"en":"to give somebody an award or medal as a sign of respect for something they have done","cn":"授给（某人）勋章（或奖章）","g":"[transitive, usually passive]","ex":{"en":"She was decorated for her efforts during the war.","cn":"她因在战争中的贡献而受到嘉奖。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"装饰;装点;点缀","en":"If you decorate something, you make it more attractive by adding things to it.","ex":{"en":"He decorated his room with pictures of all his favorite sports figures","cn":"他用自己最喜欢的几位体育明星的照片装饰房间。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"粉刷;油漆;裱糊","en":"If you decorate a room or the inside of a building, you put new paint or wallpaper on the walls and ceiling, and paint the woodwork.","ex":{"en":"When they came to decorate the rear bedroom, it was Jemma who had the final say","cn":"他们装修后面的卧室时，是耶马最后说了算。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"美化","en":"If something decorates a place or an object, it makes it look more attractive.","ex":{"en":"Constable posters decorate the walls.","cn":"康斯太布尔风景画的海报装点着那些墙面。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"授予…勋章(或其他荣誉)","en":"If someone is decorated, they are given a medal or other honour as an official reward for something that they have done.","ex":{"en":"He was decorated for bravery in battle.","cn":"他因为作战英勇而被授予奖章。"}}]},"media":{"img":["media/pic/decorating_diy_comp.jpg","media/thumb/roller.jpg","media/ldoce/img/decorate1.jpg"],"uk":"media/uk/decorate__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/decorate__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"He has his own painting and decorating business.","cn":"他经营自己的油漆和粉刷墙壁生意。"},{"en":"Photographs of actors decorated the walls of the restaurant.","cn":"演员的照片装点着餐馆的墙壁。"}]},"delightful":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/delightful__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/delightful__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈlaɪtfl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"very pleasant","cn":"使人快乐的；令人愉快的；宜人的","lab":"especially British English","ex":{"en":"a delightful book/restaurant/town","cn":"令人愉快的书；舒适的餐馆；宜人的城镇"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"令人高兴的;使人愉快的;给人快乐的","en":"If you describe something or someone as delightful, you mean they are very pleasant.","ex":{"en":"It was the most delightful garden I had ever seen","cn":"这是我所见过的最惹人喜爱的花园。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"a delightful book/restaurant/town","cn":"令人愉快的书；舒适的餐馆；宜人的城镇"},{"en":"a delightful child","cn":"讨人喜欢的孩子"}]},"demographic":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/demographic__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/demographic__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdeməˈɡræfɪk","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"data relating to the population and different groups within it","cn":"人口统计数据","g":"[plural]","lab":"statistics","ex":{"en":"the demographics of radio listeners","cn":"电台听众统计数据"}},{"en":"a section of the population who are of a similar age, the same sex, etc.","cn":"（尤指特定年龄段、同一性别等的）人群，人口","g":"[countable]","lab":"also US English, informal，，","ex":{"en":"The products are designed to appeal to a young demographic.","cn":"这些产品是为吸引年轻一代客户而设计的。"}},{"en":"relating to the population and different groups within it","cn":"人口的；人口学的","ex":{"en":"demographic changes/trends/factors","cn":"人口结构变化／发展趋势／统计要素"},"pos":"adjective"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"人口（学）的;人口统计（学）的","en":"Demographic means relating to or concerning demography."},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"(某个地方或社会的)人口特征，人口统计数据","en":"The demographics of a place or society are the statistics relating to the people who live there.","ex":{"en":"...the changing demographics of the United States.","cn":"美国不断变化的人口特征"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"(尤指特定年龄段的)人群","en":"In business, a demographic is a group of people in a society, especially people in a particular age group.","ex":{"en":"Most of our listeners are in the 25-39 demographic.","cn":"我们的大多数听众都属于 25至39 岁这个年龄段。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The products are designed to appeal to a young demographic.","cn":"这些产品是为吸引年轻一代客户而设计的。"},{"en":"demographic changes/trends/factors","cn":"人口结构变化/发展趋势/统计要素"}]},"destroyed":{"lemma":"destroy"},"debts":{"lemma":"debt"},"determined":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/determined__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/determined__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈtɜːmɪnd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"having made a definite decision to do something and not letting anyone prevent you","cn":"决心；决定；决意","g":"[not before noun]","ex":{"en":"The opposition to her plan made her more determined than ever.","cn":"她的计划遭到反对，这反而使她前所未有地更加坚定。"}},{"en":"showing determination","cn":"坚定的；坚决的；坚毅的","ex":{"en":"I made a determined effort to stop smoking.","cn":"我下定决心要努力戒烟。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"下定决心的;决意的;坚定的","en":"If you are determined to do something, you have made a firm decision to do it and will not let anything stop you.","ex":{"en":"His enemies are determined to ruin him","cn":"他的敌人决意要毁了他。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The proposal had been dropped in the face of determined opposition.","cn":"这项建议因遭到坚决反对而撤销。"},{"en":"I'm determined to succeed.","cn":"我决心要获得成功。"}],"base":"determine"},"depict":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/depict__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/depict__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpɪkt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to show an image of somebody/something in a picture","cn":"描绘；描画","ex":{"en":"a painting depicting the Virgin and Child","cn":"一幅描绘童贞马利亚和圣子耶稣的画"}},{"en":"to describe something in words, or give an impression of something in words or with a picture","cn":"描写；描述；刻画","ex":{"en":"The novel depicts French society in the 1930s.","cn":"这部小说描述了 20 世纪 30 年代的法国社会。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"描绘;描画","en":"To depict someone or something means to show or represent them in a work of art such as a drawing or painting.","ex":{"en":"...a gallery of pictures depicting Nelson's most famous battles.","cn":"描绘纳尔逊指挥的那些最著名战役的一组画作"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"描写;描述;刻画","en":"To depict someone or something means to describe them or give an impression of them in writing.","ex":{"en":"Margaret Atwood's novel depicts a gloomy, futuristic America","cn":"玛格丽特·阿特伍德的小说描述了一个黑暗无望的未来美国。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The novel depicts French society in the 1930s.","cn":"这部小说描述了 20 世纪 30 年代的法国社会。"},{"en":"The advertisements depict smoking as glamorous and attractive.","cn":"这些广告把吸烟描绘得充满刺激和富有吸引力。"}]},"determiners":{"lemma":"determiner"},"demand":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/demand__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/demand__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈmɑːnd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a very strong request for something; something that somebody needs","cn":"（坚决的）要求；所需之物","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"a demand for higher pay","cn":"增加工资的要求"}},{"en":"things that somebody/something makes you do, especially things that are difficult, make you tired, worried, etc.","cn":"（尤指困难、使人劳累、令人担忧等的）要求","g":"[plural]","ex":{"en":"Juggling the demands of work and family is never easy.","cn":"兼顾工作和家庭的需求绝非易事。"}},{"en":"the desire or need of customers for goods or services that they want to buy or use","cn":"（顾客的）需求，需要","g":"[uncountable, singular]","ex":{"en":"Demand is exceeding supply.","cn":"供不应求。"}},{"en":"to make a very strong request for something","cn":"强烈要求","lab":"British English also","ex":{"en":"They are demanding the release of all political prisoners.","cn":"他们要求释放所有政治犯。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to ask a question in an angry or aggressive way","cn":"质问；盘问","ex":{"en":"‘Who the hell are you?’ he demanded angrily.","cn":"“你到底是谁？”他气势汹汹地质问道。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to want or need goods or services","cn":"要求，需求（商品或服务）","ex":{"en":"Today's consumers are demanding a greater variety of produce.","cn":"如今的消费者要求更多种类的农产品。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to need something in order to be successful at something","cn":"需要","ex":{"en":"This sport demands both speed and strength.","cn":"这项运动既需要速度也需要体力。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（强烈）要求;强令","en":"If you demand something such as information or action, you ask for it in a very forceful way.","ex":{"en":"Mr Byers last night demanded an immediate explanation from the Education Secretary","cn":"昨晚拜尔斯先生要求教育大臣立刻作出解释。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"需要","en":"If one thing demands another, the first needs the second in order to happen or be dealt with successfully.","ex":{"en":"He said the task of reconstruction would demand much patience, hard work and sacrifice","cn":"他说重建任务将需要付出极大的耐心、艰辛和牺牲。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（坚决的）要求","en":"A demand is a firm request for something.","ex":{"en":"There have been demands for services from tenants up there","cn":"那里的房客要求提供服务。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"需求;需求量","en":"If you refer to demand, or to the demand for something, you are referring to how many people want to have it, do it, or buy it.","ex":{"en":"Another flight would be arranged on Saturday if sufficient demand arose","cn":"如果需求量足够大，周六将再安排一趟航班。"}},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"所需（或要求）的事物","en":"The demands of something or its demands on you are the things which it needs or the things which you have to do for it.","ex":{"en":"Researchers wrongly assumed that people were quite clear about the demands of the task.","cn":"研究人员错误地认为大家都很清楚该项任务的要求。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"很受欢迎;需求量大","en":"If someone or something is in demand or in great demand, they are very popular and a lot of people want them.","ex":{"en":"He was much in demand as a lecturer in the US.","cn":"他的讲座在美国很受欢迎。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"（对…）提出要求","en":"If someone or something makes demands on you, they require you to do things which need a lot of time, energy, or money.","ex":{"en":"I had no right to make demands on his time.","cn":"我无权占用他的时间。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"一经要求;承索","en":"If something is available or happens on demand, you can have it or it happens whenever you want it or ask for it.","ex":{"en":"...a national commitment to providing treatment on demand for drug abusers.","cn":"承诺在全国范围内为提出请求的吸毒者提供治疗"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"By popular demand, the play will run for another week.","cn":"应广大观众要求，这出戏将加演一周。"},{"en":"‘Who the hell are you?’ he demanded angrily. “","cn":"你到底是谁？”他气势汹汹地查问道。"}]},"decorations":{"lemma":"decoration"},"designs":{"lemma":"design"},"defeated":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfiːtɪd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"having been beaten in a battle or contest","cn":"被击败的","g":"[usually before noun]","ex":{"en":"The defeated army slowly made its way back home.","cn":"溃败的军队慢慢地回家了。"}},{"en":"looking or seeming as if you have lost confidence or hope","cn":"沮丧的，失魂落魄的","ex":{"en":"The next time I saw her, she looked totally defeated.","cn":"当我下次见到她时，她看起来完全失败了。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/3/ld41defeated.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/3/ld41defeated.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"He looked lost and defeated.","cn":"他看上去一副失落沮丧的样子。"}],"base":"defeat"},"deniers":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdeniə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a unit for measuring how fine threads of nylon , silk, etc. are","cn":"旦（测量尼龙线、丝线等的纤度单位）"}]}},"deeds":{"lemma":"deed"},"deaths":{"lemma":"death"},"dealings":{"lemma":"dealing"},"devised":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈvaɪz","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to invent sth new or a new way of doing sth","cn":"发明；设计；想出"}]}},"defined":{"lemma":"define"},"descriptions":{"lemma":"description"},"descended":{"lemma":"descend"},"decoding":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdiːˈkəʊd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to find the meaning of sth, especially sth that has been written in code","cn":"解（码）；破译（尤指密码）"},{"en":"to receive an electronic signal and change it into pictures that can be shown on a television screen","cn":"译解（电子信号）"}]}},"deliveries":{"lemma":"delivery"},"descending":{"lemma":"descend"},"deemed":{"oxford":{"phon":"diːm","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"( formal ) ( not usually used in the progressive tenses","cn":"通常不用于进行时 ) to have a particular opinion about sth 认为；视为；相信"}]}},"deeper":{"lemma":"deep"},"deans":{"lemma":"dean"},"decaying":{"lemma":"decay"},"demanded":{"lemma":"demand"},"degrees":{"lemma":"degree"},"demands":{"lemma":"demand"},"democrats":{"lemma":"democrat"},"deserved":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈzɜːvd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"if something is deserved, it has been earned by what somebody has done or how they have behaved","cn":"当之无愧：如果某事是当之无愧的，那是通过某人的所作所为或他们的举止获得的","ex":{"en":"This was a well-deserved victory indeed.","cn":"这确实是一场当之无愧的胜利。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/0/deserved0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/0/laaddeserved.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"He has a well-deserved reputation as a reliable worker.","cn":"大家都说他干活儿可靠﹐这是名副其实的。"},{"en":"Larsson’s goal gave Celtic a deserved victory.","cn":"拉尔森的进球使凯尔特人队赢得了一场应有的胜利。"}],"base":"deserve"},"decides":{"lemma":"decide"},"deciding":{"lemma":"decide"},"designed":{"lemma":"design"},"developments":{"lemma":"development"},"defenders":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfendə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a player who must stop the other team from scoring in games such as football ( soccer ), hockey , etc.","cn":"防守队员；后卫"},{"en":"a person who defends and believes in protecting sth","cn":"守卫者；保护人；防御者"}]}},"decades":{"lemma":"decade"},"describes":{"lemma":"describe"},"devices":{"lemma":"device"},"decisions":{"lemma":"decision"},"declined":{"lemma":"decline"},"developers":{"lemma":"developer"},"details":{"lemma":"detail"},"devising":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈvaɪz","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to invent sth new or a new way of doing sth","cn":"发明；设计；想出"}]}},"delights":{"lemma":"delight"},"describing":{"lemma":"describe"},"determining":{"lemma":"determine"},"decried":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈkraɪ","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"( formal ) to strongly criticize sb/sth, especially publicly （","cn":"公开）谴责；（强烈）批评"}]}},"debates":{"lemma":"debate"},"depicted":{"lemma":"depict"},"demonstrated":{"lemma":"demonstrate"},"defines":{"lemma":"define"},"demeanor":{"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈmiːnə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the way that sb looks or behaves","cn":"外表；风度；行为；举止"}]}},"depicts":{"lemma":"depict"},"designing":{"lemma":"design"},"deployed":{"lemma":"deploy"},"depicting":{"lemma":"depict"},"decreed":{"lemma":"decree"},"denied":{"lemma":"deny"},"delegations":{"lemma":"delegation"},"definitions":{"lemma":"definition"},"desired":{"lemma":"desire","media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/2/desire_n0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/f/desire1.mp3"}},"described":{"lemma":"describe"},"deteriorating":{"lemma":"deteriorate"},"departments":{"lemma":"department"},"dew":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"露;露水","en":"Dew is small drops of water that form on the ground and other surfaces outdoors during the night.","ex":{"en":"The dew gathered on the leaves.","cn":"露水在叶子上凝结。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the small drops of water that form on outdoor surfaces during the night","cn":"露﹐露水"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"Dew is moisture caused by condensation of water vapor in the air. Dew is what gets your feet wet when you walk across the grass on a summer morning."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. heavy There was a heavy dew this morning. | morning The sun had dried the early morning dew.","QUANT. drop Drops of dew shone on the grass.","DEW + VERB fall, form","DEW + NOUN drop (also dewdrop)","PHRASES damp/heavy/wet with dew The grass was still wet with dew."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/5/brelasdedew.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/2/dew.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The grass was wet with early morning dew.","cn":"清晨的露水使得青草湿漉漉的。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"djuː","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the very small drops of water that form on the ground, etc. during the night","cn":"露；露水","ex":{"en":"The grass was wet with early morning dew.","cn":"清晨的露水使得青草湿漉漉的。"}}]}},"detain":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"拘留;扣押","en":"When people such as the police detain someone, they keep them in a place under their control.","ex":{"en":"The act allows police to detain a suspect for up to 48 hours","cn":"该法令允许警方将嫌疑犯扣押最多48小时。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"阻留;耽搁","en":"To detain someone means to delay them, for example by talking to them.","ex":{"en":"Thank you. We won't detain you any further.","cn":"非常感谢。我们就不再耽搁您的时间了。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to make someone or something late - use this especially about a problem or something unexpected","cn":""},{"en":"to delay someone or something so that they arrive somewhere late","cn":""},{"en":"to make someone or something stop or go more slowly when they are going somewhere","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"When you detain someone, you hold them back, slow them down, or stop them from moving on. If you are detained by the police, you may be late for the big football game, even if you were speeding to get there by the kickoff."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. briefly He was kidnapped and briefly detained by a terrorist group.","VERB + DETAIN need not This issue need not detail us long.","PREP. for She was arrested and detained for distributing pro-democracy leaflets. | in connection with Over 60 people have been detained in c","PHRASES be detained in custody/hospital Two people were detained in hospital following the crash. | detain sb without charge/trial He has be"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/8/detain0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/f/detain.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"I'm sorry — he'll be late; he's been detained at a meeting.","cn":"对不起 — 他要晚点到，他因会议耽搁了。"},{"en":"One man has been detained for questioning.","cn":"一个男人被拘留审问。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈteɪn","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to keep somebody in an official place, such as a police station, a prison or a hospital, and prevent them from leaving","cn":"拘留；扣押；扣留","ex":{"en":"One man has been detained for questioning.","cn":"一个男人被拘留审问。"}},{"en":"to delay somebody or prevent them from going somewhere","cn":"耽搁；留住；阻留","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"I'm sorry—he'll be late; he's been detained at a meeting.","cn":"对不起，他要晚点儿到，他因会议耽搁了。"}}]}},"deploy":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"部署，调集（部队或军事力量）","en":"To deploy troops or military resources means to organize or position them so that they are ready to be used.","ex":{"en":"The president said he had no intention of deploying ground troops.","cn":"总统称并不打算部署地面部队。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to organize or move soldiers, military equipment etc so that they are in the right place and ready to be used","cn":"部署﹐调度〔士兵﹑军事装备等〕"},{"en":"to use something for a particular purpose, especially ideas, arguments etc","cn":"利用﹐调动〔尤指想法﹑论据等〕"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"The word deploy is mainly used in military contexts and to refer to the strategic arrangement of fighting forces."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. effectively Tanks were deployed effectively during the long campaign.","PREP. against She rejected the arguments that had been deployed against her."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/b/deploy0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/4/deploy.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"2 000 troops were deployed in the area.","cn":"那个地区部署了 2 000 人的部队。"},{"en":"At least 5 000 missiles were deployed along the border.","cn":"沿边境至少部署了 5 000 枚导弹。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈplɔɪ","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to move soldiers or weapons into a position where they are ready for military action","cn":"部署，调度（军队或武器）","ex":{"en":"2 000 troops were deployed in the area.","cn":"那个地区部署了 2 000 人的部队。"}},{"en":"to use something effectively","cn":"有效地利用；调动","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"to deploy arguments/resources","cn":"利用论据／资源"}}]}},"devastation":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(大面积的严重)毁坏，破坏","en":"Devastation is severe and widespread destruction or damage.","ex":{"en":"A huge bomb blast brought chaos and devastation to the centre of Belfast yesterday.","cn":"昨天一颗威力巨大的炸弹在贝尔法斯特市中心爆炸，引起一片混乱并造成严重破坏。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to damage something so badly that it no longer exists or cannot be used or repaired","cn":""},{"en":"to damage a large area very badly and destroy many things in it","cn":""},{"en":"to completely destroy a building, either deliberately or by accident","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"When there's devastation , there's terrible destruction. You can see the devastation from a violent hurricane and feel devastation over all the people that were injured."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. complete, utter | widespread | ecological, environmental | economic","VERB + DEVASTATION cause The hurricane caused widespread devastation.","DEVASTATION + VERB be wrought We surveyed the devastation wrought by the fire.","PHRASES a scene of devastation He surveyed the scene of utter devastation beneath him. | a trail of devastation The tornado left a trail of "]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/6/devastate0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/b/devastate.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The bomb caused widespread devastation.","cn":"炸弹造成大面积破坏。"},{"en":"Rob was devastated by the news of her death.","cn":""}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdevəˈsteɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"great destruction or damage, especially over a wide area","cn":"（尤指大面积的）毁灭，破坏，蹂躏","ex":{"en":"The bomb caused widespread devastation.","cn":"炸弹造成大面积破坏。"}}]}},"deity":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"神;女神","en":"A deity is a god or goddess."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a male spirit or being who is believed by some religions to control the world or part of it, or who represents a particular quality","cn":""},{"en":"a female god","cn":""},{"en":"a god. Deity is more formal than god","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"A deity is a supernatural being, like a god or goddess, which is worshipped by people who believe it controls or exerts force over some aspect of the world."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. major, supreme | lesser, minor one of the minor Greek deities | benevolent | patron a shrine to the patron deity of the city | female, ","VERB + DEITY worship a tribe that worshipped two main deities","PHRASES the incarnation/manifestation/representation of a deity Many animals were seen as the manifestation of a deity."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/e/deity0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/5/deity1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Greek/Roman/Hindu deities","cn":"希腊/罗马/印度教诸神"},{"en":"the deities of ancient Greece","cn":"古希腊诸神"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdeɪəti","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a god or goddess","cn":"神；女神","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"Greek/Roman/Hindu deities","cn":"希腊／罗马／印度教诸神"}},{"en":"God","cn":"上帝；天主","g":"[singular]","lab":"formal"}]}},"defective":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"有缺点的;有缺陷的;有毛病的","en":"If something is defective, there is something wrong with it and it does not work properly.","ex":{"en":"Her sight was becoming defective","cn":"她的视力开始出现问题。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"not made properly, or not working properly","cn":"有问题的﹐有毛病的﹐有缺陷的"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj","senses":[{"en":"Something that's defective doesn't work quite right, because it's damaged in some way. Your defective car probably won't make it all the way to California from New York."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be, prove If the goods prove defective, the customer has the right to compensation.","ADV. highly, seriously, severely Her vision is seriously defective."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/3/ld41defective.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/3/defective.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Her hearing was found to be slightly defective.","cn":"经检查，她的听力有点缺陷。"},{"en":"defective goods","cn":"有缺陷的商品"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfektɪv","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"having a fault or faults; not perfect or complete","cn":"有缺点的；有缺陷的；有毛病的","ex":{"en":"If the goods are defective you should get a full refund.","cn":"如果货物有缺陷，您应该获得全额退款。"}},{"en":"having a physical problem with part of the body or the way that it works","cn":"生理缺陷的;生理障碍的","lab":"sometimes offensive","ex":{"en":"Her hearing was found to be slightly defective.","cn":"经检查，她的听力有点缺陷。"}}]}},"dealer":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"商人;交易商","en":"A dealer is a person whose business involves buying and selling things.","ex":{"en":"...an antique dealer.","cn":"古董商"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"毒品贩子","en":"A dealer is someone who buys and sells illegal drugs.","ex":{"en":"They aim to clear every dealer from the street.","cn":"他们打算把街上所有的毒品贩子都清走。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the illegal activity of taking drugs from one country to another and selling them","cn":""},{"en":"someone who sells illegal drugs, especially to someone that they know","cn":""},{"en":"someone who sells illegal drugs, especially in order to encourage people to start taking drugs","cn":""}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. licensed It is always a good idea to sell through a licensed dealer. | reputable Always buy from a reputable dealer. | shady, unscrupul","PREP. through a/the ~ She sold the painting through a London art dealer. | ~ in a dealer in antiques • Note at JOB"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/b/dealer0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/8/dealer.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"He's a dealer in second-hand cars.","cn":"他经销二手汽车。"},{"en":"an art/antique dealer","cn":"艺术品经销商；古董商"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdiːlə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person whose business is buying and selling a particular product","cn":"交易商；贸易商","ex":{"en":"an art/antique dealer","cn":"艺术品经销商；古董商"}},{"en":"a person who sells illegal drugs","cn":"贩毒者；毒品贩子","ex":{"en":"a crack dealer","cn":"强效可卡因贩卖者"}},{"en":"the person who gives out the cards in a card game","cn":"（纸牌游戏的）发牌者"}]}},"dexterity":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(双手的)灵巧;(思维的)敏捷","en":"Dexterity is skill in using your hands, or sometimes your mind.","ex":{"en":"...Reid's dexterity on the guitar.","cn":"里德弹吉他的娴熟指法"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"skill and speed in doing something with your hands 〔","cn":"手的〕敏捷﹐灵巧﹐熟练"},{"en":"skill in using words or your mind 〔","cn":"言辞或思维的〕机敏"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"If you fall asleep with your heavy head on your arm, you might not have the dexterity, or control of your hand, to hit the OFF button on the alarm clock in the morning."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. great | manual","VERB + DEXTERITY demand, require Video games demand great manual dexterity. | have I don't have the dexterity for juggling.","PREP. with ~ She handled the discussion with dexterity."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/3/dexterity0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/7/dexterity.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"You need manual dexterity to be good at video games.","cn":"玩好电子游戏手要灵巧。"},{"en":"mental/verbal dexterity","cn":"智能；说话技巧"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dekˈsterəti","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"skill in using your hands or your mind","cn":"（手）灵巧，熟练；（思维）敏捷，灵活","ex":{"en":"You need good manual dexterity to be a dentist.","cn":"当牙医手要灵巧。"}}]}},"deny":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"否认","en":"When you deny something, you state that it is not true.","ex":{"en":"She denied both accusations","cn":"她对两项指控均予以否认。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"否认与…有关系;否认…是自己的;不承认;抛弃","en":"If you deny someone or something, you say that they have no connection with you or do not belong to you.","ex":{"en":"I denied my father because I wanted to become someone else.","cn":"我和父亲断绝了关系，因为我想成为一个不一样的自己。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"拒绝给予;拒绝…的要求","en":"If you deny someone something that they need or want, you refuse to let them have it.","ex":{"en":"If he is unlucky, he may find that his ex-partner denies him access to his children","cn":"如果不走运的话，他可能会发现前妻拒绝让他接近自己的孩子。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to say firmly that you will not do something that someone has asked you to do","cn":""},{"en":"to say that you will not do something when someone asks you","cn":""},{"en":"to refuse to accept an offer or invitation, or a formal request","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"To deny means refuse to accept, recognize, or believe. You can deny your sweet tooth all you want, but the stash of candy in your desk tells a different story."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. emphatically, fiercely, firmly, hotly, strenuously, strongly, vehemently, vigorously Both women vehemently deny the charges against the","VERB + DENY cannot You can't deny that it seems a very attractive idea. | try to I know it was you I saw, so there's no use trying to deny i","PHRASES no one could/would deny that No one would deny that there is a very great need for change. | there is no denying sth There is no den","ADV. cruelly They were cruelly denied victory by an injury-time strike from Owen. | effectively Children could be compelled to work on the f","PREP. to You cannot deny this opportunity to me."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/f/deny0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/e/deny.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"It can't be denied that we need to devote more resources to this problem.","cn":"无可否认，我们需要投入更多的资源来解决这个问题。"},{"en":"There's no denying (the fact) that quicker action could have saved them.","cn":"无可否认，如果行动快一点，本来是救得了他们的。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈnaɪ","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to say that something is not true","cn":"否认；否定","ex":{"en":"to deny an allegation/a charge/an accusation","cn":"否认指控"}},{"en":"to refuse to admit or accept something","cn":"拒绝承认；拒绝接受","ex":{"en":"She denied all knowledge of the incident.","cn":"她矢口否认知晓此事的任何情况。"}},{"en":"to refuse to allow somebody to have something that they want or ask for","cn":"拒绝；拒绝给予","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"They were denied access to the information.","cn":"他们试图取得这个情报被拒。"}},{"en":"to refuse to let yourself have something that you would like to have, especially for moral or religious reasons","cn":"（尤因道德或宗教原因）节制，克制，戒绝","lab":"formal"}]}},"dessert":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-MASS 物质名词","cn":"（饭后）甜点","en":"Dessert is something sweet, such as fruit or a pudding, that you eat at the end of a meal.","ex":{"en":"She had homemade ice cream for dessert","cn":"她用自制的冰激凌作饭后甜点。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the small first part of a meal","cn":""},{"en":"the main part of a meal. entrée is used especially on restaurant menu s","cn":""},{"en":"sweet food eaten at the end of a meal","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"Served as the last course of a meal, a dessert is often sweet, like cake or pie. If you have a sweet tooth, you may wish it were the only course of the meal."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. delicious | rich This chestnut pudding is a rich dessert with a festive flavour.","VERB + DESSERT eat, have","DESSERT + NOUN apple, wine | menu, trolley","PREP. for ~ We had mousse for dessert. | ~ of We finished off with a dessert of honey and nuts. •"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/a/brelasdedessert.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/1/dessert.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"( BrE ) the dessert trolley (= a table on wheels from which you choose your dessert in a restaurant) （","cn":"餐厅内）送甜点的手推车"},{"en":"What's for dessert?","cn":"餐后甜点吃什么？"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈzɜːt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"sweet food eaten at the end of a meal","cn":"（饭后）甜点，甜食","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"What's for dessert?","cn":"餐后甜点吃什么？"}}]}},"defendant":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"被告","en":"A defendant is a person who has been accused of breaking the law and is being tried in court."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the person who is on trial for a crime","cn":""},{"en":"the lawyers who are working for the defendant","cn":""},{"en":"the lawyers who are trying to prove that the defendant is guilty","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"In court, the person who gets sued or accused is called a defendant — they have to defend their innocence or reputation."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERB + DEFENDANT charge The defendant was charged with disturbing the peace. | sue a defendant being sued by an insurance company | convict,","DEFENDANT + VERB plead guilty/not guilty","PREP. against the ~ the plaintiff's claim against the defendant | for the ~ Several witnesses gave evidence for the defendant. | ~ in a defe"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/0/defendant0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/8/defendant.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"We find the defendant not guilty.","cn":"我们裁定被告无罪。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfendənt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the person in a trial who is accused of committing a crime, or who is being sued by another person","cn":"被告人；被告","lab":"especially North American English","ex":{"en":"Several witnesses gave evidence for the defendant.","cn":"几位证人提供了有利于被告的证词。"}}]}},"developer":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（房地产）开发商，开发公司","en":"A developer is a person or a company that buys land and builds houses, offices, shops, or factories on it, or buys existing buildings and makes them more modern.","ex":{"en":"...common land which would have a high commercial value if sold to developers.","cn":"如果卖给开发商会有很高商业价值的公共用地"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(想法、设计、产品等的)开发者","en":"A developer is someone who develops something such as an idea, a design, or a product.","ex":{"en":"John Bardeen was also co-developer of the theory of superconductivity.","cn":"约翰·巴丁也是超导电性理论的创立者之一。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"显影剂;显色剂","en":"Developer is a chemical used for developing photographs or films."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person or company that makes money by buying land and then building houses, factories etc on it 〔","cn":"房地产〕开发商﹐开发公司"},{"en":"a person or an organization that works on a new idea, product etc to make it successful 〔","cn":"新办法﹑新产品等的〕开发者﹐研制者"},{"en":"a chemical substance used for making images appear on film or photographic paper","cn":"显影剂﹐显像剂"}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. big, major | local A local developer is planning to build a supermarket on the site. | private The flats are being built by a private d","DEVELOPER + VERB build sth, develop sth"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/3/brelasdedeveloper.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/f/developer.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"property developers","cn":"房地产开发商"},{"en":"a software developer","cn":"软件开发人员"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈveləpə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person or company that buys land or buildings in order to build new houses, shops, etc., or to improve the old ones, and makes a profit from doing this","cn":"（房地产）开发商，开发公司","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"property developers","cn":"房地产开发商"}},{"en":"a person or a company that designs and creates new products","cn":"（新产品的）开发者，研制者","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"a software developer","cn":"软件开发人员"}},{"en":"a chemical substance that is used for developing photographs from a film","cn":"显影剂","g":"[uncountable]"}]}},"denounce":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"谴责;痛斥","en":"If you denounce a person or an action, you criticize them severely and publicly because you feel strongly that they are wrong or evil.","ex":{"en":"The letter called for trade union freedom and civil rights, but did not openly denounce the regime","cn":"这封信呼吁保障工会自由和公民权利，但没有公开谴责该政权。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"告发;检举","en":"If you denounce someone who has broken a rule or law, you report them to the authorities.","ex":{"en":"...informers who might denounce you at any moment.","cn":"随时都可能告发你们的那些告密者"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to say, write, or show publicly that you disapprove of someone or something","cn":""},{"en":"to clearly and publicly say that you strongly disapprove of someone or something","cn":""},{"en":"to say publicly that you strongly disapprove of something or someone and think that they are morally bad","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"1 v 2 v","senses":[{"en":"To denounce is to tattle, rat out, or speak out against something. When you stand on your desk and tell the class that your partner is cheating, you denounce him or her."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. angrily, bitterly, fiercely, strongly | publicly He was publicly denounced as a traitor. | formally","PREP. for The government was bitterly denounced for the emergency measures. | to Someone in the village must have denounced them to the auth","PHRASES be widely denounced These new regulations have been widely denounced."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/a/denounce0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/d/denounce.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The project was denounced as a scandalous waste of public money.","cn":"这项工程被斥责为挥霍公款，令人愤慨。"},{"en":"She publicly denounced the government's handling of the crisis.","cn":"她公开谴责政府处理这场危机的方式。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈnaʊns","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to strongly criticize somebody/something that you think is wrong, illegal, etc.","cn":"谴责；指责；斥责","ex":{"en":"She publicly denounced the government's handling of the crisis.","cn":"她公开谴责政府处理这场危机的方式。"}},{"en":"to tell the police, the authorities, etc. about somebody’s illegal political activities","cn":"告发（某人从事非法政治活动）","ex":{"en":"They were denounced as spies.","cn":"他们被揭发是间谍。"}}]}},"deteriorate":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"恶化;变坏;衰退","en":"If something deteriorates, it becomes worse in some way.","ex":{"en":"There are fears that the situation might deteriorate into full-scale war","cn":"人们担心形势可能恶化而演变成一场全面战争。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to become worse","cn":"恶化﹐堕落﹐退化"},{"en":"to become worse. Get worse is less formal and more common than deteriorate in everyday English","cn":""},{"en":"to become gradually worse – used especially about the standard of something","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"When something gets worse due to neglect or an unfortunate health problem, stuff starts to deteriorate — or fall apart."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. badly, seriously | dramatically, sharply, quickly, rapidly | gradually | further","VERB + DETERIORATE begin to His health began to deteriorate quite seriously. | continue to | be likely to","PREP. into The unrest rapidly deteriorated into civil war."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/6/deteriorate0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/a/deteriorate.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Her health deteriorated rapidly, and she died shortly afterwards.","cn":"她的健康状况急剧恶化，不久便去世了。"},{"en":"The discussion quickly deteriorated into an angry argument.","cn":"这场讨论迅速演变成愤怒的争吵。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈtɪəriəreɪt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to become worse","cn":"变坏；恶化；退化","ex":{"en":"Her health deteriorated rapidly, and she died shortly afterwards.","cn":"她的健康状况急剧恶化，不久便去世了。"}}]}},"detention":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(尤指出于政治原因的)拘留，扣押，监禁","en":"Detention is when someone is arrested or put into prison, especially for political reasons.","ex":{"en":"...the detention without trial of government critics","cn":"对政府批评者未经审讯的关押"}},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"(惩罚顽皮学童的)放学后留校","en":"Detention is a punishment for naughty schoolchildren, who are made to stay at school after the other children have gone home.","ex":{"en":"The teacher kept the boys in detention after school.","cn":"老师将这些男生课后留堂。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"if someone who the police think is guilty of a crime is in custody , they are kept in prison until it is time for them to be judged in a court","cn":""},{"en":"if someone is under arrest , the police are keeping them guarded because they think they are guilty of a crime","cn":""},{"en":"when someone is being forced to stay in a place where they do not want to be - use this when this situation is illegal or wrong","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"Detention is a word for confinement or imprisonment, usually for a short time. It's also a punishment where children must stay after school."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. arbitrary Opponents of the regime had been subject to arbitrary detention, torture and execution. | pre-trial | indefinite If found gui","VERB + DETENTION be in, remain in 147 of the illegal immigrants remain in detention. | hold sb in, place sb in, sentence sb to He was held i","DETENTION + NOUN camp, centre","PREP. in ~ She spent 18 years in detention. | under ~ He made the confession while under detention.","PHRASES a period/term of detention The judge will fix the period of detention."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/7/detention0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/c/detention.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"a sentence of 12 months' detention in a young offender institution","cn":"在青少年教养院拘禁 12 个月的判决"},{"en":"They can't give me (a) detention for this.","cn":"他们不能因为这事罚我课后留下来。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈtenʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the state of being kept in a place, especially a prison, and prevented from leaving","cn":"拘留；扣押；监禁","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"They were sentenced to 12 months' detention in a young offender institution.","cn":"他们被判留在少管所12 个月。"}},{"en":"the punishment of being kept at school for a time after other students have gone home","cn":"放学后留校，留堂（处罚学生）","g":"[uncountable, countable]","ex":{"en":"They can’t give me (a) detention for this.","cn":"他们不能因为这事罚我课后留下来。"}}]}},"defiant":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"违抗的;蔑视的;挑战的;不服的","en":"If you say that someone is defiant, you mean they show aggression or independence by refusing to obey someone.","ex":{"en":"The players are in defiant mood as they prepare for tomorrow's game","cn":"球员在备战明天的比赛时带着蔑视对手的情绪。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"someone, especially a child, who is disobedient does not do what he or she is told to do by a parent, teacher etc","cn":""},{"en":"not obeying people in authority and showing that you have no respect for them","cn":""},{"en":"someone, especially a young person, who is rebellious deliberately disobeys people in authority such as their parents or teachers","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj","senses":[{"en":"Have you ever seen a picture of a protester who is about to be carried off by police but is still shouting or resisting, fighting to the bitter end? That person is defiant ."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS appear, be, feel, look, seem | become | remain Despite the criticisms, she remained defiant.","ADV. very | slightly He had a slightly defiant air. | openly Sylvia tossed back her dark hair in a gesture that was openly defiant. | persis"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/a/defiant0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/0/defiant.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The terrorists sent a defiant message to the government.","cn":"恐怖分子向政府发出了挑战书。"},{"en":"a defiant teenager","cn":"一个反叛的少年"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfaɪənt","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"openly refusing to obey somebody/something, sometimes in an aggressive way","cn":"公然违抗的；反抗的；挑衅的","ex":{"en":"She had suddenly turned into a defiant teenager.","cn":"她一下子变成了一个叛逆的少年。"}}]}},"delhi":{"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"","senses":[{"en":"a large city in northern India, divided into new delhi (= the capital of India ) and Old Delhi","cn":""}]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/c/p028-000004015.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/c/delhi_.mp3"}},"deduction":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"推论;推断","en":"A deduction is a conclusion that you have reached about something because of other things that you know to be true.","ex":{"en":"It was a pretty astute deduction","cn":"那是一个颇为敏锐的推论。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"推论（过程）；演绎","en":"Deduction is the process of reaching a conclusion about something because of other things that you know to be true.","ex":{"en":"...a case that tested his powers of deduction.","cn":"考验他的推论能力的案例"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"扣除额;减除数","en":"A deduction is an amount that has been subtracted from a total.","ex":{"en":"...your gross income (before tax and National Insurance deductions)","cn":"(扣除税款和国民保险之前的)总收入"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"扣除;减除","en":"Deduction is the act or process of subtracting an amount of money from a total amount.","ex":{"en":"After the deduction of tax at 20 per cent, the interest rate will be 6.2 per cent.","cn":"扣除了 20% 的税后，利率将为 6.2%。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the process of using the knowledge or information you have in order to understand something or form an opinion, or the opinion that you form","cn":"推论﹐推断﹐演绎"},{"en":"the process of taking away an amount from a total, or the amount that is taken away","cn":"扣除﹔扣除额"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"1 n 2 n","senses":[{"en":"If you get a tax deduction it means you get to reduce the amount of your income that is subject to tax. If something's on sale, you might get a percentage deduction from the original price. Deduction means taking away, or an amount taken away."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. brilliant | logical | reasonable","VERB + DEDUCTION make","PREP. by ~ She arrived at this conclusion by logical deduction. | ~ about We can make some deductions about the history of the ruins.","PHRASES powers of deduction a detective with excellent powers of deduction | a process of deduction She arrived at the solution by a simple ","ADJ. monthly, weekly monthly deductions for health insurance | tax","VERB + DEDUCTION make The company automatically makes tax deductions from your salary.","PREP. ~ for deductions for travel costs | ~ from deductions from his wages"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/6/deduction0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/f/deduction.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"If my deductions are correct, I can tell you who the killer was.","cn":"如果我的推论正确的话，我可以告诉你谁是凶手。"},{"en":"He arrived at the solution by a simple process of deduction.","cn":"他通过一番简单的推理得出了解决问题的方法。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈdʌkʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the process of using information you have in order to understand a particular situation or to find the answer to a problem","cn":"演绎；推论；推理","g":"[uncountable, countable]","ex":{"en":"He arrived at the solution by a simple process of deduction.","cn":"他通过一番简单的推理得出了解决问题的方法。"}},{"en":"the process of taking an amount of something, especially money, away from a total; the amount that is taken away","cn":"扣除（额）；减去（数）","g":"[uncountable, countable]","ex":{"en":"The dividend will be paid without deduction of tax.","cn":"股息将免税支付。"}}]}},"deformity":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(身体的)畸形部位（或器官）","en":"A deformity is a part of someone's body which is not the normal shape because of injury or illness, or because they were born this way.","ex":{"en":"...facial deformities in babies.","cn":"婴儿的面部畸形处"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"畸形;变形","en":"Deformity is the condition of having a deformity.","ex":{"en":"The bones begin to grind against each other, leading to pain and deformity.","cn":"这些骨头开始互相挤压，造成疼痛和畸形。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a condition in which part of someone’s body is not the normal shape 〔","cn":"人体部位的〕畸形"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"A deformity happens when a body part is misshapen. A deformity can also be a change for the worse in something's appearance. A two-headed kitten has a deformity ."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. appalling, severe | slight | congenital, genetic | birth | physical | facial, hip, limb, etc.","VERB + DEFORMITY have, suffer from"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/3/deformity0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/d/deformity.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Drugs taken during pregnancy may cause physical deformity in babies.","cn":"妊娠期服用的药物可能引起婴儿身体畸形。"},{"en":"a hip deformity","cn":"臀部畸形"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfɔːməti","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a condition in which a part of the body has not developed in the usual way or does not have the usual shape","cn":"（身体的）畸形","ex":{"en":"The baby was born with a spinal deformity.","cn":"这名婴儿出生时就有脊柱畸形。"}}]}},"deliberation":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"慎重的考虑;仔细的思考","en":"Deliberation is the long and careful consideration of a subject.","ex":{"en":"After much deliberation, a decision was reached","cn":"经过深思熟虑后终于作出了一个决定。"}},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"审议;评议;商议","en":"Deliberations are formal discussions where an issue is considered carefully.","ex":{"en":"...the outcome of the deliberations","cn":"评议的结果"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"从容;不慌不忙;审慎","en":"If you say or do something with deliberation, you do it slowly and carefully.","ex":{"en":"Fred spoke with deliberation","cn":"弗雷德字斟句酌。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"careful consideration or discussion of something","cn":"细想﹔考虑﹔商议"},{"en":"if you speak or move with deliberation, you speak or move slowly and carefully 〔","cn":"说话﹑行动时的〕从容﹐谨慎"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"The process of carefully considering what to do is called deliberation , like your deliberation before making one of the most important decisions in your life."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. careful After careful deliberation, it was agreed to abandon the project. | considerable | lengthy, long","PREP. ~ about/on your deliberations on his future 2 speaking/moving slowly and carefully","ADJ. calm, cool, quiet, slow | great","PREP. with ~ With slow deliberation, he tore the letter into pieces."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/6/deliberation0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/3/deliberation.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"After ten hours of deliberation, the jury returned a verdict of ‘not guilty’.","cn":"经过十小时的商议，陪审团宣告了“无罪”的裁决。"},{"en":"The deliberations of the committee are completely confidential.","cn":"委员会的审议过程是绝对保密的。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˌlɪbəˈreɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the process of carefully considering or discussing something","cn":"细想；考虑；商议；审议","g":"[uncountable, countable, usually plural]","ex":{"en":"After ten hours of deliberation, the jury returned a verdict of ‘not guilty’.","cn":"经过十小时的商议，陪审团宣告了“无罪”的裁定。"}},{"en":"the quality of being slow and careful in what you say or do","cn":"（说话或办事）从容，审慎","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"She signed her name with great deliberation.","cn":"她非常审慎地签上了自己的名字。"}}]}},"detour":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"绕道;绕路;迂回","en":"If you make a detour on a journey, you go by a route which is not the shortest way, because you want to avoid something such as a traffic jam, or because there is something you want to do on the way.","ex":{"en":"He did not take the direct route to his home, but made a detour around the outskirts of the city.","cn":"他没有直接回家，而是绕到市郊兜了个圈子。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"绕行路线;迂回路线","en":"A detour is a special route for traffic to follow when the normal route is blocked, for example because it is being repaired."},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"绕道;绕路;绕行","en":"If you detour, you make a detour.","ex":{"en":"On the way back, Jarvis detoured to check the time of services at the church.","cn":"回去的路上，贾维斯绕道去核实了一下教堂礼拜仪式的时间。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"to keep away from a person, because you do not want to talk to them, or keep away from a place, because there are problems there","cn":""},{"en":"to not go near a person or place, because they may be dangerous or may cause problems","cn":""},{"en":"to make an effort to avoid a person or place, because there could be serious problems if you do not","cn":""}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. lengthy, long | brief, short, small","VERB + DETOUR make, take We had to make a lengthy detour through the backstreets. | be worth The monument is well worth a detour.","PREP. ~ around Trucks now face a five-mile detour around the bridge. | ~ through, ~ to The ship made a detour to the south."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/d/detour_v0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/f/detour.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"We had to make a detour around the flooded fields.","cn":"我们只得绕道避开被洪水淹没的田野。"},{"en":"The President detoured to Chicago for a special meeting.","cn":"总统绕道到芝加哥参加一个特别会议。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdiːtʊə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a longer route that you take in order to avoid a problem or to visit a place","cn":"绕行的路；迂回路；兜圈子","ex":{"en":"We had to make a detour around the flooded fields.","cn":"我们只得绕道避开被洪水淹没的田野。"}},{"en":"a road or route that is used when the usual one is closed","cn":"临时绕行路；临时支路","lab":"North American English"},{"en":"to take a longer route in order to avoid a problem or to visit a place; to make somebody/something take a longer route","cn":"（使）绕道，绕行","ex":{"en":"The President detoured to Chicago for a special meeting.","cn":"总统绕道到芝加哥参加一个特别会议。"},"pos":"verb"}]}},"detrimental":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"有害的;不利的","en":"Something that is detrimental to something else has a harmful or damaging effect on it.","ex":{"en":"...foods suspected of being detrimental to health","cn":"被怀疑有害健康的食品"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"causing physical harm – used especially about things that cause harm to your health, the environment etc","cn":""},{"en":"to have a harmful effect on someone or something. This phrase is very commonly used in everyday English when saying that something is harmful","cn":""},{"en":"used about things that cause permanent physical harm, or that have a bad effect in other ways, for example on people’s opinion of someone","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj","senses":[{"en":"Detrimental is a formal way of saying \"harmful.\" Anything detrimental hurts, hinders, or puts a damper on something. Detrimental things do damage."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be, prove, seem | become","ADV. extremely, highly, seriously, very | positively Sugar is positively detrimental to bodybuilding. | rather","PREP. to This move could be seriously detrimental to the economy."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/a/detrimental0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/3/laaddetrimental.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The policy will be detrimental to the peace process.","cn":"这项政策将不利于和平进程。"},{"en":"the sun's detrimental effect on skin","cn":"日光对皮肤的有害影响"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdetrɪˈmentl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"harmful","cn":"有害的；不利的","ex":{"en":"the sun’s detrimental effect on skin","cn":"日光对皮肤的伤害"}}]}},"denunciation":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"谴责;痛斥","en":"Denunciation of someone or something is severe public criticism of them.","ex":{"en":"On September 24, he wrote a stinging denunciation of his critics","cn":"9月24号，他写了一篇痛斥那些批评者的措词强烈的文章。"}},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"告发;检举","en":"Denunciation is the act of reporting someone who has broken a rule or law to the authorities.","ex":{"en":"...the denunciation of Jews to the Nazis during the Second World War.","cn":"第二次世界大战期间向纳粹分子告发犹太人"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a public statement in which you criticize someone or something","cn":"谴责﹐斥责﹐控诉"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"A denunciation is a public reprimand in which you are told that you've done wrong. If you get caught skipping school, expect denunciation -by teachers, your principal, parents and maybe even your friends."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. angry, bitter, fierce, violent | public","VERB + DENUNCIATION issue, make In his speech, he made a fierce denunciation of government policy.","PREP. ~ of a public denunciation of the corrupt system"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/3/denunciation0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/3/denunciation.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"All parties joined in bitter denunciation of the terrorists.","cn":"所有党派同仇敌忾地痛斥恐怖分子。"},{"en":"an angry denunciation of the government's policies","cn":"愤怒谴责政府的政策"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˌnʌnsiˈeɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an act of criticizing somebody/something strongly in public","cn":"（公开）谴责，斥责，指责","ex":{"en":"The bishop made an angry denunciation of the government's policies.","cn":"主教愤怒地谴责了政府的政策。"}}]}},"declare":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"宣称，声称（…为事实）；表明(态度、意图等)","en":"If you declare that something is true, you say that it is true in a firm, deliberate way. You can also declare an attitude or intention.","ex":{"en":"Speaking outside Ten Downing Street, she declared that she would fight on","cn":"她在英国首相官邸外发表讲话时宣称她将继续斗争下去。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"宣布;宣告","en":"If you declare something, you state officially and formally that it exists or is the case.","ex":{"en":"The government is ready to declare a permanent ceasefire","cn":"政府准备宣布永久性停火。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"申报(纳税品、收入等)","en":"If you declare goods that you have bought in another country or money that you have earned, you say how much you have bought or earned so that you can pay tax on it.","ex":{"en":"Your income must be declared on this form","cn":"必须在这张表格上申报你的收入。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：declare for"}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to tell someone something, using words","cn":""},{"en":"to say something, especially in a definite or formal way – used in official contexts","cn":""},{"en":"to publicly tell people about something","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"If you declare victory, you are ending a war by saying you have won. Hopefully, the other side agrees, or your troops might declare you a fool. To declare is to state clearly and officially."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. virtually He has virtually declared war on the right-wingers in his party. | immediately, promptly Martial law was immediately declared","PREP. to He declared his true feelings to her."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/b/declare0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/1/declare.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Germany declared war on France on 1 August 1914.","cn":"德国在 1914 年 8 月 1 日向法国宣战。"},{"en":"She declared herself extremely hurt by his lack of support.","cn":"她说自己非常伤心，因为他没有得到支持。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈkleə(r)","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to say something officially or publicly","cn":"公布；宣布；宣告","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"The government has declared a state of emergency.","cn":"政府已宣布进入紧急状态。"}},{"en":"to state something clearly and definitely","cn":"表明；宣称；断言","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"‘I'll do it!’ Tom declared.","cn":"“让我来！”汤姆果断地说。"}},{"en":"to say clearly and openly who you are or what you intend to do","cn":"亮明身份；表明意愿","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"He was the first gay player in a professional sports team to declare himself openly.","cn":"他是职业运动队中第一位公开宣布自己身份的同性恋球员。"}},{"en":"to tell the tax authorities how much money you have earned","cn":"申报（收益）","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"All income must be declared.","cn":"所有收益必须申报。"}},{"en":"to tell customs officers (= at the border of a country) that you are carrying goods on which you should pay tax","cn":"申报（应纳税物品）","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"Do you have anything to declare?","cn":"你有什么要申报的吗？"}},{"en":"to decide to end your innings (= the period during which your team is batting) before all your players have batted","cn":"（在击球员还未全部出局时）宣布结束赛局，宣布停止击球","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"England declared at 224 for 4 (= 4 batsmen had scored 224 runs).","cn":"英格兰队在 4 名击球手得 224 分后宣布结束赛局。"}}]}},"deposit":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"订金;保证金","en":"A deposit is a sum of money which is part of the full price of something, and which you pay when you agree to buy it.","ex":{"en":"A £50 deposit is required when ordering, and the balance is due upon delivery.","cn":"订货时需要交50英镑的订金，货到后余款结清。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(租赁的)押金","en":"A deposit is a sum of money which you pay when you start renting something. The money is returned to you if you do not damage what you have rented.","ex":{"en":"It is common to ask for the equivalent of a month's rent as a deposit.","cn":"要求交一个月的房租作押金是很常见的。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(尤指定期)存款","en":"A deposit is a sum of money which is in a bank account or savings account, especially a sum which will be left there for some time."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"竞选保证金(参加议会或欧洲选举时提交，如获一定比例选票便可返还)","en":"A deposit is a sum of money which you have to pay if you want to be a candidate in a parliamentary or European election. The money is returned to you if you receive more than a certain percentage of the votes.","ex":{"en":"The Tory candidate lost his deposit.","cn":"这名托利党候选人连竞选保证金都搭进去了。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"沉淀物;沉积物","en":"A deposit is an amount of a substance that has been left somewhere as a result of a chemical or geological process.","ex":{"en":"After 10 minutes the surplus material is washed away and any remaining deposit examined with ultra violet light.","cn":"10分钟后剩余的物质被冲洗掉，任何残留的沉淀物则会用紫外线进行检测。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"放下;放置;丢下","en":"To deposit someone or something somewhere means to put them or leave them there.","ex":{"en":"Someone was seen depositing a packet","cn":"有人看见一个人放下了件小包裹。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"存放;寄存","en":"If you deposit something somewhere, you put it where it will be safe until it is needed again.","ex":{"en":"You are advised to deposit valuables in the hotel safe.","cn":"建议把贵重物品存放在宾馆的保险箱里。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"将（钱）存入银行（或储蓄）账户","en":"If you deposit a sum of money, you pay it into a bank account or savings account.","ex":{"en":"The customer has to deposit a minimum of £100 monthly.","cn":"顾客必须每月至少存 100 英镑。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"使沉淀;使沉积","en":"If a substance is deposited somewhere, it is left there as a result of a chemical or geological process.","ex":{"en":"The phosphate was deposited by the decay of marine microorganisms.","cn":"海洋微生物腐烂后沉积形成磷酸盐。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an amount of money that you pay for something, especially when it is only one part of the total amount you have to pay","cn":""},{"en":"a regular payment you make to pay back money that you have borrowed or to pay for things that you have already received","cn":""},{"en":"part of the cost of something that you pay before you get it, so that it will not be sold to anyone else","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"1 n v 2 n 3 n","senses":[{"en":"You are making a deposit when you put money into your bank account. In that sentence, deposit is a noun, but you could express the same action using deposit as a verb. You deposit money into your bank account."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. bank, building society Building society deposits have increased by 2.3%. | cash | dollar, sterling, etc.","VERB + DEPOSIT make She made a deposit of &pound; 60 into her account.","DEPOSIT + NOUN account 2 money which is the first payment for sth","VERB + DEPOSIT pay, put down","PREP. ~ on We've put down the deposit on our new car. 3 money paid when you rent sth","ADJ. refundable, returnable All deposits for holiday cottages are refundable.","VERB + DEPOSIT give (sb), leave (sb), pay (sb) You have to pay a deposit of &pound; 100 as well as two months' rent. | get back You'll get b","PREP. ~ on I had to leave a &pound; 50 deposit on the bike. 4 layer of sth"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/2/deposit_v0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/2/deposit1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"( informal ) I was whisked off in a taxi and deposited outside the hotel.","cn":"一辆出租车匆匆把我送到旅馆外面，让我下了车。"},{"en":"They normally ask you to pay $100 (as a) deposit.","cn":"他们通常要求付 100 元（作为）订金。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpɒzɪt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a sum of money that is given as the first part of a larger payment","cn":"订金；订钱","g":"[usually singular]","lab":"British English","sc":"money","ex":{"en":"They normally ask you to pay $100 (as a) deposit.","cn":"他们通常要求付 100 美元（作为）订金。"}},{"en":"a sum of money that is paid by somebody when they rent something and that is returned to them if they do not lose or damage the thing they are renting","cn":"押金","g":"[usually singular]","sc":"money","ex":{"en":"to pay a deposit","cn":"付押金"}},{"en":"a sum of money that is paid into a bank account","cn":"存款","lab":"informal","sc":"money","ex":{"en":"Deposits can be made at any branch.","cn":"在任何一家分行都可以存钱。"}},{"en":"(in the British political system) the amount of money that a candidate in an election to Parliament has to pay, and that is returned if he/she gets enough votes","cn":"竞选保证金（英国议员候选人预付，获得足够的票数则退还）","sc":"money","ex":{"en":"All the other candidates lost their deposits.","cn":"所有其余候选人都失掉了竞选保证金。"}},{"en":"a layer of a substance that has formed naturally underground","cn":"（地下自然形成的）沉积物，沉积层","sc":"substance","ex":{"en":"mineral/gold/coal deposits","cn":"矿床；金矿；煤藏"}},{"en":"a layer of a substance that has been left somewhere, especially by a river, flood, etc., or is found at the bottom of a liquid","cn":"（尤指河流、洪水、液体等的）沉积物，淤积物","sc":"substance","ex":{"en":"The rain left a deposit of mud on the windows.","cn":"雨水在窗上留下一层泥。"}},{"en":"to put money into a bank account","cn":"将（钱）存入银行；存储","sc":"money","ex":{"en":"Millions were deposited in Swiss bank accounts.","cn":"巨额款项存入了瑞士的银行账户。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to pay a sum of money as the first part of a larger payment; to pay a sum of money that you will get back if you return in good condition something that you have rented","cn":"付（订金）；付（保证金）；付（押金）","sc":"money","pos":"verb"},{"en":"to put or lay somebody/something down in a particular place","cn":"放下；放置","lab":"informal","sc":"put down","ex":{"en":"She deposited a pile of books on my desk.","cn":"她把一摞书放在我的书桌上。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to leave a layer of something on the surface of something, especially gradually and over a period of time","cn":"使沉积；使沉淀；使淤积","sc":"leave substance","ex":{"en":"Sand was deposited which hardened into sandstone.","cn":"沙经沉积固结形成砂岩。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to put something valuable or important in a place where it will be safe","cn":"寄放，寄存（贵重物品）","sc":"put in safe place","ex":{"en":"Guests may deposit their valuables in the hotel safe.","cn":"旅客可将贵重物品寄存在旅馆的保险柜里。"},"pos":"verb"}]}},"deployment":{"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to organize or move soldiers, military equipment etc so that they are in the right place and ready to be used","cn":""},{"en":"to use something for a particular purpose, especially ideas, arguments etc","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"Deployment is a word, often used by the military, for sending troops into duty. A soldier could be part of a deployment to the Middle East."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. effective, efficient | rapid | full Without the full deployment of resources, we cannot achieve our aims. | staff | military, troop","VERB + DEPLOYMENT be available for"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/b/deploy0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/4/deploy.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"NATO’s decision to deploy cruise missiles","cn":""},{"en":"a job in which a variety of professional skills will be deployed","cn":""}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈplɔɪmənt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the act of moving soldiers or weapons into a position where they are ready for military action","cn":"（对军队或武器的）部署，调度","g":"[uncountable, countable]","ex":{"en":"the deployment of peacekeeping forces","cn":"维和部队的部署"}},{"en":"the act of using something effectively","cn":"善用；利用","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"the deployment of resources/staff","cn":"资源／人员的利用"}}]}},"defensive":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"防御（性）的;防卫（用）的;保护的","en":"You use defensive to describe things that are intended to protect someone or something.","ex":{"en":"The Government hastily organized defensive measures against the raids","cn":"政府急忙布置了防卫措施抵御空袭。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"（表现在行为上）防御的，戒备的，卫护的","en":"Someone who is defensive is behaving in a way that shows they feel unsure or threatened.","ex":{"en":"Like their children, parents are often defensive about their private lives.","cn":"就像子女一样，父母也常常很注重保护他们的私生活。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"处于防御姿态;处于守势","en":"If someone is on the defensive, they are trying to protect themselves or their interests because they feel unsure or threatened.","ex":{"en":"Accusations are likely to put the other person on the defensive","cn":"谴责很可能会引发对方自我防卫的反应。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(体育运动中的打法)防守（型）的","en":"In sports, defensive play is play that is intended to prevent your opponent from scoring goals or points against you.","ex":{"en":"I'd always played a defensive game, waiting for my opponent to make a mistake.","cn":"我总是采取防守型的打法，等待对手出错。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"all the weapons, soldiers, systems, or activities that a country uses to defend itself against attack by an enemy","cn":""},{"en":"methods used by countries or people to stop themselves from being attacked or harmed","cn":""},{"en":"all the soldiers and equipment that are available for defending a country or place","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n adj","senses":[{"en":"Someone on the defensive is concerned with justifying their actions or words. They have a defensive attitude as they try to protect themselves."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be","ADV. purely These are purely defensive measures. | essentially, largely a largely defensive campaign 2 showing you feel sb is criticizing yo","VERBS be, feel, look, seem, sound | become, get Whenever anyone mention women's rights, he gets rather defensive.","ADV. extremely, fiercely, very He did not once glance at his listeners and seemed fiercely defensive. | a little, rather, slightly, somewhat","PREP. about He is extremely defensive about his work."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/2/defensive_adj0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/7/defensive1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Warnings of an enemy attack forced the troops onto the defensive.","cn":"敌军显示出进攻的迹象，部队不得不进入戒备状态。"},{"en":"Their questions about the money put her on the defensive.","cn":"他们问到钱的问题时，她就警觉起来。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfensɪv","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"protecting somebody/something against attack","cn":"防御的；保护的；保卫的","ex":{"en":"As a defensive measure he built a series of coastal forts and watchtowers.","cn":"作为防御措施，他建造了一系列沿海堡垒和瞭望塔。"}},{"en":"behaving in a way that shows that you feel that people are criticizing you","cn":"戒备的；怀有戒心的；自卫的","ex":{"en":"Don't ask him about his plans—he just gets defensive.","cn":"别问他有什么计划，他老存有戒心。"}},{"en":"connected with trying to prevent the other team or player from scoring points or goals","cn":"防守的","lab":"sport","ex":{"en":"defensive play","cn":"防守型打法"}}]}},"devour":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"狼吞虎咽地吃;吞食","en":"If a person or animal devours something, they eat it quickly and eagerly.","ex":{"en":"A medium-sized dog will devour at least one can of food per day","cn":"中型犬每天至少要吃掉一罐狗粮。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"如饥似渴地阅读;热切地看","en":"If you devour a book or magazine, for example, you read it quickly and with great enthusiasm.","ex":{"en":"She began devouring newspapers when she was only 12.","cn":"年仅 12 岁时，她就开始如饥似渴地阅读报纸。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to eat something very quickly, especially because you like it very much or you are greedy","cn":""},{"en":"to eat food quickly, especially because you are very hungry or in a hurry","cn":""},{"en":"to eat food very quickly, especially because you are in a hurry","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"Proper ladies poke at a meal, gentlemen eat a meal, and teenagers devour a meal like ravenous cowhands who haven't seen the inside of a bowl since Christmas, and here it is July. Devour means to eat greedily."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. eagerly, greedily, hungrily He devoured the food greedily. | quickly The animal quickly devoured its prey."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/7/devour0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/b/devour.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"She devoured everything she could lay her hands on: books, magazines and newspapers.","cn":"无论是书、杂志，还是报纸，只要能弄到手，她都看得津津有味。"},{"en":"She was devoured by envy and hatred.","cn":"她心中充满嫉妒和憎恨。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈvaʊə(r)","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to eat all of something quickly, especially because you are very hungry","cn":"（尤指因饥饿而）狼吞虎咽地吃光","ex":{"en":"He devoured half of his burger in one bite.","cn":"他一口吞下半个汉堡包。"}},{"en":"to read or look at something with great interest and enthusiasm","cn":"津津有味地看；如饥似渴地读","ex":{"en":"She devoured everything she could lay her hands on: books, magazines and newspapers.","cn":"无论是书、杂志，还是报纸，只要能弄到手，她都看得津津有味。"}},{"en":"to destroy somebody/something","cn":"吞没；吞噬；毁灭","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"Flames devoured the house.","cn":"大火吞噬了这栋房子。"}}]}},"deprivation":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"剥夺;丧失;贫困;匮乏","en":"If you suffer deprivation, you do not have or are prevented from having something that you want or need.","ex":{"en":"...long-term patients who face a life of deprivation","cn":"面临终生贫困的长期病患"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the lack of something that you need in order to be healthy, comfortable, or happy","cn":"缺少﹐匮乏；贫困"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"A state of deprivation means something is missing, and the situation is serious. If you're suffering from \"sleep deprivation ,\" you haven't slept in a long time."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. acute, severe, terrible | sensory | emotional | economic, material, social an area of acute social and economic deprivation | inner-cit","VERB + DEPRIVATION experience, suffer Many of the people suffered terrible deprivation."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/2/ld41deprivation.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/a/deprivation.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"neglected children suffering from social deprivation","cn":"遭社会遗弃无人照管的孩子"},{"en":"the deprivation of war (= the suffering caused by not having enough of some things)","cn":"战时的物品匮乏"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdeprɪˈveɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the fact of not having something that you need, like enough food, money or a home; the process that causes this","cn":"贫困；丧失；剥夺","ex":{"en":"children living in poverty and deprivation","cn":"生活在贫困和物资匮乏中的儿童"}}]}},"demon":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"魔鬼;恶魔","en":"A demon is an evil spirit.","ex":{"en":"...a woman possessed by demons.","cn":"被魔鬼附身的女子"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"心魔;邪恶的事物","en":"Sources of worry or conflict which trouble a person or group of people are sometimes referred to as demons .","ex":{"en":"His private demons drove him to drink excessively for many years.","cn":"他个人的心魔让他多年以来酗酒度日。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"技艺出众的人;精力过人的人;高手;能手","en":"If you approve of someone because they are very skilled at what they do or because they do it energetically, you can say that they do it like a demon .","ex":{"en":"He played like a demon","cn":"他球艺惊人。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"恶人;恶棍;魔头","en":"If you refer to a powerful person such as a politician as a demon, you mean that you believe they are bad and might be dangerous.","ex":{"en":"She was a dictator and a demon","cn":"她是一个独裁者，一个女魔头。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an evil spirit or force","cn":"魔鬼﹐恶魔"},{"en":"something that makes you anxious and causes you problems","cn":"烦恼﹐心魔"},{"en":"someone who is very good at something – often used humorously","cn":"好手﹐高手〔常为幽默用法〕"}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. evil tales of travellers attacked by evil demons","VERB + DEMON be plagued by, be possessed by He is plagued by demons which go back to his traumatic childhood. The villagers believed the gir"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/7/demon0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/1/demon.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"demons torturing the sinners in Hell","cn":"地狱里折磨罪人的魔鬼"},{"en":"He skis like a demon.","cn":"他滑雪技艺超群。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdiːmən","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an evil spirit","cn":"魔鬼；恶魔","ex":{"en":"The people believed the girl was possessed by demons.","cn":"人们相信这个女孩被恶魔附体了。"}},{"en":"something that causes a person to worry and makes them unhappy","cn":"（使人担忧和不快的）邪恶事物","ex":{"en":"the demons of jealousy","cn":"恶魔一样的嫉妒心"}},{"en":"a person who does something very well or with a lot of energy","cn":"技艺出众的人；精力充沛的人","lab":"informal","ex":{"en":"He skis like a demon.","cn":"他滑雪技艺超群。"}}]}},"deplete":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（大量）减少，消耗","en":"To deplete a stock or amount of something means to reduce it.","ex":{"en":"...substances that deplete the ozone layer","cn":"大量消耗臭氧层的物质"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to gradually reduce the amount or value of something, especially money, wages, or profits over a period of time","cn":""},{"en":"if costs, rising prices, etc eat into the amount of money you have, they reduce its value","cn":""},{"en":"to reduce the amount of something to a level that is too low","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"To deplete is to use up or consume a limited resource. Visiting relatives might deplete your refrigerator of food, or a pestering friend might deplete your patience."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. heavily, seriously, severely Both teams were severely depleted by injuries."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/d/deplete0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/1/deplete.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Food supplies were severely depleted.","cn":"食物供应已严重不足。"},{"en":"the depletion of fish stocks","cn":"鱼量消耗殆尽"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpliːt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to reduce something by a large amount so that there is not enough left; to be reduced by a large amount","cn":"大量减少；耗尽；使枯竭","ex":{"en":"Food supplies were severely depleted.","cn":"食物供应已严重不足。"}}]}},"demoniac":{"vocab":{"pos":"n adj","senses":[{"en":"Use the adjective demoniac to describe something or someone who seems to be possessed by a demon, like the demoniac rantings of the actors portraying scary creatures at the haunted house."}]}},"deputation":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（尤指代表更多人提出投诉的）代表团","en":"A deputation is a small group of people who have been asked to speak to someone on behalf of a larger group of people, especially in order to make a complaint.","ex":{"en":"A deputation of elders from the village arrived headed by its chief.","cn":"村里的长者代表团在村长的带领下到达了。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a team of people who have been sent by an organization or a country to represent them at an important meeting","cn":""},{"en":"a group of people representing a larger group who are sent to talk to a person in authority in order to make a complaint or a request","cn":""},{"en":"a group of people who are sent by their government to another country in order to discuss something","cn":""}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERB + DEPUTATION organize | send They sent a deputation to the ministry to complain. | meet, receive","PREP. ~ from The managing director agreed to receive a deputation from the factory. | ~ of A deputation of 40 strikers was organized."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/f/ld41deputation.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/c/deputation.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdepjuˈteɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a small group of people who are asked or allowed to act or speak for others","cn":"代表团","ex":{"en":"The mayor agreed to receive a deputation of local residents.","cn":"市长同意接待当地居民代表团。"}}]}},"deficiency":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"（尤指身体所需物质的）缺乏，缺少，不足","en":"Deficiency in something, especially something that your body needs, is not having enough of it.","ex":{"en":"They did blood tests on him for signs of vitamin deficiency","cn":"他们给他验了血，以检查是否有维生素缺乏的迹象。"}},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"缺点;缺陷;瑕疵","en":"A deficiency that someone or something has is a weakness or imperfection in them.","ex":{"en":"...a serious deficiency in our air defence.","cn":"我们在空防上的严重缺陷"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a situation in which there is not enough of something very basic and important that people need in order to live or work","cn":""},{"en":"the amount by which there is not enough of something","cn":""},{"en":"when there is not enough of an important or necessary substance or quality","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"A deficiency is an insufficient amount of something. If feel sluggish and tired all day, you might have an iron deficiency , meaning you aren't eating enough iron-rich foods."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. major, serious, severe | slight, small | dietary, nutritional | enzyme, hormone, mineral, nutrient, vitamin | calcium, iron, etc.","VERB + DEFICIENCY have, suffer from suffering from a severe vitamin deficiency | correct, make good, make up, overcome, remedy I've been pre","PREP. ~ in serious deficiencies in the health service"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/a/deficiency0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/4/deficiency.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Vitamin deficiency in the diet can cause illness.","cn":"饮食中缺乏维生素可能导致疾病。"},{"en":"deficiencies in the computer system","cn":"计算机系统的种种缺陷"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfɪʃnsi","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the state of not having, or not having enough of, something that is essential","cn":"缺乏；缺少；不足","g":"[uncountable, countable]","ex":{"en":"Vitamin deficiency in the diet can cause illness.","cn":"饮食中缺乏维生素会导致疾病。"}},{"en":"a fault or a weakness in something/somebody that makes it or them less successful","cn":"缺点；缺陷","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"deficiencies in the computer system","cn":"计算机系统的种种缺陷"}}]}},"despondent":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"沮丧的;泄气的;失望的","en":"If you are despondent, you are very unhappy because you have been experiencing difficulties that you think you will not be able to overcome.","ex":{"en":"I feel despondent when my work is rejected.","cn":"作品被拒后我感到很沮丧。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"a sad feeling, caused especially when a happy time is ending, or when you feel sorry about someone else's unhappiness","cn":""},{"en":"the unhappy feeling you have when you are in a very difficult or unpleasant situation","cn":""},{"en":"great sadness that you feel when someone you love has died","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj","senses":[{"en":"If you are despondent , you are discouraged, very sad, and without hope. If you are depressed, you might describe your mood as despondent ."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be, feel Patients often feel despondent. | become, get, grow His work was rejected again and again, and he grew more and more desponde","ADV. very | utterly She was feeling utterly despondent. | a bit, pretty, rather, somewhat","PREP. about He had become rather despondent about his lack of progress."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/2/despondent0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/c/despondent.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"She was becoming increasingly despondent about the way things were going.","cn":"她对情况的发展越来越失望。"},{"en":"Life's not all gloom and despondency.","cn":"生活并不都是悲观和失望。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈspɒndənt","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"sad, without much hope","cn":"苦恼的；沮丧的；泄气的；失望的","ex":{"en":"There are times when it is hard not to feel despondent.","cn":"有时很难不感到沮丧。"}}]}},"deceive":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"欺骗;诓骗","en":"If you deceive someone, you make them believe something that is not true, usually in order to get some advantage for yourself.","ex":{"en":"He has deceived and disillusioned us all","cn":"他欺骗了大家，让我们失望至极。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"欺骗，蒙骗(自己)","en":"If you deceive yourself, you do not admit to yourself something that you know is true.","ex":{"en":"Alcoholics are notorious for their ability to deceive themselves about the extent of their problem.","cn":"酗酒者善于在自身问题的严重性上自欺欺人，这是人所共知的。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"误导;蒙蔽","en":"If something deceives you, it gives you a wrong impression and makes you believe something that is not true.","ex":{"en":"His gentle, kindly appearance did not deceive me","cn":"我没有被他文雅和善的外表所蒙蔽。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to make someone who trusts you believe something that is not true","cn":""},{"en":"to make someone believe something that is not true, in order to get something from them or make them do something","cn":""},{"en":"to make someone believe something that is not true by using a clever but simple trick","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"To deceive means to trick or lie. A crafty kid might deceive his mother into thinking he has a fever by holding the thermometer to a light bulb to increase the temperature."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. easily Human nature is such that we easily deceive ourselves.","VERB + DECEIVE attempt to, try to","PREP. into The public should not be deceived into buying inferior goods."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/4/deceive0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/0/deceive.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"You're deceiving yourself if you think he'll change his mind.","cn":"如果你认为他会改变主意，那你是在欺骗自己。"},{"en":"Unless my eyes deceive me, that's his wife.","cn":"如果我没有看错的话，那是他的妻子。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈsiːv","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to make somebody believe something that is not true","cn":"欺骗；蒙骗","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"Her husband had been deceiving her for years.","cn":"她丈夫多年来一直在欺骗她。"}},{"en":"to refuse to admit to yourself that something unpleasant is true","cn":"欺骗（自己）","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"You're deceiving yourself if you think he'll change his mind.","cn":"如果你认为他会改变主意，那你是在欺骗自己。"}},{"en":"to make somebody have a wrong idea about somebody/something","cn":"使人误信；误导","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","ex":{"en":"Unless my eyes deceive me, that's his wife.","cn":"如果我没有看错的话，那是他的妻子。"}}]}},"denial":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"否认","en":"A denial of something is a statement that it is not true, does not exist, or did not happen.","ex":{"en":"Despite official denials, the rumours still persist","cn":"尽管官方予以否认，但谣言仍未平息。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"拒绝;拒绝给予","en":"The denial of something to someone is the act of refusing to let them have it.","ex":{"en":"...the denial of visas to international relief workers","cn":"拒绝给国际救援人员发放签证"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(心理学上的)否认，拒绝接受，拒不承认","en":"In psychology, denial is when a person cannot or will not accept an unpleasant truth.","ex":{"en":"With major life traumas, like losing a loved one, for instance, the mind's first reaction is denial","cn":"面对生活中的重大不幸，如失去至爱的人等，人们的第一反应就是拒绝接受。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a statement saying that something is not true","cn":"否认﹐否定"},{"en":"when someone refuses to allow someone else to have or to do something","cn":"剥夺﹐拒绝给予"},{"en":"a condition in which you refuse to admit or believe that something bad exists or has happened 〔","cn":"对坏事的〕拒绝承认﹐不肯相信"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"A denial is a refusal, and often means a refusal to believe or accept something as the truth. \"When asked if he ate the powdered doughnut, he gave a flat denial . Since his face was covered with powdered sugar, the denial was ludicrous.\""}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. firm, strong, vehement, vigorous When I asked if she had cheated in the exam, she answered with a vehement denial. | explicit The docum","VERB + DENIAL issue, make The chairman of the company issued a denial of the allegations. Jefferson made no denial of his actions on that ni","PREP. ~ from a denial from senior officials","PHRASES a chorus of denials His question was greeted with a chorus of denials."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/a/denial0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/e/denial.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The terrorists issued a denial of responsibility for the attack.","cn":"恐怖分子发表声明，否认对这次袭击负责。"},{"en":"an official denial that there would be an election before the end of the year","cn":"对年底前将进行选举的正式否认"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈnaɪəl","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a statement that something is not true or does not exist; the action of denying something","cn":"否认；否定","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"the prisoner’s repeated denials of the charges against him","cn":"囚犯再三否认对他的指控"}},{"en":"an act of refusing to allow somebody to have something they have a right to expect","cn":"拒绝给予，剥夺（应有的权利）","g":"[countable, uncountable]","ex":{"en":"Pressure groups have drawn attention to the denial of human rights in some areas.","cn":"压力集团已让某些地区剥夺人权的状况受到关注。"}},{"en":"the act of refusing to accept that something unpleasant or painful is true","cn":"拒绝接受，拒不承认（令人不快或痛苦的事）","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"The patient is still in denial.","cn":"病人仍然拒不接受事实。"}}]}},"denali":{"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"","senses":[{"en":"a mountain in Denali National Park in central Alaska, which is the highest point in North America. It was formerly called Mount McKinley.","cn":""}]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/4/p028-000004031.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/4/p028-000004031.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dəˈnɑːli","pos":"","senses":[{"en":"the highest mountain in North America, with a height of 20 320 feet/6 198 metres, which is in Denali National Park in Alaska. From 1896 to 2015 it was called Mount McKinley.","cn":"迪纳利（北美最高的山峰，高度为 6 198 米，位于阿拉斯加的迪纳利国家公园。从 1896 年到 2015 年，它被称为麦金利山。）"},{"en":"a US national park in southern central Alaska. The park has glaciers (= masses of ice) and many wild animals, including bears and moose.","cn":"迪纳利国家公园和保护区（位于阿拉斯加中南部的美国国家公园。该公园有冰川和许多野生动物，包括熊和驼鹿。）"}]}},"detached":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"超然的;冷漠的;不带感情的","en":"Someone who is detached is not personally involved in something or has no emotional interest in it.","ex":{"en":"He tries to remain emotionally detached from the prisoners, but fails","cn":"他试图不带感情地对待那些犯人，但是做不到。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(房屋)独立式的，分开的","en":"A detached house is one that is not joined to any other house."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"not showing your feelings","cn":""},{"en":"not showing any feelings and especially not showing friendliness, humour, or pleasure","cn":""},{"en":"not showing the feelings that people usually show in an upsetting situation, because you have to do a job or because you really have no feelings about the situation","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj","senses":[{"en":"If something is detached , it stands apart from something else. That goes for people, emotions, retinas, garages, and just about anything else that can be disconnected or uninvolved."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be, feel, seem, sound | become | remain","ADV. largely, very | completely, totally, wholly | rather, slightly | curiously, oddly, strangely He felt curiously detached from what was g","PREP. from She tries to remain emotionally detached from her patients."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/9/brelasdedetached.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/9/detached.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"She wanted him to stop being so cool, so detached, so cynical.","cn":"她希望他不再那么冷酷无情，那么无动于衷，那么愤世嫉俗。"},{"en":"a detached observer","cn":"客观的观察者"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈtætʃt","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"not joined to another house on either side","cn":"单独的；独立的；不连接的"},{"en":"showing a lack of feeling","cn":"不带感情的；超然的；冷漠的","ex":{"en":"She wanted him to stop being so cool, so detached, so cynical.","cn":"她希望他不再那么冷酷无情，那么无动于衷，那么愤世嫉俗。"}},{"en":"not influenced by other people or by your own feelings","cn":"客观的；公正的；无偏见的","lab":"approving","ex":{"en":"a detached observer","cn":"客观的观察者"}}]}},"defer":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"推迟;拖延;延缓","en":"If you defer an event or action, you arrange for it to happen at a later date, rather than immediately or at the previously planned time.","ex":{"en":"Customers often defer payment for as long as possible","cn":"顾客常常会尽可能地拖延付款。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"遵从;听从;顺从","en":"If you defer to someone, you accept their opinion or do what they want you to do, even when you do not agree with it yourself, because you respect them or their authority.","ex":{"en":"Doctors are encouraged to defer to experts.","cn":"鼓励医生听从专家的意见。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to wait until a later time to do something","cn":""},{"en":"to change an event to a later time or date","cn":""},{"en":"to delay doing something. Put off is less formal than delay or postpone , and is the usual phrase to use in everyday English","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"Defer means to put off or delay. You can try to defer the inevitable by pushing “snooze” and falling back asleep, but eventually you're going to have to get up."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. further | indefinitely The decision has been deferred indefinitely.","VERB + DEFER agree to, decide to","PREP. for Sentence was deferred for six months. | pending Diagnosis was deferred pending further assessment. | till/until We agreed to defer"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/2/defer0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/6/defer.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The department deferred the decision for six months.","cn":"这个部门推迟了六个月才作决定。"},{"en":"We will defer to whatever the committee decides.","cn":"我们遵从委员会的任何决定。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfɜː(r)","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to delay something until a later time","cn":"推迟；延缓；展期","ex":{"en":"The department deferred the decision for six months.","cn":"这个部门推迟了六个月才作决定。"}}]}},"deception":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"欺骗;受骗","en":"Deception is the act of deceiving someone or the state of being deceived by someone.","ex":{"en":"He admitted conspiring to obtain property by deception","cn":"他承认曾与人合谋骗取财产。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the act of deceiving someone, especially by telling them lies","cn":""},{"en":"the act of deceiving someone - use this to show strong disapproval","cn":""},{"en":"a situation in which someone is tricked into doing something that results in them being punished","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"Deception is a trick or scheme used to get what you want, like the deception you used to get your sister to agree to do all your chores for a month."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. cruel | elaborate This elaborate deception fooled his family for ages. | deliberate","VERB + DECEPTION practise, use He'll use deception to get what he wants. | see through She failed to see through his deception. | obtain sth"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/d/deception0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/8/deception.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The whole episode had been a cruel deception.","cn":"整个经历都是残酷的骗局。"},{"en":"a drama full of lies and deception","cn":"充满谎言和欺骗的一出戏"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈsepʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the act of deliberately making somebody believe something that is not true (= of deceiving them)","cn":"欺骗；蒙骗；诓骗","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"a drama full of lies and deception","cn":"充满谎言和欺骗的一出戏"}},{"en":"a trick intended to make somebody believe something that is not true","cn":"诡计；骗术；骗局","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"The whole episode had been a cruel deception.","cn":"这起事件从头到尾就是一个残酷的骗局。"}}]}},"denmark":{"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"","senses":[{"en":"a country in northern Europe, north of Germany and surrounded on three sides by sea. Denmark forms part of Scandinavia, and the people there are called Danes. It is a member of the EU. Population: 5,556,452 (2014). Capital: Copenhagen.","cn":""}]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/2/p028-000004036.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/2/p028-000004036.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdenmɑːk","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a country in northern Europe","cn":"丹麦（北欧国家）"}]}},"decompose":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"(使）(死去的动植物)腐烂;（使）分解","en":"When things such as dead plants or animals decompose, or when something decomposes them, they change chemically and begin to decay.","ex":{"en":"...a dead body found decomposing in a wood","cn":"在树林里发现的一具正在腐烂的尸体"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to be slowly destroyed by a natural chemical process – use this especially about natural things such as wood or plants, or about teeth","cn":""},{"en":"to decay. Rot is less formal than decay and is more common in everyday English","cn":""},{"en":"if food goes off, it starts to smell bad and is no longer be safe to eat","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"1 v 2 v","senses":[{"en":"The verb decompose means to break down or decay, like tree leaves that decompose into dirt, or cell phone batteries that decompose , resulting in more frequent charging for the user."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["PHRASES badly/partially/partly decomposed His badly decomposed body was found many weeks later."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/5/decompose0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/8/decompose.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"As the waste materials decompose, they produce methane gas.","cn":"废物腐烂时会产生沼气。"},{"en":"a decomposed body","cn":"已经腐烂了的尸体"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdiːkəmˈpəʊz","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to be destroyed gradually after death by natural processes","cn":"腐烂","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","ex":{"en":"a decomposing corpse","cn":"正在腐烂的尸体"}},{"en":"to break down something into smaller and simpler parts; to break a substance down into smaller and simpler parts","cn":"（使）分解，降解","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","lab":"chemistry","ex":{"en":"Water decomposes into oxygen and hydrogen.","cn":"水分解成氧气和氢气。"}}]}},"dependable":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"可靠的;可信赖的","en":"If you say that someone or something is dependable, you approve of them because you feel that you can be sure that they will always act consistently or sensibly, or do what you need them to do.","ex":{"en":"He was a good friend, a dependable companion.","cn":"他是一个很好的朋友，一个可以信赖的伙伴。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"if someone is trustworthy, you can trust them because they are honest","cn":""},{"en":"someone who is reliable can be trusted to do what they say they will do and not make any mistakes","cn":""},{"en":"someone who is responsible can be trusted to behave in a sensible way","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj","senses":[{"en":"Dependable means \"reliable, steady, trustworthy.\" If people can always count on you, that means you are dependable."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be, seem | find sb I find him very dependable.","ADV. extremely, very | absolutely, totally, utterly She is loyal and totally dependable. | not entirely"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/b/dependable0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/c/dependable.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"our most dependable ally","cn":"我们最可靠的盟友"},{"en":"a dependable source of income","cn":"可靠的收入来源"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpendəbl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"that can be relied on to do what you want or need","cn":"可信赖的；可靠的","ex":{"en":"She is loyal and totally dependable.","cn":"她很忠诚，完全值得信赖。"}}]}},"deceptive":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"欺骗性的;造成假象的","en":"If something is deceptive, it encourages you to believe something which is not true.","ex":{"en":"Appearances can be deceptive.","cn":"外表可能是靠不住的。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"use this to say that someone or something is more interesting, important, intelligent etc than they seem to be","cn":""},{"en":"seeming to be good, friendly, safe etc, but in fact being very different","cn":""},{"en":"seeming simple, easy etc, but actually very difficult","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj","senses":[{"en":"Something that's deceptive is not what it seems. A deceptive person will lead you to believe something other than the truth. Of course, I would never be deceptive when explaining the word deceptive ."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be","ADV. highly, very | dangerously","PHRASES can be deceptive Appearances can be deceptive?dangerously deceptive."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/a/deceptive0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/3/deceptive.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"the deceptive simplicity of her writing style (= it seems simple but is not really)","cn":"她那看似简单实则不然的写作风格"},{"en":"Appearances can often be deceptive (= things are not always what they seem to be).","cn":"外表常常靠不住。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈseptɪv","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"likely to make you believe something that is not true","cn":"欺骗性的；误导的；骗人的","ex":{"en":"a deceptive advertisement","cn":"虚假广告"}}]}},"devalue":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"降低…的价值;贬低","en":"To devalue something means to cause it to be thought less impressive or less deserving of respect.","ex":{"en":"They spread tales about her in an attempt to devalue her work","cn":"他们散布一些有关她的流言，企图贬低她的工作。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"使(货币)贬值","en":"To devalue the currency of a country means to reduce its value in relation to other currencies.","ex":{"en":"India has devalued the Rupee by about eleven per cent","cn":"印度已将卢比贬值了约 11%。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to make something less important, valuable, or powerful, especially by giving it less money or support","cn":""},{"en":"to make someone or something seem less important or valuable","cn":"贬低"},{"en":"to give someone or something a less important position than before","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"When you make something less valuable or less important, you devalue it. You might devalue your car by spray painting it black and letting your dog chew the upholstery."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. effectively","PREP. against The pound was devalued against the US dollar. | by The Cambodian currency was effectively devalued by 25 per cent."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/e/devalue0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/1/devalue.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Work in the home is often ignored and devalued.","cn":"家务劳动常常被忽视和贬低。"},{"en":"There has been a further small devaluation against the dollar.","cn":"兑美元的比值继续小幅下跌。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdiːˈvæljuː","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to reduce in value when it is exchanged for the money of another country; to reduce the value of money in this way","cn":"（使）贬值","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","lab":"finance","ex":{"en":"The local currency was rapidly devaluing.","cn":"当地货币迅速贬值。"}},{"en":"to give a lower value to something, making it seem less important than it really is","cn":"降低…的价值；贬低","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"Work in the home is often ignored and devalued.","cn":"家务劳动常常被忽视和贬低。"}}]}},"deceased":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"死者","en":"The deceased is used to refer to a particular person or to particular people who have recently died.","ex":{"en":"The identities of the deceased have now been determined.","cn":"死者的身份现在已经确定。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"（近期）死去的，去世的","en":"A deceased person is one who has recently died.","ex":{"en":"...his recently deceased mother.","cn":"他刚刚去世的母亲"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"someone or something that is dead has stopped living","cn":""},{"en":"use this as a polite way of talking about someone who has died, especially someone who died recently","cn":""},{"en":"completely dead - use this when you are completely certain that someone or something is dead","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n adj","senses":[{"en":"When someone is deceased , they are dead — not dying or even just about to die. They are dead."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be","ADV. recently her recently deceased husband | sadly His mother is now sadly deceased."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/9/brelasdedeceased.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/8/deceased1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"her deceased parents","cn":"她已故的双亲"},{"en":"The deceased left a large sum of money to his children.","cn":"死者留给子女一大笔钱。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈsiːst","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"dead","cn":"死去了的；已死的；亡故的","ex":{"en":"her deceased parents","cn":"她已故的双亲"}},{"en":"a person who has died, especially recently","cn":"死者；已故者","ex":{"en":"the family of the deceased","cn":"死者家属"}}]}},"dejected":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"沮丧的;失意的;泄气的","en":"If you are dejected, you feel miserable or unhappy, especially because you have just been disappointed by something.","ex":{"en":"Everyone has days when they feel dejected or down.","cn":"每个人都有沮丧失意或情绪低落的时候。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"not happy","cn":""},{"en":"sad, especially for a long time – used about people and periods of time","cn":""},{"en":"sad because you are away from your home, family, and friends","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj","senses":[{"en":"If you're ejected from an important game, you're going to feel dejected . If you're rejected by the love of your life, you'll feel dejected again."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS appear, be, feel, look She looked sorrowful and dejected. | become, grow","ADV. completely, thoroughly, totally, utterly They were thoroughly dejected and miserable. | rather","PREP. about feeling rather dejected about the future"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/c/dejected0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/5/dejected.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"She looked so dejected when she lost the game.","cn":"她输掉比赛时情绪显得非常低落。"},{"en":"The unemployed stood at street corners, dejected.","cn":"失业者沮丧地站在街角。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈdʒektɪd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"unhappy and disappointed","cn":"沮丧的；情绪低落的；垂头丧气的","ex":{"en":"She looked so dejected when she lost the game.","cn":"她输掉比赛时情绪显得非常低落。"}}]}},"depart":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"离开;启程;动身;出发","en":"When something or someone departs from a place, they leave it and start a journey to another place.","ex":{"en":"Our tour departs from Heathrow Airport on 31 March and returns 16 April","cn":"我们这次旅行于 3月 31 号从希思罗机场出发，4 月 16 号返回。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"背离;违背","en":"If you depart from a traditional, accepted, or agreed way of doing something, you do it in a different or unexpected way.","ex":{"en":"Why is it in this country that we have departed from good educational sense?","cn":"为什么在这个国家我们背离了教育上明智的选择？"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"辞（职）；离（职）","en":"If someone departs from a job, they resign from it or leave it. In American English, you can say that someone departs a job.","ex":{"en":"Lipton is planning to depart from the company he founded.","cn":"利普顿打算离开他创立的那家公司。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"去世;离开人世","en":"When someone departs this life, or departs this earth, they die.","ex":{"en":"He departed this world with a sense of having fulfilled his destiny.","cn":"他带着一种已完成使命的满足感离开了这个世界。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to leave somewhere","cn":""},{"en":"to leave somewhere and begin a journey","cn":""},{"en":"if a plane takes off, it leaves the ground at the beginning of a flight","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"To depart is to go away or to choose a different direction. If you are catching a plane, you are soon to depart . And, if you are wearing a kilt instead of jeans, you depart from your usual look."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERB + DEPART be due to, be scheduled to The plane was scheduled to depart at 8.30. | be waiting to | prepare to They shook hands all round ","PREP. for He departs for New York tomorrow morning. | from We depart from Heathrow at ten o'clock tonight."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/4/depart0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/8/depart.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"( NAmE ) The train departed Amritsar at 6.15 p.m.","cn":"火车在下午 6 点 15 分离开了阿姆利则。"},{"en":"Flights for Rome depart from Terminal 3.","cn":"飞往罗马的班机从 3 号航空站出发。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpɑːt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to leave a place, especially to start a trip","cn":"离开；离去；启程；出发","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","lab":"North American English","ex":{"en":"Flights for Rome depart from Terminal 3.","cn":"飞往罗马的班机从 3 号航站楼出发。"}},{"en":"to leave your job","cn":"离职","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","lab":"North American English","ex":{"en":"the departing president","cn":"行将卸任的总裁"}}]}},"desolate":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"荒凉的;荒芜的;荒废的;无人烟的","en":"A desolate place is empty of people and lacking in comfort.","ex":{"en":"...a desolate landscape of flat green fields broken by marsh","cn":"平坦绿野被沼泽割裂开的荒凉景色"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"凄凉的;孤寂的;孤独忧伤的","en":"If someone is desolate, they feel very sad, alone, and without hope.","ex":{"en":"He was desolate without her.","cn":"没有她，他感到孤独而凄凉。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"使不悦;使痛苦;使悲惨","en":"If something desolates you, it upsets you and makes you very unhappy.","ex":{"en":"Their inclination to wait and demand more resources desolated President Lincoln.","cn":"他们总是等待并要求得到更多资财的倾向让林肯总统甚感不快。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"a place that is empty has no-one in it","cn":""},{"en":"a place that is deserted is empty and quiet because there is no one there, or the people who are usually there have left","cn":""},{"en":"an area or place that is uninhabited has no people living in it","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj v","senses":[{"en":"If you feel alone, left out, and devastated, you feel desolate . A deserted, empty, depressing place can be desolate too."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be, seem, stand The house stands desolate and empty. | become | leave sth The land was left desolate.","ADV. completely, quite The landscape was quite desolate. | rather a rather desolate place 2 very unhappy","VERBS be, feel, look, sound He looked as desolate as Ruth felt. | become","ADV. quite, utterly She was utterly desolate after losing her baby. | a little Her voice sounded a little desolate."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/a/desolate_adj0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/7/l3desolate.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"She had been desolated by the death of her friend.","cn":"朋友的去世使她感到十分悲伤。"},{"en":"a bleak and desolate landscape","cn":"一片荒凉的景色"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdesələt","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"empty and without people, making you feel sad or frightened","cn":"无人居住的；荒无人烟的；荒凉的","ex":{"en":"They looked out on a bleak and desolate landscape.","cn":"他们向外望去，触目一片荒凉。"}},{"en":"very lonely and unhappy","cn":"孤独凄凉的；不幸的；忧伤的","ex":{"en":"The loss of his friend made him feel utterly desolate.","cn":"失去朋友让他感到无比的悲凉。"}},{"en":"to make somebody feel sad and without hope","cn":"使感到悲惨；使感到凄凉；使悲伤绝望","ex":{"en":"She had been desolated by the death of her friend.","cn":"朋友的去世使她感到十分悲伤。"},"pos":"verb"}]}},"delegate":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"代表;(尤指)会议代表","en":"A delegate is a person who is chosen to vote or make decisions on behalf of a group of other people, especially at a conference or a meeting."},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"授(权);把(职责、责任等)委托(给)","en":"If you delegate duties, responsibilities, or power to someone, you give them those duties, those responsibilities, or that power so that they can act on your behalf.","ex":{"en":"He plans to delegate more authority to his deputies","cn":"他打算把更多的权力交给副手。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"授权，委派（做）","en":"If you are delegated to do something, you are given the duty of acting on someone else's behalf by making decisions, voting, or doing some particular work.","ex":{"en":"Officials have now been delegated to start work on a draft settlement.","cn":"现在已经委派官员着手起草解决方案。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"someone who has been chosen to represent an organization or country","cn":""},{"en":"a person who officially gives the opinions of an organization, company, government etc","cn":""},{"en":"a word meaning spokesman or spokeswoman , used especially when you do not want to say whether the person is a man or a woman","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n v","senses":[{"en":"Delegate lends an official air to passing off your work. If you don't like cleaning the bathroom, you can try to delegate that task to your little brother."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. conference, congress, convention | government, party, trade union","VERB + DELEGATE elect | send They decided not to send a delegate to the conference.","DELEGATE + VERB attend (sth) No fewer than 2,000 delegates attended the conference.","PREP. ~ from a delegate from the local Labour party | ~ to the British delegate to the United Nations"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/3/delegate_n0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/6/l3delegate.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The conference was attended by delegates from 56 countries.","cn":"此次会议有来自 56 个国家的代表出席。"},{"en":"Some managers find it difficult to delegate.","cn":"有些经理认为难以做到知人善任。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdelɪɡət","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person who is chosen or elected to represent the views of a group of people and vote and make decisions for them","cn":"代表；会议代表","ex":{"en":"Congress delegates rejected the proposals.","cn":"国会代表拒绝了这些提议。"}},{"en":"a person who attends a conference","cn":"参会人员；会议出席者","ex":{"en":"The conference was attended by delegates from 56 countries.","cn":"此次会议有来自 56 个国家的代表出席。"}},{"en":"to give part of your work, power or authority to somebody in a lower position than you","cn":"授（权）；把（工作、权力等）委托（给下级）","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","ex":{"en":"Some managers find it difficult to delegate.","cn":"有些经理认为难以做到下放权力。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to choose somebody to do something","cn":"选派（某人做某事）","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"I've been delegated to organize the Christmas party.","cn":"我被选派来组织圣诞聚会。"},"pos":"verb"}]}},"decency":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"合宜;得体;正派;合乎礼仪","en":"Decency is the quality of following accepted moral standards.","ex":{"en":"Unfortunately, on Friday night he showed neither decency nor dignity","cn":"不幸的是，周五晚上他表现得既不得体，也不庄重。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"（出于礼貌）应该做（但没做）…","en":"If you say that someone did not have the decency to do something, you are criticizing them because there was a particular action which they did not do but which you believe they ought to have done.","ex":{"en":"Nobody had the decency to inform me of what was planned.","cn":"竟然没有一个人最起码地通知我一声计划了些什么。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"what is good in a person's character","cn":""},{"en":"good actions, characteristics, or behaviour","cn":""},{"en":"kindness, honesty, and fairness in the way that you treat other people","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"The personal quality of decency is one of honesty, good manners, and respect for other people."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. common, human a lack of common decency | public Your behaviour is an affront to public decency.","VERB + DECENCY have He might have had the decency to let us know.","PHRASES a sense of decency, standards of decency"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/e/decency0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/5/decency.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Her behaviour showed a total lack of common decency.","cn":"她的举止显示她连起码的礼节都不懂。"},{"en":"the basic decencies of civilized society","cn":"文明社会的基本行为准则"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdiːsnsi","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"honest, polite behaviour that follows accepted moral standards and shows respect for others","cn":"正派；得体；彬彬有礼","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"Her behaviour showed a total lack of common decency.","cn":"她的举止显示她连起码的礼节都不懂。"}},{"en":"standards of behaviour in society that people think are acceptable","cn":"礼仪；行为准则","g":"[plural]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"the basic decencies of civilized society","cn":"文明社会的基本行为准则"}}]}},"defenceless":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"无防御的;无保护的;不能自卫的;无助的","en":"If someone or something is defenceless, they are weak and unable to defend themselves properly.","ex":{"en":"...a savage attack on a defenceless young girl.","cn":"对一名没有自卫能力的年轻女子的野蛮攻击"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"someone who is vulnerable can easily be harmed or attacked","cn":""},{"en":"not strong enough or not able to protect yourself against an attack","cn":""},{"en":"someone who is unarmed is not carrying a gun or other weapon","cn":""}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be, feel, lie The city lay defenceless before the most powerful fighting force on the continent. | leave sb They were left virtually d","ADV. entirely, quite, totally, utterly She felt utterly defenceless. | almost, virtually","PREP. against They were completely defenceless against enemy attack.","PHRASES poor defenceless stealing money from a poor defenceless old lady"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/b/ld44defenceless.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/b/ld44defenceless.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The village is defenceless against attack.","cn":"这个村庄毫无防御能力。"},{"en":"defenceless children","cn":"没有自卫能力的儿童"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfensləs","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"weak; not able to protect yourself; having no protection","cn":"软弱的；不能自卫的；无防御的","ex":{"en":"defenceless children","cn":"没有自卫能力的儿童"}}]}},"deadlock":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"僵局;僵持","en":"If a dispute or series of negotiations reaches deadlock, neither side is willing to give in at all and no agreement can be made.","ex":{"en":"They called for a compromise on all sides to break the deadlock in the world trade talks","cn":"他们呼吁各方作出让步以打破世界贸易谈判中的僵局。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a situation in which no further progress can be made because two groups or organizations cannot find a way to end a disagreement","cn":""},{"en":"a situation in which progress has stopped completely, especially because people cannot agree on what to do next","cn":""},{"en":"to slowly stop making any progress","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"Use the noun deadlock to describe a standstill, as when two people or sides cannot move beyond a disagreement."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. complete | political","VERB + DEADLOCK end in, reach The negotiations ended in deadlock. The strike appeared to have reached a deadlock. | break, resolve","PREP. in ~ The negotiations were adjourned in deadlock last week. | ~ between the deadlock between striking workers and their employer | ~ i","PHRASES a state of deadlock Talks between the two sides remain in a state of complete deadlock."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/0/deadlock0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/2/deadlock.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"European agriculture ministers failed to break the deadlock over farm subsidies.","cn":"欧洲各国农业部长在农业补贴问题上未能打破僵局。"},{"en":"Despite months of discussion the negotiations remained deadlocked.","cn":"尽管已讨论数月，谈判仍僵持不下。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdedlɒk","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a complete failure to reach agreement or settle an argument","cn":"僵持；僵局；相持不下","g":"[singular, uncountable]","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"European agriculture ministers failed to break the deadlock over farm subsidies.","cn":"欧洲各国农业部长在农业补贴问题上未能打破僵局。"}},{"en":"a type of lock on a door that needs a key to open or close it","cn":"需用钥匙开关的门锁","g":"[countable]","lab":"British English"}]}},"deport":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"驱逐(非本国居民)出境","en":"If a government deports someone, usually someone who is not a citizen of that country, it sends them out of the country because they have committed a crime or because it believes they do not have the right to be there.","ex":{"en":"...a government decision earlier this month to deport all illegal immigrants","cn":"本月早些时候出台的将所有非法移民驱逐出境的政府决议"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to make a foreigner leave a country because they have broken the law, or for political reasons","cn":""},{"en":"if the authorities in a country deport a foreign person or a member of a particular race who is living in that country, they force them to leave","cn":""},{"en":"to officially send someone back to another country where they are believed to have committed a crime, in order to be tried in a court of law","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"1 v 2 v","senses":[{"en":"To deport is to kick someone out of a country. Deporting is also to deliver a person to the authorities of another country. Although you might like to deport your little brother from your room, it’s something governments do."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. forcibly","PREP. (back) to Many refugees were forcibly deported back to the countries they had come from. | from He was deported from Britain last week"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/8/deport0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/a/deport1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Several of the asylum seekers now face deportation.","cn":"寻求避难的人中有几个正面临递解出境。"},{"en":"a deportation order","cn":"驱逐出境令"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpɔːt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to force somebody to leave a country, usually because they have broken the law or because they have no legal right to be there","cn":"把（违法者或无居留权的人）驱逐出境；递解出境","ex":{"en":"He was convicted of drug offences and deported.","cn":"他被判犯了毒品罪被驱逐出境。"}}]}},"deter":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"威慑住;吓住;阻止;制止","en":"To deter someone from doing something means to make them not want to do it or continue doing it.","ex":{"en":"Supporters of the death penalty argue that it would deter criminals from carrying guns","cn":"死刑的支持者认为它能阻吓罪犯携带枪支。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to make someone decide not to do something, by giving them reasons why they should not do it","cn":""},{"en":"to talk to someone about something they are planning to do, and persuade them not to do it","cn":""},{"en":"to stop someone wanting to do something, by making them think that it will be difficult or unpleasant","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"Deter means to discourage. Many believe that the use of capital punishment deters people from committing murder. Others think that is hogwash."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. hardly Her words of warning would hardly deter him. | effectively, sufficiently Will this harsher punishment effectively deter criminal","VERB + DETER be likely/unlikely to | be enough to, be sufficient to | attempt to | be designed to | do little to, do nothing to The present ","PREP. from These new rules are likely to deter people from coming forward for help."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/3/deter0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/9/deter.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"I told him I wasn't interested, but he wasn't deterred.","cn":"我已告诉他我不感兴趣，可他却不罢休。"},{"en":"The high price of the service could deter people from seeking advice.","cn":"这么高的服务费可能使咨询者望而却步。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈtɜː(r)","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to make somebody decide not to do something or continue doing something, especially by making them understand the difficulties and unpleasant results of their actions","cn":"制止；阻止；威慑；使不敢","ex":{"en":"I told him I wasn't interested, but he wasn't deterred.","cn":"我已告诉他我不感兴趣，可他却不罢休。"}}]}},"deficit":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"差额;赤字;亏损;逆差","en":"A deficit is the amount by which something is less than what is required or expected, especially the amount by which the total money received is less than the total money spent.","ex":{"en":"They're ready to cut the federal budget deficit for the next fiscal year.","cn":"他们已准备好削减下一财年的联邦预算赤字。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the difference between the amount of something that you have and the higher amount that you need","cn":"逆差﹐亏损﹐赤字﹐不足额"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"If you're running a deficit , you are losing. You might be losing money or losing a game. Either way, you better make up for it."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. huge, large, massive, serious, substantial | small | net, overall | balance-of-payments, budget, budgetary, financial, fiscal, trade","VERB + DEFICIT face, have, run, show If the government didn't run such huge deficits, the country would not have financial problems. The tra","DEFICIT + VERB run at sth a budget deficit running at 7% of GDP | grow, increase, rise, widen | decrease, fall, narrow, shrink","PREP. in ~ The UK remained in deficit with all countries outside the EU. | ~ with the US trade deficit with Japan"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/8/deficit0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/a/deficit.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"There's a deficit of $3 million in the total needed to complete the project.","cn":"完成这项工程所需资金中有 300 万元的亏空。"},{"en":"The team has to come back from a 2–0 deficit in the first half.","cn":"这支队得扳回上半场 0:2 的落后局面。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdefɪsɪt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the amount by which money spent or owed is greater than money earned in a particular period of time","cn":"赤字；逆差；亏损","lab":"economics","ex":{"en":"a budget/trade deficit","cn":"预算赤字；贸易逆差"}},{"en":"the amount by which something, especially an amount of money, is too small or smaller than something else","cn":"不足额；缺款额；缺少","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"There's a deficit of $3 million in the total needed to complete the project.","cn":"完成这项工程所需资金还缺少 300 万美元。"}}]}},"deprived":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"贫困的;贫穷的","en":"Deprived people or people from deprived areas do not have the things that people consider to be essential in life, for example acceptable living conditions or education.","ex":{"en":"...probably the most severely deprived children in the country.","cn":"可能是这个国家里最贫困的儿童"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"having very little money and not many possessions – used about people or places","cn":""},{"en":"having very little money, especially for a short period of time. Skint is more informal than the other words","cn":""},{"en":"a developing country is poor and has very little industry","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj","senses":[{"en":"Being deprived means lacking important things like food and water. For example, when warm clothing, housing, and nutrition are in short supply, the people are deprived of basics of life."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be, feel","ADV. extremely, severely, terribly, very | totally | relatively | economically, emotionally, materially, socially emotionally deprived child","PREP. of children who are deprived of love"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/0/brelasdedeprived.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/4/deprived.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"economically/emotionally/socially deprived","cn":"经济困难的；感情失落的；社会遗弃的"},{"en":"a deprived childhood/background/area","cn":"贫穷的童年/出身/地区"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpraɪvd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"without enough food, education, and all the things that are necessary for people to live a happy and comfortable life","cn":"贫穷的；贫困的；穷苦的","ex":{"en":"a deprived childhood/background/area","cn":"贫穷的童年／出身／地区"}},{"en":"suffering from a lack of the thing mentioned","cn":"被剥夺的；缺乏的","ex":{"en":"The American adult population is chronically sleep-deprived.","cn":"美国成年人长期睡眠不足。"}}]}},"detect":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"发现;查出;测出","en":"To detect something means to find it or discover that it is present somewhere by using equipment or making an investigation.","ex":{"en":"...a sensitive piece of equipment used to detect radiation","cn":"一件用于探测辐射的灵敏设备"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"觉察;发觉","en":"If you detect something, you notice it or sense it, even though it is not very obvious.","ex":{"en":"Arnold could detect a certain sadness in the old man's face.","cn":"阿诺德能觉察到老人脸上的一丝悲伤。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to realize that something is there or that something is happening, because you can see, hear, or feel it","cn":""},{"en":"to notice something that is difficult to see, hear etc because it is very small, faint, or unclear. Detect is used about people and machines, and is more formal than notice","cn":""},{"en":"to notice something, especially something that is difficult to see or that you see for a short time only. Spot is more informal than notice","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"The verb detect means to discover or observe the existence of something. If you walk into your house and detect the odor of burnt food, you can deduce from the evidence that you will be going out to dinner tonight!"}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. early, late A lot of cancers can now be cured if they are detected early. | quickly | easily, readily Some substances can be detected f","VERB + DETECT be able to, be sensitive enough to, can a machine that is sensitive enough to detect tiny amounts of explosives | be unable to","PHRASES be capable of detecting sth, a means/method/way of detecting sth"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/c/detect0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/0/detect.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The noise is barely detectable by the human ear.","cn":"这种声音人的耳朵几乎是察觉不到的。"},{"en":"Do I detect a note of criticism?","cn":"这里面是不是好像带有批评的意味？"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈtekt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to discover or notice something, especially something that is not easy to see, hear, etc.","cn":"发现；查明；侦察出","ex":{"en":"The tests are designed to detect the disease early.","cn":"这些检查旨在早期查出疾病。"}}]}},"degenerate":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"恶化;变糟;衰退;堕落","en":"If you say that someone or something degenerates, you mean that they become worse in some way, for example weaker, lower in quality, or more dangerous.","ex":{"en":"Inactivity can make your joints stiff, and the bones may begin to degenerate","cn":"长期不活动会导致关节僵硬，骨骼也可能开始退化。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"堕落的;腐化的","en":"If you describe a person or their behaviour as degenerate, you disapprove of them because you think they have low standards of behaviour or morality.","ex":{"en":"...a group of degenerate computer hackers.","cn":"一群堕落的计算机黑客"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"堕落的人;腐化的人","en":"If you refer to someone as a degenerate, you disapprove of them because you think they have low standards of behaviour or morality."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to become worse","cn":"恶化﹐堕落﹐退化"},{"en":"to become worse. Get worse is less formal and more common than deteriorate in everyday English","cn":""},{"en":"to become gradually worse – used especially about the standard of something","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n adj v","senses":[{"en":"If something degenerates , it gets worse, like a food fight that degenerates to an all-out spaghetti-throwing war. Degenerate can also describe an immoral person — or the behavior of such a person."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. rapidly | easily","PREP. into The solemn event rapidly degenerated into farce."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/d/degenerate_v0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/c/l3degenerate.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Her health degenerated quickly.","cn":"她的健康状况迅速恶化。"},{"en":"The march degenerated into a riot.","cn":"示威游行变成了暴动。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈdʒenəreɪt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to become worse, for example by becoming lower in quality or weaker","cn":"恶化；蜕变；衰退","ex":{"en":"Her health degenerated quickly.","cn":"她的健康状况迅速恶化。"}},{"en":"having moral standards that have fallen to a level that is very low and unacceptable to most people","cn":"堕落的；颓废的","ex":{"en":"a degenerate popular culture","cn":"颓废的大众文化"},"pos":"adjective"},{"en":"a person whose behaviour shows moral standards that have fallen to a very low level","cn":"堕落的人","pos":"noun"}]}},"derelict":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"破败的;弃置的;年久失修的","en":"A place or building that is derelict is empty and in a bad state of repair because it has not been used or lived in for a long time.","ex":{"en":"Her body was found dumped in a derelict warehouse less than a mile from her home.","cn":"在距离她家不到一英里的一座废弃仓库里发现了她遭弃的尸体。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"无家可归者;露宿街头者","en":"A derelict is a person who has no home or job and who has to live on the streets."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"a building that is dilapidated is in very bad condition because it has not been looked after or has not been repaired for a long time","cn":""},{"en":"a run-down area of a town is one in which the buildings and roads are all in bad condition, especially because the people who live there do not have enough money to look after them properly","cn":""},{"en":"something, such as a house or piece of land, that is derelict is in very bad condition because it has been empty and not used for a very long time","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n adj","senses":[{"en":"If something has been abandoned, you can call it derelict . Even if a person has abandoned his responsibilities, you can say that he is derelict in his duties. But don't call a lost child derelict — unless, of course, he has neglected his chores."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be, lie, look, seem, stand The land lay derelict for ten years. | become | make sth The houses were made derelict by the fire.","ADV. totally | almost, virtually | partially, partly a partially derelict mill"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/5/derelict_adj0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/c/derelict1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"derelict land/buildings/sites","cn":"荒废的土地；被废弃的建筑物；破旧的遗址"},{"en":"derelicts living on the streets","cn":"流落街头的乞丐"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈderəlɪkt","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"not used or cared for and in bad condition","cn":"荒废的；被弃置的；破旧的","ex":{"en":"derelict land/buildings/sites","cn":"荒废的土地；被废弃的建筑物；破旧的遗址"}},{"en":"failing completely to do your duty or perform your obligations","cn":"玩忽职守的","lab":"especially North American English","ex":{"en":"They have been grossly derelict in their duty.","cn":"他们严重失职。"}},{"en":"a person without a home, a job or property","cn":"无家可归者；乞丐；社会弃儿","ex":{"en":"derelicts living on the streets","cn":"流落街头的乞丐"},"pos":"noun"}]}},"depreciate":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"(使)(货币等)贬值;（使）跌价","en":"If something such as a currency depreciates or if something depreciates it, it loses some of its original value.","ex":{"en":"Countries may also find their currency is depreciating in foreign markets.","cn":"一些国家也可能会发现自己的货币正在国外市场上贬值。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to become gradually less valuable over a period of time","cn":""},{"en":"to decrease in value or price","cn":"贬值﹐跌价"},{"en":"to reduce the value of something over time, especially for tax purposes","cn":"使折旧"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"Something depreciates when it loses value. If you bought shares of a company for $10 each a year ago and now they’re worth $1 each, guess what: they have depreciated ."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. quickly, rapidly","VERB + DEPRECIATE be expected to, be likely to","PREP. against Sterling is expected to depreciate against the dollar. | by The rupee depreciated by 9 per cent.","PHRASES depreciate in value Cars depreciate in value fairly rapidly."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/0/depreciate0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/e/depreciate.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The bank depreciates PCs over a period of five years.","cn":"这家银行把个人计算机分五年折旧。"},{"en":"New cars start to depreciate as soon as they are on the road.","cn":"新车一上路就开始贬值。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈpriːʃieɪt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to become less valuable over a period of time","cn":"贬值；跌价","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"New cars start to depreciate as soon as they are on the road.","cn":"新车一上路就开始贬值。"}},{"en":"to reduce the value, as stated in the company’s accounts, of a particular asset over a particular period of time","cn":"折旧","g":"[transitive]","lab":"business","ex":{"en":"The bank depreciates laptops over a period of five years.","cn":"这家银行把笔记本电脑的折旧年限定为五年。"}},{"en":"to make something seem unimportant or of no value","cn":"贬低；轻视","g":"[transitive]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"I had no intention of depreciating your contribution.","cn":"我并不想贬低你的贡献。"}}]}},"detection":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"觉察;发觉","en":"Detection is the act of noticing or sensing something.","ex":{"en":"...the early detection of breast cancer.","cn":"乳腺癌的早期发觉"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"发现;查出","en":"Detection is the discovery of something which is supposed to be hidden.","ex":{"en":"They are cheating but are sophisticated enough to avoid detection.","cn":"他们在作弊，但因为手法老练没有被发现。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"侦查;侦破","en":"Detection is the work of investigating a crime in order to find out what has happened and who committed it.","ex":{"en":"The detection rate for motor vehicle theft that year was just 11.7 per cent","cn":"那一年机动车盗窃案的侦破率仅为11.7%。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"when something is found that is not easy to see, hear etc, or the process of looking for it","cn":"察觉﹐发现﹔侦察"},{"en":"detection of Early detection of the disease is vital.","cn":"这种病关键在于及早发现。 escape/avoid detection By flying low, the plane avoided detection by enemy radar. 飞机低空飞行﹐躲过了敌人雷达的探测。"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"Detection is the act of noticing or discovering something. At the airport, you might see German Shepherds trained in the detection of drug smuggling or explosives in luggage."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. early Our aim is the early detection and treatment of all cancers.","VERB + DETECTION avoid, escape, evade Their prey can sometimes escape detection by remaining still.","DETECTION + NOUN rate The latest figures show falling crime detection rates."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/8/ld44detection.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/c/detection.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Last year the detection rate for car theft was just 13%.","cn":"去年汽车盗窃案的侦破率仅为 13%。"},{"en":"Early detection of cancers is vitally important.","cn":"癌症的早期查出是极为重要的。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈtekʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the process of discovering or noticing something, especially something that is not easy to see, hear, etc.; the fact of being discovered or noticed","cn":"侦查；探测；察觉；发现","ex":{"en":"crime prevention and detection","cn":"犯罪的预防和侦查"}}]}},"defy":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"违抗;反抗;不服从","en":"If you defy someone or something that is trying to make you behave in a particular way, you refuse to obey them and behave in that way.","ex":{"en":"This was the first (and last) time that I dared to defy my mother","cn":"这是我第一次(也是最后一次)胆敢反抗我的母亲。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"挑战;激;认为…不敢(或无法)（做）","en":"If you defy someone to do something, you challenge them to do it when you think that they will be unable to do it or too frightened to do it.","ex":{"en":"I defy you to come up with one major accomplishment of the current Prime Minister","cn":"我敢说你讲不出现任首相的哪怕一项重大成就。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"无法，难以(描述或理解)","en":"If something defies description or understanding, it is so strange, extreme, or surprising that it is almost impossible to understand or explain.","ex":{"en":"When the flowers open in spring they fill the night air with a fragrance that defies description","cn":"春天鲜花开放时，夜里的空气中会弥漫一种难以名状的香气。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"看上去比实际年轻","en":"If you say that someone defies their age, or defies the years, you mean that their appearance or behaviour suggests that they are younger than they really are.","ex":{"en":"The singer continues to defy her age by wearing the scantiest of outfits.","cn":"那名女歌手依旧穿着非常暴露的服装，完全不似她这把岁数。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to not obey a person, order, rule, or law","cn":""},{"en":"to not obey a law or rule","cn":""},{"en":"to deliberately refuse to obey a rule or law, or what someone in authority tells you to do","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"To defy is to openly refuse to do something. You can defy the no-costumes-in-class rule if you wear your fairy wings to school, but just don’t try to defy the laws of gravity unless you can actually fly."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. openly openly defying the authorities","VERB + DEFY be prepared to, be ready to Campaigners have said that they are prepared to defy the law in order to achieve their aims. | conti"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/5/defy0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/d/defy.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Hundreds of people today defied the ban on political gatherings.","cn":"今天有数百人违抗禁止政治集会的规定。"},{"en":"I defy anyone not to cry at the end of the film.","cn":"我倒要看看有谁在电影结尾时不哭。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfaɪ","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to refuse to obey or show respect for somebody in authority, a law, a rule, etc.","cn":"违抗；反抗；蔑视","ex":{"en":"I wouldn't have dared to defy my teachers.","cn":"我可不敢不听老师的话。"}},{"en":"to be impossible or almost impossible to believe, explain, describe, etc.","cn":"不可能，无法（相信、解释、描绘等）","ex":{"en":"a political move that defies explanation","cn":"无法解释的政治举动"}},{"en":"to successfully resist something to a very unusual degree","cn":"经受住；顶住；抗住","ex":{"en":"The baby boy defied all the odds and survived (= stayed alive when it seemed certain that he would die).","cn":"这名男婴九死一生活了下来。"}}]}},"deed":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（做的）事情;作为;（尤指）事迹，功绩，劣迹","en":"A deed is something that is done, especially something that is very good or very bad.","ex":{"en":"His heroic deeds were celebrated in every corner of India.","cn":"他的英勇事迹在印度各地广为传颂。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"契约;证书;(尤指)地契，房契","en":"A deed is a document containing the terms of an agreement, especially an agreement concerning the ownership of land or a building.","ex":{"en":"He asked if I had the deeds to his father's property.","cn":"他问我是否有他父亲房产的房契。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"something that someone does","cn":""},{"en":"a particular type of action","cn":""},{"en":"things that people do, especially for enjoyment or to achieve an aim","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"A deed is an action that you perform with intent, like turning in a lost wallet you find in a store. Definitely a good deed ."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. brave, daring, glorious, good, great, heroic, mighty, noble She felt that she had done her good deed for the day. | dark, dastardly, di","VERB + DEED do, perform, perpetrate She would not be able to relax until the deed was done. warriors who performed glorious deeds evil deeds","PREP. in ~(s) He frequently expressed his love for her in words if not in deeds."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/c/brelasdedeed.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/2/deed.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"a brave/charitable/evil/good deed","cn":"勇敢的行为；善举；恶行；善行"},{"en":"a tale of heroic deeds","cn":"英雄事迹的故事"}],"oxford":{"phon":"diːd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to give somebody property or rights using a deed","cn":"立约转让（财产，权利）","ex":{"en":"He deeded the property to his wife shortly before his disappearance.","cn":"他在失踪前不久将财产转让给了他的妻子。"}},{"en":"a thing that somebody does that is usually very good or very bad","cn":"行为；行动","lab":"formal, literary，，","ex":{"en":"It's a stirring tale of heroic deeds.","cn":"这是一则激动人心的英雄事迹。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a legal document that you sign, especially one that proves that you own a house or a building","cn":"（尤指房产）契约，证书","lab":"especially North American English","ex":{"en":"The deeds of the house are missing.","cn":"房子的房产证不见了。"},"pos":"noun"}]}},"deranged":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"精神错乱的;发狂的;发癫的","en":"Someone who is deranged behaves in a wild and uncontrolled way, often as a result of mental illness.","ex":{"en":"A deranged man shot and killed 14 people.","cn":"一个精神失常的男子开枪打死了 14 人。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"having an illness that affects your mind and your behaviour","cn":""},{"en":"mentally ill","cn":""},{"en":"mentally ill. This word is now usually considered offensive, and is usually used in a different meaning, when you think that someone’s ideas are not sensible","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj","senses":[{"en":"Deranged means insane. You've probably read headlines about deranged murderers, but someone might also be called deranged for bizarre behavior like wearing a bathing suit while skiing."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be, seem | become","ADV. a bit, slightly | mentally They took her into hospital because she was mentally deranged."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/d/brelasdederanged.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/3/deranged.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"He seemed to be on the verge of total derangement.","cn":"他似乎已濒临精神崩溃的边缘。"},{"en":"a deranged attacker","cn":"疯狂的攻击者"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈreɪndʒd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"unable to behave and think normally, especially because of a mental illness","cn":"精神错乱的；精神失常的；疯狂的","ex":{"en":"mentally deranged","cn":"精神错乱"}}]}},"deviate":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"偏离;背离","en":"To deviate from something means to start doing something different or not planned, especially in a way that causes problems for others.","ex":{"en":"They stopped you as soon as you deviated from the script","cn":"一旦你偏离了剧本的内容，他们就会喊停。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to change what you are doing so that you are not following an expected plan, idea, or type of behaviour","cn":"背离﹐偏离﹐违背"},{"en":"deviant","cn":"偏常的﹐不正常的﹐离经叛道的"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n adj v","senses":[{"en":"If something turns off course or is diverted, it deviates from the expected or the norm. Deviating from explicit recipe directions is never a good idea, unless you want inedible food or a kitchen fire."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. considerably, significantly","PREP. by Output may deviate from the average by as much as 30%. | from We had to deviate significantly from our usual route."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/d/deviate_v0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/f/l3deviate.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The bus had to deviate from its usual route because of a road closure.","cn":"因为道路封闭，公共汽车只得绕道而行。"},{"en":"He never deviated from his original plan.","cn":"他从未偏离自己最初的计划。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdiːvieɪt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to be different from something; to do something in a different way from what is usual or expected","cn":"背离；偏离；违背","ex":{"en":"The bus had to deviate from its usual route because of a road closure.","cn":"因为道路封闭，公共汽车只得绕道而行。"}}]}},"deduct":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"扣除;减去","en":"When you deduct an amount from a total, you subtract it from the total.","ex":{"en":"The company deducted this payment from his compensation","cn":"公司从他获得的赔偿金中扣去了这笔付款。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to take one number from another and calculate the answer","cn":""},{"en":"to take one number from another and calculate the answer","cn":""},{"en":"use minus between numbers or amounts to show that you are taking one figure from another","cn":""}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. at source Tax is deducted at source. | automatically This amount will be deducted automatically from your salary.","PREP. from"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/c/deduct0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/6/deduct.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The cost of your uniform will be deducted from your wages.","cn":"制服费将从你的工资中扣除。"},{"en":"Ten points will be deducted for a wrong answer.","cn":"答错一题扣十分。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈdʌkt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to take away money, points, etc. from a total amount","cn":"（从总量中）扣除，减去","ex":{"en":"Ten points will be deducted for a wrong answer.","cn":"答错一题扣十分。"}}]}},"devotee":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（狂热的）爱好者，热衷者","en":"Someone who is a devotee of a subject or activity is very enthusiastic about it.","ex":{"en":"Mr Carpenter is obviously a devotee of Britten's music.","cn":"很显然，卡彭特先生是布里顿音乐的狂热爱好者。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（某一宗教团体的）教徒","en":"A devotee is a member of a religious group.","ex":{"en":"Monks shave their heads, as do devotees of the Hare Krishna movement.","cn":"和尚要剃度，克利须那派教徒也一样。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"someone who likes a particular sport, team, or famous entertainer very much","cn":""},{"en":"someone who likes a particular activity very much","cn":""},{"en":"someone who likes a subject, activity, performer etc very much, is very interested in them and knows a lot about them","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"Devotee is a fancy word for \"fan.\" Some people are super fans of Neil Diamond. Others save their love and adoration for Mozart. Either way, they are huge devotees of the musicians they love."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. ardent, committed, fervent, great, serious I'm a great devotee of jazz."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/5/ld41devotee.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/f/l3devotee.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"devotees of Krishna （","cn":"印度教）黑天的虔诚信徒"},{"en":"a devotee of science fiction","cn":"科幻小说的狂热爱好者"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdevəˈtiː","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person who admires and is very enthusiastic about somebody/something","cn":"（狂热的）崇拜者，爱好者","ex":{"en":"a devotee of science fiction","cn":"科幻小说的狂热爱好者"}},{"en":"a very religious person who belongs to a particular group","cn":"虔诚的宗教信徒","ex":{"en":"devotees of Krishna","cn":"（印度教）黑天的虔诚信徒"}}]}},"detachable":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"可拆卸的;可分开的;可分离的","en":"If a part of an object is detachable, it has been made so that it can be removed from the object.","ex":{"en":"...a cake tin with a detachable base.","cn":"活底蛋糕烤模"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"able to be removed and put back","cn":"可拆卸的﹐可分离的"}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be","ADV. fully The lid is fully detachable. | easily, readily","PREP. from The handle is detachable from the bag."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/c/detachable0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/4/laaddetachable.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"a coat with a detachable hood","cn":"带有活风帽的外套"},{"en":"The coat has a detachable lining.","cn":"这件外套的衬里可拆卸。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈtætʃəbl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"that can be taken off","cn":"可拆卸的；可分开的","ex":{"en":"a coat with a detachable hood","cn":"带有活风帽的外套"}}]}},"debris":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"（被毁物的）残骸;碎片;垃圾","en":"Debris is pieces from something that has been destroyed or pieces of rubbish or unwanted material that are spread around.","ex":{"en":"I stood at the foot of the collapsed tower and watched the rescue workers sifting through the debris","cn":"我站在倒塌的高塔脚下，看着救援人员在瓦砾堆中搜寻。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the pieces of something that are left after it has been destroyed in an accident, explosion etc","cn":"碎片﹐残骸"},{"en":"pieces of waste material, paper etc","cn":"残渣﹐垃圾﹐废弃物"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"Debris is trash scattered around after a disaster, like shattered glass on the road after a car accident."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. flying She was hit on the head by flying debris. | food, plant, rock These worms feed on plant debris. | garden, industrial, volcanic","QUANT. piece | heap, pile","VERB + DEBRIS scatter, shower The tank exploded, scattering debris all over the field. | clear (away/up), clear sth of, remove Teams of peop","DEBRIS + VERB accumulate Debris accumulates at the bottom of the bottle.","PREP. among the ~, in the ~ She found a pair of children's shoes among the debris. | through the ~"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/0/debris0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/8/debris.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Clear away leaves and other garden debris from the pond.","cn":"把池塘里的树叶和其他庭园垃圾清除干净。"},{"en":"Emergency teams are still clearing the debris from the plane crash.","cn":"各抢救小组仍在清理失事飞机的残骸。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdebriː","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"pieces of wood, metal, building materials, etc. that are left after something has been destroyed","cn":"残骸；碎片；破片","ex":{"en":"Emergency teams are still clearing the debris from the plane crash.","cn":"各抢救小组仍在清理失事飞机的残骸。"}},{"en":"rubbish or pieces of material that are left somewhere and are not wanted","cn":"残渣；垃圾；废弃物","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"Clear away leaves and other garden debris from the pond.","cn":"把池塘里的树叶和其他庭园垃圾清除干净。"}}]}},"deterrent":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"威慑力量;威慑因素;遏制物","en":"A deterrent is something that prevents people from doing something by making them afraid of what will happen to them if they do it.","ex":{"en":"They seriously believe that capital punishment is a deterrent","cn":"他们真的相信死刑具有威慑作用。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"威慑武器","en":"A deterrent is a weapon or set of weapons designed to prevent enemies from attacking by making them afraid to do so.","ex":{"en":"...a nuclear deterrent.","cn":"核威慑武器"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"威慑的;吓阻的;遏制的","en":"If something has a deterrent effect, it has the effect of preventing people from doing certain things.","ex":{"en":"Hopefully, that will have a deterrent effect on drug syndicates in the future.","cn":"希望这能在将来对贩毒集团起到威慑作用。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"something that makes people afraid to or less likely to do something","cn":""},{"en":"a disadvantage which makes people less willing to do something","cn":""},{"en":"something that makes someone less likely to do something, by making them realize it will be difficult or have bad results","cn":"遏制物﹐威慑物﹐威慑力量"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n adj","senses":[{"en":"A deterrent makes you not want to do something. Let's say there's a giant pile of cookies being guarded by an angry dog — the dog is a deterrent ."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. effective, good, great, powerful, real | the ultimate Defenders of the death penalty clearly regard it as the ultimate deterrent. | nuc","VERB + DETERRENT act as, be a punishment that will act as a deterrent to other offenders","DETERRENT + NOUN effect They were arguing about the deterrent effect of nuclear weapons.","PREP. as a ~ The bodies of executed criminals were hung on the city gates as a deterrent. | ~ against a deterrent against cheating | ~ for T"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/3/deterrent0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/d/deterrent.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Hopefully his punishment will act as a deterrent to others.","cn":"对他的惩罚但愿能起到杀一儆百的作用。"},{"en":"the country's nuclear deterrents (= nuclear weapons that are intended to stop an enemy from attacking)","cn":"这个国家核武器的威慑力"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈterənt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"something that makes somebody less likely to do something (= that deters them)","cn":"威慑因素；遏制力","ex":{"en":"Hopefully his punishment will act as a deterrent to others.","cn":"对他的惩罚但愿能起到杀一儆百的作用。"}},{"en":"making somebody less likely to do something","cn":"威慑因素；遏制力","ex":{"en":"They were arguing about the deterrent effect of nuclear weapons.","cn":"他们在争论核武器的威慑效果。"},"pos":"adjective"}]}},"deputy":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"副职;副手;副主管","en":"A deputy is the second most important person in an organization such as a business or government department. Someone's deputy often acts on their behalf when they are not there.","ex":{"en":"...Jack Lang, France's minister for culture, and his deputy, Catherine Tasca.","cn":"法国文化部长杰克·朗和他的副部长凯瑟琳·塔斯卡"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"代表;议员;立法委员","en":"In some parliaments or law-making bodies, the elected members are called deputies .","ex":{"en":"The president appealed to deputies to approve the plan quickly.","cn":"总统呼吁议员尽快通过这一方案。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"someone who is immediately below the rank of another manager, and who is officially in charge when that other person is away or ill","cn":""},{"en":"a manager who is in charge of an organization or department when a more senior manager is not there","cn":""},{"en":"someone who is directly below another person in rank, and who is officially in charge when that person is not there","cn":"代理人﹐副手﹐副职"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"1 n 2 n","senses":[{"en":"A deputy is a sheriff's assistant, the person who fills in when the sheriff isn't available. When a deputy is in charge, she has the same powers and authority as the sheriff."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. acting | former a former deputy chairman of the Democratic Party","VERB + DEPUTY appoint (sb as) A new deputy has not yet been appointed. | act as","DEPUTY + NOUN chair, chairman, director, governor, head, leader, manager, minister, president, etc. He was appointed deputy head of the scho","PREP. ~ to She is acting as deputy to the chairman of the board. 2 member of a parliament","ADJ. congressional, parliamentary 133 of the parliamentary deputies voted against the treaty. | opposition | right-wing, socialist, etc.","VERB + DEPUTY elect Three women were among the 77 deputies elected."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/8/deputy0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/4/deputy.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"I'm acting as deputy till the manager returns.","cn":"我在经理回来之前代行他的职务。"},{"en":"the deputy head of a school","cn":"副校长"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdepjuti","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person who is the next most important person below a business manager, a head of a school, a political leader, etc. and who does that person’s job when they are away","cn":"副手；副职；代理","ex":{"en":"I'm acting as deputy till the manager returns.","cn":"我在经理回来之前代行他的职务。"}},{"en":"the name for a member of parliament in some countries","cn":"（某些国家的）议员","ex":{"en":"23 women were among the 77 deputies elected.","cn":"当选的77名议员中有23名女性。"}},{"en":"(in the US) a police officer who helps the sheriff of an area","cn":"（美国协助地方治安官办案的）警官"}]}},"demonstrator":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"示威者;示威游行（或集会）者","en":"Demonstrators are people who are marching or gathering somewhere to show their opposition to something or their support for something.","ex":{"en":"I saw the police using tear gas to try and break up a crowd of demonstrators.","cn":"我看见警察正试图用催泪弹驱散一群示威者。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"示范者;演示者","en":"A demonstrator is a person who shows people how something works or how to do something."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"样品;试用品","en":"A demonstrator is an item for sale that customers can use and test so they can decide whether they want to buy it.","ex":{"en":"Saab dealers are currently giving away unaccompanied 24-hour test drives in posh demonstrator models.","cn":"萨博汽车的经销商目前正推出高档样品车无人陪同的 24 小时试驾活动。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"someone who believes that all war and violence is wrong","cn":""},{"en":"strongly against war, especially a war that your country is fighting at the present time","cn":""},{"en":"a group of people or countries that are peace-loving believe strongly in peace rather than war","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"If you participate in a political protest demonstration, you are a demonstrator . Demonstrate means to show, and by dint of your presence, you are showing that you agree with the protest message."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. angry Angry demonstrator s threw stones. | peaceful | anti-government, pro-democracy, etc.","QUANT. crowd, group Polic e opened fire on a crowd of peacefu l demonstrators .","VERB + DEMONSTRATOR disperse Troops were brought in to dispers e the demonstrators. | clash with, fire on, open fire on, use sth against Wat","DEMONSTRATOR + VERB gather The demonstrators had gathered in the cathedral square. | march Demonstrators marched on the parliament building.","PHRASES clashes between police and demonstrators"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/4/demonstrator0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/4/demonstrator.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"anti-war demonstrators","cn":"反战示威者"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdemənstreɪtə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person who takes part in a public meeting or march (= an organized walk by many people) in order to protest against somebody/something or to show support for somebody/something","cn":"（集会或游行的）示威者","ex":{"en":"Troops opened fire on the demonstrators.","cn":"部队朝示威人群开枪。"}},{"en":"a person whose job is to show or explain how something works or is done","cn":"示范者；演示者","ex":{"en":"He works as a demonstrator in anatomy at Wolfson College.","cn":"他在沃尔夫森学院担任解剖学演示员。"}}]}},"defunct":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"不再存在的;停止运转的;坏了的","en":"If something is defunct, it no longer exists or has stopped functioning or operating.","ex":{"en":"...the leader of the now defunct Social Democratic Party","cn":"现已不复存在的社会民主党的领导人"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"not existing anymore, or not useful anymore","cn":"不再存在的﹐不再使用的"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj","senses":[{"en":"Defunct describes something that used to exist, but is now gone. A magazine that no longer publishes, like Sassy , the girl-power mag from the '90s, is defunct , for example."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be | become | make sth The long-playing record was made defunct by the arrival of the CD. | consider sth These machines are now consid","ADV. almost, virtually | largely | sadly He wrote many articles for the now sadly defunct newspaper, the Daily Correspondent. | long, now th"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/6/defunct0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/2/defunct.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"the now-defunct nuclear reactor","cn":"现已废弃的核反应堆"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfʌŋkt","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"no longer existing, operating or being used","cn":"已灭绝的；不再起作用的；不再使用的","ex":{"en":"a largely defunct railway network","cn":"基本上已经不复存在的铁路网络"}}]}},"deduce":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"推论;推断;演绎","en":"If you deduce something or deduce that something is true, you reach that conclusion because of other things that you know to be true.","ex":{"en":"Alison had cleverly deduced that I was the author of the letter.","cn":"艾莉森已经聪明地推断出那封信就是我写的。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to think that something is true, after thinking about it, checking it, or looking at it","cn":""},{"en":"to decide that something is true after thinking carefully about all the facts","cn":""},{"en":"to decide that something is true or to make a judgment about it after carefully considering all the facts","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"To deduce is to figure something out based on what you already know. When you see a person crying, it's easy to deduce that the person is sad. Unless they're happy, of course. Sometimes happy people cry."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. easily | logically The total amount can be deduced logically from the figures available.","VERB + DEDUCE be able to, can | be possible to Using the evidence available it is possible to deduce quite a lot about how these people live","PREP. from We deduce from his behaviour that he is trying to gain attention."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/f/deduce0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/7/deduce.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Can we deduce from your silence that you do not approve?","cn":"你保持沉默，我们是否可以据此而推断出你不赞成？"},{"en":"We can deduce a lot from what people choose to buy.","cn":"从人们选购的东西可以作出多方面的推断。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈdjuːs","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to form an opinion about something based on the information or evidence that is available","cn":"推论；推断；演绎","ex":{"en":"We can deduce a lot from what people choose to buy.","cn":"从人们选购的东西可以作出多方面的推断。"}}]}},"decree":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"法令;政令","en":"A decree is an official order or decision, especially one made by the ruler of a country.","ex":{"en":"In July he issued a decree ordering all unofficial armed groups in the country to disband","cn":"他于 7 月份下令解散国内所有的非正式武装组织。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"决定;规定;命令;颁布","en":"If someone in authority decrees that something must happen, they decide or state this officially.","ex":{"en":"The UN Security Council has decreed that the election must be held by May","cn":"联合国安理会已通过决议，规定选举必须在5月前举行。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"判决;裁决","en":"A decree is a judgment made by a law court.","ex":{"en":"...court decrees.","cn":"法庭的裁决"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an official statement ordering you to do something, given by someone with the power to do this, especially a military officer","cn":""},{"en":"a statement telling someone what they must do, usually giving them details of how they should do it","cn":""},{"en":"an official order by someone such as a king or a military officer which must be obeyed","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n v","senses":[{"en":"Look carefully! A decree isn't something you get when you graduate. That one little letter change makes it something else altogether: a legally binding command or the announcement of such a thing."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. emergency The government had the power to legislate by emergency decree independently of Parliament. | papal, presidential, royal | cou","VERB + DECREE adopt, issue, pass, publish The president issued a decree prohibiting trade unions. | sign | enforce Local inspectors helped e","PREP. in a/the ~ In an emergency decree, the government banned all rallies. | ~ on a decree on property rights"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/3/decree_v0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/7/decree1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"We cannot decree what the committee should do.","cn":"我们不能命令委员会做什么。"},{"en":"It was decreed that the following day would be a holiday.","cn":"法令宣布第二天为休假日。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈkriː","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an official order from a leader or a government that becomes the law","cn":"法令；政令","g":"[countable, uncountable]","ex":{"en":"to issue/sign a decree","cn":"颁布／签署法令"}},{"en":"a decision that is made in court","cn":"（法院的）裁定，判决","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"a decree on property rights","cn":"关于财产权的法令"}},{"en":"to decide, judge or order something officially","cn":"裁定；判决；颁布","ex":{"en":"The government decreed a state of emergency.","cn":"政府下令进入紧急状态。"},"pos":"verb"}]}},"designate":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"标示;把…定名为;称呼","en":"When you designate someone or something as a particular thing, you formally give them that description or name.","ex":{"en":"...a man interviewed in one of our studies whom we shall designate as E","cn":"在我们的一项研究中接受访谈的男子，我们称之为 E"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"指定","en":"If something is designated for a particular purpose, it is set aside for that purpose.","ex":{"en":"Some of the rooms were designated as offices.","cn":"其中一些房间被指定用作办公室。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"指派;选派;委任","en":"When you designate someone as something, you formally choose them to do that particular job.","ex":{"en":"Designate someone as the spokesperson","cn":"指派某人为发言人"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"（已受委派）尚未上任的;（已当选）尚未就职的","en":"Designate is used to describe someone who has been formally chosen to do a particular job, but has not yet started doing it.","ex":{"en":"Japan's Prime Minister-designate is completing his Cabinet today.","cn":"日本的当选首相今日将完成组阁。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to officially choose someone or something for a particular purpose, often with the result that they cannot be used for anything else","cn":""},{"en":"to choose someone or something from among a larger group so that they can be used for a particular purpose in the future","cn":""},{"en":"to choose someone or something for a particular job or purpose 〔","cn":"为特定工作或目的〕任命﹐选定﹐指派"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v adj","senses":[{"en":"To designate is to give something a specific status. If you designate your house an opera-free zone, it means that you've officially declared that no opera is allowed to be played there."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. formally, officially The area has now been formally designated as a Site of Special Scientific Interest. | specially | clearly","PREP. for These areas have been specially designated for children."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/f/designate_v0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/c/l3designate.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The different types are designated by the letters A, B and C.","cn":"不同的类型分别用字母 A、B 和 C 标明。"},{"en":"Several pupils were designated as having moderate or severe learning difficulties.","cn":"几名学生被认定有中等或严重学习困难。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdezɪɡneɪt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to say officially that somebody/something has a particular character or name; to describe somebody/something in a particular way","cn":"命名；指定；认定","g":"[often passive]","ex":{"en":"This area has been designated (as) a National Park.","cn":"本区已定为国家公园。"}},{"en":"to choose or name somebody for a particular job or position","cn":"选定，指派，委任（某人任某职）","ex":{"en":"The director is allowed to designate his/her successor.","cn":"主任获准选定自己的继任人。"}},{"en":"to show something using a particular mark or sign","cn":"标明；标示；指明","g":"[often passive]","ex":{"en":"The different types are designated by the letters A, B and C.","cn":"不同的类型分别用字母 A、B 和 C 标明。"}},{"en":"chosen to do a job but not yet having officially started it","cn":"（已受委派）尚未上任；（已当选）尚未就职","ex":{"en":"an interview with the director designate","cn":"与未到任主任的面谈"},"pos":"adjective"}]}},"defiance":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"违抗;蔑视;挑战","en":"Defiance is behaviour or an attitude which shows that you are not willing to obey someone.","ex":{"en":"...his courageous defiance of the government.","cn":"他对政府的勇敢挑战"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"违抗（某人）；无视，不顾(规定、法律等)","en":"If you do something in defiance of a person, rule, or law, you do it even though you know that you are not allowed to do it.","ex":{"en":"Thousands of people have taken to the streets in defiance of the curfew.","cn":"成千上万的人不顾宵禁涌上街头。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"behaviour that shows you refuse to do what someone tells you to do, especially because you do not respect them","cn":"违抗﹐拒绝服从"},{"en":"→ defy act/gesture of defiance Running away was an act of defiance against his parents.","cn":"离家出走是他对父母的反抗。 in defiance (of something) Many people were drinking in the streets, in flagrant defiance of the ban. 许多人在"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"Stand up when the powers that be order you to sit down, and you've given a fine example of defiance . It happens when someone or a group of someones openly flouts or challenges authority."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. blatant, flagrant, open flagrant defiance of the rules | childish","PREP. in ~ (of) She held up a clenched fist in defiance. They organized a street demonstration in defiance of the government ban. | out of ~","PHRASES an act of defiance, a gesture of defiance"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/4/defiance0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/1/defiance.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Nuclear testing was resumed in defiance of an international ban.","cn":"尽管国际上明令禁止，核试验又在进行了。"},{"en":"a look/an act/a gesture of defiance","cn":"反抗的神色/行动/表示"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈfaɪəns","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the act of openly refusing to obey somebody/something","cn":"违抗；反抗；拒绝服从","ex":{"en":"a look/an act/a gesture of defiance","cn":"反抗的神色／行动／表示"}}]}},"delicious":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"美味的;可口的","en":"Food that is delicious has a very pleasant taste.","ex":{"en":"There's always a wide selection of delicious meals to choose from","cn":"总是有很多美味可口的饭菜可供选择。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"美妙的;怡人的;有趣的","en":"If you describe something as delicious, you mean that it is very pleasant.","ex":{"en":"There is a delicious irony in all this.","cn":"这一切中包含了一种绝妙的讽刺。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"something that is delicious tastes very good, and you enjoy eating or drinking it","cn":""},{"en":"food that is tasty has a strong taste that you like","cn":""},{"en":"succulent food contains a lot of juice and tastes good – used especially about fruit, vegetables, or meat","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj","senses":[{"en":"Delicious is an adjective describing a tasty item. If you’re a chocolate fanatic, you will probably find triple chocolate fudge cake to be absolutely delicious ."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be, look, smell, sound, taste The recipe sounds delicious. The beef tasted delicious.","ADV. most, really, truly The meal was really delicious. | absolutely, quite | rather"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/c/delicious0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/9/delicious.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Who cooked this? It's delicious.","cn":"谁做的？味道好极了。"},{"en":"the delicious coolness of the breeze","cn":"微风送爽"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈlɪʃəs","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"having a very pleasant taste or smell","cn":"美味的；可口的；芬芳的","ex":{"en":"Who cooked this? It's absolutely delicious.","cn":"这是谁做的？太好吃了。"}},{"en":"extremely pleasant","cn":"令人愉快的；令人开心的；宜人的","lab":"literary","ex":{"en":"the delicious coolness of the breeze","cn":"微风送爽"}}]}},"delegation":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"代表团","en":"A delegation is a group of people who have been sent somewhere to have talks with other people on behalf of a larger group of people.","ex":{"en":"...a delegation from Somaliland","cn":"来自索马里兰的代表团"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a team of people who have been sent by an organization or a country to represent them at an important meeting","cn":""},{"en":"a group of people representing a larger group who are sent to talk to a person in authority in order to make a complaint or a request","cn":""},{"en":"a group of people who are sent by their government to another country in order to discuss something","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"A delegation is a group of people who act as representatives of a larger group. If you’re a member of Congress from the Sunshine State, you’re a member of the Florida delegation."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. large, small | high-level, high-powered, high-ranking, important | international | all-party, joint The prime minister met with an all-","VERB + DELEGATION send | head, lead A well-known academic will head the delegation. | form | invite The government invited an international ","DELEGATION + VERB represent sth a delegation representing the new regime | include sth The delegation included representatives from nine nat","PREP. in a/the ~ all the ministers in the delegation | ~ from an official delegation from Austria | ~ of a high-powered delegation of Asian ","PHRASES the chairman/head/leader of a delegation, a member of a delegation 2 giving a job to sb with a lower rank","ADJ. effective, successful All managers should learn effective delegation.","PREP. by ~ Many of these tasks can be dealt with by delegation. | ~ of delegation of responsibility"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/6/delegation0703.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/3/delegation.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"the Dutch delegation to the United Nations","cn":"出席联合国会议的荷兰代表团"},{"en":"delegation of authority/decision-making","cn":"授予权力/决策权"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdelɪˈɡeɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a group of people who represent the views of an organization, a country, etc.","cn":"代表团","g":"[countable + singular or plural verb]","lab":"US English","ex":{"en":"the Dutch delegation to the United Nations","cn":"出席联合国会议的荷兰代表团"}},{"en":"the process of giving somebody work or responsibilities that would usually be yours","cn":"委托；委派","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"delegation of authority/decision-making","cn":"授予权力／决策权"}}]}},"descendant":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"后代;后裔;子孙","en":"Someone's descendants are the people in later generations who are related to them.","ex":{"en":"They are descendants of the original English and Scottish settlers.","cn":"他们是最初的英格兰和苏格兰定居者的后代。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"派生物;衍生物;后代产物","en":"Something modern which developed from an older thing can be called a descendant of it.","ex":{"en":"His design was a descendant of a 1956 device","cn":"他的设计是从一个 1956 年的装置衍生而来的。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a member of your family, especially one who does not live with you","cn":""},{"en":"a member of your family. Relation means the same as relative . It is often used when talking about whether someone is in the same family as another person","cn":""},{"en":"someone who is a family member of a person who lived and died a long time ago, for example the great-grandchild of that person","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n adj","senses":[{"en":"The word descendant refers to something that has come down. For example, everyone is a descendant , or the end of a line of ancestors, just as modern art is a descendant of past art that contributed to its style and technique."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. direct, lineal Quechua, the lineal descendant of the Inca language | collateral | immediate | distant, remote He was an O'Conor and a d"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/d/descendant0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/3/descendant.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"He was an O'Conor and a direct descendant of the last High King of Ireland.","cn":"他属于奥康纳家族，是爱尔兰最后一位君王的嫡系后裔。"},{"en":"Many of them are descendants of the original settlers.","cn":"他们中许多人都是早期移民的后裔。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈsendənt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person’s descendants are their children, their children’s children, and all the people who live after them who are related to them","cn":"后裔；后代；子孙","ex":{"en":"He was an O'Conor and a direct descendant of the last High King of Ireland.","cn":"他属于奥康纳家族，是爱尔兰最后一位君王的嫡系后裔。"}},{"en":"something that has developed from something similar in the past","cn":"（由过去类似物发展来的）派生物","ex":{"en":"Quechua, the lineal descendant of the Inca language","cn":"克丘亚语 － 印加语的直系派生语言"}}]}},"debatable":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"有争议的;有疑问的;未定的","en":"If you say that something is debatable, you mean that it is not certain.","ex":{"en":"Whether we can stay in this situation is debatable","cn":"在这种情况下我们能否留下还很难说。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"causing a lot of disagreement and angry argument, especially in the newspapers, on television etc","cn":""},{"en":"likely to cause a lot of disagreement and argument","cn":""},{"en":"used when you think that something is not certain and that people have different opinions about it, especially in the phrase it is debatable/arguable whether","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj","senses":[{"en":"We know the sky is blue and the earth has one moon. But is there life on other planets? And how old is the universe anyway? Such things are debatable ."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be | remain","ADV. highly, very This is a highly debatable point. | somewhat"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/3/debatable0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/b/debatable.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"It is highly debatable whether conditions have improved for low-income families.","cn":"低收入家庭的生活状况是否已得到改善是一个颇有争议的问题。"},{"en":"a debatable point","cn":"有争议的观点"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈbeɪtəbl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"not certain because people can have different ideas and opinions about the thing being discussed","cn":"可争辩的；有争议的","ex":{"en":"a debatable point","cn":"有争议的观点"}}]}},"derive":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"获得;取得;得到","en":"If you derive something such as pleasure or benefit from a person or from something, you get it from them.","ex":{"en":"Mr Ying is one of those happy people who derive pleasure from helping others.","cn":"英先生属于那种助人为乐的快活人。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"（使）起源于;（使）来自","en":"If you say that something such as a word or feeling derives or is derived from something else, you mean that it comes from that thing.","ex":{"en":"Anna's strength is derived from her parents and her sisters","cn":"安娜的坚强源自于她的父母和姐姐们。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"use this to say that something that exists now developed from something else that existed before","cn":""},{"en":"if a film, story, idea, plan etc is based on something else, that is where its basic ideas or facts come from","cn":""},{"en":"to have developed in a particular place or from a particular situation","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"If you want to talk about something that comes from something else, but you want to sound sophisticated and maybe financial or scientific, use derive , like so: That scent? It's derived from a solution of roses boiled with toothpicks."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. clearly Females and cubs clearly derive some benefit from living in groups. | largely, mainly, primarily | partly | solely | directly T","PREP. from We can derive some comfort from this fact."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/8/derive0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/6/derive.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The word ‘politics’ is derived from a Greek word meaning ‘city’. * politics","cn":"一词源自希腊语，意思是 city。"},{"en":"The new drug is derived from fish oil.","cn":"这种新药是从鱼油中提炼出来的。"}]},"deciduous":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(树、灌木）每年落叶的","en":"A deciduous tree or bush is one that loses its leaves in the autumn every year."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"deciduous trees lose their leaves in winter 〔","cn":"树木〕落叶的"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj","senses":[{"en":"Hemlock, blue spruce, and white pine are all evergreens. These trees have leaves throughout the year. Oak, maple, and elm are examples of deciduous trees. They lose their foliage in the fall and grow new leaves in the spring."}]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/1/deciduous0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/d/deciduous.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dɪˈsɪdʒuəs","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"that loses its leaves every year","cn":"落叶的"}]}}});
